window.AKK_AFTER_REBIRTH_I_WAS_FORCED_TO_BECOME_THE_MAFIA_PRINCESS_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_AFTER_REBIRTH_I_WAS_FORCED_TO_BECOME_THE_MAFIA_PRINCESS_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":801,"title":"Chapter 801: 802, Regret The Chairman Won't Let You Regret.","paragraphs":["\"Erniu, I heard you quit the electronics factory in W City and went back to work at some logistics company in Pearl City?\"","\"So how much do you make a month there? Is it enough to get by?\"","Zhang Erniu's head hurt the moment she asked this question.","Third Aunt wasn't a bad person, really, but her mouth never stopped running. She loved showing off her son to anyone who'd listen.","Her son, Zhang Xiaodong, had gone to a vocational college and now worked in sales at a company in the provincial capital. Every time he came home for the holidays, he'd be all decked out, talking with that smug city air about him.","The whole family, really, had this way of acting like they were better than everyone else.","\"Not much, just enough to scrape by,\" Zhang Erniu mumbled, brushing her off.","Third Aunt's ears perked up at that. She spit a sunflower seed shell onto the ground and said, \"Oh my, Erniu, it's not that I'm lecturing you, but if you'd worked as hard as Xiaodong and gone to college, you'd be sitting in an air-conditioned office right now. You wouldn't have to do that kind of back-breaking labor.\"","Zhang Erniu smiled but said nothing.","Third Aunt continued, \"Erniu, your logistics company must keep you pretty busy, right?\"","\"Not too bad. Three shifts, eight hours a day.\"","\"Eight hours?\"","Third Aunt was genuinely surprised to hear that.","Everyone from the village who worked outside the city put in twelve or more hours a day, often pulling graveyard shifts.","Erniu only worked eight hours? That couldn't be right.","\"So you're just like someone in an office? Do you sit at a desk at the logistics company too?\"","\"No, I'm a sorter. I move goods.\"","\"Moving goods, but only eight hours? Then how much can you even make? Two thousand?\"","\"Something like that,\" Zhang Erniu said casually.","In truth, his base pay plus performance bonuses came to about four thousand a month, with an annual bonus of over ten thousand at year-end. But he didn't want to tell the truth—if he did, Third Aunt would just accuse him of bragging.","After all, in most people's minds, doing manual labor in Pearl City for over four thousand a month, plus some mythical year-end bonus, was simply impossible.","So he didn't bother explaining. Let her guess whatever she wanted.","Once Third Aunt confirmed that Erniu's salary was only around two thousand, maybe less, her sense of superiority shot through the roof. She brought up her precious son again.","\"Let me tell you, Xiaodong got promoted last month. He's a sales team leader now, making four to five thousand a month with commission. Just the other day he called and said he wanted to earn more money to take us to the south coast for a trip—said he'd show us old folks the sea and put us up in a fancy hotel.\"","By this point, the wrinkles on Third Aunt's face were all spread out in a grin.","Zhang Erniu's father, sitting on the doorstep, showed a hint of envy when he heard this. \"Xiaodong's really made something of himself. You two are in for a good life.\"","\"You bet we are!\"","Third Aunt was on a roll now. \"Xiaodong said once he saves up enough to buy a big house in the city, he'll move us in. No more living out here in the countryside.\"","Zhang Erniu's mother couldn't hold it in anymore. \"Alright, enough showing off. That's not even a sure thing yet.\"","\"How is it not sure? My son is filial!\"","Zhang Erniu's mother didn't bother arguing. She turned and headed to the kitchen.","Third Aunt redirected her attention to Zhang Erniu. \"Erniu, does your company ever organize trips or anything? I hear a lot of big companies have that kind of perk.\"","Zhang Erniu shook his head. \"We're in logistics. Manual labor. No trips or anything like that.\"","Third Aunt nodded. \"Figured as much. Moving goods—having a steady job is plenty, never mind trips. Not like Xiaodong's big company. They organized a two-day employee trip once. Two whole days.\"","\"Erniu, don't mind me saying this, but if you'd studied hard back in the day, you'd be going on company trips too.\"","\"When Xiaodong goes on his next trip, I'll have him take lots of pictures so you can see what good company benefits look like. Open your eyes a bit.\"","\"Yeah, sure, sure,\" Zhang Erniu said absentmindedly, a strange feeling stirring in his chest.","He thought about his childhood. Back then, his family wasn't just poor—it wasn't that he couldn't study. It was that he'd been a lazy, playful kid who didn't like school. He dropped out after fifth grade.","It wasn't until he followed the villagers into the real world and got knocked around by life that he regretted not taking his studies seriously.","Back then, he'd thought that once he earned enough money working, he'd take his family on a trip, show them the world outside.","But reality had other plans. He'd worked over a decade and never really made anything. Now that he finally had a decent job, he had to save for a house, raise a kid, pay for food and bills—there was never any extra money left.","That dream of taking his parents to see the world stayed buried at the bottom of his heart, surfacing every now and then.","Third Aunt just kept yapping away without pause.","Zhang Erniu couldn't take it anymore. He turned and went inside.","Inside, six-year-old Zhang Xiwa was hunched over the table, drawing.","\"Xiwa, what are you drawing?\"","\"Daddy!\"","The little kid looked up, holding up his drawing to show him: \"I drew the sea. The teacher said the sea is blue, really really big. Dad, have you ever seen the sea?\"","Zhang Erniu shook his head: \"Dad... never seen it.\"","\"What about Mom?\"","\"Mom's never seen it either.\"","\"What about Grandpa?\"","\"Nope.\"","\"What about Grandma?\"","\"Nope.\"","Zhang Xiwa: \"Then who in our family has seen the sea?\"","Zhang Erniu opened his mouth, but no words came out.","Zhang Xiwa: \"When I grow up, I'm going to earn lots and lots of money, and take Dad and Mom, and Grandpa and Grandma, to go see the sea!\"","When Zhang Erniu heard that, his nose stung. He reached out and ruffled his son's head: \"Alright, then when you grow up and earn money, you take us there.\"","As he said this, he couldn't help turning his head to look at his parents outside the door, their hair already half white. When he was little, he seemed to have said the same thing to his own parents.","But in the blink of an eye, over a decade had passed—his parents had grown old, and he still hadn't kept that promise.","Just then, the phone in his pocket buzzed.","He pulled it out and saw a text message from a coworker at the logistics center.","[Erniu! Erniu! Have you checked the company intranet? If you haven't, go look now!]","Zhang Erniu saw the message content and was a little confused.","[No, I'm back in my hometown. What's going on?]","[Do you have a computer? If you do, go check it now.]","[I'm in my hometown and there's no internet café. I can't check it.]","The moment he sent that text, the other person quickly replied with a multimedia message.","The resolution was pretty bad, but he could still barely make out the words.","It turned out to be an internal letter issued by the group chairman.","\"To All Employees of Wanlonghui: Walking Together in Heart and Mind, Facing the Future Together, Never Letting Any Effort Go Unrewarded!\"","Zhang Erniu read it word by word.","The earlier parts about restructuring he didn't quite understand, but the later content he understood all too well.","[The first employee immediate-family travel season of Wanlonghui Group is now open, eligible for fully company-subsidized domestic travel...]","[The entire trip includes five-star hotel accommodation, with professional tour guides and a medical support team...]","[Employees can choose travel routes based on their family's wishes, such as the Imperial Capital Culture Tour, Southern Coastal Tour, BS Province Scenery Tour, and more...]","[For employee children, the company will organize a summer camp program, covering educational visits to the aquarium, zoo, science museum, and outdoor team-building activities...]","[All expenses are covered by the group, without taking up any of the employees' personal benefits quota...]","After reading the content, this tough, rugged man found his hands trembling involuntarily.","From excitement!","He rubbed his eyes hard and read it again.","He wasn't mistaken!","Five-star hotels!","Seven-day domestic trips!","All expenses fully covered by the company!","And the kids' summer camp—aquarium, zoo, science museum, all of it—fully covered too.","After confirming there was no mistake, Zhang Erniu turned abruptly to look at the drawing his son had made.","The sea.","Blue, stretching endlessly to the horizon.","\"Dad, what's wrong?\"","Zhang Erniu didn't answer his son right away. He read the letter once more.","After confirming it wasn't fake, and that the signature was indeed the chairman's name, Zhang Erniu's eyes went red, as if sand had gotten into them.","He was thirty years old. Although he'd left the province before, he had never once seen the sea.","But at least he still had a chance to go traveling someday.","But his parents—they were nearly sixty, and had barely ever left their village or town.","The farthest they'd ever gone was to the hospital in Mingzhu City to have their legs checked. Their whole lives had been spent working the land.","Once they got even older and their legs gave out, this life might truly just pass them by.","With regrets.","But now, the chairman was suddenly telling them...","The company would take your parents and your kids out to see the world.","That feeling—he couldn't put it into words. He just couldn't quite hold back the tears threatening to spill from his eyes."]},{"number":802,"title":"Chapter 802: Chapter 803: Angering Third Lady.","paragraphs":["\"Dad, why are you crying?\"","Only then did Zhang Erniu realize he was actually in tears.","He quickly wiped his face and scooped up his son: \"Dad's not crying, Dad's just happy! Happy!\"","\"Happy about what?\"","Zhang Erniu didn't have time to explain. He just ran out of the house with his son in his arms.","In the yard, Third Aunt was still chatting with his father, going on and on about her son. That woman had talked his mother into leaving, talked him into leaving, and now she was starting on his father, bragging about her son again. Relentless.","\"Second Brother, if you ask me, you shouldn't keep yourself cooped up in this countryside forever. Have Erniu take you out for a change of scenery. Look at my Xiaodong—he said in a couple of years he'll take us to see the ocean...\"","\"Third Aunt!\" Zhang Erniu suddenly spoke up, cutting her off.","Third Aunt was in full swing and wasn't pleased at the interruption: \"Erniu, what's wrong? Why the sudden shouting?\"","\"Oh? Erniu, your eyes are red—did you cry?\"","\"Not that I'm one to lecture you, but even if your job isn't great right now, there's no reason to cry about it, is there?\"","Zhang Erniu ignored her and looked at his father sitting on the doorstep, saying excitedly: \"Dad, the company just sent out a notice—starting in July, they're organizing trips for employees' family members. We can go south to see the ocean, or head to the capital to watch the flag-raising and see the Great Wall. Seven days total, staying at five-star hotels, eating big meals, and the company covers every single expense!\"","The yard fell silent instantly.","Third Aunt couldn't sit still. She shot up from her seat.","\"What did you say?\"","\"The company is inviting your parents on a trip? Did you say that wrong?\"","Zhang Erniu looked at Third Aunt's face—like she'd just seen a ghost—and felt an immense satisfaction inside.","\"Third Aunt, my company is inviting my parents on a trip. Food, drink, and fun all covered, staying at the finest five-star hotels! And not just my parents—Xiwa gets to go to summer camp too, and visit the aquarium!\"","Just to make sure she believed him, he deliberately held out his phone.","\"Third Aunt, take a look. This is the letter sent by our company's chairman. The direct relatives of every full-time employee can go—from top management all the way down to ordinary guys like me. Everyone's included!\"","Third Aunt couldn't read much, but seeing the neat notice on the phone screen and the bright red official seal stamped at the bottom, she was about seventy or eighty percent convinced.","For a moment, whether from anger or something else, she couldn't even get a word out.","Zhang Erniu's father quickly stood up, also somewhat in disbelief: \"Your boss is inviting us on a trip? Really? How much money must that cost?\"","Zhang Erniu: \"Dad, it's true. No matter how much it costs, the chairman said the company covers everything. We don't pay a penny—it's an employee benefit!\"","\"Dad, do you want to see the ocean? Then let's head south this time and go look at the sea!\"","Zhang Erniu's mother happened to be walking out of the kitchen with a basin of water in her hands. When she heard her son's words, she hurriedly asked: \"Erniu, are you serious? The company is inviting us old folks on a trip? And staying in a five, five... five-star hotel?\"","\"Really, Mom! You and Dad are both going, and Xiwa too. The company even arranged a summer camp for the kids—there'll be staff to take them to the aquarium, the zoo, and places like that. You and Dad can just relax and enjoy yourselves.\"","\"Well... but how much does all this cost?\" His mother's reaction matched his father's exactly—her first thought was the money.","\"Don't worry about the money, Mom and Dad. The company's got it covered. Our chairman said you've worked hard your whole lives, and you deserve to get out and see the world.\" Zhang Erniu said.","Tears streamed down Zhang Erniu's mother's face.","She remembered the year she married into the Zhang family—she was only eighteen then, and she'd started working the fields with Erniu's father right away, barely scraping together a few coins year after year.","Then Erniu was born, and things got even tighter.","Later, Erniu dropped out of school, farmed for a few years, and then went off to be a migrant worker—but he never made much money either.","It wasn't until Erniu married and had children that their life started to ease up a little.","But she was already past fifty now.","Over thirty years had slipped by in the blink of an eye. She'd never been anywhere far. The farthest place she'd ever gone was Pearl City, and that had been just to see a doctor.","The ocean. Mountain scenery. Watching the flag-raising in the capital.","Those were things she could only dream about.","But now her son was suddenly saying the company wanted to make those dreams come true.","How could she not be happy, not be moved?","Her son had really found himself a good company!","\"Xiwa, did you hear that?\"","Zhang Erniu looked down at his son in his arms: \"You and Grandma and Grandpa are going to see the ocean for real—the real ocean, blue, stretching as far as the eye can see!\"","Zhang Xiwa bounced with joy: \"Really, Daddy? I want to go too! I want to pick up seashells by the beach! I want to build sandcastles! I want to see a great big shark!\"","\"We're all going! Everyone!\"","Third Aunt stood off to the side, watching this heartwarming family scene. She'd crushed the melon seeds in her hand into powder, and her face was growing redder by the second.","Just moments ago, she'd been bragging that her son would take her traveling in the future and put her up in a big hotel.","But now, Erniu had turned around and told her the company was covering the whole family's trip—from the grandparents down to the kid—and they didn't have to spend a single cent.","And they'd be staying at some five-star grand hotel, on a seven-day tour, no less.","Her son's company only offered a two-day trip, and family members couldn't even come along.","The more she thought about it, the angrier she got. The more envious.","Why?","Why was it that her son—a university graduate—had a company whose benefits were worse than Erniu's, a man who did backbreaking labor?","\"Erniu, you'd better not be getting scammed. Let me tell you, there are tons of scammers out there these days, and they love preying on honest folks like you.\"","\"Third Aunt, have you ever been on a trip?\"","\"Erniu, listen to me. Don't go on that trip. Who knows—maybe your boss is just trying to sweet-talk you first and then dock it from your paycheck later.\"","\"Third Aunt, have you ever stayed in a five-star hotel?\"","\"What does it matter to you whether I've traveled or not?\"","\"Third Aunt, my parents are about to stay in a five-star grand hotel.\"","\"I...\"","\"Seven days, six nights. Company's paying for everything.\"","\"I...\"","\"Third Aunt, when are you going on a trip?\"","\"You...\"","\"Third Aunt, I'll have the tour guide take lots of photos of my parents and show them to you.\"","Third Aunt went fully red in the face: \"I... I'm leaving! Talking with your family is just no fun!\"","\"Take care, Third Aunt. No need to see you out.\"","After Third Aunt had stormed off in a huff, Zhang Erniu's mother broke into a smile through her tears: \"Look at you, getting your Third Aunt all riled up like that—her face was practically black.\"","Zhang Erniu laughed: \"Mom, it's not about comparing with her.\"","\"I know, I know. I'm just happy!\"","His mother wiped her tears and looked at Zhang Erniu: \"Erniu, that boss of yours—he's a truly good man! You make sure you work hard for him, you hear?\"","Zhang Erniu nodded: \"Don't worry, Mom. I'll give it my all!\"","With that, he glanced down at the signature at the bottom of the letter on his phone screen:","[Chairwoman of Wanlonghui Group: Liu Yutong.]","Seeing that name, five words rose unbidden in his mind.","Through fire and water."]},{"number":803,"title":"Chapter 803: 804, Dragon Country's Good Voice Goes Live.","paragraphs":["That evening, the Zhang family's dinner was especially pleasant, filled with laughter from start to finish.","\"Erniu, your mother and I talked it over. We're not going to the capital, and we're not going south to see the sea either.\"","Zhang Erniu was taken aback. \"Dad, why? Didn't we already agree on that?\"","Father Zhang said, \"It's a bit hot this time of year. We're worried we can't handle it. We thought it over and decided to go somewhere cooler instead.\"","Mother Zhang nodded along. \"Your father's right. Heading south in this heat would be torture.\"","Zhang Erniu: \"So where do you want to go?\"","Father Zhang thought for a moment. \"How about BS Province?\"","Zhang Erniu was a little surprised.","BS Province — the site of last year's major earthquake.","\"That earthquake last year killed so many people. Houses collapsed, schools were destroyed. When I saw those kids on TV, it broke my heart.\"","\"Later I heard that a lot of the schools have been rebuilt, and I think your company donated money to build schools too, right? We want to go see them.\"","\"Your mother and I didn't get to help back then. Going to see those kids now would be like fulfilling a wish. Besides, BS Province has lots of mountains, so it should be cooler in the summer, right?\"","Zhang Erniu's nose tingled, and he nodded. \"Alright, let's go to BS Province then.\"","\"Dad, Mom, don't worry — I'll make sure the tour guide takes plenty of photos for you. We'll capture all the new schools and new houses and bring them back to show everyone.\"","\"Good! Good!\"","After dinner and a shower, Zhang Erniu lay on his bed back home, tossing and turning, unable to sleep.","He picked up his phone again, opened that multimedia message, and read it over and over again.","Five-star hotel.","Seven-day domestic tour.","Fully covered by the company.","Even after he drifted off to sleep, a smile still lingered on his face.","He wasn't the only one too excited to sleep — many Wanlong Club employees felt the same.","The next morning at work, almost everyone was talking about the company's plan to treat employees' parents and children to a trip.","\"Yesterday my mom heard the company was treating them to a vacation, and she was so excited she didn't sleep all night. She got up at five in the morning to pack, and she's been trying on clothes.\"","\"Haha, my parents picked the capital route. They said their lifelong dream is to watch the flag-raising ceremony. Thank you, Chairwoman!\"","\"I chose the BS Province route. My mom wants to see the rebuilt disaster area. She cried for days watching the news last year, so this is finally fulfilling her dream.\"","\"Anyone else pick the island route? My mom said she's always wanted to go to the seaside and catch clams and pick shells.\"","\"Guys, I'm using my saved annual leave for this — going on a trip with my family. The company pays, I put in the effort. Perfect!\"","\"......\"","After all the lively discussion.","Nearly every employee who could get online would reply on the internal forum with the slogan that had spread from the big meeting.","【Wanlong Club! Invincible!】","Of course, because this travel benefit was arranged somewhat hastily, and with such a large number of employees' family members, the trips had to be organized in batches.","After all, trying to send over a hundred thousand people on vacation all at once would be impossible to arrange.","So it had to be coordinated based on parents' preferences and distance.","For example, some destinations might be too hot, risking heatstroke for the elderly, so those trips were postponed to September or October.","Priority was given to destinations suitable for the current season — like the mountain retreats in BS Province, or the northern seaside and grassland routes.","While Wanlong Club Group was buzzing with vacation preparations,","Season 1, Episode 1 of \"Dragon Kingdom's Voice\" officially premiered simultaneously on the provincial radio station and the LongKanShiJie platform.","The show was pre-recorded and used an unprecedented blind audition format — four coaches sat with their backs to the stage, deciding whether to turn around based purely on the voice.","In the current domestic variety show market, this was an incredibly fresh concept.","On the night of the premiere, the data team at LongKanShiJie was working overtime, all eyes glued to the numbers.","\"How's the data looking?\" Lin Muyang stood in front of the monitoring room, staring at the constantly changing figures on the big screen.","\"President Lin, fifteen minutes in, views have surpassed three million!\"","\"Thirty minutes — eight million!\"","\"One hour — fifteen million! Still climbing!\"","\"What about the comments? How are the bullet comments looking?\"","\"Exploded! The comments are flooding the screen! The system is barely keeping up! And almost all of them are positive!\"","On another big screen, dense bullet comments flashed across, an overwhelming number of them.","【Holy crap! What kind of amazing show is this? They're doing blind auditions? So creative!】","【That short guy sings so well — why hasn't the coach turned around yet? I'm dying here!】","【Ahhh! J Lun turned! J Lun finally turned!】","【The host's mouth is so fast — his ad reads sound like rap, he doesn't stop!】","【Haha, I noticed too. That guy's called Hua Shao, right? The way he rattles off ads probably left the sponsors stunned.】","【I don't know if the sponsors are stunned, but I do know I replayed the slow-motion dozens of times just to figure out what ads he was reading. Can you believe it?】","【Same here. I watched an ad segment over a dozen times just to understand it. Ridiculous!】","【.........】","The host, Hua Shao, was indeed an unexpected breakout after the show aired.","At the opening of the show, this young host delivered an astonishingly fast monologue, rattling off a sponsorship list of over a hundred characters in one breath so quickly that it left viewers dumbfounded.","\"Wanlong Plaza, Wanlong Supermarket, Wanlong Convenience Store, YuYueFang Dining, HuangQuan Internet Cafe, QingYin Tea Drinks, WanHui Select, LongKanShiJie, Weibo...\"","In one go — a dozen or more brands — all in ten seconds, not a single word wrong, not a single stumble.","Just absolutely insane!","Of course, the reaction to this kind of advertising was surprisingly positive.","【What kind of godlike speaking speed is this?】","【Is this guy a human gatling gun? It's just non-stop dakka dakka dakka.】","【I just tried to mimic it and almost bit my tongue. Too hard!】","【Hua Shao has a new nickname now — Dragon Kingdom's Fast Tongue!】","【That ad read was hardcore. Now I actually want to go grab a QingYin tea drink. Speaking of which, where do they sell that milk tea?】","【........】","As the audience marveled at the host's tongue, some eagle-eyed netizens from Pearl City had already spotted something interesting.","The title sponsor, co-sponsors, and partners of \"Dragon Kingdom's Voice\" were all Wanlong Club Group brands — without exception.","From food by YuYueFang, to drinks by QingYin, to shopping at Wanlong Plaza, from the online platforms of LongKanShiJie, Weibo, and WanHui Select, to the offline Wanlong Supermarkets...","One show had presented Wanlong Club's massive business empire in full view to the national audience.","Netizens immediately joked: \"This isn't 'Dragon Kingdom's Voice' — this is 'Wanlong Club's Voice'!\"","\"Wanlong Club Group is way too bold! Producing their own show, advertising their own brands, and still making it this good — impressive!\"","\"Speaking of which, I heard from folks back home that this company was only founded about two years ago.\"","“Only two years? That’s terrifyingly fast!”","“........”"]},{"number":804,"title":"Chapter 804: 805, Start with Zhou Ran.","paragraphs":["The day after the show aired, the official ratings were released.","CSM50 city ratings: 2.87%, taking the top spot in its time slot without any suspense.","Online views: over 30 million on the first day, setting a new record for the Longkan Vision platform since its launch.","The Douban score also hit an impressive 8.9.","The comment section was almost entirely five-star reviews.","[This is what a real music show should be — no looks, just voices, getting back to the music itself.]","[All four mentors are true heavyweights, professional and funny in their critiques. Love it, love it.]","[I've watched that ad from Flower Boy ten times now. It just gets better every time. All I can think about now is Qingyin Tea.]","[During the blind auditions, there was one contestant whose voice gave me goosebumps the moment they opened their mouth. I still can't forget that voice.]","[Can't wait for the next episode! Hurry up!]","[........]","Discussions about the show on Weibo also showed a trending-dominating momentum.","Out of the top ten trending topics on Weibo, seven were related to The Voice of Longguo.","Of course, the reason there were so many trending topics wasn't just the show's explosive popularity — Weibo, being the host platform, also \"tilted\" a bit of resources their way.","Among those seven trending topics, six were about the show's format and mentors. Only one was an exception, given to a contestant from the first episode — his name was Zhou Ran.","And it was because of him that this episode truly broke through to a wider audience.","Not because he was handsome, nor because his backstory was tragic, but because he gave the audience a powerful sense of contrast.","He could sing female vocals as a man, and his voice was incredibly beautiful and ethereal.","The episode had the highest volume of bullet comments during his appearance.","Almost everyone, including the mentors, was stunned.","[Holy shit holy shit holy shit!!! What kind of voice is this!!!]","[I've got goosebumps. This is really a guy?]","[Haha, J-Lun and Brother Huan are still discussing how well this girl sings.]","[I really want to see their faces when they turn around and find out it's a guy.]","[You could blindfold me, and I'd still think it was a woman singing.]","[Turn around already! Stop chatting!]","Besides the netizens, some veteran music critics in the industry also rushed to post their reviews late into the night.","[This is the most stunning voice I've heard in recent years, bar none.]","[Zhou Ran's vocal quality is top-tier even nationwide. High notes are piercing, low notes are steady, and his transitions between chest and head voice are seamless. Most importantly, he sings with emotion, with story, with soul. That's not something technique can teach. That's true talent given by God.]","[I dare to predict that this boy, as long as he doesn't screw up, will become the next national-level singer.]","Three days after the show aired, Zhou Ran's newly registered Weibo account saw its followers explode from a few hundred to over 300,000.","His performance video surpassed 100 million views across Longkan Vision and Weibo.","He was famous.","Famous beyond belief!","...","While The Voice of Longguo dominated the trending charts, another music talent show also went live.","The Best Music in Longguo.","It was produced under the lead of Xingyao Media and aired simultaneously on several other major domestic video platforms.","The show also brought in three mentors at the level of heavenly kings and queens. Production costs were claimed to be 200 million yuan, with massive fanfare and overwhelming advertising.","It launched only one week after The Voice of Longguo.","In truth, the show was rushed to air — preparation time was severely insufficient, and post-production was done through overtime crunch.","But Chu Junlin didn't care about any of that. He created this show for one purpose: to counter Liu Yutong.","Especially after seeing how hot The Voice of Longguo was — ratings breaking 2%, first-day online views surpassing 30 million — he grew even more anxious and directly ordered the show to premiere early.","Besides, it could ride on the coattails of The Voice of Longguo's popularity and steal some traffic.","However, reality was cruel.","The show's ratings after airing were completely crushed by The Voice of Longguo.","CSM50 city ratings: 0.87%, third place in its time slot.","Online views: 8 million on the first day, less than a third of its competitor's.","The Douban score was only 5.2.","The comment section was sharply polarized. Even with a large number of paid trolls controlling the reviews, many negative comments could still be seen.","[The mentor lineup is indeed strong, but the format is way too outdated. Isn't this just a traditional talent show with a new shell? I'm tired of it.]","[The contestants' levels are inconsistent. Several are obviously just filler, too many retreads.]","[The stage effects are decent, but compared to The Voice of Longguo, it's still a tier below.]","[Honestly, after watching The Voice of Longguo, this feels a bit bland.]","[The Best Music picked a bad time to air — it collided with The Voice of Longguo. Too bad for those three mentors.]","[I heard the show invested 200 million. At this rate, they'll be losing money back to their grandma's house.]","Only two Weibo trending topics, and those were bought.","The buzz lasted less than two hours before being pushed down by The Voice of Longguo's related topics.","After Chu Junlin finished reading the data report, his face turned ashen. He slammed the report onto the table.","\"How could this happen!\"","\"Two hundred million in investment! Two hundred million! And this is what you show me!\"","The assistant stood trembling to the side, not daring to even breathe loudly.","\"President Chu, the market feedback really isn't ideal. Internet users generally think our show format is too traditional, lacking innovation, while the blind audition format of The Voice of Longguo is... more appealing.\"","\"If the format can't compete, then what about the promotion? Did the promotion go to the dogs?\"","\"President Chu, the production team has already put 30 million into publicity — Weibo, TV, outdoor ads, all covered. But The Voice of Longguo has the natural advantage of Weibo as their home platform. The trending chart is basically wrapped up by them. Our ads on Weibo are getting diluted too much, and... and Weibo even deliberately restricted our traffic...\"","\"Liu Yutong again!\"","\"Always her!\" Chu Junlin gritted his teeth in hatred.","The assistant couldn't help but think to himself when he heard this: What does this have to do with Liu Yutong? You're the one who decided to create a show to go head-to-head with hers.","Now that you're getting crushed, can you really blame her?","Chu Junlin cursed Liu Yutong as shameless again, accusing her of using Weibo to strangle their show.","But there was absolutely nothing he could do about it.","\"Get me Ma Qingliu!\"","\"Yes, sir!\"","The assistant hurried out to fetch him.","Before long, Ma Qingliu — Xingyao Media's vice president and the chief planner of The Best Music in Longguo — walked into the office.","His face was full of fear and anxiety, because he knew that Chu Junlin summoning him suddenly could only mean bad news.","\"P-President Chu.\"","Chu Junlin stared straight at him, his gaze icy cold.","\"Ma Qingliu, you're the chief planner of this show. The show turned out like this. Don't you think you owe me an explanation?\"","Cold sweat broke out on Ma Qingliu's forehead instantly. \"Chu... President Chu, this show went from concept to launch in less than two months. The timeline really was too tight. If we could just have a bit more time...\"","\"Don't give me excuses!\"","Chu Junlin cut him off outright. \"I'm asking you—what are we doing about the next episode!\"","Ma Qingliu had no idea how to answer, stammering and unable to get a word out.","Seeing him look so pathetic and useless, Chu Junlin's anger flared up even more. He grabbed the documents on his desk and hurled them at him.","Ma Qingliu, terrified, kept begging for forgiveness and admitting his mistakes.","Only after Chu Junlin had vented enough did he coldly issue the final order: \"I don't care what methods you use—you have to bring down that 'Voice of Dragon Nation' show. Do you hear me!\"","Ma Qingliu wiped the sweat from his forehead. He knew full well that if he couldn't come up with a plan that satisfied Chu Junlin today, his vice president position would be done for—and worse, he'd be in real trouble.","Just as he was racking his brain for a solution, a thought suddenly struck him, and he became excited.","\"President Chu! President Chu! I've got it!\"","\"Speak!\"","\"It's like this—I've analyzed it carefully. The reason 'Voice of Dragon Nation' blew up after its first episode is largely because of one person.\"","\"Who?\"","\"Zhou Ran, that guy who sings female vocals in a man's voice.\"","\"We can go after him...\"","..."]},{"number":805,"title":"Chapter 805: 806, Despicable, Inspecting the Construction Site.","paragraphs":["“The first episode of 'Voice of the Dragon Kingdom' blew up largely because of one person: Zhou Ran, that kid who sings female vocals with a male voice.”","“We can use him as our angle.”","“Go on.”","“President Chu, I've looked into that kid's background. He was on a show called 'Show Me' before, but got eliminated in the second round. The show wasn't produced by our Star Shine Media, but the production team has ties with us, so we can definitely pull some strings through our connections.”","“And as you know, President Chu, contracts in this industry basically all come with hidden clauses. We can totally use that contract to stir up some trouble.”","Chu Junlin's eyes lit up when he heard this.","Indeed, contracts in the entertainment world are notoriously shady.","On the surface, they look fine, but buried inside are all sorts of overbearing terms—exclusive management agreements, rights of first refusal for renewal, sky-high penalty clauses... any one of them alone is enough to squeeze someone dry.","Especially for those small-time artists with no backing, no resources, and no worldly experience, signing a contract like that is basically signing away their soul. If they ever breach it, the penalties alone could bankrupt them.","“Can we pull off the contract angle?” Chu Junlin asked.","To be honest, with his status, he wouldn't even need these tactics to mess with a nobody. A flick of his pinky finger would be enough.","But the thing is, this show belongs to Liu Yutong. If he freely threw his connections around, that woman could retaliate in kind—her network was nothing to sneeze at either.","So he had to keep this 'competition' strictly between him and her, and avoid dragging other people into it as much as possible.","Ma Qingliu said, “Shouldn't be a problem. I'll have someone look into it right away to confirm. Even if the contract automatically lapsed after Zhou Ran got eliminated, I can still find a way to doctor things—say, forge a supplemental agreement and produce a valid contract out of thin air. Even if it doesn't stop him outright, we can drag him down in red tape and keep him from recording future episodes of 'Voice.'”","Chu Junlin nodded, barely giving the plan his grudging approval.","Seeing that President Chu wasn't all that impressed, Ma Qingliu cooked up an even more despicable idea.","“President Chu, just using the contract to force Zhou Ran out of the competition isn't enough. It won't shake the foundation of 'Voice of the Dragon Kingdom,' and it won't truly satisfy your grudge either.”","“There's another opening we can exploit.”","“What opening?”","“President Chu, you might not know this, but that Zhou Ran has a girlfriend, and she happens to be signed under one of Star Shine Media's subsidiary companies.”","“I don't know much about Zhou Ran himself, but that kid looks like one of those honest, straight-arrow types. These honest types value feelings the most, and they're the easiest to provoke. So all we have to do is let him see with his own eyes how his girlfriend gets, step by step, ... heh heh...”","He let out a lecherous, filthy chuckle that any man would recognize.","After listening, Chu Junlin waved him over, pulled him close, threw an arm around his neck, and squeezed hard. “God damn, you really are a piece of scum! You can actually dream up something this vile and low.”","Even though he was being cursed at, Ma Qingliu still fawned with a sycophantic grin: “President Chu, you flatter me. I'm just thinking about the company, thinking about you.”","Chu Junlin let go of his neck and asked, “So, you think Zhou Ran will play along with us?”","Ma Qingliu: “Don’t worry, we don’t need his cooperation. All we have to do is send him a few photos at the moment he’s angriest. Even if he knows it was us, there’s nothing he can do about it. And I have a backup plan.”","“What backup plan?”","“We can have people pose as Zhou Ran’s friends and family, spread rumors online that he was blacklisted by ‘The Voice of Dragon Country’ for refusing to sleep his way to the top. We could even write a letter of complaint in his name, post it online, and play the victim to win sympathy.”","“Anyway, things on the internet are a mix of truth and lies—no one can tell for sure. Once the narrative takes off and online mobs get riled up, the truth stops mattering. By the time his reputation is ruined, we step in to ‘rescue’ him, and he’ll have no choice but to do whatever we say.”","Chu Junlin nodded with satisfaction: “Good. Leave this to you. I only care about the results.”","“Understood!”","“You can count on me, President Chu. I’ll handle this beautifully.”","“And make sure Lin Ya is kept under control—no mistakes. If she doesn’t cooperate, make her disappear from this industry for good!”","“Yes, sir!”","..................","In June, Pearl City was already sweltering, with average temperatures hitting 96 to 99 degrees Fahrenheit.","Liu Yutong sat in the car, frowning slightly as she looked out the window at the sun-bleached road.","“Miss Liu, we’ve arrived.” Yun Cheng parked the car outside a construction site.","The moment Liu Yutong pushed open the car door, a wave of heat hit her in the face.","This construction site was where the future headquarters of Wanlong Group would stand. Most of the main structures had already been topped off, but to keep on schedule, workers were still toiling under the blazing sun despite the heat.","“Director Liu, what brings you here?” The project manager jogged over to greet her, drenched in sweat.","“Just checking on the progress.” Liu Yutong took the hard hat Yun Cheng handed her, put it on, and walked into the site.","Under the scorching sun, workers were laboring on scaffolding. Some were tying rebar, some were pouring concrete, others were hauling heavy materials. Almost every one of them was sunburnt dark, their clothes perpetually soaked then dried, then soaked again...","Liu Yutong stood at the base of the building, gazing up at the figures working high above, lost in thought.","“Director Liu, conditions out here are tough, I admit. We’ve tried to stagger the shifts to avoid the hottest part of midday—starting earlier and working later in the day.” The project manager explained carefully from beside her.","Liu Yutong nodded but said nothing, continuing to walk forward.","In a shaded corner, she spotted several workers on their break squatting on the ground, eating lunch. The food was boxed meals provided by the site—basically plain white rice topped with a few slices of meat and some greens.","The workers ate fast, wolfing down their food in two or three mouthfuls, then grabbing their oversized water jugs to chug a few gulps before getting back to work.","“How many hours a day do they work?” Liu Yutong asked.","The project manager hesitated briefly before reporting: “From six to ten in the morning, then three to seven in the afternoon—eight hours total. But some workers put in extra hours for more pay. They show up around five in the morning and don’t leave until eleven or twelve at night.”","“How is overtime compensated?”","“One and a half times their regular pay rate.”","Liu Yutong thought for a moment, then turned to Yun Cheng and said, \"Yun Cheng, arrange for more large freezers to be bought, and have the supermarket send over some heatstroke-prevention supplies every day — mung bean soup, ice water, chilled watermelon, Huoxiang Zhengqi water, and the like. There needs to be enough for the entire construction site. If it's not enough, go and get more. Every single person must have access to ice water.\"","Yun Cheng nodded and immediately took out his phone to make arrangements: \"Got it, Miss!\"","Liu Yutong then looked at the project manager. \"Gather the workers for me in a bit — I have something to announce.\"","The project manager nodded and bowed repeatedly. \"Yes, yes, of course. I'll go call everyone right away, right away!\"","While he ran off to round up the workers, Liu Yutong took out a black card from her bag and handed it to Yun Cheng. \"Go to the bank and withdraw a million in cash.\"","Yun Cheng took the card without asking a single question, turned around, and drove off.","As he left, Lan Die automatically moved closer to Liu Yutong, watching their surroundings with heightened alertness."]},{"number":806,"title":"Chapter 806: 807, Distributing Money, Offering Worship.","paragraphs":["Half an hour later, Yun Cheng returned with his people, pulling a truck full of mung bean soup, ice water, watermelons, and even over a dozen cases of ice pops.","The workers were gathered in the shade, looking a bit confused, not knowing why they had been summoned so suddenly.","\"Everyone, let me introduce you. This is Chairman Liu of our Wanlong Group. She's here to visit you all,\" the project manager announced through a megaphone.","The workers all turned to look at the young girl standing in the shade, and they were all stunned.","Such a young girl, and she was the chairman.","Liu Yutong was wearing a white blouse, her hair tied up in a high ponytail. Her skin was fair, her features delicate, and she seemed completely out of place among these rugged construction workers.","It was like she belonged to a different world.","She took the megaphone and called out to the crowd: \"Uncles and aunties, you've all worked so hard.\"","\"The weather is hot, so I've had people prepare mung bean soup, watermelon, and some cold drinks for you all. Take a break, have something to eat and drink—don't get heatstroke!\"","The workers looked at each other, hardly believing their ears.","They had worked on construction sites for years, switched between so many bosses, and this was the first time they had ever seen a boss personally come to deliver heatstroke-prevention items—let alone such a beautiful female boss.","\"What are you standing around for? Go get your share! Don't let Director Liu's kindness go to waste!\" the project manager shouted when he saw no one moving.","Only then did the workers react, lining up to collect their mung bean soup and watermelon.","\"Thank you, boss!\"","\"Thank you, boss!\"","\"...\"","Once everyone had just about finished their watermelon, Liu Yutong picked up the megaphone again.","\"Everyone, I came here today not only to give you all something, but also for another matter.\"","She took a heavy black briefcase from Yun Cheng and, in front of everyone, opened it with a click.","Inside were stacks of brand-new hundred-yuan bills, the red banknotes glowing brilliantly.","The workers' eyes lit up instantly.","\"High-temperature allowance: two thousand yuan per person.\"","\"This isn't from your salaries—it's a small token of my personal appreciation for your hard work in building the Wanlong headquarters.\"","The moment she finished speaking, the crowd erupted in enthusiastic applause.","\"Long live the boss!\"","\"Thank you, boss!\"","\"Director Liu is such a good person!\"","\"...\"","Liu Yutong didn't have the finance department distribute the money—she handed it out personally, one by one.","She walked up to each worker, handed over two thousand yuan with both hands, and said with a smile: \"Thank you for your hard work, and take care of yourself.\"","The workers took the money—some smiled warmly, some were too moved to speak, and others secretly wiped away tears.","\"Boss, what's... what's your name?\" an older worker asked nervously as he took the money.","\"Liu Yutong.\"","\"Boss Liu, um... are you still hiring? I'd like my son to work at your company—he... he's a college graduate.\"","\"A college graduate? Of course, that's fine.\"","\"But... but he has a bit of an issue.\"","The worker pointed to his own head and said: \"A lot of bosses said he had a problem and refused to hire him. He's gotten anxious and withdrawn now, but he really is a good kid, and there's nothing wrong with his mind. He was the first person in our village to get into a top university—he's really smart. Could you give him a job to make a living?\"","When he said this, his eyes were full of humility and pleading.","Liu Yutong said to Yun Cheng behind her: \"Make a note of his son's information.\"","Yun Cheng nodded: \"Yes!\"","The worker immediately thanked her profusely: \"Thank you, boss! Thank you, boss!\"","\"Don't worry, I'll work extra hard, I promise I'll build the building beautifully, and I'll never cut corners!\"","\"Good, thank you! But safety comes first.\"","\"...\"","Only after the workers had gradually dispersed did the project manager sidle up, flattering her with a fawning smile: \"Director Liu, we really needed you to show up—the workers' motivation went straight up after your visit.\"","Liu Yutong glanced at him: \"From today on, the site meals must include at least three hearty dishes, with plenty of meat and generous portions. If I see them eating the same as today again, you're out.\"","A cold sweat immediately broke out on the project manager's forehead: \"Yes, yes, yes—I'll fix it right away, I'll make sure everyone eats well!\"","\"Get lost!\" Yun Cheng snapped coldly.","The project manager scrambled away.","Afterward, Liu Yutong told Yun Cheng to send someone every day to hand out high-temperature subsidies—two hundred yuan a day—until the weather cooled down, and she would cover it all out of her own pocket.","After all, the construction company hired for the project paid the wages, so she couldn't just arbitrarily raise them—that would be unfair to the contracting company. That's why she chose to give the workers extra subsidies herself.","Once she had given all her instructions, Liu Yutong left the site. Yun Cheng drove her to the police station to see Gao Min.","About ten minutes later, she appeared in Gao Min's office.","\"Sis, busy?\"","Gao Min was organizing case files. Seeing Liu Yutong, a tired smile crossed her face: \"What are you doing here?\"","\"Just came to see you, and to ask about the case.\"","Liu Yutong walked in and sat down in a nearby chair, studying her sister.","Gao Min had lost weight, but her spirits were still good—that sharp look in her eyes hadn't dimmed.","\"The case against Jiang Yuan is basically settled now,\" Gao Min said, pouring a glass of water for Liu Yutong.","\"The Port City side cooperated well. Most of his assets have been frozen. Zhao Weixiang's evidence is solid—just on the charges of hiring a killer and smuggling alone, he's looking at a firing squad.\"","\"He confessed?\"","\"Not at first—he was stubborn. But once the evidence was laid out in front of him, he had no choice.\"","\"Still, he's never admitted to having anything to do with Liu Lei's death.\"","Liu Yutong said: \"It doesn't matter whether he admits it or not. As long as the chain of evidence is complete.\"","Gao Min nodded: \"The prosecution has already approved his arrest. The next step is indictment. This case spans too many areas, so it'll be a while before it goes to trial.\"","\"Yeah. Sis, you've lost weight—you need to eat more.\"","\"The case keeps me busy. Once I get through this stretch, it'll be fine.\"","\"Take care of yourself, don't wear yourself out.\"","\"I know, you too—don't overdo it.\"","Liu Yutong then suggested: \"Sis, how about going with me to see them?\"","Gao Min froze for a moment, then realized who \"them\" referred to.","\"Alright.\"","The two got into the car, first stopping at a flower shop to buy two bunches of white chrysanthemums and two bunches of yellow chrysanthemums.","Then they drove to the cemetery on the outskirts of Bright Pearl City.","The cemetery was situated on a gentle hillside, surrounded by evergreen pines and cypresses—a pleasant setting.","Liu Yutong and Gao Min walked up the steps one behind the other.","Soon, they arrived before a tombstone.","It wasn't large—made of ordinary bluestone—with an inscription carved across it: \"The tomb of our late father, Liu Lei.\"","In the corner, the names Liu Yutong and Gao Min were carved side by side.","This was a grave Liu Yutong had had restored, for the original one had been far too shabby, with barely even a proper marker.","Only after confirming his identity and the sacrifices he had made to protect his family did she allow a headstone to be erected for him with an inscription.","Unfortunately, due to certain circumstances, he could no longer be granted the title of martyr.","Liu Yutong crouched down, placed the bouquet of white chrysanthemums in front of the gravestone, and gently brushed the dust off its surface with her hand.","\"Dad, I've come to see you.\"","\"We're all doing well now. Sister has become the squadron leader, and my Wanlong Society is growing bigger and bigger. No one dares to bully us anymore. You can rest assured.\"","Gao Min then placed a bouquet of yellow chrysanthemums in front of the grave as well.","After a simple memorial for Liu Lei, they went to the Martyrs' Cemetery to pay their respects to Uncle Gao.","\"Dad, I have a sister now, a mother now, and a... stepfather. He's a good man and treats us well.\"","\"I'll live well and work hard. I won't let you down.\"","\"Please watch over us from above—keep us all safe.\"","After speaking, she stood up, straightened her police uniform, and bowed deeply.","Liu Yutong bowed as well.","The two bouquets of chrysanthemums—one white, one yellow—stood side by side in front of the grave, blooming perfectly under the sunlight.","After the memorial service, they found a small farmhouse restaurant at the foot of the mountain and ordered a few home-style dishes.","While they were eating, Gao Min suddenly remembered something and put down her chopsticks.","\"By the way, little sister, there's something I might need your help with.\"","\"What is it?\"","\"It's about part of Jiang Yuan's assets—about two billion yuan. He transferred it to his son Jiang Ximing's name a few months in advance. The money is overseas, so our police can't easily touch it. Do you have a way?\"","\"Jiang Ximing?\"","\"Yes, Jiang Yuan's eldest son. He used to manage the family business in Hong Kong and stayed abroad before the incident, so he never came back.\"","\"Jiang Yuan was pretty shrewd—he set up an escape route for his son in advance.\"","\"And we don't have evidence that Jiang Ximing was involved in his father's crimes, so we can't issue a warrant either.\"","\"Then I'll—\"","Liu Yutong was about to say she'd figure something out when her phone suddenly rang.","It was Lin Muyang.","\"Chairman, something's wrong! Zhou Ran is in trouble!\""]},{"number":807,"title":"Chapter 807: 808, Public Opinion Is Rising.","paragraphs":["Liu Yutong frowned slightly and asked, \"What's wrong with Zhou Ran?\"","On the other end of the phone, Lin Muyang's voice sounded somewhat anxious: \"Zhou Ran suddenly came to the production team today and said he wants to withdraw from the competition.\"","\"Withdraw? What's his reason?\"","\"He absolutely refused to say. He just kept insisting that he didn't want to participate anymore, and even asked us to cut out all of his previous footage. As for the penalty for breach of contract, he said he's willing to pay the full amount, even if it bankrupts him.\"","Liu Yutong already had a vague idea of what was going on. Chu Junlin moved fast—it hadn't been long, and he was already targeting the contestants.","\"Where is he now?\"","\"In his hotel room. He's locked himself in and won't come out. He won't answer the door when we knock, and the food we've sent up hasn't been touched.\"","\"Got it.\"","Liu Yutong hung up and called Yu Xin, giving her a few instructions. Gao Min, who was nearby, asked curiously, \"What happened?\"","Liu Yutong smiled. \"Nothing major. One of the contestants on 'China's Good Voice' had a bit of trouble. I've already asked Yu Xin to check on him—she happens to be over there.\"","Gao Min said, \"By the way, there's actually something serious I wanted to tell you. Once the current case I'm handling is closed, I'm planning to go to the capital for a while.\"","Liu Yutong: \"For further studies?\"","Gao Min nodded. \"Yeah.\"","Liu Yutong: \"That's great news! When you come back, I'll have to start calling you Director Gao, won't I? Oh, Director Gao, you'll have to look out for this ordinary citizen in the future.\"","Gao Min: \"Cut the flattery. It's just a regular training program, not a direct promotion. Don't go putting me on a pedestal.\"","\"Still, it means the organization is grooming you—they clearly see you as the rising star of the police force.\"","\"Alright, alright, you're getting more and more ridiculous. Stop mocking me.\"","\"Don't you have things to take care of? Go handle your business first.\"","\"Let's leave together—I'll drop you off first.\"","\"Okay.\"",".........","That evening.","Yu Xin finished handling her end of things and called Liu Yutong back with a detailed report. This girl was truly capable—other people might not have been able to get through to Zhou Ran, but she could.","\"Yutong, I talked to Zhou Ran. Just as you guessed, he's being threatened. Someone is using his girlfriend against him, trying to force him to withdraw from the competition—and maybe even cause some trouble for our show.\"","\"What do you think of his girlfriend?\" Liu Yutong asked suddenly.","Yu Xin thought for a moment and said, \"How should I put it? I think Lin Ya is the kind of person who is desperate to become famous. The only problem is she can't see where she really stands.\"","\"Do you think we need to find someone to talk some sense into her?\"","\"Some people can only grow after going through storms and hardship, after being battered and bruised until they're hardly recognizable.\"","Yu Xin didn't spell it out completely, but the message was clear enough.","Liu Yutong let out a soft \"mm\" and changed the subject.","\"What's Zhou Ran's state right now?\"","\"Anxious, restless—but he's still holding up.\"","\"Good. Tell him the production team will give him some leeway. We'll push back his scheduled recording time so he can relax for a bit and not feel pressured.\"","\"Yutong, so you mean we let the other side dance around for a while first?\"","\"The higher they jump, the harder they fall!\"","\"Understood.\"","After hanging up, Liu Yutong dialed Zhao Tianyi's number.","\"Tianyi, I've got a contract dispute that needs your expertise as a lawyer.\"","...........","The next few days were quiet.","The second episode of \"China's Good Voice\" aired on schedule. The show's sheer quality was enough to keep it at number one in its time slot, even without Zhou Ran appearing.","But online, a few scattered voices began to emerge.","People on forums and message boards started posting, asking why Zhou Ran had suddenly disappeared—had something happened to him?","Others, pretending to \"accidentally\" leak information, claimed that Zhou Ran had signed a management contract before joining the show, and that his participation in \"Good Voice\" constituted a breach of contract—and that the production team might be complicit.","These voices were small, but they were trickling out bit by bit, like ants moving their colony.","When Liu Yutong heard the reports from her team, she knew exactly what was happening. Chu Junlin was laying the groundwork. First, let a little noise escape. Then, once public opinion has brewed enough, strike with something heavy.","Sure enough.","Five days later, the big bombshell came!","A weibo influencer with hundreds of thousands of followers, claiming to be an industry insider, suddenly published a long post.","The headline was explosive—\"Exposing Zhou Ran, the Popular Contestant of 'China's Good Voice': Breach of Contract, Stunt Marketing, Zero Integrity—The Real Face of a 'Fan Favorite'.\"","The article was written with sharp, aggressive, and inflammatory language. It claimed that Zhou Ran had signed a contract with another production team and an exclusive management agreement with a company before joining \"Good Voice.\" But the moment he gained a little fame, he wanted to break his contracts and run, not even bothering to inform anyone before joining another show—completely disregarding contractual obligations and professional ethics.","At the end of the article, a so-called \"contract\" was attached, and indeed, it bore Zhou Ran's signature.","The moment the post went up, amplified by a swarm of paid trolls sharing it around, public opinion exploded.","[What the hell! This is hard evidence! The contract is right there—how can Zhou Ran possibly defend himself?]","[Damn, and here I was loving his voice. Turns out he's this kind of person. So disappointed. Unfollowing and turning black!]","[Participating in a competition in breach of contract—isn't that just deceiving the audience? The production team must have known, right?]","[I knew it! A bar singer couldn't possibly be that good. Turns out he had a company backing him the whole time. His whole image is a fraud!]","[To the comment above, what does being good at singing have to do with having a contract? What kind of twisted logic is that?]","[Whatever the case, signing a contract and then joining another show is a character problem!]","[Zhou Ran, come out and apologize! You owe your fans an explanation!]","The topic shot up to the top ten on weibo's trending list, climbing higher by the minute.","Lin Muyang's phone call came almost immediately.","\"Chairman, it's blowing up online. The comments are all trashing Zhou Ran.\"","\"I saw.\"","\"Do we need to issue a statement to clear things up? Or... maybe have weibo take down the trending topic? It's still within a manageable range right now.\"","\"No rush.\"","\"Someone else paid to put our show on trending. That's free traffic delivered right to our doorstep. Taking it down would just be wasting this free publicity.\"","\"Understood!\""]},{"number":808,"title":"Chapter 808: 809, Breaking Out of the Circle, Here's a Big Gift for You.","paragraphs":["That afternoon, the second wave of explosive material hit.","This time it wasn't text, but two photos.","In the first photo, Zhou Ran was having a meal with a young woman at a small restaurant, the scene looking warm and intimate, like an ordinary couple's everyday life.","The second photo showed that same young woman, face flushed red, drinking with several middle-aged men whose faces were pixelated.","The caption read: 【In order to gain fame and climb the ranks, Zhou Ran didn't hesitate to pimp out his girlfriend to drink with men in exchange for resources.】","As soon as these two photos dropped, public opinion spiraled completely out of control, escalating once again.","【I can't take this anymore. Is this guy even human? Selling out his own girlfriend for fame? Animal!】","【Look at that woman's red face in the photo, and those old men next to her — clearly up to no good. Do I even need to spell out what's happening?】","【Trash like Zhou Ran doesn't deserve to stand on any stage. Get the hell out of the entertainment industry!】","【If the show's production team dares to let him keep competing, I will never watch this show again! Lifetime blacklist!】","【The comment above is right. If the production team shields this scumbag, I'll call on my whole family to boycott the show!】","【Just seeing Zhou Ran's face makes me want to puke. Disgusting! People like him existing is just polluting the air!】","【..........】","Besides comments purely attacking Zhou Ran's character, some started dragging in the production team and even the company behind them.","【Wait, has anyone thought about this — how did Zhou Ran get out of \"Show Me\" and then directly land a spot on The Voice?】","【Right? \"Show Me\" might not be as popular as The Voice, but they still had a contract. Zhou Ran broke his contract and ran, and The Voice still dared to take him in. The water behind this has to be deep.】","【Now that you mention it, I'm starting to get chills. Could it be that Zhou Ran used his girlfriend... ugh...】","【Holy crap! That's the real truth! I did some digging — when Zhou Ran competed in the \"Show Me\" semifinals, The Voice auditions were already over. How did he get into the show? That doesn't match the process at all!】","【Damn, the entertainment industry's water is way too deep! This is way too corrupt!】","【Too disgusting! This isn't a talent show — it's a pimping platform!】","【I've also heard from some netizens from XX province that the parent company of this show is extremely shady locally, practically untouchable!】","【Wow, no wonder the production team dares to play this dirty — turns out they've got underworld forces backing them!】","【Boycott! We must boycott!】","【+1, definitely boycott! We demand an investigation into the production team! Investigate Wanlonghui Group!】","【...........】","Public opinion had completely spiraled out of control.","The tide shifted from attacking Zhou Ran's personal morals to a full-scale siege on the entire \"China's Voice\" production team and Wanlonghui Group.","Conspiracy theory hashtags like 【Zhou Ran bought off the production team】, 【The Voice took bribes】, 【Wanlonghui's underworld background】 were surging up the trending lists of major web portals at alarming speed.","Topic views broke 30 million within just a few hours, with discussions surpassing one million.","The official Weibo account of The Voice was completely overrun — under its latest post, nearly 100,000 comments poured in within a single hour, all of them abuse.","【Trash show, get out of the entertainment industry!】","【Wanlonghui Group? Come out and show yourselves! Stop playing dead!】","【Underworld forces running a talent show — trying to whitewash your image?】","【Tsk tsk tsk, your industry is messy, your industry is corrupt!】","【.........】","The storm of public opinion swirling around The Voice's production team and Wanlonghui Group continued to ferment for a full three days before finally reaching its peak.","On Weibo, the three hashtags #ZhouRanCollapse, #TheVoiceScandal, and #WanlonghuiMayBeUnderworld accumulated a staggering one billion views, with discussions exceeding three million posts.","The entertainment sections of all major web portals featured this controversy as their lead headlines, one after another.","TV entertainment news programs also refused to be left behind, producing special segments and inviting so-called \"industry insiders\" and \"senior media personalities\" to analyze and comment.","Even some financial media outlets that rarely paid attention to the entertainment industry began investigating the rise of Wanlonghui Group — a private company that had shot to prominence in just two years.","In short, the versions of the story circulating online grew more absurd with each passing day as the Zhou Ran incident escalated, reaching a point of near total chaos.","Some said Zhou Ran was a pretty boy kept by Wanlonghui's top brass. Some said The Voice's blind auditions were completely fake and the mentors already knew who the contestants were. Others claimed Wanlonghui Group was a mafia-like organization that made its fortune through violence and loan sharking...","All sorts of stories, true and false, mixed together in an increasingly tangled mess.","That said, there's no denying that \"China's Voice\" was gaining popularity at a ferocious rate, becoming a show known by virtually everyone in the country.","Even if the bulk of the attention was negative.","The official Weibo following of \"China's Voice\" exploded from 1.2 million at the start of the show's run to 8.6 million in just three days.","Weibo's registered user numbers also surged by nearly ten million over that period.","Of course, most of those new users signed up just to get in on the gossip or hurl insults.","Even the show's four mentors were caught in the crossfire, and they all approached the production team asking for the controversy to be resolved as quickly as possible, saying they were under tremendous pressure.","Countless netizens were completely immersed in this carnival of outrage, never once stopping to consider that — aside from forums and other portal platforms — the country's largest new media platform, Weibo, was actually itself a subsidiary of Wanlonghui Group.","If Wanlonghui had truly wanted to manage the public relations fallout, the Weibo official platform could have easily suppressed the hype. At least damping the heat on Weibo itself would have been no problem.","But Wanlonghui did absolutely nothing, letting the storm rage on.","No one stopped to ask why.","Well — almost no one. Except for certain people in the capital.","Some senior executives at Xingyao Media had already begun feeling a vague sense of dread.","Because things were starting to slip out of control...","...","Danan City, Yunsan Capital, Chairman's Office.","Liu Yutong leaned back in her chair, holding a cup of a new milk tea from the Qingyin brand.","On the computer screen before her, nearly every major portal's trending list featured topics related to The Voice and Wanlonghui.","Even though she could clearly see the whole internet cursing at her company and the show, she wasn't the slightest bit angry. Instead, she took a satisfied, generous sip of her milk tea.","\"Our new milk tea formula turned out pretty well. It tastes good.\"","\"Yun Cheng, aren't you drinking yours?\"","Standing off to the side, Yun Cheng paused for a moment, then picked up a cup from the table, stuck in the straw, and took a sip.","\"It is pretty good. Not as sweet, and the tea flavor is stronger.\"","\"Right — too sweet is no good either. It gets cloying.\"","The two of them traded remarks in perfect rhythm, paying not the slightest attention to the trending topics that would have crushed a normal person under their weight.","Lan Die sat on the sofa nearby, a laptop resting on her knees, monitoring public opinion in real time.","It was clear she'd been reading too many vicious comments and was getting angry.","\"Miss, do you want me to go deal with some of those big influencers who are stirring the pot?\"","\"The people on Chief Zhang's side have already replied. They've locked down thirty-seven accounts, and every single one of them is more or less connected to Star Media.\"","Liu Yutong set down her milk tea and shook her head. \"No rush. Let's wait a bit longer. Let the bullet fly a little more.\"","Lan Die was getting anxious. \"Are we really not going to fight back? I think the comments online are already starting to affect the group's day-to-day operations. Everyone's saying we're corrupt...\"","Liu Yutong: \"What's the reaction from Ma Da and the others?\"","Lan Die thought for a moment, then said, \"Ma Da and the crew said... they're all used to it?\"","Actually, Ma Da's exact words were: \"Oh, Sister Lan Die, it's not like our Wanlong Association has never been dragged through the mud before. As the mud keeps coming, you just get used to it. Honestly, I think a little bad press is fine...\"","And then they just went about their business as if nothing happened, almost even taking a weird pride in being vilified?","\"Anything else?\"","\"Yes.\"","Lan Die continued her report: \"Longkan Vision is under a lot of pressure. People have started spamming the comment section with boycott calls, and there are even joint petitions demanding that all videos of 'The Voice of Dragon Nation' be taken down. The higher-ups haven't made any moves yet, but if the public outcry keeps building like this, they might step in.\"","Hearing her analysis, Liu Yutong suddenly realized that she really couldn't let things spiral too far out of control.","Otherwise, if she was about to strike back and the higher-ups suddenly shut it all down, forbidding either side from attacking the other, she'd be stuck suffocating with nowhere to vent.","\"Then let's begin.\"","Liu Yutong picked up her phone from the table, brought up the number she'd asked around for, and dialed.","The phone rang five times before it was picked up.","On the other end came Chu Junlin's voice, laced with a barely concealed smugness.","\"Miss Liu, why are you in such a hurry to call me? Our bet isn't over yet.\"","\"Young Master Chu, have you seen the recent news about 'The Voice of Dragon Nation' online?\"","\"I have, of course I have. Quite lively, isn't it? Miss Liu, I was just about to congratulate you. Your show is exploding, it's even broken into the mainstream!\"","\"And how long do you think this news will last?\"","\"Well, with the current level of buzz, it's safe to say it'll keep spreading for another week or two, no problem.\"","\"Of course, if you're willing to come out and clarify things personally, it might die down sooner. But the innocent have nothing to fear, right? If you don't care about your reputation, then it doesn't really matter.\"","As he said this, the triumph in Chu Junlin's voice was almost naked.","In his view, Liu Yutong making this call meant she couldn't take it anymore, that she was here to sue for peace.","After all, no one can feel good after being mobbed by the entire internet for seven or eight days straight.","And she was just a woman, a woman barely twenty years old. Her psychological endurance couldn't possibly be that strong.","He'd been waiting for this moment for almost two whole months.","Ever since he was forced to sign that ten-billion-dollar bet, he'd been waiting for Liu Yutong to lower her head.","And now, she'd finally called.","\"Chu Junlin, I think you've got one thing wrong.\"","\"What?\"","\"I didn't call you to talk about 'The Voice of Dragon Nation' or my company's situation. I called you to say: you've been doing such a hard job promoting us all this time that as a thank-you, I've prepared a special gift for you. Make sure you receive it properly.\"","\"Beep, beep, beep...\"","\"Hello? Hello?\"","Chu Junlin listened to the dial tone from his phone, frozen for a few seconds.","A gift?","What gift?","Before he could even figure it out—","Suddenly!","The door to his office was shoved open from the outside.","His assistant rushed in, flustered and panicked.","\"Chu... Chief Chu! Something terrible has happened! A big disaster!\"","\"What is it?\"","\"The Hong Kong stock market... something's going on over there! Our company's stock price has collapsed!\"","\"What did you say?!\""]},{"number":809,"title":"Chapter 809: 810, Short Selling Battle.","paragraphs":["At the top floor of a financial tower in Danan City.","Cloud Mountain Capital, trading room.","This trading room was Cloud Mountain Capital's primary command center, featuring a massive electronic screen wall that displayed real-time indices and stock quotes from the Hong Kong, A-share, and U.S. markets in a continuous scroll.","Below the screen was a row of operational desks, lined with dozens of computers, each occupied by a trader.","Some of these traders came from Cloud Mountain Capital, others from Wanlong Capital. They had mostly been recruited over the past year, and every single one was a top-tier operator.","When Liu Yutong walked into the trading room, everyone was already in position.","Chen Mo, the vice president of Cloud Mountain Capital, stepped forward with a thick stack of documents.","\"Chairman, all the primary market funds allocated by Cloud Mountain Capital have been fully deployed—approximately 10.8 billion.\"","Yun Cheng, right behind him, immediately reported as well: \"All of Wanlong Overseas Capital's funds are also in place, around 23 billion.\"","For this precision short-selling campaign against Hong Kong stocks, Liu Yutong had directly mobilized total ammunition equivalent to 33.8 billion.","33.8 billion.","That number stunned many in the room, especially the new members of the Cloud Mountain Society who had come to observe. They knew Liu Yutong commanded immense financial resources, but they hadn't realized just how immense.","More than thirty billion in cash flow, mobilized at a moment's notice—what did that even mean?","Across the entire country, the number of companies that could pull together that much available cash at once could be counted on one hand.","What they didn't know was that for Liu Yutong, this was barely a warm-up. If she really wanted to go all out, conjuring up a hundred billion in cash wasn't out of the question either.","After hearing their reports, Liu Yutong walked straight to the huge electronic screen and stood there with her hands behind her back.","Chen Mo followed closely, pointing at the K-line charts of three stocks on the screen as he continued his briefing.","\"Chairman, according to your strategic deployment, we've locked in three short targets. First: Xingyao Media, HK stock code 016XX, current price 7.8 HKD, total market cap around 12 billion HKD. Second: Qiyuan Real Estate, HK stock code 023XX, current price 4.2 HKD, total market cap around 15 billion HKD. Third: Caiguang Paper, HK stock code 036XX, current price 3.5 HKD, total market cap around 6.5 billion HKD.\"","Chen Mo paused, then summarized: \"Together, the three companies have a total market cap of roughly 33.5 billion HKD. Chairman, with the capital we have on hand, shorting these three companies is more than manageable.\"","Liu Yutong nodded. \"Is everyone ready?\"","\"Ready.\"","\"Then let's begin.\"","Chen Mo spun around and barked the order to the room full of traders: \"All hands, execute!\"","Instantly, the trading room erupted with the clatter of keyboards.","On the big screen, the previously calm Hong Kong market began to churn violently...","...","Imperial Capital, Xingyao Media headquarters.","Chu Junlin's eyes were bloodshot, wild with rage.","\"What did you say? Someone's heavily shorting my company?!\"","\"Y-yes, CEO Chu.\"","\"Starting about ten minutes ago, a massive wave of sell orders suddenly hit the market, targeting exactly one thing—Xingyao Media's stock. The sell pressure is highly concentrated, doesn't care about cost, and it's clearly a premeditated ambush.\"","\"How big?\"","\"A-a-round eight million shares have already been executed, and it's still growing.\"","Chu Junlin's face turned ashen.","Eight million shares—at the current price, that meant more than sixty million HKD in sell orders had smashed straight into the market.","And this was clearly just a probing strike.","\"Have you found out who it is? Which institution?\"","\"N-not yet. But based on the trading channels and account locations, the funds are widely dispersed—some through local Hong Kong brokers, some through offshore accounts, and some through the Shanghai-Hong Kong Stock Connect. It looks like a bear raid that was set up a long time in advance.\"","Suddenly, Chu Junlin remembered the phone call from earlier.","Liu Yutong had said something cryptic about sending him a gift.","It was her!","It had to be her!","No one else besides that crazy woman had the nerve for a move this big!","\"Find out! I want to know their hand!\" Chu Junlin nearly roared the words.","\"Yes, sir!\"","The assistant scrambled out of the room in a panic.","Chu Junlin dropped back into his office chair, the veins in his forehead bulging and pulsing.","He really hadn't expected Liu Yutong to pull something like this.","All he'd done was pay to splash some mud on her name—and this woman, instead of playing by the rules, had decided to steal his whole base out from under him.","Shouldn't she be scrambling to manage the PR crisis right now?","How did she still have the energy to attack his stock?","No, wait.","Chu Junlin suddenly realized something.","The rumor mill had been churning for days, but Liu Yutong had never responded. No clarification, no statement, no police report, nothing.","As if she didn't care about the backlash at all.","Now it all made sense.","She hadn't been ignoring it—she'd been enduring.","She'd been waiting too.","Waiting for the media frenzy to pull everyone's attention away, for him to let his guard down, for the stock to sit at its peak—and then she struck.","And once she struck, it was lethal.","Chu Junlin sprang to his feet, grabbed the phone, and dialed Xingyao Media's CEO.","\"Old Zhang, someone's shorting the company. Activate the defense fund immediately. Whatever it costs, push the stock back up!\"","\"CEO Chu, we already activated it, but... but the sell orders are too massive, like a bottomless pit. Every time we push it up a little, a flood of sell orders slams it right back down. We can't hold the line!\"","\"Hold it anyway! That's an order!!!\"","Chu Junlin slammed the phone down, heart still racing. He quickly dialed the heads of Qiyuan Real Estate and Caiguang Paper as well.","The answers were all the same: all three companies were being massively shorted at once.","Three companies, hit simultaneously.","This was no coincidence. This was a carefully orchestrated hunt.","And the hunter was that detestable woman—Liu Yutong!"]},{"number":810,"title":"Chapter 810: 811, Cornered.","paragraphs":["Da Nancheng, Yunsan Capital trading room.","On the massive screen, the K-line chart of Xingyao Media's stock price cascaded downward like a waterfall.","7.8, 7.7, 7.6, 7.5...","The numbers flickered faster and faster, each green tick representing millions or even tens of millions in capital evaporating in an instant.","\"Chairman, reporting in—Xingyao Media has started defending their stock. Buy orders are visibly increasing; significant capital is entering the market,\" a senior trader reported.","Liu Yutong stood before the large screen, staring at the real-time trading data with a mocking smile.","\"Let them defend.\"","\"Break up our sell orders into smaller sizes, distribute them across different accounts, and sell in batches. Don't dump it all at once. I want to boil the frog slowly.\"","\"Understood.\"","The traders immediately began executing her orders.","On the big screen, Xingyao Media's stock price bounced briefly, but instead of the V-shaped recovery Chu Junlin might have hoped for, it seemed caught in an invisible net, slowly starting to decline again.","7.5, 7.4, 7.3...","Each rebound was like a drowning man's struggle—a few flailing kicks before being pushed back under the water.","This was exactly the effect Liu Yutong wanted.","She didn't want Chu Junlin to die all at once; that would be over too quickly.","She wanted him to watch his wealth evaporate bit by bit, to watch his hopes crumble piece by piece.","She wanted him to fully experience the torment of being flayed alive, one slice at a time.","\"Chairman, Qiyuan Real Estate has also started defending their stock. The push is even stronger than Xingyao Media's. Looks like Chu Junlin is trying to protect his real estate arm,\" Chen Mo walked over and reported.","Liu Yutong gestured for the operator to switch the big screen to Qiyuan Real Estate's trading page.","This real estate company's stock had already fallen from HK$4.20 to HK$3.90, a drop of over seven percent.","When defensive capital entered the market, the price quickly rebounded to 4.00, but before long, sell orders came flooding in again, pushing the price back down.","\"Keep selling!\"","\"The real estate sector is already in an adjustment cycle. We're just going with the flow. Even without us, Qiyuan Real Estate's inflated stock price couldn't hold up much longer.\"","That was Liu Yutong's brilliance.","She hadn't launched a blind short-sell. She had been waiting for the perfect moment all along.","In the summer of 2009, despite the domestic real estate market still rising, it was also in a period of regulatory tightening. Real estate stocks were under heavy pressure, and investor confidence was fragile.","Caiguang Paper, operating in the papermaking industry, was facing enormous environmental compliance pressures and surging raw material costs. Its cash flow was already badly strained.","She was simply biding her time, waiting for the right window, and then she gave them a push.","As for Xingyao Media—the entertainment sector's valuations were already inflated and the bubble was severe. And she still held an unexploded bombshell in her hand that she hadn't yet detonated.","Once she released that, it wouldn't be a mere halving—it would be an outright decapitation.","\"What about Caiguang Paper?\"","\"It's taken the biggest hit—down twelve percent, currently at 3.08. The defense is very weak. Looks like they're ready to give up.\"","Liu Yutong nodded. \"The papermaking industry generally has tight cash flow. Caiguang Paper has been borrowing recklessly to expand over the years, with a high debt ratio. Chu Junlin's capital will most likely prioritize protecting Xingyao Media with its healthier cash flow and Qiyuan Real Estate with its heavier assets. A sunset industry like Caiguang Paper is probably the first pawn he'll sacrifice.\"","Sure enough, no sooner had she spoken.","On the big screen, Caiguang Paper's stock price began to accelerate downward—and then completely collapsed.","3.5, 3.3, 3.1, 2.9...","The numbers suddenly plunged without mercy, crushing through the buy-level support orders as if they were paper.","\"Chairman, should we close the net now?\" Chen Mo asked, watching the terrifying drop.","\"Not yet.\" Liu Yutong shook her head.","She took the milk tea handed to her by Yun Cheng and took a sip, looking as relaxed as if she were watching a movie.","And in truth, this financial hunt was more thrilling than any film.","...","While the battle in the trading room was reaching its peak, the tide of public opinion outside had begun to turn.","The crew of \"China's Greatest Voice\" was suddenly hit by a shocking scandal. During a recording session, a contestant's emotions spun out of control and he went off script, publicly exposing the show's behind-the-scenes manipulation.","During his outburst, he hurled his microphone to the ground and hurled insults at the director and others—and a video of the scene 'accidentally' captured by a staff member on set spread across the internet.","It immediately grabbed the attention of netizens looking for juicy gossip.","Before long.","On Weibo, an account verified as \"Lin Ya\" appeared and posted a post with clear video evidence attached.","\"I am Zhou Ran's ex-girlfriend and a signed artist under Xingyao Media. I was coerced by capital...\"","That post exploded like a nuclear bomb, igniting the already-boiling public opinion.","In the video, Lin Ya appeared without makeup, tears streaming down her face, pouring out how she had been deceived by Xingyao Media, and trapped by a contract riddled with exploitative clauses.","The company, she said, had forced her to attack her ex-boyfriend Zhou Ran and smear \"China's Voice,\" and also forced her to attend all kinds of drinking parties and business dinners, entertaining various so-called \"investors\" and \"producers.\"","She didn't want to go, so they threatened to shelve her, to sue her for breach of contract, and even to extract tens of millions in punitive compensation.","\"Those photos—they were taken secretly at those dinners. People plied me with alcohol, even groped me... I never sold myself, I was forced into it. If Zhou Ran hadn't sent someone to get me out, I might have actually been ruined by them...\"","\"After that, I was truly terrified. I went into hiding, living like a rat. I thought if I kept my mouth shut, everything would pass. But when I saw Zhou Ran being attacked by the whole internet, when I saw him choose to take all that hatred on himself alone just to protect me, I knew I'd been wrong. Completely wrong.\"","\"I realized I couldn't stay silent anymore. I had to tell the truth—even if I get blacklisted, even if they retaliate, I don't care anymore.\"","\"I have evidence of the coercion by Xingyao's vice president, a man named Ma Qingliu. Besides forcing artists to accompany clients at drinking parties, I also overheard them in conversation, quite openly, discussing insider matters—financial fraud, tax evasion. I was genuinely shocked. A publicly listed company worth billions, and they were so blatantly breaking the law. I kept every piece of this evidence...\"","\"And Xingyao Media is no place for human beings...\"","At the end of the video, Lin Ya revealed solid corroborating evidence.","First, a scanned copy of the contract she signed with Xingyao Media, with the abusive clauses circled in red by legal professionals, shocking to behold.","Second, an audio recording capturing conversations at a dinner party, where senior executives of Xingyao Media talked openly about how they cooked the books and laundered money using dual contracts.","Within half an hour of the post going live, it had been shared over 100,000 times.","The comment section exploded. All the previous condemnation had dramatically reversed course.","Holy crap, holy crap, holy crap! Plot twist! A massive plot twist! I knew I wasn't wrong about him!","I knew it! I knew Zhou Ran was framed! All you people who called him a scumbag and a loser before? Come out and apologize!","Star Shine Media? Isn't that the company listed in Hong Kong? This is beyond shady! Coercing artists, forging contracts, buying paid online mobs to manipulate public opinion, and now financial fraud and tax evasion on top of it all... How the hell is this company still in business? It should be shut down!","For Lin Ya to come forward and tell the truth at a time like this, to go head-to-head with such a huge corporate powerhouse—it takes incredible courage.","So from the very beginning, Zhou Ran and The Voice were framed? It was Star Shine Media pulling the strings behind the scenes? To crush their competition?","This is terrifying to think about, folks. Why did Star Shine Media go after Zhou Ran? Because The Voice was their biggest rival in the talent show arena! This is corporate warfare! They used two young singers as cannon fodder! Absolutely shameless!","Boycott Star Shine Media! Boycott China's Greatest Music!","...........","At almost the exact same moment the public opinion flipped, Zhao Tianyi had already arrived in the capital with his legal team and over a hundred core members of the Wànlóng Society.","Their target: straight for the headquarters of Star Shine Media."]},{"number":811,"title":"Chapter 811: 812, Halftime Break.","paragraphs":["Chu Junlin had no idea yet about the online storm of public opinion or the crisis that was about to hit him.","By now, he had already ripped off his tie, his eyes fixed intently on the ever-plunging intraday line on the computer screen.","\"President Chu, we've already used 1.3 billion yuan of support funds, but the stock price just won't stop falling! The selling pressure is too heavy!\"","\"What about Qiyuan Real Estate?\"","\"We've also used nearly 1.8 billion there, barely holding it steady around 3.8. But over at Caiguang Paper...\"","\"What's wrong with Caiguang Paper?\"","\"It's already dropped to 2.7, down more than twenty percent. We... we've given up on supporting that one.\"","Chu Junlin slammed his fist hard against the mahogany desk.","Abandoning Caiguang Paper meant that its market value of 6.5 billion had evaporated by over a billion in just one hour.","And this was only the beginning.","If the stock price kept falling, the pledged shares would hit the forced liquidation line. Then the bank would forcibly sell off the shares, triggering a chain reaction—that would be the true disaster.","\"Find out for me. Find out exactly how much capital she's mobilized! Spare no expense—just find out!\"","His assistant reported nervously, \"Initial estimates suggest... about twenty billion yuan.\"","Twenty billion.","Hearing that number, Chu Junlin felt his head spin, his blood pressure shooting straight to the top of his skull.","That woman had lost her mind!","Just to vent her anger, she was throwing twenty billion at him!","He knew that the combined market value of his three listed companies was only about thirty billion to begin with—now it was down to just over twenty.","That still didn't matter. Didn't Liu Yutong know that he still had the hundred billion in funds raised by the Junlin Society?","The Junlin Society was a new organization he had set up, modeled after the Yunshan Society. Together, they had raised a hundred billion in capital and chips.","Wasn't she afraid he'd deploy that hundred billion to defend the stock prices and fight her to the bitter end?","Or had she been prepared from the very start, planning to settle everything in one decisive round and win that ten-billion-yuan bet outright?","In fact, his guess was spot on.","Liu Yutong was indeed planning to settle it all in one single round.","Just then, the assistant's phone suddenly rang. After hearing the report, his face turned ashen.","\"President Chu... do we keep defending?\"","Chu Junlin closed his eyes, paused for ten seconds, then suddenly opened them.","\"Defend!\"","\"Move every resource we can get our hands on! Bring over the reserve funds from the Junlin Society as well! We have to protect Xingyao Media and Qiyuan Real Estate! As for Caiguang Paper... let it go.\"","It was a move of cutting off a limb to save the body.","But he had no choice.","He had guessed what Liu Yutong was really trying to do, but he could not admit defeat!","And he would never bark like a dog!","...........","Great South City, Yunshan Capital Trading Room.","\"Chairman, the support for Qiyuan Real Estate has suddenly increased—likely from a new influx of large capital.\"","\"Caiguang Paper appears to have given up resistance.\"","Liu Yutong watched the numbers jumping on the screen, a slight smile curling at the corner of her mouth.","Chu Junlin's response was exactly what she had expected.","Abandoning Caiguang Paper and concentrating all firepower on protecting Xingyao Media and Qiyuan Real Estate—that was the most rational choice.","But no matter what, against absolute strength, all of it was futile.","Also, did that fool really think she wouldn't notice that he had moved outside funds?","If he failed to protect the stock prices and lost all that money, she'd love to see how he explained it to those heirs of wealthy families.","\"For Xingyao Media, increase the sell orders.\"","\"For Qiyuan Real Estate, increase them as well.\"","\"Fight on two fronts. Let's see how much money he has to burn.\"","Inside the trading room, the sound of keyboard clattering suddenly grew intense.","On the large screen, stock prices began another round of plunging.","Xingyao Media fell from 7.0 to 6.8, 6.5, 6.2...","Qiyuan Real Estate fell from 3.8 to 3.6, 3.4, 3.2...","The numbers slipped like sand through an hourglass—every single second meant tens of millions in wealth evaporating.","Yet the woman standing before the big screen never changed her expression.","Chen Mo watched her, a wave of indescribable, complicated emotions rising in his chest.","This was his boss.","A terrifying woman who had used tens of billions in capital to sweep over a hundred billion in profits from overseas markets.","A young mistress of a powerful family, ruthless and decisive, with countless men in black at her command.","How could such a woman ever be affected by a bit of online noise?","Those who insulted her, those who slandered her—they had no idea what kind of force they were up against.","\"Chairman, Xingyao Media's support funds appear to be exhausted. The stock price is accelerating downward,\" one trader shouted excitedly.","Liu Yutong glanced at the screen.","Xingyao Media's stock price had already fallen below 6 HKD, a drop of more than twenty-three percent.","According to Hong Kong stock exchange rules, a drop exceeding twenty percent triggers a mid-session trading halt mechanism.","Sure enough.","Three seconds later, a red message appeared on Xingyao Media's trading page—【Trading Halted, Pending Disclosure of Inside Information】.","Immediately after, Qiyuan Real Estate also triggered a trading halt.","Three companies—two halted, one abandoned.","From start to finish, this financial attack had taken less than two hours.","The trading room fell silent for a moment, then erupted into enthusiastic applause and cheers.","\"Brilliant!\"","\"The chairman is incredible!\"","\"Over a billion in profit—in less than two hours!\"","\"...\"","Chen Mo took off his glasses, wiped them, and put them back on, swelling with pride.","He had worked in the industry for years and had witnessed countless battles between bulls and bears, but this was the first time he had seen such a clean, overwhelming, one-sided crushing.","Liu Yutong, however, was not getting carried away by this small victory.","She glanced at the stock codes of the two halted companies on the screen and said calmly, \"It's not over yet.\"","Chen Mo was stunned. \"Chairman, you mean...\"","\"The trading halt is just halftime. Chu Junlin won't sit still—he'll definitely apply for resumption of trading and find new capital to rescue the stocks. That's when the real harvest begins.\"","\"First, close out all our short positions. Lock in the profits first. After trading resumes, the stock price will have a rebound, and then we'll open new positions.\"","\"Understood!\" Chen Mo turned and went to arrange everything immediately.","Yun Cheng couldn't help but ask from the side, \"Miss, do you think Chu Junlin can still find more money?\"","Liu Yutong said, \"He's a member of the Chu family after all, and the family has real foundations. If he's willing to swallow his pride and beg, scraping together eight or ten billion isn't impossible. However...\"","She paused before continuing, \"Even if he finds the money, it won't help. Caiguang Paper is already finished, and he can't fill the hole at Qiyuan Real Estate either. As for Xingyao Media... there's some big drama coming its way soon.\"","Just as she finished speaking, her phone buzzed.","It was an unknown number.","\"Miss Liu, I've already posted the video online. Does your promise about the role and helping me terminate my contract still hold?\"","\"Of course. I never go back on my word.\""]},{"number":812,"title":"Chapter 812: 813, Completely Losing It","paragraphs":["At the headquarters of Xingyao Media.","Chu Junlin's office was already in chaos, with broken things scattered everywhere.","He paced anxiously like a trapped beast backed into a corner.","His assistant stood trembling in the corner, afraid that any wrong move might make him the target of Chu Junlin's rage.","\"Where's the money? When will their money arrive!\"","\"President Chu... I've already contacted the members of the Junlin Society. They were hesitant at first, but I explained the stakes to them, and they've agreed to transfer the funds they've raised again—about eight billion. Combined with the two billion we still have on hand, that makes ten billion in total. That should be enough to support our market defense.\"","\"Ten billion.\"","\"That's enough. As long as we can pull the stock price back up, as long as we can beat that crazy woman Liu Yutong, this ten billion will be money well spent!\"","Chu Junlin never stopped to consider that the rich heirs of the Junlin Society were only willing to help pool the money because of the Chu family's reputation. If this market defense failed, he alone would have to bear this enormous hole, or the entire Chu family's prestige in the imperial capital's inner circle would be ruined.","Nor did he consider that Liu Yutong had long anticipated his all-or-nothing gamble, waiting for him to dump in his last chips before crushing him completely.","Within less than an hour, the eight billion from the Junlin Society arrived in full.","Chu Junlin immediately called in the company's CEO.","\"Old Zhang, get ready right now. After trading resumes, spare no expense to pull the stock prices of Xingyao and Qiyuan Real Estate back up. Even if we burn through all ten billion, I want Liu Yutong to know that I, Chu Junlin, am not someone to be messed with.\"","Old Zhang looked troubled: \"President Chu, this is too risky. The other side's financial strength far exceeds what we imagined. Even if we spend money to defend the market, the investors may not buy into it.\"","Hearing this, Chu Junlin flew into a rage, pointing at him and cursing: \"I told you to do it, so do it! What's with all the nonsense! If we lose, we're all finished! If you don't have the guts to do it, then get the hell out right now and I'll find someone else!\"","Old Zhang didn't dare say another word and could only grit his teeth and agree: \"Yes, President Chu. I'll get on it right away.\"","Meanwhile, in the trading room of Yunshan Capital in Danan City.","Chen Mo had already received word that Xingyao Media and Qiyuan Real Estate had applied to resume trading, and immediately reported it to Liu Yutong.","\"Chairman, Chu Junlin really is going all in. They've applied to resume trading. I think the final funds are in place, and they're ready to fight us to the death.\"","\"Does he really think he's worthy of fighting us to the death?\" Liu Yutong said with a sneer.","\"Pass the word down. As soon as Xingyao Media and Qiyuan Real Estate resume trading, immediately increase the selling pressure. No testing the waters. Throw in five billion first and pin the price firmly at the daily limit down! In addition, have the remaining funds ready to coordinate. I want Chu Junlin's ten billion to evaporate completely within half an hour!\"","\"Yes!\"","At 2:30 in the afternoon, when the Hong Kong stock market reopened, the stocks of Xingyao Media and Qiyuan Real Estate resumed trading right on time.","Chu Junlin sat in front of his computer, staring at the screen: \"Rise! Rise!\"","In the early stage of the resumption, driven by Chu Junlin's ten billion in defense funds, Xingyao Media's stock price rebounded from 6 HKD to 6.3 HKD, and Qiyuan Real Estate also bounced from 3.2 HKD to 3.5 HKD, at one point gaining more than nine percent.","Seeing this, Chu Junlin finally cracked a smile, and the weight on his heart lightened a little.","\"Hahaha, Liu Yutong, you're not all that special!\"","\"I said it, as long as I pour in money, I can pull the stock price back up. Once I win, just you wait and see how I deal with you, how I make you bark like a dog!\"","But his smile didn't last long before the stock price on the screen began to plummet.","A flood of sell orders suddenly surged in, instantly drowning out Chu Junlin's buy orders defending the price. Xingyao Media's stock price fell from 6.3 HKD straight through 6 HKD, then broke through 5.8, 5.5, 5.2...","Qiyuan Real Estate's stock price also dropped in tandem, falling from 3.5 HKD to 3.2, 3.0, 2.8...","\"What's going on?\"","Chu Junlin's smile froze on his face, his eyes filled with disbelief: \"What about the defense funds? Where are our defense funds? Why aren't they working? Old Zhang! Old Zhang!\"","Old Zhang rushed in in a panic: \"President Chu, their sell orders are too massive—several times larger than we estimated! We've already used over three billion of our defense funds, but their sell orders are like a bottomless pit that we can't fill! And... on top of that, there are massive sell orders in overseas markets shorting our stocks as well. They're squeezing us from every direction, and we can't hold the line!\"","Chu Junlin roared with bloodshot eyes: \"How is that possible! How much capital has Liu Yutong actually mobilized? Tell me!\"","\"I don't know.\"","Old Zhang said, nearly in tears: \"But based on our estimates, the other side has mobilized at least thirty billion, and it's still growing. Our ten billion is nowhere near enough!\"","Thirty billion.","Hearing that number, Chu Junlin staggered back a step, his head spinning.","He thought that going all in would let him turn the tables, but he never expected Liu Yutong to be even more ruthless, having prepared thirty billion—not the two hundred billion guessed earlier—determined to wipe him out completely with overwhelming force.","The stock price kept falling at a furious pace.","Xingyao Media's stock price had already fallen below 5 HKD, down more than thirty-five percent, while Qiyuan Real Estate's stock price had fallen below 2.5 HKD, down more than forty-two percent. The combined market value of the two companies had evaporated by more than fifteen billion HKD.","Of Chu Junlin's ten billion in defense funds, less than two billion remained after just half an hour.","\"No... impossible... impossible!\"","Chu Junlin collapsed to the floor in despair: \"How could I lose? How could I lose to a twenty-year-old girl...\"","He refused to accept it. He truly refused to accept it.","He was the young master of the Chu family, a darling of fortune born with a silver spoon in his mouth, the leader of the Junlin Society.","From childhood to now, anything he wanted, he got—whether it was women, status, or money.","Yet today, he had lost so miserably at the hands of a woman, and he simply could not bear it.","Just as Chu Junlin was sinking into despair, the assistant in the corner took a phone call and delivered an even worse piece of news.","\"President Chu... bad news! That Lin Ya—she's a mole!\"","Chu Junlin snapped his head up: \"What did you say?\"","The assistant stammered: \"That... that Lin Ya was hiding it too well. She's released video evidence online exposing Vice President Ma and others at our company for forcing performers to drink at parties and for financial fraud!\"","\"The internet is blowing up now. Xingyao is truly finished this time!\"","Hearing this, Chu Junlin completely lost it. He leaped up and kicked over the desk, sending the computer, documents, and water cup crashing and shattering across the floor.","Like a raging beast, he screamed hysterically: \"Go find her! No matter where she is, bring her here now!\"","That trashy bitch with no backing and no talent dares to shit on my head? I'll make her wish she were dead—she'll beg for death and I'll deny her every time."]},{"number":813,"title":"Chapter 813: 814, Total Defeat","paragraphs":["\"Damn it!\"","\"Damn it!\"","Chu Junlin kicked over the trash can beside him again, his face twisted with rage like he wanted to eat someone alive.","That woman Liu Yutong was someone he truly couldn't afford to mess with — she had connections everywhere and plenty of people under her command.","But who the hell did Lin Ya think she was?","A nobody with no background, no power, an ant of a minor entertainer—he could crush her with ease.","\"Biao! Get in here!\"","\"Boss.\" A burly man with a crew cut walked in from outside. This was his bodyguard, someone who'd been with Chu Junlin for nearly a decade.","\"Go, take some men and find that bitch named Lin Ya. Bring her to me.\"","\"I'm going to make her know what happens when you cross Chu Junlin!\"","\"On it!\"","However, less than an hour later, A Biao called back.","\"Boss, we've got a problem.\"","\"What problem?\"","\"Our guys just found where Lin Ya lives. Before we could even make a move, we got surrounded by a group of men in black — at least forty or fifty of them. We... we all got caught.\"","\"What?!\" Chu Junlin couldn't believe his ears.","In the imperial capital, there wasn't a single person he couldn't get his hands on, and his men had never suffered a loss like this. How had they been completely wiped out in such a short time?","\"What the hell are you even good for? Are you all a bunch of idiots?!\"","\"Boss, there were too many of them, and they were lying in wait in advance. The minute we arrived, we were surrounded. There was no way to fight.\"","Chu Junlin took a deep breath, forcing down his fury: \"Where are you now?\"","\"Locked in an underground parking garage. They're not roughing us up, they just won't let us leave.\"","Chu Junlin hung up, shaking with rage.","Liu Yutong!","It had to be Liu Yutong!","That woman was practically his nemesis!","Frustrated to the point of exploding, Chu Junlin simply couldn't take it anymore. He dialed Liu Yutong's number directly.","Before he could even say a word, her lazy voice came through the other end.","\"Young Master Chu, are you planning to send me more money again? Didn't you already give me enough today?\"","\"Liu Yutong, you—\"","\"Young Master Chu, I advise you to calm down. Don't go sending people to snatch others at the drop of a hat. What era do you think this is? Playing such dirty tricks—if word gets out, you'll embarrass the Chu family name.\"","\"You—\"","\"Also, I've already taught your men a lesson. No need to thank me. Oh, and if you're thinking of sending more people, give me a heads-up first so I can arrange a place. I'm afraid the garage won't have enough room.\"","\"Liu Yutong, I—\"","\"Click... click...\"","The line went dead.","\"Aaahhh!!!\"","Chu Junlin let out a furious roar and hurled his phone against the wall.","The phone shattered instantly, pieces scattering everywhere.","Just then, his assistant, who had just left moments ago, came scrambling back in, stumbling over himself.","\"Pre... President Chu! Bad news! Downstairs... downstairs...\"","\"What about downstairs?\" Chu Junlin roared with bloodshot eyes.","\"Downstairs... a group of men in black just barged in. Our security couldn't stop them!\"","Chu Junlin's head buzzed.","Liu Yutong, what exactly does she want? Is she trying to wipe me out completely?","If she pushes me too far, nobody's going to have an easy time!","Just as he was about to find another phone to call Liu Yutong, a dense wave of footsteps echoed through the hallway.","Then, the office door slammed open with a loud kick.","A group of young men in black suits, each wearing a dragon-shaped badge on their chest, filed into the room, instantly packing the entire office wall to wall.","At the center of these black-clad men, a young man walked in wearing a gray suit and gold-rimmed glasses, radiating the vibe of a reckless outlaw.","\"Who the hell are you? You dare barge into my office with your men? Do you know who I am?!\" Chu Junlin said coldly.","\"Of course I do — Young Master Chu of the Chu family, Chu Junlin.\"","The young man pushed up his gold-rimmed glasses and said with a grin: \"Allow me to introduce myself. My name is Zhao Tianyi, founder of Tianyi Law Firm, and also the lead counsel of Wanlonghui Group.\"","Chu Junlin frowned: \"A lawyer? What are you doing here? Don't tell me you're planning to lay a hand on me. I'm warning you, this is the imperial capital. You're digging your own grave!\"","\"NO! NO! NO!\"","Zhao Tianyi wagged his finger: \"Young Master Chu, you misunderstand. We are law-abiding citizens. We would never engage in illegal activities.\"","\"Young Master Chu, I'm here on behalf of my client, Miss Liu Yutong, Chairman of Wanlonghui Group, to discuss a matter of compensation.\"","\"Compensation? What compensation?\"","Zhao Tianyi sat down casually on the sofa, crossed his legs, pulled out a pack of cigarettes from his pocket, lit one, took a deep drag, and slowly exhaled a cloud of smoke. Through the haze, he squinted at Chu Junlin.","\"Young Master Chu, you sent people to spread rumors and slander my client's show 'The Voice of the Dragon Nation,' hired online trolls to steer public opinion, and coerced an artist into forging contracts in an attempt to frame my client's company... these are all illegal acts.\"","Chu Junlin's face changed: \"You... you're talking nonsense! Do you have proof? Careful, or I'll sue you for defamation!\"","Zhao Tianyi smiled and shook his head upon hearing this: \"Young Master Chu, you're from the prestigious Chu family in the imperial capital, yet you don't seem to have much sense upstairs.\"","\"I'm a professional lawyer with proper credentials. Would I show up at your door with all these men if I didn't have evidence?\"","With that, he pulled a thick stack of documents from his briefcase and slammed them onto the coffee table, pointing at them as he spoke to Chu Junlin.","\"In here, we have the transfer records of your Xingyao Media's vice president paying for trolls, as well as forged contracts coercing artist Lin Ya into signing a predatory agreement — that's fraud.\"","\"We also have transcripts and audio recordings of your company executives discussing financial fraud and tax evasion at banquets. We have the originals too — would you like to have a listen?\"","Chu Junlin's face grew uglier and uglier, but he still refused to admit anything, stubbornly holding his ground.","\"These... these are all fabricated! You made them up!\"","Zhao Tianyi: \"Young Master Chu, if you say they're fabricated, then let's meet in court. But I should kindly warn you — since I started practicing, I've fought hundreds of cases, big and small, with a perfect record of zero losses. If you don't believe me, go ahead and try. We'll see if your stubborn mouth is sharper than mine.\"","Chu Junlin's jaw twitched, unable to speak.","Zhao Tianyi then pulled out a blank sheet of A4 paper and began scribbling on it with a pen: \"Alright, enough small talk. Let's settle the compensation matter.\"","\"First, your rumors and slander of 'The Voice of the Dragon Nation' program have damaged its reputation. Advertisers are strongly demanding reduced sponsorship fees and seeking compensation... I estimate the economic loss at about sixty million yuan.\"","\"You people are shameless! What advertisers are demanding compensation? Aren't those advertisers your own company? Moving money from your left hand to your right hand, and expecting me to pay for it!\" Chu Junlin fumed.","Zhao Tianyi smiled: \"Look at what you're saying. Our own investment is still money too. Even brothers settle accounts clearly. These are all real losses! Doesn't Young Master Chu understand even that?\"","\"You sent people to intimidate the actress Lin Ya, which drove her to a mental breakdown and left her needing long-term psychological treatment. Medical bills, compensation for emotional distress, lost wages, nutritional expenses... add it all up and one hundred million for you—that's not excessive, is it?\"","\"You ordered people to spread rumors online, attacking the reputation of our Wanlong Group, which caused an extremely severe negative impact on society and brought our brand, once valued at eight billion, down to a valuation of only seven billion. Don't you owe us the difference—one billion to make up the shortfall?\"","\"And also, as a renowned entrepreneur, philanthropist, and outstanding representative of young professionals, Miss Liu's reputation is priceless. Your attacks have damaged my client's standing... so let's call it five hundred million. That's still a friendly price—not too much to ask, is it?\"","At this point, Chu Junlin could no longer hold back his anger and cursed out loud: \"Fifteen hundred million? Why don't you just go rob a bank!\""]},{"number":814,"title":"Chapter 814: 815, Compensation, and Peacemaking.","paragraphs":["Zhao Tianyi smiled as he looked at Chu Junlin. \"Young Master Chu, don't be impatient. We're not done yet.\"","He pulled out another document. \"This here is about how you sent people to pressure Zhou Ran into withdrawing from the competition, forcing the production crew to adjust their filming schedule at the last minute and incurring an extra twenty million in production costs. Zhou Ran also suffered online harassment because of it—five million in emotional distress damages.\"","\"In addition, your company Star Media has a long history of financial fraud and tax evasion, seriously disrupting order in the financial markets. My client, as an investor in Hong Kong stocks, suffered massive losses because of your fraudulent activities... Let's call that a hundred million.\"","\"And... thirty million.\"","\"Eight million...\"","\"...\"","Finally, Zhao Tianyi pulled out a calculator and started tapping away, the relentless sound of numbers adding up making Chu Junlin's heart sink with dread.","After quickly tallying everything up, he said to Chu Junlin, \"After the final calculation, the total amount you need to compensate comes to roughly one billion seven hundred forty-three million. That number doesn't sound very nice, so let me just shave off the odd bits—you can pay eighteen billion instead.\"","Chu Junlin: \"???\"","That's what he calls shaving off the odd bits? He just added over fifty million to the total!","Why don't you just go rob a bank?!","\"You... this is blackmail and extortion! I'll call the police! I'll have you arrested!\"","Zhao Tianyi stood up, walked over to Chu Junlin, and patted him on the shoulder, whispering in his ear, \"Young Master Chu, at your age, you're still talking like a child. Don't you know you need evidence to back up your words? Blackmail and extortion? My claims are all well-documented and justified. This is called exercising one's legal rights, understand?\"","Then he pulled his lawyer's license from his pocket and flashed it in front of Chu Junlin's face. \"Take a good look. Official, fully licensed, issued by the Ministry of Justice.\"","Chu Junlin: \"...\"","I'm not blind, dammit!","\"Young Master Chu, I'll say it again—if you really don't accept this, we can take it to court.\"","\"But let me warn you: once this goes to court, some things won't have any room for negotiation anymore. At that point, it won't just be eighteen billion you owe. Your Star Media will be forced into bankruptcy and liquidation, and you personally could face criminal charges.\"","\"Oh, and I almost forgot—you still owe our Young Lady a hundred billion from that bet, plus the hole of nearly a hundred billion you've dug yourself. That adds up to about two hundred billion, doesn't it? Can you even fill that?\"","\"The Young Lady doesn't want to take things too far. As long as you pay the eighteen billion, she might consider letting you off the hook.\"","\"Think it over carefully. I'll be going now.\"","With that, Zhao Tianyi stood up, straightened his suit, and turned to leave.","Just as he reached the door, he stopped and looked back. \"Oh, right—the men you sent to grab Lin Ya are all in my custody. Under the law, they're looking at charges of illegal detention and picking quarrels and provoking trouble... I can absolutely send them away for a few years. But Miss Liu is generous. As long as you pay up, we'll release them.\"","\"Also, Ma Qingliu and several other senior executives at your company are already under our control. They're facing charges of financial fraud, tax evasion, and coercing artists... Add all that up, and it's enough to put them behind bars for over a decade. If you want to bail them out, that's not impossible...\"","He paused, then added three final words: \"It'll cost extra.\"","Chu Junlin almost spat out blood at those last words.","Extra?","Are you a lawyer or a kidnapper?","After Zhao Tianyi left, the office fell into a deathly silence.","Chu Junlin, as if drained of all strength, collapsed onto the floor, staring blankly at the ceiling with lifeless eyes.","Eighteen billion!","He'd already lost nearly a hundred billion today just defending his stock price, and now he had to pay another eighteen billion.","The funds raised by the Junlin Association were almost completely gone—money he still had to repay. Add to that the collapse of his company's stock price, and he'd gone from being a billionaire to being a hundred billion in debt.","And then there was still that hundred billion bet.","What was he supposed to pay with? His life?","Just as he closed his eyes in despair, his assistant came back with another piece of devastating news.","\"Mr. Chu... Mr. Chu... it's over... it's all over!\"","\"Mr. Chu, the CSRC is here. They say they want to investigate our company for financial fraud.\"","Chu Junlin sat bolt upright.","The CSRC.","How did they get here so fast?","\"Also... the tax bureau sent people too. They're here to audit our company's taxes.\"","\"And the Hong Kong Stock Exchange sent a letter of inquiry demanding we explain the abnormal fluctuations in our stock price, and whether the evidence Lin Ya exposed is true.\"","CSRC, tax bureau, Stock Exchange...","They're trying to crush him completely!","\"And... and...\" The assistant stammered, not daring to continue.","Chu Junlin closed his eyes again. After about ten seconds, he slowly opened them.","This time, he didn't lose his temper. He just waved his hand and told the assistant to leave.","Then he got up, pulled a backup phone from his drawer, and with trembling hands dialed the number he least wanted to call but had no choice but to call.","It was his father—the current head of the Chu family.","..........","At Cloud Mountain Capital's trading room in the Southern City.","Liu Yutong hadn't yet received a message back from Zhao Tianyi when she got a call from Lin Yi instead.","\"Lin Yi, what made you think to call me?\"","\"Yutong, you've had your fun, haven't you? People up top have spoken. That's enough—don't push him completely into a corner. The Chu family head has found someone to intercede. They want both sides to each take a step back and let this matter be laid to rest.\"","Hearing this result, Liu Yutong wasn't surprised in the least.","Everything was going exactly as she'd predicted.","No matter how useless Chu Junlin was, he was still a member of the Chu family. And the Chu family, after all, was one of the deeply entrenched top-tier aristocratic families in the capital.","If she truly pushed Chu Junlin to the edge, the Chu family could not stand by and do nothing.","But then again, her goal had never been to completely destroy Chu Junlin.","Just to beat him into submission. That was enough.","\"Fine, I understand.\"","\"Since the higher-ups have spoken, I'll give them that face.\"","\"But pass along my terms, Lin Yi—compensation has to be paid, no question. And Chu Junlin needs to come here, admit defeat in front of me, and apologize.\"","\"Alright.\""]},{"number":815,"title":"Chapter 815: 816, The Arrival of Chu Junlin.","paragraphs":["She hung up the phone.","Liu Yutong turned to the people in the trading room and said two words: \"Wrap it up.\"","Chen Mo froze for a moment: \"Chairman, you mean... it's over?\"","Liu Yutong nodded: \"It's over. Close out all short positions. Stop adding sell pressure on Star Shine Media and Origin Real Estate. Let them digest it on their own.\"","\"But Chairman, this is the perfect time to reap the rewards. If we pull back now...\" Chen Mo was still reluctant, because he felt this wave could easily net another seven or eight hundred million.","Liu Yutong raised her hand to cut him off: \"Listen to me. Wrap it up.\"","Although Chen Mo felt a pang of regret, he immediately turned and went to execute the order.","In the trading room, the clatter of keyboards rang out once more, but this time, it wasn't to open short positions—it was to close them and exit the market.","On the big screen, the stock prices of Star Shine Media and Origin Real Estate, no longer crushed by the massive sell pressure, finally stopped their decline and began to rebound slowly.","The rebound was weak, but at least the crash had halted.","\"Remove the trending topics,\" Liu Yutong instructed Lan Die.","Lan Die immediately contacted the technical team at Weibo.","Within less than ten minutes, all the hot searches about Zhou Ran, The Voice, and Wanlong Group disappeared from the trending list one by one, as if erased by a rubber band.","Those traces were wiped clean, as if they had never existed.","At the same time, on the Longkan Vision platform, malicious comments and videos about the show's behind-the-scenes scandals began to be purged on a massive scale.","In just about half an hour, the once-boiling public opinion went from a raging storm to dead calm.","This almost magical operation left countless onlookers stunned.","[What the hell? Where did the trending topics go? They're all gone!]","[I can't see a single hot search about The Voice anymore. That's insane!]","[Wait, it's over? I haven't even finished my popcorn!]","[The power of capital is truly terrifying...]","[Can someone explain what the hell just happened?]","[Hey, don't ask. That kind of stuff isn't for us to know.]","[Damn, it feels like the internet itself is turning dark.]","[...]","Just as Liu Yutong left the trading room, Yun Cheng followed behind her and asked in a low voice: \"Miss, did someone higher up step in?\"","Liu Yutong nodded: \"The Chu family found someone to mediate.\"","\"So that means Chu Junlin has admitted defeat?\" Yun Cheng pressed.","Liu Yutong: \"He's lost whether he admits it or not. That's inevitable. He'll come to Mingzhu City to apologize in person.\"","\"Oh, and by the way, for the first batch of our employee family tours here in Mingzhu City—where are they headed?\"","Yun Cheng: \"BS Province. A lot of people want to see how the post-disaster reconstruction is going over there. There are also plenty of tourist spots there, perfect for sightseeing.\"","Liu Yutong nodded: \"Got it.\"","...","Two days later, Mingzhu City.","At six in the morning, the sky was already bright. The square in front of the Wanlong Group headquarters was already buzzing with noise and activity.","Today was the departure day for the first batch of Wanlong Group's employee direct family member tour groups.","Most of them were family members of employees on the BS Province route—about twelve hundred people in total, mostly middle-aged and elderly folks in their forties, fifties, and sixties, along with some younger employees who'd taken annual leave to travel with their parents.","For this trip, the group had mobilized over thirty luxury tour buses, each equipped with a professional guide, a team doctor from the medical university, and two black-suited security guards from Wanlong.","On the square, thirty buses were lined up in a single row, with big red flowers tied to the front—festive and imposing.","The employees' parents participating in the tour were all dressed in new clothes. Some had even dyed their hair specially. They looked spirited, with smiles all over their faces.","\"Mom, make sure to call us when you get there. Don't be stingy with money. If you want to eat something, just buy it,\" a young female employee said, holding her mother's hand.","\"I know, I know. Don't worry about me. Your company said everything will be arranged. All I have to do is follow the guide and enjoy myself.\"","\"...\"","\"Dad, your blood pressure is a bit high. Remember to take your meds on time. The guide will remind you, so don't be shy.\"","\"Don't worry, your old man is still tough as nails. You just take care of yourself at home. Don't skip meals, and eat well.\"","\"...\"","Similar conversations echoed across the square.","Meanwhile, around the perimeter of the square, core members of Wanlong wearing dragon-shaped badges on their chests were maintaining order.","Everyone entering the square had to pass their identity verification.","Every vehicle approaching the square was politely stopped and directed to the outer parking lot.","Such a spectacle—even the police officers who saw it couldn't help but silently marvel.","\"What's going on here? Why so many middle-aged and elderly people?\"","\"I heard Wanlong Group invited its employees' parents on a trip. This seems to be the first batch.\"","\"All these people and they're just the first batch? That's insane!\"","\"No wonder they're the biggest group in Mingzhu City. They're loaded and they don't hide it.\"","\"I'm so jealous. I want to work for a company like that, with free trips for family members.\"","\"...\"","While the square was orderly distributing food and water for the family members to take on the road, a black Audi with out-of-town plates pulled into the outer parking lot.","The door opened, and Chu Junlin, dressed in a blue suit, stepped out. Two bodyguards followed behind him.","When he saw the thirty buses on the square and the middle-aged and elderly people queuing up for provisions, his brows furrowed slightly.","These people are Wanlong's employees?","Hadn't the rumors said Liu Yutong's staff were all young men in black suits, with burly builds and fierce combat skills?","But looking at this now, it didn't match the rumors at all.","Could it be that Liu Yutong was just bragging to scare outsiders?","The more Chu Junlin thought about it, the more he believed it might be true. After all, who in their right mind would keep thousands of black-suited thugs on the payroll?","But if it was true, then all his previous fear and dread had been ridiculous.","Before coming to Mingzhu City, when he'd heard those black-suited men numbered in the thousands, he'd been genuinely terrified.","He'd even debated whether to come to Mingzhu City at all.","He admitted that in the battle on the Hong Kong stock exchange, Liu Yutong had won fair and square.","Over thirty billion in capital, crushing him completely. He had nothing to say.","But that didn't mean he was truly convinced.","It wasn't until he heard that Liu Yutong had an army of underlings, and that they were especially dark and menacing, that he truly began to consider surrendering.","\"Boss, should we go in?\" one of the bodyguards asked.","Chu Junlin straightened his tie, restoring his usual arrogant demeanor: \"In, of course we're going in. Let's see if this Miss Liu is really a paper tiger or not.\"","With that, he led his two bodyguards into the building.","The lobby was spacious, and the decor was impressive enough, but it was far from the den of dragons and tigers he'd imagined.","Is this it?","Chu Junlin felt even more scorn rising in his heart.","“Mr. Chu, this way, please.” A man in black walked over from the direction of the elevator and made a gesture of invitation.","Chu Junlin stepped into the elevator with his bodyguards.","The man in black swiped the badge on his chest and pressed a button that had no number printed on it. The elevator began to rise.","Chu Junlin noticed that there was no floor indicator inside the elevator—only that single illuminated button.","“Which floor are we going to?” he asked casually.","The man in black didn’t even turn his head. “You’ll know when we get there.”","Chu Junlin frowned slightly, a flicker of displeasure crossing his face, but he said nothing more.","The elevator ran for about ten-odd seconds before finally coming to a stop.","The moment the doors slid open, the expression on Chu Junlin’s face visibly hardened.","It was just an ordinary corridor ahead of him, yet for no clear reason, his heart suddenly felt uneasy—as if something heavy were pressing down on his chest.","“Mr. Chu, after you.” The man in black stepped out of the elevator first and gestured again.","Chu Junlin nodded and walked out.","As for his bodyguards, they tried to follow, but two men in black standing at the elevator entrance blocked them with outstretched arms.","“You two can’t go in. Just wait here.”","“Boss...”","Chu Junlin glanced back at his two bodyguards, gave a slight nod, and followed the man in black alone toward the front.","The closer he got to the closed door not far ahead, the stronger the sense of unease and suffocation grew inside him.","When he reached the door, the two men in black guarding it pulled it open.","The man leading the way made another gesture of invitation.","Chu Junlin took a deep breath and strode inside.","The moment he set foot beyond the threshold, his steps came to an abrupt halt. The expression on his face—and even the blood in his veins—seemed to freeze solid.","Because before his eyes stretched a dense, suffocating expanse of blackness..."]},{"number":816,"title":"Chapter 816: 817, Welcome to the Dragon Society","paragraphs":["What appeared before Chu Junlin's eyes was a conference room.","The meeting hall was enormous—it was as if the walls of the entire floor had been knocked down to create one single space. It was filled with chairs, enough to accommodate two to three thousand people.","And at this moment, those rows upon rows of chairs were already packed with people, each one dressed in identical black suits, with a dragon-shaped emblem pinned to their chests—an emblem Chu Junlin recognized all too well.","Especially when thousands of icy-cold gazes simultaneously fixed on a single person, the sheer pressure bearing down on you was enough to break even the strongest of nerves.","Under this weight, beads of sweat began to form on Chu Junlin's forehead.","As a young master raised in the imperial capital since childhood, he felt true fear for the first time in his life.","Not the fear of being beaten, but the fear of suddenly coming face-to-face with something so vast and overwhelming that he couldn't even begin to comprehend it.","It was as though he were nothing more than an ant in comparison.","\"Young Master Chu, this way, please.\"","A man in black led him through that sea of darkness, toward the very front of the banquet hall.","Chu Junlin's legs had gone weak, but he forced himself to hold it together and hide it, following stiffly behind the man.","None of the men in black spoke; they simply stared silently at this unfamiliar intruder.","Chu Junlin was guided to one of the chairs in the very front row and seated.","The entire row he was sitting in was almost completely empty, which meant many important people had yet to arrive—important figures, no less.","\"The young lady will be here shortly. Please wait a moment,\" the man in black said, then turned and walked away.","Chu Junlin sat in his chair, shifting uncomfortably from time to time. It wasn't that the chair was uncomfortable—it was that he felt completely out of place.","Within just a few minutes, he had turned his head more than once to glance back at the thousands of men in black behind him, each time only daring to steal a quick look before snapping his head back around.","Just how many men like this did that woman, Liu Yutong, actually have?","And these were only the ones he could see.","Earlier, his father had said Liu Yutong had several thousand such men under her command, and he had thought it was an exaggeration. Now, it seemed his father had undersold it.","Just as his mind was wandering, the doors to the banquet hall were pushed open once more.","This time, it wasn't one person—it was a whole group.","Leading the way was a row of young men in black suits, each radiating an extraordinary air.","Behind them followed several young men and women.","Chu Junlin recognized a few of them—Shangguan Ling'er, Shen Cheng, and others he had seen at the Imperial Capital Club.","As for those striking young men in black, aside from recognizing one infuriating fellow who wore gold-rimmed glasses, he didn't know a single one of them.","But these people weren't the main event.","After they entered, they automatically stepped aside to the two sides, as if waiting for someone else to appear.","Chu Junlin's heart began to race.","Then he heard it—the sound of high heels clicking on the floor, drawing closer from outside.","Click. Click. Click.","In an instant, the thousands of people in the banquet hall fell utterly silent.","Chu Junlin found himself rising to his feet involuntarily, his eyes locked on the doors.","Soon, at the entrance of the conference room, a striking figure in black appeared.","—Liu Yutong!","Today, Liu Yutong wore a black long dress with a stand-up collar that elegantly revealed her slender neck and delicate collarbones. A wide belt of the same color cinched her waist, accentuating her graceful figure to perfection.","Her long, jet-black hair was swept up into a high bun, secured with a dragon-shaped hairpin, revealing her smooth forehead and a face so cold and breathtaking it was almost blinding.","Her makeup was minimal—almost nonexistent—yet it was that kind of pristine, unadorned beauty that made people afraid to even look at her directly.","What drew the most attention, however, was the emblem on her chest—a golden dragon-shaped badge, gleaming brilliantly.","That was the highest-ranking symbol of the Ten Thousand Dragons Society. Only one person in the world had the right to wear it.","That person was Liu Yutong herself.","The instant Liu Yutong stepped into the banquet hall—","Whoosh!!!","Thousands of men in black rose to their feet simultaneously.","The sight was enough to make one's scalp tingle.","And then...","\"Greetings to the young lady!\" Thousands of voices in unison.","The wave of sound rolled through the room!","Chu Junlin was so startled by that thunderous greeting that he nearly jumped out of his skin. He even noticed the chandeliers overhead swaying from the force of the noise.","At the same time, seeing this scene, he realized just how wrong he had been.","When he had left the imperial capital, he had only planned to offer a half-hearted apology and be done with it—there was no way he was going to be intimidated by some twenty-year-old woman.","It wasn't until this very moment that he understood how utterly mistaken he was.","In that instant, he genuinely considered dropping to the ground and prostrating himself before her.","Liu Yutong walked up to the podium, step by step.","Chu Junlin's gaze followed her movements, and only then did he notice that on the wall behind her hung a large banner with four massive characters—\"Ten Thousand Dragons, Return to One!\"","Liu Yutong's gaze swept calmly across the entire hall, including the members of the Cloud Mountain Society and the high-ranking leaders of the Ten Thousand Dragons Society seated in the front rows.","\"Sit.\"","Whoosh!","Everyone sat down at once.","With only one exception—Chu Junlin, who was standing in the front row, still dazed and frozen in place, having not yet processed what was happening.","Liu Yutong finally turned her eyes toward him, a faint smile curling at the corner of her lips.","\"Young Master Chu, welcome to the Ten Thousand Dragons Society!\""]},{"number":817,"title":"Chapter 817: 818, Target of Ten Thousand People, Halfway Done.","paragraphs":["\"Young Master Chu, welcome to the Dragon Assembly.\" Liu Yutong crossed her arms, watching him with a faint, knowing smile.","Chu Junlin felt at that moment as if his legs no longer belonged to him.","Now he understood exactly why Liu Yutong had insisted he come to Bright Pearl City to apologize in person—this was her way of showing off her power to him on purpose.","Half a minute passed before he finally lifted his foot and walked toward the stage.","That suffocating sensation of thousands of eyes fixed on his back at once was truly crushing.","What should have been just a dozen or so steps felt to him like walking for an entire century, until he finally stood before Liu Yutong.","She simply looked at him, still smiling.","\"Young Master Chu, since you're here, say what you've come to say.\"","Deep down, Chu Junlin still felt resistance—shame, even.","Before arriving, he had already braced himself for the worst.","Apologize.","Admit defeat.","Pay damages.","He had thought of all of that.","The one thing he hadn't anticipated was that Liu Yutong would be so merciless as to make him apologize in front of thousands of people.","It was no different from a public execution.","In the end, he lowered his proud head.","\"Miss Liu... I lost.\"","\"I admit my defeat wholeheartedly.\"","\"I apologize to you—sincerely, from the bottom of my heart.\"","With that, he bowed deeply, a perfect ninety degrees.","The moment he bent over, he closed his eyes.","Growing up, when had Chu Junlin ever shown such deference to anyone?","In the imperial capital, he was the young master of the Chu family, the object of countless people's flattery, standing at the very top of the pyramid.","But today, before a twenty-year-old girl, he had not only lowered his head but bent his back.","Liu Yutong watched the bowing Chu Junlin and fell silent for a moment.","To be honest, she hadn't expected him to be so straightforward.","She had assumed that with the pride of this Young Master Chu, he might have struggled, or even lashed out and stormed off on the spot.","But he didn't.","It seemed that that battle had truly hurt him—and knocked some sense into him.","\"Young Master Chu, you may raise your head.\"","Chu Junlin straightened up to face the woman in the black dress.","Gone from his eyes was the arrogance and resentment he'd brought with him; in their place was an indescribable complexity of emotions.","There was reverence, wariness—and a trace of... resignation.","Yes, resignation.","When you've lost everything down to your last shred of dignity, what's the point of clinging to face?","\"Young Master Chu, the fact that you came all the way to Bright Pearl City and stood here to apologize tells me you're not beyond redemption like some spoiled rich kid.\"","\"Your apology, I accept.\"","\"And with it, that hundred-billion wager is hereby voided,\" Liu Yutong said.","Chu Junlin's tense shoulders finally relaxed.","He'd actually been afraid she wouldn't accept.","Given this woman's personality, if she'd refused his apology, he might not have walked out of this building alive today.","One look at those men in black told him that much.","More importantly, he really couldn't afford that hundred-billion wager, and he still owed money to the members of the Junlin Society. He could only slowly fill that enormous hole once his company got back on its feet, supplemented by his family's support.","Now that the hundred-billion debt was wiped away, he could finally breathe a little easier.","\"I'm willing to forgo the wager money, but the compensation of one-point-eight billion still needs to be paid. You don't have a problem with that, do you?\" Liu Yutong shifted the topic.","Chu Junlin's heart tightened.","One-point-eight billion!","Sure, it was far less than a hundred billion, but his cash flow was completely severed right now—he truly couldn't come up with that kind of money.","Liu Yutong, naturally aware of his situation, added, \"As for the one-point-eight billion, I can give you some extra time.\"","Chu Junlin let out a wry laugh. \"Miss Liu, I really can't produce that much cash at the moment. Would it be possible to pay in installments?\"","Liu Yutong nodded. \"Fine. Within two years, paid in two batches of nine hundred million each. I won't charge you interest.\"","Two years.","Nine hundred million a year.","Chu Junlin did the mental math quickly—as long as his company survived, this proposal was barely within his means.","At least he still had a chance at a comeback.","\"Fine, I agree.\"","\"Then let's sign an agreement, put it all down in black and white so there's no room for disputes later,\" Liu Yutong said.","\"Alright.\"","Zhao Tianyi stepped forward from the side, holding a prepared agreement, and handed it to Chu Junlin.","\"Just sign at the bottom.\"","Chu Junlin shot him a dark look—this bastard was the one who'd piled the extra one-point-eight billion in damages on him.","An absolute scumbag.","He took the agreement, carefully read through it, and after confirming there was nothing problematic, picked up the pen and signed his name.","The moment the pen touched the paper, his mind flashed with images of figures from history books. Did they feel the same humiliation when they signed their names?","As the ink dried, he exhaled a long breath, feeling some weight lift off his shoulders.","\"Young Master Chu, go take your seat.\" Liu Yutong gestured to the front row.","Chu Junlin nodded and walked back to sit down.","Only then did he notice the figures in the front row looking at him with rather intriguing expressions.","Shangguan Ling'er, Shen Cheng, Wei Xiao, Xu Ke.","These four—the reserve members who had chosen to stay with Cloud Mountain Society rather than follow him—were now sitting in the front row, gazing at him with a mixture of relief and pity.","So glad we didn't go with you.","So glad we stayed at Cloud Mountain.","Otherwise, today it might be us up on that stage, apologizing before thousands.","Chu Junlin's mouth twitched at the corners. A jumble of emotions churned in his chest.","Back then, he'd boasted he would start his own faction and crush Cloud Mountain Society. And now?","Less than two months later, here he stood, a cautionary tale.","Meanwhile, those who had chosen to follow him were now his creditors. They hadn't openly turned on him, but there was definitely resentment simmering beneath the surface.","At least Liu Yutong hadn't gone for the kill. She'd left him a way out.","After admitting defeat and apologizing, Chu Junlin was now genuinely reconciled with Liu Yutong. He no longer felt as uneasy as before.","During the rest of the assembly, he came to realize that Liu Yutong hadn't gathered all her people just to intimidate him.","Or rather, intimidating him was just a side bonus—the real purpose was some kind of induction ceremony.","He'd thought it would be the usual kind of promotion ceremony, but when he saw over eight hundred men in black go up one by one to receive their honors and pledge their oaths, he realized how wrong he was.","\"I swear to follow the Young Mistress to the death!\"","\"Born for Dragon Assembly, soul bound to Dragon Assembly!\"","\"Unity of knowledge and action!\"","\"...\"","That fervor overwhelmed Chu Junlin yet again, leaving him staring in disbelief.","This was already Dragon Assembly's third induction of the year—a higher frequency than last year. With another likely coming at the end of the year, that would make four, or one per quarter.","Core membership had also grown from less than three thousand at last year's annual meeting to over five thousand, completing half of that goal of ten thousand that Ma Da and the others had bragged about when they first started.","As for the total number of ordinary employees in the group, because the count includes full-time riders and delivery couriers, the latest figure has already exceeded 150,000.","The number is extremely large.","Similarly, they are no longer able to promote core members using the previous 10-to-1 ratio, since the requirements for core members are quite demanding. Some people with little formal education—especially older grassroots employees, such as some riders—may not even have an elementary school diploma and cannot even meet the threshold for reading legal texts. Without outstanding contributions, they can hardly become core members, which has caused this ratio to keep widening.","That’s simply unavoidable.","Moreover, in addition to legal knowledge, there are physical fitness and combat-skills assessments.","Taken together, the average age of the core members of the Wanlong Society remains between 18 and 28—very youthful—with only a very few exceptional cases over the age of 30.","After the meeting ended, apart from those assigned to provide security for the tour groups, everyone else dispersed normally and went about their own business."]},{"number":818,"title":"Chapter 818: 819, Go Be a Nanny.","paragraphs":["Chu Junlin was completely numbed after watching the entire promotion ceremony.","It was only at this moment that he truly realized he had been nothing but a clown, daring to go up against a woman like her.","Her ability to command and control subordinates was, without a doubt, the highest level he had ever seen—almost no one from the younger generation could match her.","If this woman ever went crazy and ran off abroad one day, anyone who had a grudge against her would probably die without even knowing how.","And that might well include him.","As he followed Liu Yutong downstairs, Chu Junlin finally couldn't hold it in any longer and asked to rejoin the Cloud Mountain Society.","Even if it meant being just a regular member, he would accept it.","\"The Cloud Mountain Society isn't a place anyone can just walk into,\" Liu Yutong said.","\"What I need isn't a turncoat. I need people who are truly of one heart, people who can really get things done.\"","Chu Junlin immediately asked, \"Miss Liu, what do you want me to do? Whatever I can do, I won't hesitate for a second.\"","Liu Yutong saw that he seemed sincere enough, thought for a moment, and said, \"We'll talk about that later. Before that, you'll only count as a probationary member of the Cloud Mountain Society. If you can't even get through the probation period, then don't blame me.\"","Chu Junlin nodded.","That condition was reasonable. After all, given what he had done before, Liu Yutong not kicking him out outright was already doing him a favor.","\"Before that, you need to do something first,\" Liu Yutong said.","\"What is it?\" Chu Junlin asked.","Liu Yutong glanced at Yun Cheng.","Yun Cheng understood the signal, stepped forward, and said to Chu Junlin, \"Young Master Chu, our group recently organized employee family trips and staff children's summer camp activities. We're short on manpower and need someone to help out.\"","Chu Junlin: \"You mean... you want me to look after kids?\"","Yun Cheng nodded: \"Yes, looking after kids.\"","Chu Junlin's mouth twitched.","He, the young master of the Chu family, the head of three listed companies, was going to babysit?","If word got back to the capital, where would he put his face?","\"What, not willing?\" Liu Yutong said.","Chu Junlin gritted his teeth: \"I'm willing! I'm willing!\"","\"That's good.\"","Liu Yutong nodded: \"The summer camp just happens to be short-staffed. You'll be in charge of taking the kids to places like the aquarium, the zoo, and the science museum, and making sure they're well taken care of in terms of meals and daily life.\"","\"Remember, those kids are all children of our group's employees. The youngest is only three, and the oldest is around ten. If you dare mess up even a little, you know the consequences.\"","Chu Junlin immediately assured her: \"Don't worry, I'll take good care of them.\"","\"Then it's settled. Report to the summer camp tomorrow.\"","\"Alright.\"","When Chu Junlin agreed, he had already fully accepted reality in his heart.","He now saw things clearly: if you go against Liu Yutong, she'll crush you to death.","But if you genuinely admit defeat and are willing to follow her arrangements, she doesn't seem that heartless after all.","As for his desire to rejoin the Cloud Mountain Society, it wasn't an impulsive decision—he truly had no other choice.","He was already buried in enormous debt. Although the billion-yuan bet had been waived, between the 1.8 billion yuan in compensation and the messy accounts from the Junlin Society, he still faced a shortfall of nearly ten billion.","To close that gap, he had to find a chance to turn things around.","Right now, his best option could only be found through Liu Yutong.","His father had managed to help mediate the situation, but as for the debts he had racked up, his father didn't ask or care, leaving Chu Junlin to solve it on his own.","It couldn't really be said that his father was cold-hearted—this hole was of his own making, and the bulk of it had to be filled by him.","Sometimes he found it laughable. Not long ago, he had been her opponent, even her enemy.","Now, in the blink of an eye, he was groveling at her feet, wanting nothing more than to be part of her camp.","Not to mention, after this battle, he had come to see a lot of things clearly.","Especially Liu Yutong.","This woman might be young, but her vision, her insight, and her methods were the most top-tier he had ever seen among the younger generation.","And her strength was also the greatest, even when you set aside her background.","When Liu Yutong came down with the group of men in black, the staff's family members had mostly already boarded the buses.","Then the core members accompanying the team also got on board one after another, each holding two cartons of cigarettes, handing them to the drivers as they got on.","The two cartons of cigarettes were a way of hoping the drivers would stay alert and do their utmost to ensure the families' safety.","After all, when you're out and about, safety comes first.","The next day.","Early in the morning, Chu Junlin was woken up by Yun Cheng.","\"Chu Junlin, time to go.\"","Chu Junlin groggily glanced at his phone—it was only five in the morning.","\"So early?\"","\"The kids assemble at seven-something. As one of the escorts, you need to arrive early.\"","Chu Junlin resignedly dragged himself out of bed, washed up, got dressed, and followed Yun Cheng out the door.","After he finished breakfast and arrived at the assembly point, he was completely dumbfounded.","The square was packed with kids, all different ages from three or four to ten. Some were crying, some were making a fuss, some were chasing each other around, and some were clinging to their parents' legs, refusing to let go.","\"These... all of these are—\"","\"Yes, the first batch of summer camp kids. Around two hundred of them, divided into ten groups. Each group gets two preschool teachers and two security guards. Honestly, it's basically like being nannies. As for you, you're the head nanny.\"","Chu Junlin: \"...\"","He suddenly felt like he had boarded a pirate ship.","\"Young Master Chu, don't stand there in a daze. The kids need to get on the buses. Go help keep order.\"","Chu Junlin took a deep breath and strode toward the kids.","\"Okay, kids, line up! One by one, get on the bus, no pushing!\"","\"You, yes you, stop running! Come back!\"","\"Hey, you there, hold onto your water bottle, don't drop it!\"","\"Damn, this kid can't even hold his pee—he just sprayed all over me...\"","An hour later, all two hundred kids had finally boarded the buses.","Chu Junlin was dripping with sweat, feeling completely drained, like his body had been hollowed out.","He truly never imagined looking after kids would be this exhausting—more tiring than negotiating deals worth billions.","And this was only the beginning. The real torture was still ahead.","......"]},{"number":819,"title":"Chapter 819: 820, Steady Development.","paragraphs":["Time flew by, and before we knew it, more than two months had passed.","The originally scorching hot weather had gradually taken on a hint of coolness.","Liu Yutong had also advanced from a sophomore to a junior.","During this period, with the successful restructuring of Wanlong Corporation and the gradual integration between departments, the massive machinery of Wanlong Group was finally able to operate more efficiently.","Previously, Liu Yutong basically had to handle everything herself, keeping an eye on every project out of fear that even the slightest thing would go wrong.","Now, with the establishment of the six business groups, she had fully delegated the decision-making authority for day-to-day operations to the executive presidents and department managers below her, only needing to oversee decisions at the strategic level. This made things much easier.","This was exactly the situation she wanted to see and had to make happen.","A truly mature business empire could not rely on her alone.","The new semester of her junior year began.","At the freshman orientation ceremony, after Liu Yutong gave a speech on stage as an outstanding alumni representative, she went straight to the company and briefly handled the matters at the group that needed her attention.","Progress at LoongCore was encouraging.","Qiu Ciyun had sent a detailed quarterly report: the 90-nanometer production line had been in stable mass production for three months, with the yield rate soaring from less than 70% at initial production to the current 92%, surpassing the industry average. This meant LoongCore had already gained a certain level of profitability.","Research into the 65-nanometer process had also already begun, with expectations for the first tape-out test to be completed by mid-next year at the earliest, or even as early as the start of next year.","At the same time, a veteran domestic color TV giant had taken the initiative to extend an olive branch, wanting to sign a long-term supply agreement with LoongCore to purchase at least two million chips per year for their set-top box and digital TV product lines.","Once this cooperation agreement was signed, along with the previous orders from Qiming Appliances, LoongCore would be able to fully shake off the stage of simply burning money and officially enter a virtuous cycle of self-sustaining revenue generation.","Over in the provincial capital, Yu Xin's mobile phone division was also making rapid progress.","That girl's leadership skills were growing by the day. In just half a month, she had integrated the technical teams recruited from all over the world, quickly negotiated parts supply channels, and established the chip design department for the mobile phone division.","The first engineering prototype was also being rapidly assembled and debugged, and in all likelihood, it wouldn't be long before they could produce a qualified \"knockoff\" sample device.","Why call it a \"knockoff\" engineering prototype? Because, apart from the phone's exterior design and an operating system deeply customized from the Android kernel, all other hardware—such as the screen, sensors, and so on—was implemented by piecing together mature, off-the-shelf public mold solutions available on the market.","There was no way around it; at this stage, the domestic smartphone supply chain was still very weak, and the accumulated technical expertise was still far from reaching the heights needed for fully independent research and development.","However, if domestic phones were to truly rise and flourish, the entire domestic industry chain would also be upgraded along with them, shaking off the less-than-glorious label of \"knockoff.\"","The premise was that there had to be a domestic phone maker that could first survive and carve out a path to victory both at home and abroad.","If things went smoothly for Yu Xin, the first phone would be released in the first half of next year.","Aside from Yu Xin's side, there was also the Rice Company in the capital.","Lei Jobs' Rice Company was also developing its first phone at a very fast pace. Their optimistic projection was to release the first Rice phone in the second half of next year.","This pace was a full year earlier than the timeline Liu Yutong remembered from her past life.","Wanlong Aerospace also had good news.","Professor Zhou Yingpei had ultimately accepted her invitation, resigning from his faculty position at National Aerospace University and officially assuming the role of Chief Technology Officer and Chief Engineer at Wanlong Aerospace Technology.","This professor, already past fifty, said something to her over the phone that she remembered clearly:","\"Chairman Liu, I didn't accept this because of the high salary you're offering. I accepted because of what you said about making the Dragon Nation's rockets fly higher and farther.\"","Liu Yutong really wanted to say, \"That's not exactly what I said, is it? I recall it was something about being bored and wanting to go sightseeing on Mars.\"","But no matter what had been said originally, it didn't matter anymore.","The first thing Professor Zhou Yingpei did after taking office was to restart the liquid-oxygen kerosene staged combustion cycle rocket engine project he had been working on for years.","He also brought in some of the key members from the original project team, recruited several young technical talents from the aerospace system through his personal connections, and rented a three-story building in the suburbs of the capital, putting up a sign that read [Wanlong Aerospace Technology R&D Center].","The approval from the Defense Science, Technology, and Industry Bureau had come down, with both the launch vehicle manufacturing license and the satellite frequency band usage rights obtained. The research funding on Zhou Yingpei's side had also started trickling in in batches.","Everything was proceeding according to plan.","Over at the Digital Business Group, Zhang Dalong had also submitted a progress report.","The beta version of WeiChat had been completed and was undergoing final internal testing.","This instant messaging application was different from Big Goose's QQ—the interface was more streamlined, and there were no cluttered flashing images, live-streaming gimmicks, or value-added services. Its key selling point was purely clean communication.","LoongPay was also advancing in parallel; the payment license application had already been submitted, and while the approval process would likely take some time, there wouldn't be much of a problem.","Meanwhile, monetization on Weibo had made progress, with the advertising system now live and delivering decent results.","Weibo's registered user count had surpassed 160 million, active users had exceeded 80 million, and daily active users had stabilized at 20 to 30 million.","The pace of new user registrations in recent months had visibly accelerated, thanks to the monumental success of \"The Voice of the Dragon Nation.\" As an almost universally known phenomenon-level music variety show, when its contestants and mentors joined Weibo, it brought a massive influx of traffic to the platform.","On the other side, Pony Ma's Weibo had also been rushed online, making a big splash with a celebrity onboarding strategy from the start.","But what Pony Ma didn't realize was that QQ's social DNA and Weibo's media DNA were simply incompatible—the result of forcing them together could be summed up in one word: failure.","After QQ Weibo was launched, Liu Yutong still gave Pony Ma a call to offer her congratulations.","Until WeiChat was officially released, the relationship between the two sides remained relatively cordial.","In the afternoon, Liu Yutong met again with Wei Xiao, an ordinary member of Cloud Mountain Society.","This was Wei Xiao's second time visiting Pearl City.","The first time was when Chu Junlin came to apologize, where Wei Xiao, as a provisional member of Cloud Mountain Society, had joined Shangguan Ling'er and the others at Wanlong Society's awe-inspiring promotion ceremony.","Back then, he had toured Wanlong Society's security department with great enthusiasm, focusing on the division headed by Yun Cheng and Chu Yang.","But after the tour, he left in complete bewilderment.","Clearly, Wanlong Society's security system had exceeded anything he had imagined, leaving him utterly dumbfounded.","You'd be forgiven for thinking it was some kind of arrogant, shady criminal syndicate.","Wei Xiao had come again this time, mainly to discuss deeper cooperation between the two sides."]},{"number":820,"title":"Chapter 820: 821, Deep Cooperation.","paragraphs":["\"President Wei, have some tea.\" Liu Yutong sat across from him, raised her teacup, and gestured.","Wei Xiao quickly picked up his cup and took a sip.","\"President Wei, after your last visit, have you given any more thought to what we discussed?\" Liu Yutong set down her teacup and got straight to the point.","When they had first met at the Emperor Club, Wei Xiao had chosen to stay with Yunsan Hui instead of leaving with Chu Junlin. That was when Liu Yutong had taken notice of him.","Not because of his family background, but because of the temperament he carried.","Steady. Composed. Not restless.","Most importantly, in a place like the imperial capital, he ran a security company that could take on overseas contracts—which meant he had connections, networks, and things other people didn't.","\"Miss Liu, if you'll forgive my bluntness, the security market in the West is very mature. The local security firms are incredibly strong. It would be very difficult for an outsider like us to break in. Investment there requires caution—one misstep and things could go wrong.\"","\"I've never expected this to turn a profit.\"","\"Then what exactly are you suggesting...?\"","\"President Wei, you know I own a chip company called Dragon Core, right?\"","Wei Xiao nodded. \"I do.\"","Liu Yutong said, \"In the chip manufacturing industry, there's still a huge gap between what we have domestically and what they have abroad. Many key pieces of equipment and technologies are blockaded by foreign countries—you can't buy them even with money.\"","\"I'm not planning to charge straight at the blockade. I intend to go around it.\"","Wei Xiao's brow furrowed slightly, as if he were weighing her words.","\"In the West, there are many high-tech companies, and a lot of talented people there want a change of environment. Quite a few of them are senior engineers and technical experts in chip manufacturing. Some of these people are restricted in their freedom because of their status—even if they wanted to change environments, they can't.\"","\"My idea is to use certain special channels to safely 'invite' these people into the country.\"","When Wei Xiao heard this, he finally understood her intention. He wasn't stupid; he could read between the lines well enough.","The normal headhunting route—poaching through legitimate channels, applying for work visas—that was the visible path. But Liu Yutong had come to him, which meant what she needed was not the visible path.","\"Miss Liu, when you say 'special channels,' could you be more specific...?\"","Liu Yutong didn't hide anything: \"I need you to set up a standalone route from your overseas bases, so that those talents willing to come develop in China can enter the country safely and covertly.\"","\"The entire process cannot leave any paper trail or electronic trace. Every step has to be person-to-person, point-to-point.\"","\"Once they're in the country, they'll be given new identities and assigned to work in Dragon Core's secret laboratory. I'll have people handle all the paperwork so that everything is legal and above board.\"","Wei Xiao fell silent.","He wasn't hesitating over whether to do it—he was assessing the risks and feasibility of the operation.","What Liu Yutong was proposing, to be frank, was skating the edge of the law.","Is it illegal? Those experts are genuinely 'willing' to come, and proper procedures can be arranged.","Is it not illegal? The entire process deliberately avoids foreign oversight—it's clearly exploiting a loophole.","\"Miss Liu, can I ask you a question?\"","\"Go ahead.\"","\"Why me? With your resources and connections, you could easily find a much larger and more capable company to do this.\"","\"Because I don't trust anyone else.\"","\"Something like this requires absolute trust, and with your background and profile, I'm completely at ease.\"","There was no way around it—bringing in talent with access to cutting-edge process technology and core lithography machine secrets through normal channels was nearly impossible. Even the people she'd recruited through Jace and through Zeng Jin hadn't reached the core circle. The powers that be were guarding against China with every means available. If she went for an open, blatant poaching approach, the likely outcomes were sanctions—or worse, the people involved ending up behind bars. The risk was substantial.","So she felt it was worth trying to create another secret channel—run people in under the radar, give them new identities, and have them work in a secret lab to speed up the domestication of lithography machines.","Of course, she was only testing the waters. Whether it would work remained uncertain.","The real topic of today's meeting was actually about the overseas subsidiary of Wanlong Group and the personal security arrangements for its senior executives abroad—which required in-depth cooperation with Wei Xiao.","After all, the overseas market was important too. There would be dangers there as well, and a certain level of personal protection had to be arranged.","Wei Xiao didn't agonize over it. He simply extended his hand: \"Pleasure doing business.\"","Liu Yutong extended hers: \"Pleasure doing business.\"","After Wei Xiao left, Liu Yutong had just finished handling the last bits of company business and was about to head back to school when her phone rang.","It was an unknown number from BS Province.","She hesitated for a second, then picked up.","\"Hello, is this Chairman Liu Yutong?\" A middle-aged man's voice came through the line.","\"This is she. Who am I speaking with?\"","\"Chairman Liu, hello. This is the General Office of the BS Provincial Party Committee. My surname is Zheng.\"","Liu Yutong was slightly taken aback.","The General Office of BS Province.","Uncle Zhu's secretary?","\"Director Zheng, hello. Is there something I can help with?\"","Director Zheng said over the phone, \"Chairman Liu, the leadership would like to invite you to BS Province for a visit, to take a look at our investment environment. The leadership mentioned that if it's convenient for you, the province can arrange a private plane to pick you up.\"","Liu Yutong felt a swell of emotion at those words.","A private plane to pick her up—that was a high honor indeed.","Though she understood. In previous phone calls, Uncle Zhu had subtly hinted that he hoped she could bring more investment his way. Right now, apart from Wanlong Plaza and supermarket operations, her other business ventures hadn't expanded into the region.","She wondered what Uncle Zhu hoped she'd invest in this time.","Tourism development? Or some kind of specialty agriculture?","Whatever it was, she had to go.","\"Director Zheng, no need for the private plane. I'll make my own travel arrangements. Just give me the dates, and I'll figure out my schedule.\"","Director Zheng quickly said, \"The dates are entirely up to you. The leadership said to work around your convenience.\"","Liu Yutong thought it over, then said, \"Let's go with next Tuesday. I'll arrive in BS Province next Tuesday, and I'll get in touch with you then.\"","\"Excellent, excellent. Then on behalf of the leadership, let me thank you in advance, Chairman Liu. See you then.\"","\"Okay, good-bye.\"","After hanging up, Liu Yutong leaned back in her chair and thought about the last time she'd been in BS Province.","Back then, she was a freshman, organizing sports events with the teachers and students there. When the earthquake came, she'd immediately donated two billion through the Wanlong Charity Foundation, and later added another two hundred million of her own. More than a year had passed since then, and she hadn't been back to BS Province yet. This visit—disguised as an assessment trip—would let her check on the state of the regional branches and the construction of the schools she'd donated to.","And those lovely students.","With that thought, she pressed the intercom and called for Lan Die.","\"Help me make arrangements. Next Tuesday I'm heading to BS Province, and the trip will last about three to five days.\"","\"Understood. I'll arrange everything right away.\"","\"By the way, help me prepare some gifts—some for the teachers and some for the children. As for the quantity... hmm... let's start with ten thousand sets.\"","\"Understood.\"","After arranging the itinerary, Liu Yutong finally left the office and returned to the school. But no sooner had she arrived at the dormitory than she was dragged out by Li Xiaohui."]},{"number":821,"title":"Chapter 821: 822, Birthday Surprise","paragraphs":["\"Sister Yutong, get down here! Get down here! Something huge is happening!\"","Liu Yutong had just arrived at the dorm and hadn't even put her backpack down when Li Xiaohui burst through the door, shouting urgently at her.","Liu Yutong was caught off guard by her energy: \"What's wrong? Why are you in such a panic?\"","\"Don't tell me someone's picking a fight on campus?\"","That would take some serious nerve.","\"Oh no, it's not that! Stop asking—just come with me, that's all you need to do.\" Li Xiaohui grabbed Liu Yutong by the wrist and dragged her out the door.","Liu Yutong stumbled forward, one of her shoes nearly flying off her foot: \"Little Hui, slow down! What is going on?\"","\"You'll see when we get there! Hee hee hee...\"","Li Xiaohui let out a weird little giggle, casually wiped the corner of her mouth, and pulled Liu Yutong toward the stairwell, sprinting all the way.","A few classmates in the hallway, holding books, saw the scene. They froze for a second, then, as if remembering something all at once, tossed their books back in the dorm and chased after them.","Liu Yutong had a vague feeling something was off, but she couldn't for the life of her figure out what Li Xiaohui was up to.","The two ran out of the dormitory building, crossed the main road lined with plane trees, and headed straight for the sports ground.","Along the way, Liu Yutong noticed something very strange: the campus was too quiet.","Sure, it was the weekend, but usually there would still be plenty of people around at this hour. Yet she hadn't seen a single soul the entire way. It was bizarre.","\"Little Hui, slow down! What's going on?\"","\"Shh~ We're here!\"","Li Xiaohui stopped abruptly, pointing ahead with the proud look of someone showing off a treasure.","\"Ta-da! Take a look!\"","Liu Yutong stepped forward a few paces, glanced down at the sports ground below, and froze.","The field was packed with people—a sea of heads as far as the eye could see.","This wasn't just a few hundred people. There were at least a few thousand, maybe more.","Freshmen, sophomores, juniors, and a scattering of seniors had all shown up at the school, and even the teachers were out there on the field.","And every single one of them was holding something in their hands.","The moment Liu Yutong appeared—","A blinding spotlight suddenly blasted from the platform on the far side of the field, engulfing her entirely in its beam.","At the same time.","The students, as if receiving a signal, all lit up whatever they were holding at once—they were glow sticks.","Thousands of glow sticks were ignited in nearly the same instant.","Red, yellow, green, blue, purple... a dazzling array of colors burst to life, transforming the entire sports ground into a shimmering, rippling sea of stars.","Then, all at once, the crowd shouted in unison, their voices thunderously loud.","\"Liu Yutong! Happy birthday!!!\"","Nearly ten thousand voices converged into one, enough to make your scalp tingle from the vibrations.","Liu Yutong stood frozen in place, not knowing what to say or how to express the storm of emotions inside her. It felt like sand had gotten in her eyes.","She'd never really celebrated her birthday growing up.","She'd never let anyone celebrate it for her either.","She'd grown used to that.","But today...","\"Hee hee hee... Sister Yutong, surprise? Excited?\" Li Xiaohui hopped out from beside her, holding up a giant purple glow board that she'd somehow conjured out of nowhere. Written on it in neon marker were the words: [The best Sister Yutong in the world, happy birthday!]","Below that, she'd drawn a crooked little smiley face.","\"Little Hui, what have you all...\" Liu Yutong's voice caught slightly, and she found herself at a loss for words.","\"Don't be mad, Sister Yutong. I know you don't like celebrating your birthday, but we all really wanted to do this for you. Truly.\"","\"Don't worry—I cleared it with the principal in advance. He said have fun, just try not to tear down the school.\"","Liu Yutong was speechless at that.","The principal really was... so open-minded there was nothing left to say.","\"And there's more, more!\"","Li Xiaohui spun around and pulled out a megaphone straight out of the movies, aiming it at the crowd.","\"Begin!\"","The moment she said it, the students gathered in the middle of the field moved back in perfect sync, clearing an open space.","A temporary stage was revealed, already set up with a drum kit, guitars, keyboards, bass... every kind of instrument you could name.","Before long, members of the school's music club walked up to the center and started playing.","They played the happy birthday song, but the arrangement had been reworked to a much livelier tempo.","Nearly ten thousand students immediately started waving their glow sticks to the rhythm, singing along.","\"Happy birthday to you~ Happy birthday to you~\"","Li Xiaohui pulled Liu Yutong to the very middle of the field, and the students formed a circle around her, like stars orbiting the moon.","\"Sister Yutong, don't just stand there!\"","Li Xiaohui had somehow managed to appear again, still holding that giant purple board in front of her, shaking it right in Yutong's face: \"This is just the beginning—the real surprise hasn't come yet!\"","She then grabbed a walkie-talkie, pushed the button, and called out: \"Let's go.\"","From the open area at the east side of the field came a deep, rumbling boom.","BANG!","Everyone, as if on cue, lifted their heads and looked at the night sky.","A golden trail of light shot up into the air, dragging a long fiery tail behind it, and exploded high above with a thunderous crack—blossoming into an enormous golden peony. Layer upon layer of petals unfurled slowly outward, painting half the sky in radiant gold.","\"Fireworks! They're fireworks!\"","\"Oh my god! That's gorgeous!\"","\"Look, look, here comes another one!\"","\"...\"","Then came the second volley, the third, the fourth... countless fireworks rose simultaneously from all four corners of the campus—reds, golds, purples—illuminating the entire sky.","Among them, dozens of golden fireworks formed the dragon emblem of the Wanlong Society, and it was nothing short of breathtaking.","Not long after the emblem faded, over a hundred more fireworks shot into the sky at once, exploding at the highest point to form a huge line of text—【Happy Birthday to The Young Lady!】","Those words hung in the night sky for a good ten-plus seconds before slowly dissolving.","The whole city of Mingzhu was shaken.","On the streets outside campus, passersby stopped in their tracks, all craning their necks to stare at the sky lit up by fireworks—a sight beyond words.","\"No way, what's going on? So many fireworks!\"","\"Incredible! How much did this cost?\"","\"I've never seen fireworks this amazing in my entire life.\"","\"Same here. This makes New Year's look like a joke!\"","\"Ridiculous amounts of money!\"","\"Look, there are even words in the sky—someone's birthday?\"","\"Rumor has it it's the Young Lady of the Wanlong Society.\"","\"Now that's impressive.\"","\"...\"","The firework show lasted close to a full hour before it finally wound down.","As Liu Yutong was still savoring the moment, she heard a soft, sweet little voice by her ear.","\"Big sis! Big sis!\"","Through the crowd came her grandpa and grandma, holding a little round-faced bundle of cuteness in their arms, walking straight toward her.","Yaya was wearing a snow-white little princess dress today, with two round little buns on her head tied with pink hair ties, looking just like a doll that had stepped right out of a fairy tale book.","Her two little hands were also holding a bouquet of fresh flowers.","“Sister! Happy birthday!”","Liu Yutong bent down to take the flowers and gave Yaya a kiss on the forehead: “Thank you, Yaya.”","“Sweetheart, happy birthday!” Grandpa and Grandma also smiled and offered their birthday wishes.","“Thank you, Grandpa and Grandma!”","Just then, the principal also walked over with a cheerful chuckle.","This principal, who was always stern on a daily basis, had surprisingly worn a bright red traditional Chinese Tang suit today, looking all jolly and full of good cheer.","“Principal, how come you’re here too?” Liu Yutong said with a smile while holding the flowers, greeting him.","Principal: “Liu Yutong, today is your birthday. How could I, as your principal, not come?”","With that, he pulled out a document from behind him and handed it to Liu Yutong.","“What is this?”","“Take a look and you’ll see.”","Liu Yutong opened the document, and after reading the words on it, she froze.","[After deliberation by the university party committee, it has been decided to grant Liu Yutong the honorary title of ‘Distinguished Alumna’ and to appoint her as an Honorary Professor of the University of Finance and Economics.]","“Principal, I haven’t even graduated yet. Isn’t this inappropriate?”","“Oh, it’s perfectly appropriate.”","“Do you have any idea how much pressure you, a current student, are putting on your fellow classmates? Plenty of them feel utterly hopeless after seeing your resume.” The principal made a little joke.","“I figured I might as well give you a promotion. Anyway, being an Honorary Professor is just an honorary title—you don’t need to come to class every day. It’s enough if you can occasionally come back to campus when you have some free time and share your experiences with the younger students.”","Liu Yutong closed the document and nodded: “Thank you, Principal.”","The principal laughed heartily: “What’s there to thank me for? I’m honored that our school could have such an outstanding alumna as you.”","With that, he stepped aside and waved to the crowd: “Students, what are you waiting for? Bring out the cake and let’s get this party going!”","Liu Yutong: “.....”","She never expected the principal to be this... festive too.","Very soon, one cart after another was slowly wheeled out.","On every cart sat a giant eight-tier cake, each tier a different color and flavor, with a specially made firework candle on top, crackling and sparking away.","And on the side of every cake, different blessing messages were written in cream.","It looked like the school had really spared no expense this time.","From organizing the students to make such a huge fuss, to the singing and the cakes—and the fireworks were clearly arranged by the Yunchéng people.","Under everyone’s gaze, Liu Yutong closed her eyes, made a wish, and blew out the candles.","Then she took the microphone, looked at everyone present, and expressed her gratitude.","“Thank you all for your wishes!”","“To thank you all for celebrating my birthday so grandly, I announce that all your expenses tonight are on me!”","“Everyone, eat your fill and have a great time!!!”","“Ah!!!!”","“Yutong, you’re awesome!!!” A wave of cheers soared into the sky."]},{"number":822,"title":"Chapter 822: 823, Heading to BS Province.","paragraphs":["Two days later.","A civilian airliner took off from Danancheng Airport, heading southwest.","Liu Yutong sat in business class, gazing at the clouds outside the window, when a thought suddenly crossed her mind—maybe she should buy a few private jets.","With the group's business expanding rapidly, she and some senior executives needed to travel frequently across the country and even around the world. Taking commercial flights was becoming increasingly inconvenient and time-consuming.","If she could get a few planes, that would make things much easier.","\"Miss, the reception plan from BS Province has arrived.\"","\"Read it.\"","\"Tomorrow at 9 a.m., Leader Zhu will meet with you at the provincial party committee guesthouse, followed by a lunch meeting. In the afternoon, there will be a visit to the post-disaster reconstruction demonstration projects, including the school funded by Wanlong Group. The morning after tomorrow is an investment symposium, attended by heads of the BS Province Investment Promotion Bureau, Development and Reform Commission, and Science and Technology Department. After that, your schedule is free—if there's anywhere you'd like to go, they can arrange it in advance.\"","\"For the afternoon of the day after tomorrow, no need to bother them. I'll just wander around on my own.\"","\"Understood.\"","Liu Yutong suddenly thought of something and turned around to ask: \"For the employees' family members, which batch is departing for BS Province today?\"","Lan Die quickly checked the records and looked up: \"The fifth batch, just left this morning—24 buses, over 800 people.\"","\"How have the earlier batches been received?\"","\"Very well.\"","\"Many parents of employees from the first travel group have personally called the company to express their gratitude, and some have even sent banners.\"","Liu Yutong nodded.","From July until now, the employee family travel plan of Wanlong Group had been in operation for over two months.","Based on the health conditions and personal preferences of employees' parents, the travel routes were divided into several options—the Imperial Capital Culture Route, Jiangnan Water Town Route, Southern Guangdong Coastal Route, Southwest Scenic Route, Northern Frontier Grassland Route, and the BS Province Post-Disaster Reconstruction Route.","Each batch was capped at no more than two thousand people, accompanied by professional tour guides, on-site medical staff, and security personnel, with all arrangements for food, lodging, and transport fully covered.","As for employees' children, since their numbers were relatively smaller, all summer camp activities had already been completed.","Especially that Chu Junlin—he led a children's group for the entire summer, and by the time it ended, he looked several years older.","After all, looking after kids, and so many of them—the mental toll was unimaginable.","When he finally returned to Mingzhu City for the last time and saw Liu Yutong, he didn't say a word, silently getting into his car and heading back to the capital.","To date, the group had sent over 100,000 employees' family members on trips, with total spending exceeding 400 million yuan.","Was the money worth it?","From a financial standpoint, certainly not.","Many listed companies couldn't even earn that much in a full year.","But from the perspective of winning people's hearts, it was worth every penny.","Ordinary employees were noticeably more motivated than before, and everyone spoke of the company with genuine pride.","When the company treated their families so well, how could they not want to stay loyal to Wanlong Group and give it their all?","This was the principle of buying a horse's bones with gold.","And it was also Liu Yutong's consistent style—if she did something, she did it to the fullest.","The plane broke through the clouds and began its slow descent.","Liu Yutong looked down through the window, and a stretch of rolling mountains came into view.","The mountains were tall and steep, ridgeline after ridgeline in blue-gray, their peaks shrouded in white mist. Winding rivers and scattered villages nestled between the slopes, like silver coins casually tossed across the earth.","This was BS Province.","A land of frequent calamities, yet one that refused to break.","Last year's massive earthquake claimed thousands of lives, destroyed countless families, and left this region scarred and devastated.","The images of crumbling ruins on the nightly news still made her chest tighten when she thought of them.","But barely a year had passed, and the scene had transformed—rows of new buildings had risen from the ground, roads had been rebuilt.","A completely new face!","The plane landed at the capital airport of BS Province.","As the cabin door opened, a cool, fresh breeze rushed in.","Located in the southwest, BS Province sat at a much higher elevation than Mingzhu City. Though it was only early September, temperatures had already dropped to around twenty degrees—far more pleasant than the weather back home.","At the bottom of the gangway, a black Audi was already waiting.","Standing beside the car were two people—one was Director Zheng, whom Liu Yutong had spoken with on the phone before.","The other was Uncle Zhu himself.","Seeing him, Liu Yutong was taken aback for a moment.","She hadn't expected Uncle Zhu to come to the airport in person to pick her up.","\"Uncle Zhu, why did you come all the way yourself?\" She extended her hand, a little flattered.","Uncle Zhu smiled and shook her hand: \"Little Liu, you are the great benefactor of BS Province. You donated over two billion yuan to help us rebuild our homes. If I, as the head of this province, didn't even come to the airport to welcome you, that would be a grave breach of etiquette.\"","Liu Yutong: \"Uncle Zhu, you're too kind. I only did what I could.\"","Uncle Zhu: \"Regardless, the people of BS Province will always remember this kindness.\"","The two exchanged pleasantries and then got into the car one after the other, heading toward the city.","..."]},{"number":823,"title":"Chapter 823: 824, Target Acquired: Wanlong Aerospace.","paragraphs":["After leaving the airport, the vehicles drove along a newly paved asphalt road toward the city center.","Liu Yutong looked out the window at the rapidly changing scenery and couldn't help speaking up.","\"It's changed a lot.\"","\"Yes, it has.\"","Uncle Zhu echoed with emotion: \"The development of J City is changing with each passing day. Look, new houses, new schools, new hospitals—they're all being built. The future will only get better.\"","\"Mm, I think so too.\" Liu Yutong nodded.","Uncle Zhu shifted the topic and probed gently: \"Girl, I heard you've been working on something big lately?\"","Liu Yutong was slightly taken aback: \"What is Uncle Zhu referring to?\"","\"Wanlong Aerospace Technology.\"","Uncle Zhu looked at her meaningfully: \"The launch vehicle manufacturing license and satellite frequency band usage rights you secured in the capital—quite a few people know about this by now. A twenty-year-old girl, building rockets, launching satellites—they all say you're crazy.\"","Liu Yutong smiled: \"And what does Uncle Zhu think?\"","\"I don't think you look crazy.\"","Uncle Zhu let out a hearty laugh and said: \"You've been in BS Province before, so you should know the situation here. Although BS Province is located in the southwest and its economy can't compare with the coastal regions, we still have unique advantages in certain areas.\"","\"You mean... aerospace?\"","\"Exactly.\"","Uncle Zhu nodded: \"Our province has an aerospace industry foundation left over from the Third Front construction period. Not to mention the XC Satellite Launch Center, we also have several national-level aviation engine research institutes and special materials laboratories.","Over the years, the province has been thinking about how to revitalize these resources and make the aerospace industry a new calling card for BS Province. But your Uncle Zhu here comes from an administrative background—I'm not well-versed in business operations, and I've never found the right entry point.\"","\"Then I heard you were getting into aerospace, and I knew—the opportunity had arrived.\"","Liu Yutong finally understood.","Uncle Zhu's real purpose in inviting her to BS Province for this inspection wasn't tourism development or specialty agriculture.","It was aerospace.","He wanted Wanlong Aerospace to set down roots in BS Province and turn it into China's commercial aerospace industry base.","This idea, she had to admit, was remarkably forward-thinking.","BS Province did indeed have unique advantages.","First, the XC Satellite Launch Center was located within BS Province—one of China's three major aerospace launch sites, handling a large number of commercial satellite launch missions.","If Wanlong Aerospace's rockets were launched here, it could indeed save considerable costs.","Second, BS Province had a complete aerospace industry chain left from the Third Front period.","From special materials to precision machining, from engine testing to ground tracking and control, there were ready-made enterprises and talent reserves. Although most of these resources were state-owned, through mixed-ownership reform and industrial cooperation, they could provide strong support for commercial aerospace.","Third, labor costs and land costs in BS Province were far lower than in the coastal regions, which was a considerable advantage for a company like Wanlong Aerospace that needed large numbers of engineers and technical workers.","\"Uncle Zhu, what exactly do you want me to do?\"","\"I want you to put Wanlong Aerospace's core R&D and manufacturing base here in BS Province. At the very least, set up one of them here.\"","\"Girl, if you're willing to place Wanlong Aerospace's R&D and production base in BS Province, the province can give you the most favorable policies—land, taxes, talent recruitment, research support—as long as it's within policy limits, I can give you the green light.\"","\"For example, in terms of land, you can pick any site you like. The province will handle acquisition and leveling, and waive land use fees for five years. For taxes, full corporate income tax exemption for the first five years, and half exemption for the following five. For talent recruitment, the province will handle household registration, children's schooling, and spousal employment for any experts you bring in from outside, plus additional relocation allowances. For research support, the province's aerospace-related research institutes can open up to you—joint R&D, shared results.\"","Liu Yutong listened and began calculating in her mind.","Uncle Zhu's conditions were indeed very generous.","If all these policies were actually delivered, Wanlong Aerospace's upfront costs for landing in BS Province could be reduced by at least thirty percent.","Most importantly, there were those research support resources.","The aerospace research institutes left over from the Third Front period should be hiding many treasures.","Special welding techniques, ultra-precision machining technology, composite material forming processes... If they had to develop these technologies from scratch, it would take eight to ten years at minimum.","But if they could be shared through joint R&D, Wanlong Aerospace's rate of technological accumulation could at least be boosted by one to two times.","\"Uncle Zhu, I need time to consider.\" Liu Yutong didn't agree on the spot.","The conditions were tempting, but business decisions couldn't be made on impulse alone.","Wanlong Aerospace's headquarters were already set in the capital, and its R&D center was already established on the outskirts of the capital. Placing the production base in BS Province would mean a dispersed layout, increasing management and communication costs.","Besides, she also needed to consult Professor Zhou Yingpei.","The old professor was the chief technical officer, and the selection of a production base site involved numerous technical issues—she had to hear his thoughts.","\"No rush—take your time thinking it over.\"","Uncle Zhu smiled: \"If you have free time these days, feel free to look around the province, see the changes here and the industrial foundation we have. Once you have a clear picture, we can talk in more detail.\"","\"Alright.\"","Half an hour later, the convoy arrived at the SW Guesthouse.","It was a small building tucked amid green trees, unremarkable on the outside but elegantly decorated on the inside.","Liu Yutong was assigned the best suite on the third floor. Opening the window, she could see the distant green mountains—a view that lifted the spirits.","Uncle Zhu chatted with her for a while and then left due to other commitments.","After all, tomorrow was the official inspection; today she was still free to do as she pleased.","After spending some time at the guesthouse, Liu Yutong changed into a more casual outfit and went out directly.","While the daylight was still good, she figured she'd take a stroll around the city.","Actually, Liu Yutong knew this city very well, because in her previous life, she had attended university here.","Back then, she hadn't been reborn yet—she was just an ordinary college student.","After several years of hard work, she finally obtained her lawyer's license and joined a fairly large law firm in J City, where she was overworked and spent years as a trainee.","After that, she was reborn.","In this life, she chose to stay in her hometown of Pearl City, chose the University of Finance and Economics, and chose a different path.","But J City remained the most special place in her memory.","Here lay her previous life's youth, dreams, and the traces of her struggles.","After driving around the city for a while, Liu Yutong brought Yun Cheng and the others to an old street called Qintai.","This old street was a famous historical and cultural district in J City, lined with shops in antique architectural style—selling calligraphy and paintings, Shu brocade, silverware, bamboo crafts, and other handicrafts, along with quite a few snack stalls and tea houses.","Every day, a steady stream of tourists comes to visit, making the place lively and bustling.","She remembered that in her previous life, during her college years, she often came here with her roommates to stroll around.","They didn't come to buy anything—it was simply for the love of the neighborhood's lively, homey atmosphere.","After walking for a while, the three of them arrived at a teahouse.","A few bamboo tables and chairs were set up outside the teahouse's entrance. Liu Yutong and her companions ordered three bowls of covered-bowl tea and sat down on the bamboo chairs by the street, slowly sipping their drinks.","The tea was ordinary jasmine tea, a few yuan a bowl, but it tasted wonderful—the floral fragrance was rich and fragrant.","The teahouse owner was an old man in his sixties, wearing a blue button-front jacket. He sat on a bamboo chair by the door, a purple clay teapot in his hand, squinting in the sun like he was truly enjoying life.","Not far from them, at another table, some people were playing mahjong, the shuffling of tiles making a crisp clattering sound.","\"Peng! Bastard! That's the tile I've been waiting for!\"","\"Hahaha, Old Li, you've dealt into the pot again. How many times is that today?\"","\"Bullshit! That was strategic defense. You lot don't know a thing!\"","\"...\"","Liu Yutong listened to the familiar Sichuan-Chongqing dialect and a smile crept onto her lips.","This feeling was just wonderful."]},{"number":824,"title":"Chapter 824: 825. An Acquaintance from a Previous Life.","paragraphs":["After finishing their tea, Liu Yutong took Yun Cheng and the others for a stroll through the streets. She also planned to pick up a few small trinkets to bring back as gifts for Yaya.","As she stepped into a silver jewelry shop to browse the ornaments, a burst of heated arguing suddenly erupted from up ahead.","\"You people are trying to rip me off! This bracelet snapped on its own—why should I have to pay for it?!\"","\"Little miss, don't talk like that. The bracelet was sitting just fine on the counter, and the moment you put it on, it broke. If you didn't break it, who did? According to our store's rules, anyone who damages merchandise must pay double!\"","\"This is a scam! I'm calling the police!\"","\"...\"","Liu Yutong followed the sound with her eyes.","At the entrance of a handicraft shop across the street, a crowd of onlookers had gathered in a circle.","In the middle of the crowd, a girl in her early twenties was arguing with the shopkeeper, her face flushed red.","The girl had straight bangs, delicate features, and wore a pair of black-framed glasses. She was dressed in a T-shirt bearing the name of some university.","Standing opposite her was a man with a sharp, weasel-like face—the shopkeeper himself. Behind him loomed two young punks with dyed yellow hair, cigarettes dangling from their lips, looking smug and shiftless.","\"Oh, you're going to call the cops? Go ahead and call 'em! Even the police would side with me on this one!\"","The sharp-faced shopkeeper was emboldened: \"You break it, you pay for it—it's only fair! That's the rule anywhere you go. You damaged my merchandise, so pay up!\"","\"I... I just tried it on, and it broke by itself. Clearly, your product is defective.\"","\"Enough of your nonsense! Whether it's defective or not, if you break it, you pay! And look around—my store has a sign right up there that says intentional damage requires double compensation. This bracelet sells for two thousand five, so double is five thousand. Hand over the money!\"","\"You... that's completely illegal! According to regulations, businesses can't use terms, notices, declarations, or in-store signage to add extra burdens on consumers. Even if I compensate you, I only owe the cost price, not double the retail price. You're literally trying to extort me!\"","\"Oh, the little miss knows her law, huh? Fancy that, quoting regulations at me.\"","\"Boys, what do you think we should do with her?\" the sharp-faced shopkeeper said, shooting a glance at the yellow-haired punks behind him.","The two thugs immediately stubbed out their cigarettes and advanced on the girl with hostile expressions.","\"You... what are you trying to do? I'm telling you, this is a society ruled by law, don't you dare do anything rash!\" The girl stepped back in fright.","Then, as if trying to muster her courage, she raised the books she was holding: \"I'm warning you, I'm a law student at BS University. What you're doing is illegal!\"","\"A law student? Hahaha...\"","The sharp-faced man burst out laughing: \"Little miss, you've been watching too many TV dramas. You think quoting some laws will scare us? I'll tell you, your laws mean nothing here. In this shop, I am the law! Pay up quietly, and we'll call it a day. Refuse to pay... and don't even think about walking away!\"","In the crowd, the murmurings began.","\"Poor girl, that shop is notorious for scamming tourists and students.\"","\"Yeah, last time some out-of-towner got shaken down here and had to cough up three thousand before they let him leave.\"","\"The boss is supposedly connected to gangs. He's bold and ruthless—calling the police is useless. If you try, they'll come after you for revenge.\"","\"Really? That brazen?\"","\"You bet...\"","\"Ugh, she looks like just an ordinary student. How is she going to come up with that kind of money?\"","\"...\"","The girl bit her lip, holding back tears, and stubbornly retorted to the shopkeeper: \"I'll pay for the damage, but I won't pay a single cent more than what's fair. If you keep blocking my way, I really will call the police and shout for help!\"","\"Shout for help? Go ahead and shout! See if anyone dares to step in!\"","The sharp-faced man waved his hand, signaling his two thugs to move in.","The crowd on the sidelines kept growing, but no one stepped forward to speak up for the girl.","Considering the kind of thugs these were, the best anyone might do was call the police—no one wanted to court trouble.","Standing outside the crowd, Liu Yutong had been watching for a while. But when she got a clear look at the girl's face, she froze.","The girl looked familiar.","Not from this life.","From her past life.","She racked her brain for a long while before it came to her: Xu Yi.","Her university classmate from her previous life, a law student one year ahead of her. When Liu Yutong had first gotten into university in Jincheng, Xu Yi had been a volunteer at the freshman welcome, helping her carry luggage and walking her through registration. Later, they'd joined the debate club together. Their relationship wasn't particularly close, but they were definitely acquaintances.","To think they'd meet again in this life under such circumstances.","A law student, being extorted and cornered by a shady shopkeeper right on the street.","Liu Yutong couldn't help but shake her head.","This world—sometimes, knowing the law just isn't enough.","Like when you're dealing with these kinds of scum.","Without hesitation, she pushed through the crowd and stepped forward.","\"Hey, boss.\"","The sharp-faced shopkeeper instinctively turned around, only to see a stunning girl in a white shirt walking out from the crowd.","When he laid eyes on her, he froze for a moment, and then his eyes gradually lit up.","Damn, this girl is beautiful.","\"Well now, isn't this a pretty miss? Here shopping? Come on in! We've got everything you could want—guaranteed you'll love it.\"","Liu Yutong walked straight up to the girl and held out a hand: \"Let me take a look at that bracelet.\"","The girl was taken aback, then instinctively handed over the bracelet broken into two pieces.","Liu Yutong took it and examined it carefully, turning it over in her hands.","The red string was cheap acrylic. The beads were recycled plastic. The glue at the joints hadn't even been spread evenly.","This kind of thing cost a few yuan at the wholesale market, max.","\"This bracelet of yours—did you even pay more than ten yuan for it?\" Liu Yutong asked the shopkeeper after finishing her inspection.","\"What nonsense are you talking about?! That's our store's premium bracelet. No way the wholesale cost was under ten yuan!\"","\"But judging from the material, it doesn't look premium at all. Just looks like cheap plastic beads. How dare you hang a two-thousand-five price tag on something like this? Are you trying to scam your customers?\" Liu Yutong said.","The sharp-faced shopkeeper flew into a rage: \"So what if I am? So what if I'm not? You break something, you pay for it—that's the rule! I'm warning you, don't stick your nose where it doesn't belong, or you'll get what's coming to you too!\"","Liu Yutong smiled at his words: \"Alright, then let's play by your rules.\"","She tossed the bracelet back at him, walked over to the shop entrance, and reached up to pull down the wooden sign hanging on the door that read: [A Century-Old Establishment, Run with Integrity].","The sharp-faced shopkeeper's expression changed: \"What do you think you're doing! That's our shop's sign!\"","Liu Yutong ignored him. Turning to the crowd gathered around, she said: \"Excuse me, everyone. Please make some room.\"","Although the onlookers had no idea what she was about to do, they instinctively stepped back a few paces, clearing an open space.","Liu Yutong placed the wooden sign on the ground, then raised her foot.","CRACK!","With one stomp, the sign bearing the words 【Century-Old Shop】 snapped clean in two.","The entire crowd fell silent in an instant.","The sharp-faced shop owner froze for several seconds before snapping out of it, then erupted in fury: “You damn brat, you dare smash my sign!”","“So I smashed it. What about it?”","Liu Yutong glanced down at the broken wooden board and put on a look of feigned innocence: “Oh dear, how did it just break like that?”","“Boss, what shoddy material is this sign of yours made of? It broke way too easily.”","The sharp-faced owner’s face turned green with rage: “What material I used is none of your business! Now that you’ve smashed my sign, how are you going to settle this?”","“If you don’t give me a proper explanation today, you’re not leaving this place!”","“I’ll definitely give you an explanation. Damaged goods must be compensated—that’s the rule, right?” Liu Yutong asked.","The sharp-faced owner nodded: “That’s right!”","Liu Yutong pointed again at the two broken pieces of wood on the ground and said: “Since your sign says ‘Century-Old Shop,’ that must make it an antique, right? It must be worth a lot, right? Well, I won’t ask for too much. Let’s just go by the price of your bracelet here, times ten. I’ll count this sign as twenty-five thousand, and double compensation means fifty thousand.”","After doing the math, she held out her hand: “Boss, pay up.”","Sharp-faced owner: “???”","Wait, did I hear that right?","You broke my sign, and now YOU want ME to pay?","And you expect fifty thousand?","Why don’t you just rob a bank?!","The two blond punks were stunned too—they’d never seen such an arrogant girl. They said to the shop owner, “Boss, she’s messing with you!”","“No kidding! You think I can’t see that?!”","The sharp-faced owner’s face darkened as he glared at Liu Yutong: “Little girl, looks like you really came here to pick a fight. If I don’t teach you a lesson today, you won’t know who runs this street!”","“Get her!”","The two blond punks immediately grinned, cracked their knuckles, and lunged at Liu Yutong.","Then... Yun Cheng and Lan Die suddenly appeared right in front of them.","The next second, all three men fell neatly onto their knees, clutching their heads and wailing.","“Wahhh...”","“You... you people... assaulting others in broad daylight like this—is there no law anymore?!”"]},{"number":825,"title":"Chapter 825: 826, Going to School. (Thanks to the half-baked literary master for the big spa treatment)","paragraphs":["\"Wrong! Wrong! Ma'am, we're really wrong!\"","\"Please, have mercy, let us go!\"","The sharp-mouthed shopkeeper and the two thugs with dyed yellow hair had long lost their earlier arrogance. They were all kowtowing and begging for mercy.","Liu Yutong walked over to the shopkeeper and looked down at him from above.","\"Boss, you said it yourself earlier — damaged goods must be compensated at double the price. What, are you backing out now?\"","The sharp-mouthed shopkeeper felt deeply wronged inside: If you keep this up, I'll really call the cops!","You smashed my sign and still want me to pay up — is there any justice in this world?","Has everyone lost their sense of right and wrong?!","\"No, no, no! I was just joking, just joking, ma'am. That bracelet really isn't worth anything — it's a cheap street-stall trinket, three for ten bucks. No need to compensate, really!\"","\"That won't do.\"","\"Rules are rules. You can't just change them on a whim.\"","Liu Yutong bent down, picked up the bracelet — now snapped into two pieces — and dangled it in front of the bald shopkeeper's eyes.","\"Tell you what, I won't make things hard for you.\"","\"This bracelet — since you sold it for twenty-five hundred, double the compensation for damage would be five thousand. I'll pay you that.\"","\"But...\"","She pointed at the sign that was broken in half: \"This sign is worth far more than your bracelet. At ten times the value, that's twenty-five thousand. Damaged, double the compensation — that's fifty thousand.\"","\"Fifty thousand minus five thousand — you still owe me forty-five thousand.\"","\"I didn't get the math wrong, did I?\"","The sharp-mouthed shopkeeper: \"...\"","How was he supposed to answer that?","Liu Yutong tossed the bracelet at him and held out her hand again. \"Pay up.\"","The bald shopkeeper was on the verge of tears. \"I... I don't have that much money, ma'am.\"","\"Really?\"","\"Really!\"","Liu Yutong took a step back and glanced at Yun Cheng behind her. \"Yun Cheng.\"","\"Here.\" Yun Cheng rolled up his sleeves, expressionless.","The bald shopkeeper's face changed dramatically, and he quickly begged for mercy again: \"I'm sorry! I'm really sorry! Ma'am! Granny! Please, have mercy, let me off the hook — I won't dare do it again! Never again!\"","There was no pity in Liu Yutong's eyes. \"When you were bullying her just now, why didn't you say, 'Let her off the hook'?\"","\"Besides, how many people you've swindled on this street — you know that better than anyone. Running into me today is just your bad luck.\"","The bald shopkeeper opened his mouth but could say nothing.","Liu Yutong gave Yun Cheng another order: \"Call some people over to keep these three under control. Gather up all the fake-goods purchase receipts from their shop, and deal with it as it should be dealt with.\"","\"Yes.\" Yun Cheng immediately made a call to summon backup.","After handing off the matter, Liu Yutong finally came over to Xu Yi.","\"You alright?\"","The senior schoolmate from her previous life hadn't cried when she was surrounded by those men, but now being asked this by Liu Yutong, she felt her nose sting.","She quickly sniffled and thanked her repeatedly.","\"Thank you! Thank you so much!\"","\"My name is Xu Yi. I'm a law student at BS University. What's yours?\"","\"Liu Yutong. HS Province, Finance University.\"","\"Miss Liu, thank you so much! If it weren't for you just now, I really don't know what I would have done.\"","Xu Yi bowed again. \"I... let me treat you both to a meal!\"","Liu Yutong nodded and accepted right away. \"Sure!\"","\"But I'd like to eat at your school cafeteria.\"","Xu Yi was taken aback, clearly not expecting that request, but then smiled. \"Alright, then I'll take you to the campus. Our cafeteria's dan dan noodles are known to be amazing.\"","\"Let's go!\"","The group quickly made their way to two black Mercedes parked by the roadside.","Xu Yi looked at the two black cars without much surprise — she had already guessed that this Miss Liu was probably some wealthy heiress.","After all, she was out with two bodyguards, so riding in Mercedes made perfect sense.","Soon, they arrived by car at the university gate.","The main entrance of BS University was an ancient gray stone archway, its lintel carved with bold, powerful characters said to have been personally inscribed by a historical figure.","Xu Yi led Liu Yutong through the archway and down the straight ginkgo avenue, entering the campus.","Lined along both sides of the road were many old, aged teaching buildings — gray bricks, dark tiles, their walls covered in thick ivy, a lush expanse of green against the dark red window frames, giving off a sense of history.","\"Our school has a long history. It traces back to a school founded before the founding of the nation. Through several mergers, it became what is now BS University.\" Xu Yi introduced as they walked, a note of pride in her voice.","Liu Yutong nodded. As she saw those familiar buildings, a trace of nostalgia surfaced in her eyes.","She knew this place all too well.","In her previous life, she had spent four full years here.","During autumn and winter, the ginkgo avenue would turn into a golden tunnel, breathtakingly beautiful — so many people from outside the campus would come specifically to take photos.","That intersection ahead, turning left, led to the library, where she once pulled all-nighters studying for the bar exam, dozing off at the desk when she was tired, then splashing water on her face and continuing to memorize legal provisions.","Further down was the cafeteria, where she loved the dan dan noodles.","About three yuan a bowl, the lady serving food recognized her and would always add an extra scoop of crushed peanuts.","And that red building for the law school — the debate club was on the third floor. She had once taken second place in the provincial intercollegiate debate tournament with her teammates there.","Later, after graduation, she had been reborn back into 2007.","And now, in this life, she had returned to her old alma mater in the most unexpected way.","\"Miss Liu? Miss Liu?\" Xu Yi noticed Liu Yutong was lost in thought and waved a hand in front of her face.","Liu Yutong snapped back to reality. \"What is it?\"","\"You zoned out just now. Did you think our school is too plain?\"","\"No, it's just... it feels familiar.\"","\"Familiar? Have you been to our school before?\"","\"Maybe I've been here in my dreams.\"","\"In your dreams? Really? Then maybe you've dreamed of me too.\"","\"Maybe I actually have.\"","\"Hahaha... Miss Liu, you sure know how to joke.\"","\"So, you're from Finance University — what's your major, by the way?\"","\"Business Administration.\"","\"Business Admin, huh. That's nice too.\"","The two chatted casually, until Xu Yi suddenly asked: \"You know, it's strange, Miss Liu — I feel like I've heard your name somewhere before. It feels so familiar, like we've met before. But I'm absolutely sure this is the first time we've seen each other.\"","\"Really?\"","\"Maybe you saw me in the news.\" Liu Yutong said casually.","\"News?\" Xu Yi was even more puzzled.","A college student at Finance University — how would they end up in the news?","But she didn't press further. She showed Liu Yutong and the others around the campus for a good while, and as the sky gradually darkened, she led them toward the cafeteria.","\"Come on, dinner's on me!\"","BS University had several cafeterias, and the one they came to was the largest on campus.","Xu Yi led them up to the second floor and found a seat by the window. \"What do you two want to eat? I'll go buy it.\"","\"Anything's fine—just get whatever you recommend,\" Liu Yutong said.","\"Okay, our cafeteria's dan dan noodles and brown sugar glutinous rice cakes are especially good, and the bon bon chicken is a must-try. I'll grab a few things; you guys sit and rest for a bit.\"","With that, Xu Yi got up and headed to the counter, and Yun Cheng followed along to help carry the trays.","Liu Yutong sat in her seat, her gaze sweeping across the students coming and going in the cafeteria. For a moment, she felt a strange sense of being out of sync with time.","Nothing had changed.","The longest line still stretched in front of the dan dan noodle window, the serving auntie's hand still shook with that familiar little tremor every now and then, the \"Clean Plate Campaign\" slogan still hung on the wall just as she remembered, and the old TV set in the corner was still broadcasting the evening news.","So many places, so many details—exactly as they had been in her past life's memory."]},{"number":826,"title":"Chapter 826: 827, Plague God Professor (Thanks to Half-Baked Literature Master for the Great God Certification)","paragraphs":["Not long after, Xu Yi and Yun Cheng returned carrying trays.","The trays held four steaming bowls of dan dan noodles, two portions of brown sugar glutinous rice cakes, two portions of boiled chicken skewers in chili oil, a few plates of refreshing side dishes, and four bottles of chilled soy milk.","“Come on, come on, eat while it's hot! Our cafeteria's dan dan noodles are famous for being delicious. Lots of alumni still come back just to eat them.”","Liu Yutong picked up her chopsticks and brought a strand of noodles to her mouth.","The familiar flavor burst across her palate—spicy, numbing, savory—exactly the same as she remembered.","“Is it good?” Xu Yi asked, looking at her expectantly.","Liu Yutong nodded. “Very good.”","Xu Yi let out a relieved breath and smiled, then gestured to Yun Cheng and Lan Die. “You two eat too, don't be shy. It may not compare to fancy restaurants, but our cafeteria food is pretty solid.”","Yun Cheng and Lan Die didn't stand on ceremony. They thanked them and picked up their chopsticks to dig in.","As time passed, the cafeteria gradually filled with more diners.","Just as they were finishing their meal,","suddenly, the sound of hurried footsteps came from the stairwell, drawing the attention of quite a few people.","A middle-aged man in his forties or fifties appeared on the second floor, and the faculty members eating nearby instantly fell into disarray, each one looking as if they were facing a crisis.","“Oh no! Old Xu is here! Eat fast!”","“Finish up and run! Don't hesitate!”","“...”","The middle-aged man had messy hair, as if it hadn't been washed in days, a face full of stubble, and a white dress shirt that was wrinkled and crumpled.","The moment he spotted the faculty members eating, his eyes lit up with a hungry gleam. Without a word, he charged straight at them.","Behind him followed a middle-aged woman of similar age, wearing black-rimmed glasses.","She jogged after him, calling out, “Old Xu, slow down! Wait for me!”","“Wait for what? If I wait any longer, there'll be no one left in the cafeteria!”","The middle-aged man shot back without turning his head, quickly locking onto a middle-aged professor who was eating. His eyes brightened, and he beelined toward the man.","The professor spotted him at the same time, jolted in alarm, and immediately grabbed his half-finished tray to make a run for it.","But he was a step too slow and got blocked.","“Professor Liu, why are you running before you've finished your meal? Can't you see the sign up there about not wasting food?”","“Professor Xu, why are you here again... Didn't I tell you to stop coming to me?” Professor Liu said awkwardly.","Damn it, this Xu Skinner is back again!","Professor Xu didn't care what the man thought. He pulled him back down into his seat without a word, then pulled out the materials he'd prepared and began pitching.","“Come on, don't rush off. Let me show you something good. This is my latest revised new-energy battery plan. For just five million, I can build the first-generation prototype!”","And then, without caring whether Professor Liu wanted to hear it, he flipped open the file and started talking a mile a minute.","“Look at this battery management system architecture. I've completely optimized the control algorithm. I estimate we can improve charge/discharge efficiency by at least ten percentage points! Ten percentage points—do you understand what that means? The same battery capacity will last longer, and the driving range can increase by at least dozens of kilometers!”","“And this motor controller plan—I've adopted a brand-new vector control strategy. Torque response speed is up twelve percent, and current harmonics are down twenty percent. Do you know what that means? It means the motor is more efficient, quieter, and lasts longer. These numbers would be top-tier on the international stage!”","“And this integrated thermal management system plan...”","Professor Liu got sprayed with a face full of saliva and leaned back in misery.","“Professor Xu, I really can't understand any of this. I'm a law professor, not an engineer. Isn't explaining this to me like playing music to a cow?”","“It doesn't matter if you don't understand. You just need to know this thing is impressive.”","A light burned in Professor Xu's eyes—something close to obsession. “Professor Liu, let me tell you, new energy is the big trend. In the future it's guaranteed to become a mainstream industry. Whoever masters the core technology first will dominate the entire supply chain! This plan of mine is at least five years ahead of everything currently on the market. Five years, do you understand?”","Professor Liu was on the verge of tears. “Professor Xu, I understand. I understand all of it... But I really don't have the money. I'm just a teacher. My monthly salary is modest, my mortgage isn't paid off yet, and my kids still need to go to school. Where am I supposed to get five million to invest in you?”","“No five million? Three million will do.”","“I don't have three million either.”","“What about one million?”","“Professor Xu, I really have to hand it to you...”","“Five hundred thousand! You must have five hundred thousand, right?”","“Even if five hundred thousand is a bit short, I can still build the core module first. Once I have a prototype, I can go to venture capital firms. Someone will definitely invest. As an angel investor, your return will be at least ten times your money!”","Professor Liu, backed into a corner, could only appeal to the middle-aged woman behind Professor Xu. “Professor Zhou, please talk some sense into Professor Xu. I really don't have any money.”","To his surprise, Professor Zhou pushed up her glasses and said with a perfectly straight face, “Old Liu, just give us a little investment. Consider it supporting scientific research.”","Professor Liu: “...”","He was truly done with this couple.","No wonder the old saying goes: birds of a feather flock together.","These two becoming husband and wife—there was clearly a reason for it.","“Professor Xu, Professor Zhou, I truly have no money. Please, just let me go.”","Professor Liu grabbed his tray and tried to flee.","Professor Xu was quick. He slapped a hand down on the tray to stop him.","“Professor Liu, don't rush. Let's keep talking. Even if you don't understand the technical details, you surely understand the value of research, don't you? You know me—I never lie. I promise you, if you invest, within five years... no! Within three years, I'll make sure you see a return!”","“I really have no money...”","“Then how much do you have? Do you have a hundred thousand?”","“No.”","“Fifty thousand?”","“No.”","“Ten thousand! You must have ten thousand, right?”","“Borrow ten thousand from me then. I'll write you an IOU, with interest calculated at the bank rate, and I absolutely won't renege.”","Professor Liu's face twisted into a painful grimace from the sheer pressure.","He'd finally realized that if he didn't bleed a little cash today, he wasn't walking out of this cafeteria.","“I... I only have two thousand yuan on me.”","“Two thousand works too!”","Professor Xu didn't give him a chance to change his mind. He immediately pulled out a crumpled notebook and a ballpoint pen from his pocket, flipped it open, and scribbled furiously.","[Today borrows two thousand yuan from Professor Liu, for the new-energy battery R&D project. Borrower: Xu Yangeng. September 9, 2009.]","If anyone looked closely, they'd see that this notebook was filled with countless similar loan entries, densely packed together.","[March 12, borrowed 3,200 yuan from Professor Zhang.]","[May 8, borrowed 800 yuan from Teacher Li.]","[Jan 15, 2008, borrowed 500 yuan from Old Zhou in the Logistics Department.]","[......]","Professor Xu jotted down the loan details, then wrote out a separate IOU and handed it to Professor Liu with both hands.","“Professor Liu, here’s the IOU. Keep it safe. Once my project succeeds, I’ll pay you back with interest.”","Professor Liu looked at the IOU and twitched at the corner of his mouth.","“Professor Xu, why don’t you just keep the money? Consider it my contribution. Just... don’t come looking for me again...”","“That won’t do!”","Xu Yangeng cut him off, his expression dead serious: “A loan is a loan—how can I not pay it back? Don’t worry, I, Xu Yangeng, am a man of my word. A debt must be repaid, it’s only right. Once my research succeeds, I’ll pay you double!”","“Fine, fine.” Professor Liu let out a final sigh, pulled out all the cash from his wallet—a thick wad of crumpled bills and loose change mixed together—and handed it over.","The moment Xu Yangeng got the money, he sprang to his feet, his eyes blazing as he scanned the other diners in the cafeteria, already hunting for his next target.","The teachers who were eating all froze in terror, then grabbed their trays and bolted for the exit.","Afraid that if they lingered even a second, they’d get caught.","But the Xu couple clearly weren’t about to let them off that easily.","“Professor Wang! Professor Wang, don’t run! Take a look at my proposal...”","“Teacher Li, let’s talk! Didn’t you say last time you were interested in new energy?”","“Director Zhao, Director Zhao...”","In an instant, the entire cafeteria turned into chaos. The teachers scattered like mice chased by a cat, running in every direction—quite the lively scene."]},{"number":827,"title":"Chapter 827: 828, Two Paranoid \"Madmen\".","paragraphs":["Liu Yutong and the others happened to see the so - called Professor Xu shamelessly pestering someone to borrow money.","Xu Yi's face grew increasingly ugly, and her ears burned red. She lowered her head, with an urge to bury her whole face in the bowl.","Liu Yutong glanced at her and suddenly asked, \"Are they your parents?\"","Xu Yi suddenly looked up, asking in surprise, \"How do you know?\"","She had never mentioned who her parents were.","\"Just a guess,\" Liu Yutong replied casually.","Of course, it wasn't a guess.","In her past life, she already knew about Xu Yi's parents.","At that time, Xu Yi had told her that her parents were both professors at Imperial University.","Her father, Xu Yangeng, was a doctoral supervisor in the School of Electrical Engineering, and her mother, Zhou Wanqing, was a professor in the School of Materials Science and Engineering.","Both of them were outstanding in their respective fields, having brought up many excellent students and enjoying a fairly good reputation in the academic circle.","However, their research directions were a bit too advanced.","In that era, the concept of new - energy vehicles was still very vague in China. Most people thought that electric vehicles were just the slow sightseeing cars on the golf course, or at most, elderly - mobility scooters, which could never amount to anything, let alone be industrialized.","Their research was almost regarded as heresy and a waste of time in the academic circle at that time.","So every time they applied for research funds, the review experts rejected their applications, with reasons such as the direction being immature, lacking application prospects, and not being worthy of funding.","They were rejected once, twice, and even three times.","Xu Yangeng was not willing to give up. He and his wife, Zhou Wanqing, took their technical plans to outside enterprises and investment institutions.","The results were much the same.","Some would politely see them out, while others wouldn't even let them in.","Later, they made a decision that no one could understand.","They both resigned from their teaching positions at Imperial University.","When the news spread, many people were shocked.","Relatives and friends took turns to dissuade them, and even their parents were so angry that they pounded the table and scolded them for being ungrateful.","A professor at Imperial University was a position that many people would fight tooth and nail for. It was an iron - rice - bowl job with high pay and high social status. How could they resign?","They were crazy, absolutely crazy!","Xu Yangeng and Zhou Wanqing didn't give any explanations.","Later, they sold their house, emptied all their savings, and shamelessly borrowed money from relatives and friends. They managed to scrape together more than three million yuan and rented an abandoned factory building in the suburbs of the imperial city, which they transformed into a laboratory.","That year, Xu Yi was just in high school.","From that year on, her life completely changed.","She lost her home and moved in with her grandparents. Later, she also lived in her uncle's and aunt's houses.","Her parents threw themselves into the factory building in the suburbs, and she hardly saw them throughout the year.","Occasionally, when they came back, they were in a hurry and left soon.","If it weren't for the support from her grandparents and relatives, she might not even be able to afford her tuition. Her situation was that miserable.","Every time she saw her parents, all they talked about were things she couldn't understand at all.","Terms like battery energy density, motor efficiency curve, vehicle control system, and permanent - magnet synchronous motor...","She didn't understand and didn't want to listen.","She just wanted to ask them one question: Why did they abandon her?","Why couldn't they work steadily like other parents and accompany her?","But every time the words were on the tip of her tongue, seeing the almost pathological paranoia in her parents' eyes, she swallowed them back.","She knew the answer without asking, but she just didn't want to accept it.","What happened later also proved others' judgments.","After the laboratory was established, due to the lack of follow - up funds, the research progress was extremely slow.","Three million yuan was indeed a large sum of money in that era, but in the face of extremely money - burning scientific research, it was just a drop in the ocean.","Buying equipment cost money, buying materials cost money, conducting tests cost money, and repairing broken equipment also cost money. Everything cost money.","Money was spent like water, but no results were achieved.","In the first year, their savings were gone.","In the second year, the money from selling the house was also used up.","In the third year, the borrowed money was spent to the last cent.","Xu Yangeng and Zhou Wanqing started borrowing money everywhere.","Relatives, friends, classmates, former colleagues, and students they had taught... They didn't let anyone off.","At first, people were willing to lend them money.","After all, they were once professors at Imperial University. People thought they were just in a temporary financial difficulty and that they were capable of repaying the money.","But as time passed, people found something was wrong. The couple never repaid the money they borrowed, and they borrowed more and more frequently.","Most importantly, there was no sign of their so - called new - energy research.","So people started to avoid them.","They didn't answer the phone, didn't reply to text messages, and walked around them when they met.","Xu Yangeng and Zhou Wanqing became the \"plague gods\" that everyone avoided.","At the most difficult time, the rent of the laboratory was overdue for too long. The landlord came with some people and changed the lock.","All the equipment, materials, manuscripts, etc., were thrown onto the open space outside the factory building.","It rained heavily that day.","Xu Yangeng and Zhou Wanqing stood in the rain, desperately covering the equipment with plastic sheets. They were in a complete mess and looked very embarrassed.","Passers - by looked at them strangely, as if they were looking at two madmen.","Finally, a former classmate of Zhou Wanqing couldn't stand it anymore and lent them a sum of money, which allowed them to find a smaller and shabbier place and barely set up the laboratory again.","That former classmate was the vice - president of BS University and their last straw.","Later, with the vice - president's multiple mediations, the old president of BS University, out of consideration for old colleagues, agreed to invite them to teach at BS University, providing them with a place to stay and a living.","The condition was that they had to teach normally and couldn't put all their energy into researching new energy as before.","Xu Yangeng and Zhou Wanqing agreed.","But they never thought of stopping.","They taught during the day and continued their research at night and on weekends. As soon as they got their salaries, except for the most basic living expenses, the rest was all thrown into that seemingly bottomless pit.","It was still far from enough.","Then the professors, teachers, and even students at the school \"suffered\".","Anyway, as long as someone looked like they had money, they wouldn't let them go.","From tens of thousands to thousands, from thousands to hundreds, as long as they could borrow money, no matter how much, it was okay.","They were just that crazy.","...","Xu Yi lowered her head. Thinking of her experiences over the years, tears welled up in her eyes.","\"They weren't like this before.\"","\"Back in the imperial capital, they were very popular professors at the college. My classmates were extremely envious of me, saying that I had a pair of very amazing professor parents and that I must be extremely happy. At that time, there were always many of my parents' students visiting our home, and they were highly respected.\"","\"Then, somehow, everything changed.\"","\"They quit their jobs, sold the house, and moved into that shabby laboratory. Since high school, I've been living with my grandparents and even relatives. I rarely see them. Every time we meet, all they keep talking about are things I don't understand. When I say I don't want to listen, they tell me that everything will be okay once the research is successful.\"","\"But things have never gotten better over the years.\"","\"They've owed a huge amount of money. Relatives and friends avoid them like the plague. My mom used to be such an intellectual and elegant woman, but later, in order to borrow money, she endured all kinds of people's looks and said all kinds of humble words. My dad used to be such a proud man, but now, he chases after colleagues to borrow money and is treated like a con artist. He even asks for as little as a few hundred yuan and doesn't even let the canteen aunt off.\"","\"I really don't know what they're after.\"","After Xu Yi finished sharing her experience, tears finally welled up and rolled down her cheeks.","She quickly wiped them away with the back of her hand and turned her head away.","After listening, Liu Yutong sighed inwardly. She looked again at Professor Xu, who was chasing after a young teacher not far away. Professor Zhou was approaching from the other side. The couple really had good teamwork.","\"Teacher Chen, you just got the Youth Fund, right? Support scientific research. Consider it an investment.\"","\"Yes, Teacher Chen. Just do a good deed and lend us a few thousand yuan. We'll pay you back double later.\"","\".........\"","The young teacher looked extremely embarrassed. He didn't know whether to leave or stay. Finally, unable to withstand their repeated requests, he sighed and counted out five hundred yuan from his wallet and handed it over.","Xu Yangeng took the money and skillfully took out the notebook for recording debts and noted down the information about this sum of money.","\"Teacher Chen, thank you! Really thank you! Once my project is successful, I'll definitely pay you back!\"","The young teacher quickly waved his hand and walked away with his tray without looking back.","Over there, Xu Yangeng was sharing today's \"harvest\" cheerfully with his wife, but there was more sadness in his expression.","Looking at this scene, Liu Yutong felt as if something had touched her heart.","They were regarded as a laughingstock by everyone, knew they'd probably be rejected, had to humble themselves for just a few hundred yuan, and were already so down and out. Yet, they still didn't give up.","Such persistent people were really rare.","It's a pity...","According to the development trajectory of the previous life, it seemed that they didn't get a good result.","Professor Xu had an accident and died, and Professor Zhou went crazy.","In the previous life, she accidentally heard this news from an alumnus later and was quite sigh with emotion at that time.","So, she didn't know whether they finally managed to develop that so - called new - energy battery that could change the world..."]},{"number":828,"title":"Chapter 828: 829. What Matters Most in Entrepreneurship (Thanks to 'Yu Yan Niao Niao' for the God-tier Certification)","paragraphs":["Just as Liu Yutong was lost in her memories, Professor Xu Yangeng suddenly glanced over at their table.","He first spotted his daughter Xu Yi, and then his gaze shifted to the young girl sitting beside her.","The moment he saw what she was wearing, his eyes lit up instantly.","After years of going around begging for funding, he had developed a keen eye for spotting wealth.","With just one look, he could tell this girl came from a wealthy family.","From the expensive wristwatch on her wrist, to the earrings on her earlobes, and the outfit she was wearing—it looked custom-made.","This was definitely a big catch!","Xu Yangeng didn’t hesitate for a second. He waved at his wife and headed straight for Liu Yutong’s table.","When Xu Yi saw her parents walking over, her face turned pale in an instant.","Her first reaction wasn’t to greet them—it was to tug at Liu Yutong’s sleeve, urging her to leave quickly.","“Classmate Liu, let’s go. I’m done eating.”","“Hold on.” Liu Yutong pressed her hand down gently.","Xu Yi was frantic: “You don’t understand—my parents are really not normal lately. They see anyone and think they’re rich, and they want to borrow money from everyone they meet. I’m afraid they’ll latch onto you. They really will latch onto you, the kind you can’t shake off no matter what. Please just go, I’m begging you!”","As she spoke, there was a tone of shame in her voice.","After all, she had only just met Liu Yutong. If her parents came over and started begging for money, how would that look to her new friend?","As their daughter, she knew her parents all too well.","They had become two research beggars. They saw everyone as a potential wealthy benefactor, hitting up anyone and everyone for funding, with no regard for time, place, or person. They didn’t even spare the cafeteria ladies or the students. It was utterly shameless.","She didn’t want to be embarrassed like this.","“It’s fine.” Liu Yutong waved her hand.","By then, Xu Yangeng and Zhou Wanqing had already reached their table.","Xu Yangeng first gave Liu Yutong a full once-over, his gaze moving from her watch to her earrings, from her clothes to her shoes, blatantly and without any attempt to hide it.","After confirming he hadn’t misjudged, a smile—one he thought was warm and friendly—spread across his face as he greeted her.","“Xiao Yi, is this your classmate?”","Xu Yi bit her lip and said nothing.","In fact, she didn’t want to talk to her parents at all.","“Hello, Uncle. Hello, Auntie. My name is Liu Yutong. I’m a friend of Xu Yi’s.” Liu Yutong stood up on her own and greeted them politely.","“Good, good, good. Hello, Classmate Liu, hello, hello!”","Xu Yangeng nodded repeatedly, then eagerly took the folder from his wife’s hands and placed it in front of Liu Yutong.","“Classmate Liu, since you’re Xiao Yi’s friend, I won’t beat around the bush. Take a look at this—it’s a project my wife and I have been researching for years. It’s about the core three-electric system for new energy vehicles, covering batteries, motors, and electronic control. Let me tell you, the prospects for this project are incredibly bright. In the future, new energy vehicles will dominate the roads—gasoline cars will be phased out sooner or later. Whoever masters the core three-electric technology will lead the entire industry. This is a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity...”","“Dad!”","Xu Yi finally couldn’t hold it in anymore. She shot up from her seat, cutting him off.","Her voice was so loud that students eating nearby turned to look.","Xu Yangeng’s words died in his throat, and he looked at his daughter awkwardly.","“Dad, haven’t you had enough!” Xu Yi’s whole body was trembling—from anger, and from hurt.","“All these years, you’ve gone around looking for investors. You’ve asked so many people—has anyone given you even a single cent? Not one! Everyone treats you like con artists, like lunatics! And do you know what people at school say about me? They call me the daughter of a madman, the daughter of a fraud! No one even dares to be friends with me anymore—who would want to be friends with someone whose parents are like lunatics!”","“Today, I finally made a new friend. I brought her to campus for a meal, and here you go again with this routine! Can’t you just be normal? Can’t you just be an ordinary father, sit down and have a meal with my friend, have a chat, instead of pitching your nonsense that nobody believes the second you meet someone! You’ll even borrow a few hundred bucks, and you won’t even spare my friend. You—you really embarrass me!”","“Please, for once, think about how I feel, okay!” She screamed those last words, completely hysterical.","She had been holding all of this in for a very long time.","Today, she couldn’t hold it back anymore. It all came pouring out.","Zhou Wanqing stood beside her husband, watching her daughter fall apart. She opened her mouth as if to say something, but in the end, she only let out a sigh and lowered her head in guilt.","The smile on Xu Yangeng’s face slowly faded.","After a moment of silence, he quietly took the folder back.","“I’m sorry, Xiao Yi.”","“It’s Daddy’s fault. I’ll stop talking.”","Then he turned to face Liu Yutong and gave a slight bow.","“Classmate Liu, I apologize for the spectacle. Enjoy your meal. I have some things to take care of, so I’ll be going now.”","Zhou Wanqing also nodded at Liu Yutong, forcing a faint smile before preparing to leave.","Just as they turned around, Liu Yutong suddenly called out to stop them.","\"Professors, please wait a moment.\"","Xu Yangeng stopped in his tracks, turned around, and looked at Liu Yutong with some confusion.","Liu Yutong pointed at the stack of documents in their hands and asked, \"Could I take a look at that?\"","Xu Yangeng was taken aback for a moment and instinctively looked at his daughter.","Xu Yi was also stunned, her eyes red as she looked at Liu Yutong and shook her head at her.","\"Classmate Liu, you...\"","\"I want to see it,\" Liu Yutong said.","Xu Yangeng hesitated for only a second before quickly handing the documents over to Liu Yutong, a faint glimmer of hope welling up in his chest.","Liu Yutong took the documents, opened to the first page, and began reading carefully.","The pages were packed with technical jargon and formula derivations.","Things like battery cell voltage characteristic curves, SOC estimation algorithm flowcharts, vector control block diagrams for permanent magnet synchronous motors...","And then... she couldn't understand it.","Not at all.","Most of the content was far beyond the scope of what she had studied.","A moment later.","She closed the documents and looked up at Xu Yangeng.","\"Professor Xu, about this project of yours—how much R&D funding would it roughly require?\"","Xu Yangeng almost reflexively answered, \"For a complete prototype vehicle development, from start to finish, it would take about two hundred million.\"","\"Of course, you could also do it in stages instead of investing all at once. If we start with the battery system first, that's cheaper—eighty million would be enough. If eighty million is still too much, we could start with the BMS software system. That's the cheapest option—thirty million to get started. Once we have a demo, we can take it to venture capital firms, and the subsequent funding rounds would flow more smoothly...\"","Liu Yutong raised her hand to interrupt him: \"Professor Xu, I'm not going to invest in you.\"","The moment those words left her mouth, the expression on Xu Yangeng's face froze instantly.","But he quickly recovered. He was long accustomed to this kind of situation—so accustomed that even his disappointment had grown fleeting.","\"It's fine, it's fine.\"","\"Classmate Liu is still young after all. A big decision like this naturally has to be discussed with family. It's perfectly normal if the adults at home don't agree. Uncle understands, he really does.\"","He figured that a wealthy young lady like Liu Yutong, though well-dressed and well-off, was still just a student in the end. The real financial power surely rested with her parents, and she likely had no authority to move large sums of money on her own. So it was only natural that she couldn't invest in them.","Neither the couple nor Xu Yi herself had ever once considered that this girl, who appeared to be nothing more than a rich heiress, was actually a self-made, hidden female richest person in the country.","\"Professor Xu, the reason I'm declining to invest isn't because your research direction is flawed, nor because I don't believe in the new energy sector. On the contrary, I'm extremely bullish on it.\"","Xu Yangeng's head shot up, a light rekindling in his eyes.","\"Then... then why?\"","\"Because you two don't actually understand what it means to build a business.\"","Xu Yangeng: \"...\"","His face slowly reddened.","Not from shame, but from feeling offended. Here was a young girl who looked even younger than his own daughter, telling him he didn't understand entrepreneurship?","Do you even know what entrepreneurship is?","Do you know what we've been through all these years?","\"Classmate Liu, we've been doing research for over a decade. We know exactly what we're doing. When it comes to technology, we have absolute confidence.\"","\"At the end of the day, building a business is just turning technology into a product. What's there not to understand?\"","Liu Yutong: \"Is that so?\"","\"Then let me ask you both a question—what do you think matters most when starting a business?\"","Xu Yangeng answered almost without hesitation: \"Money, of course. With money, everything is easy.\"","If he had money, he wouldn't have had to sell his house and car. He wouldn't have had to humble himself and go begging, scraping and clawing for funds like a beggar.","If he had money, he could stay in the lab with peace of mind, pouring all his energy and talent into his research. It wouldn't be long before he could produce a finished product.","But after hearing his answer, Liu Yutong shook her head.","\"Professor Xu, you're wrong.\"","\"In my view, money has never been the real issue when starting a business.\""]},{"number":829,"title":"Chapter 829: 830, Make a proposal.","paragraphs":["Xu Yangeng was stunned.","Zhou Wanqing was stunned too.","Xu Yi was just as stunned.","A female college student who looked no older than twenty dared to say, bold as brass, in front of two university professors: \"Money isn't the problem when it comes to starting a business.\"","If anyone else had said that, Xu Yangeng would have long since stormed off, mentally filing the speaker under \"people who don't understand technology yet love to lecture.\"","But somehow, hearing this girl say those words, he actually found himself wanting to hear her take on it.","Maybe because he sensed a very special aura about her.","It was an aura remarkably similar to the one worn by the big shots he knew who had weathered countless storms. It was astonishing.","\"Classmate Liu, you probably don't know what we've been through all these years.\"","\"Over the years, people have tried to talk us out of starting a company... but for you to say money isn't the issue—that's a bit much, don't you think? If it's not money, then what is it?\"","Liu Yutong didn't answer him directly. Instead, she asked, \"Professor Xu, let me ask you a few questions.\"","\"Go ahead.\"","\"This document of yours—how many investors have you shown it to?\"","\"I can't remember exactly. A few dozen, I guess.\"","\"Did anyone put in money?\"","\"Some did.\"","\"But they offered too little and the terms were too harsh, so I turned them down.\"","Liu Yutong nodded. \"So that's as good as getting nothing, isn't it?\"","Xu Yangeng: \"If you insist on putting it that way... yeah, that's fair.\"","\"Then do you know why, exactly?\"","Xu Yangeng opened his mouth, instinctively wanting to say, \"Because they don't understand the technology—they're just a bunch of profit-grubbing capitalists.\"","But the words died in his throat.","He had devoted himself entirely to new energy battery R&D, and besides his genuine love for the technology, there was also the belief that this would be a market worth hundreds of billions in the future—a chance to claim a slice of the pie and make a name for himself.","Seeing him hesitate, Liu Yutong said it for him: \"Do you think those investors didn't fund you because they don't understand the technology and can't see just how amazing your proposal really is?\"","Xu Yangeng fell silent.","But silence is often an answer.","Liu Yutong held up two fingers. \"Professor Xu, let me ask you a second question.\"","\"If someone handed you two hundred million yuan right now, how would you spend it?\"","Xu Yangeng thought for a moment, then said, \"Well, first I'd build a lab, buy equipment, and then follow the technical roadmap we've planned—start with the battery system, move on to the motor and electronic control, and finally the complete vehicle integration...\"","\"Specifically?\" Liu Yutong cut him off.","\"Specifically what?\" Xu Yangeng blinked.","\"How much does it cost to build the lab? Rent or buy the space? What size? In which city? What equipment are you buying? What are the model numbers and quotes for each machine? Domestic or imported? How long is the procurement cycle? How many people does the team need? How many for R&D? How many for testing? How long from battery system R&D to prototype? How many phases are there? What's the acceptance standard for each phase? If phase one fails, will the remaining money be enough to last through phase two? And how can you guarantee success—and how soon? How long until you achieve commercial viability...\"","Liu Yutong fired off a rapid torrent of questions, leaving Xu Yangeng's head spinning.","These were things he genuinely hadn't thought through.","Or rather, he had been thinking only about the technical side.","How to optimize control algorithms, how to improve charging and discharging efficiency, how to reduce current harmonics, how to break ground in thermal management, and so on.","As for how the money was spent, where it went, how long until it produced results, how staff were assigned, how projects were managed—in his view, these were trivial details.","If you had money, couldn't you just solve everything?","Hire an accountant, for instance.","Liu Yutong could read what was written on his face.","She let out a soft sigh.","\"Professor Xu, Professor Zhou.\"","\"Both of you are top-tier scientific minds. In your fields of expertise, I'm not even fit to tie your shoes.\"","\"But when it comes to starting a business—turning technology into a product, a product into a commodity, and a commodity into a business that can sustain itself—you two genuinely don't have a clue.\"","Xu Yangeng's face instantly darkened. Zhou Wanqing's brows furrowed as well.","\"What is the essence of starting a business?\"","\"It's turning an idea into a sustainable business. Not a one-off. Not something that burns through money and then dissolves. Something that can generate its own cash flow and slowly grow.\"","\"Technology is just one piece of it. Important, sure, but often not the most important piece.\"","\"More important than technology is knowing who your customers are, where your market is, what your competitors are doing, how you price your product, how you build your channels, how you manage your team, how your cash flow operates, how you control risk, how you achieve your goals...\"","\"All of these things together are what you call a business plan.\"","\"But both of you—you haven't even put together a proper business plan. I honestly can't wrap my head around it.\"","Liu Yutong pointed at the documents in their hands. \"What you've got there is called a technical specification. And to put it bluntly, nobody besides yourselves can understand it.\"","\"Taking that to an investor is like a chef bringing a basket of raw ingredients to a customer and saying, 'Look how fresh my ingredients are.' But what the customer wants is a finished dish—or at the very least, something that could appear on a menu—not a pile of uncooked produce.\"","\"What investors really want to know is: What's your edge when making this dish? How many servings can you sell a day? Can you open a franchise in the future? You can't even answer those basic questions, so why would anyone fund you?\"","\"If you can't show anything concrete, how is anyone supposed to invest in you?\"","\"Or do you think every investor out there is blind? Or that everyone who turned you down simply can't see the value of your technology?\"","Xu Yangeng's face grew redder, as if she'd struck a raw nerve.","He had spent years hitting dead ends—running around, seeing investor after investor, repeating the same pitch countless times.","Every time he was rejected, he told himself: it's them, they don't get it, they don't have vision, and this quick-buck era doesn't deserve real technology.","But now, with a girl in her early twenties cutting straight to the heart of the problem, he suddenly realized—maybe the problem really was with him.","\"Then what do you suggest we do?\"","\"First thing first: figure out exactly what you want to do, then set a goal.\"","\"The new energy battery track is a bit too far off in the distance. You can start with a closer goal—e-bike batteries, phone batteries, things like that. Start with batteries that are already widely used and whose technical routes are mature.\"","\"Second, put together a business plan, and that's it.\"","Xu Yangeng was taken aback. \"Is it really that simple?\"","Liu Yutong nodded. \"Yes, that simple.\"","Xu Yangeng was speechless. He still felt that doing all this flashy, insubstantial stuff was a waste of time. With all that effort, they might as well run another couple of sets of data.","\"Then how do we make a business plan?\"","Now it was Liu Yutong's turn to be speechless.","You two are professors, even doctoral supervisors — how can you not know this?","But she still patiently laid out the core framework of a business plan.","Things like team background and core strengths, technical barriers and innovation points, market analysis and potential customers, competitor analysis, business model and revenue streams, financial projections and stage-by-stage goals, and so on.","She explained it in great detail with clear logic, completely stunning the three professors. They were mesmerized.","Their impression was that she didn't seem like a student at all — more like a top-tier investor who had managed enormous amounts of capital. She was extremely professional.","\"Once you've finished the plan, Xu Yi can get in touch with me.\"","\"But I'll say this upfront: I want to see a plan that even a layman like me can understand. If I can't understand it, then there's no point showing it to anyone else. It'd be a waste of time.\"","In truth, for Liu Yutong, making an investment was just a matter of a quick word — no need for all this hassle. She even agreed with the field the two professors had chosen.","But she wasn't sure they would succeed. Because based on how things had played out in her previous life, the giant of new energy batteries hadn't emerged from BS Province.","Moreover, the two of them genuinely lacked the kind of temperament that made a successful person.","That temperament wasn't about their knowledge, nor their diligence, nor even their persistence — they had all those in spades.","What they lacked was something far more subtle...","To play it safe, she could only judge based on their business plan first.","Of course, if she could take their research materials with her and have professionals verify the real value of the technology, that would also work.","But they would never give that to her.","Their research was years of hard work and painstaking effort. They definitely wouldn't hand it over to an outsider casually.","So she had to settle for the next best thing.","After the conversation, Liu Yutong said goodbye to a still-stunned Xu Yi and left with Yun Cheng and the others.","Not long after they were gone, Xu Yi suddenly felt someone tug at her sleeve.","She looked down — it was her father's hand.","\"Xiao Yi.\"","\"Huh?\"","\"She really is your classmate?\"","Xu Yi shook her head. \"No, I just met her today.\"","\"Just met her?\"","\"Yeah.\"","\"She's really not a new teacher at the school?\"","\"Like the kind who looks young for her age? A counselor or teaching assistant?\"","\"Dad, no, really. She's a student at HS Provincial University of Finance and Economics. She's only a junior — a year below me.\"","Xu Yangeng: \"...\"","A junior?","Were college students these days really this ridiculous?","He genuinely felt she was on par with top-tier business tycoons, one for one. Could it be that he was just imagining things?"]},{"number":830,"title":"Chapter 830: 831. Busy Work.","paragraphs":["For the next two days, Liu Yutong’s schedule was largely devoted to matters involving Uncle Zhu.","On the first day, Uncle Zhu and several other officials accompanied her on an inspection tour of several key development zones planned for BS Province.","Uncle Zhu and the others hoped that the Wanlonghui Group would further increase its investment in BS Province, particularly in commercial consumption and the technology industry.","After several rounds of in-depth negotiations, two agreements were finalized.","The first was to continue expanding Wanlong Plaza into the province’s major prefecture-level cities, while also adding two major projects: a logistics hub and an agricultural-products deep-processing base.","Yang Xin, president of the Commercial Consumption and Retail Business Group, signed the agreements with the local governments on behalf of the group.","Yang Xin had now become one of the most publicly visible executives in the Wanlonghui Group.","Under his leadership, the commercial consumption and retail division held signing ceremonies, groundbreaking ceremonies, and grand openings of all sizes. He was almost always the one who appeared onstage.","He was increasingly coming to resemble the successful version of himself from his previous life. Both his appearance and bearing had taken on the air of a true corporate president, and he was completely at ease in front of cameras and the media.","Liu Yutong, meanwhile, continued to remain half-hidden behind the scenes. She never attended any occasion that required photographs or group pictures.","It wasn’t that she was being pretentious.","At her level, keeping a low profile was actually a good thing.","Being too prominent could easily lead to trouble.","Besides, the Wanlonghui Group had never relied on her personal image to drive its business. If it really wanted to depend on her personal brand, then she would have to make frequent public appearances—go on shows, give speeches, and even film promotional videos.","The two Mas, for instance, had completely different styles. Old Ma loved being in the spotlight, while Pony Ma preferred to stay out of it.","Liu Yutong was the same way.","It wasn’t that she was afraid of anything. She simply didn’t want to be harassed.","Just imagine: if everyone in the country recognized your face, could you still eat dan dan noodles at a street stall like an ordinary person?","Wherever you went, you’d probably be surrounded by onlookers.","Liu Yutong liked having a little freedom in her private life, so her photographs had never appeared on the internet, in the media, or through any other public channels.","On the rare occasions when one did get leaked, her subordinates would use various means to have it removed.","So even if people had heard her name, they might not know what she looked like.","As a result, the people who appeared publicly on behalf of the group were now mostly the heads of its various business divisions and several other core executives.","People like Yu Xin, Yang Xin, and Zhang Dalong, among others.","These individuals had gradually become the public faces representing the Wanlonghui Group.","The second matter concerned Wanlong Aerospace.","Liu Yutong and Uncle Zhu, representing their respective sides, signed a letter of intent. In the future, they might build a rocket-engine test stand and production bases for certain components in BS Province.","Located in southwestern China, BS Province was mountainous and covered in valleys. It was vast and sparsely populated, making it an ideal location from the perspectives of safety and confidentiality.","Of course, this was only a letter of intent for now. There was still a long way to go before the project could truly be implemented.","The subsequent environmental impact assessments, land acquisition, construction of supporting infrastructure, and coordination and approval procedures with the relevant departments would all take time.","In the best-case scenario, it might take a year or two. In the worst case, three to five years was entirely possible.","Uncle Zhu was already very satisfied.","After the signing ceremony, Uncle Zhu personally escorted Liu Yutong to the expressway entrance.","Liu Yutong was heading next to inspect schools built with funding from the Wanlong Charity Foundation and visit their teachers and students.","That was the matter she cared about most during this trip to BS Province.","As they were nearing the expressway entrance, Uncle Zhu suddenly asked Liu Yutong a question.","“Yutong, what’s your view on lithium mines?”","Liu Yutong turned her head slightly, somewhat surprised. “Why are you suddenly asking about that, Uncle Zhu?”","Just two days earlier, she had happened to run into Xu Yangeng and his wife, Zhou Wanqing, in the cafeteria at BS University. She hadn’t expected Uncle Zhu to bring up the subject less than forty-eight hours later.","“Just making conversation,” Uncle Zhu said.","Then he continued, “It suddenly crossed my mind, so I thought I’d ask. Do you have any plans to invest in the new-energy sector?”","Liu Yutong thought for a moment and answered honestly, “I’ve only gained a basic understanding of the battery industry. So far, I haven’t found a suitable entry point.”","“Are you interested?” Uncle Zhu asked again.","“Yes, I am,” Liu Yutong replied immediately.","Uncle Zhu nodded and gave a quiet hum, but said nothing more. The conversation ended there.","Liu Yutong was completely puzzled, but she didn’t ask any further questions. The two of them parted ways at the expressway entrance.","Meanwhile, the several trucks loaded with gifts that Yun Cheng had arranged were also in place. They were filled with presents Liu Yutong had prepared for the teachers and students at the schools she would be visiting.","Once everyone had assembled, a convoy consisting of several cars and several trucks set off directly for the city that had suffered the worst damage in last year’s disaster.","For most of the journey, Liu Yutong found herself thinking about what the schools looked like now and how the students were faring in their studies and daily lives after moving into their new buildings.","After the devastating earthquake last year, the Wanlong Charity Foundation funded the construction of more than a hundred schools in BS Province, covering several counties and more than a dozen townships in the hardest-hit areas.","More than a year had passed, and she still hadn’t visited any of them in person.","The convoy drove along the expressway for nearly two hours. After exiting, it turned onto a provincial road and continued for another forty minutes. Gradually, the houses on both sides grew denser, and the outlines of the townships came into view.","As they neared the school in the first township, Liu Yutong asked again, “Are you sure none of the gifts for the school are missing?”","“We checked everything, Miss,” came the reply. “As you requested, every child has a gift: a schoolbag, a stationery set, candy and snacks, and a red envelope. We also prepared separate gifts and red envelopes for the teachers.”","“Good.”"]},{"number":831,"title":"Chapter 831: 832. Leaving Final Words.","paragraphs":["The faculty dormitory at BS University.","Xu Yangeng had been sitting in front of his computer for three straight days.","His eyes were bloodshot, as if he hadn’t slept in days. Another layer of stubble had grown across his face, a dark bluish shadow that made him look several years older.","And yet, he had written less than a third of the business plan.","It wasn’t because he had been slacking off.","Quite the opposite—he had spent nearly every waking moment of those three days working on it.","But for some reason, the more he wrote, the more he felt that something was wrong.","Market analysis, competitor comparisons, business models, financial projections... Every time he finished a paragraph, he had to stop to look up information, find data, and run the numbers.","Yet some things simply couldn’t be found through public channels.","Take the technical specifications of future competitors, for instance. The companies that would eventually become serious contenders did not seem to exist yet, and the information available online was scarce—mostly vague concepts that were incredibly difficult to write about.","What frustrated him most wasn’t that he couldn’t write it.","It was the question of whether any of it was useful at all.","That girl, Miss Liu, had said investors would want to see these things.","But for all anyone knew, she was merely an undergraduate who hadn’t even graduated yet.","Even if she came from a wealthy family, even if she really took the business plan home to show her parents, did that mean they would definitely invest?","Not necessarily, right?","The more Xu Yangeng thought about it, the more he felt like an idiot.","He was Xu Yangeng, a professor at BS University and once a doctoral supervisor at Teidu University. Yet now he was holed up in his dormitory, racking his brain over a business plan whose usefulness he wasn’t even sure of, like an elementary school student preparing for an exam.","And while writing the plan, he had vaguely sensed an “invisible wall” appearing inexplicably in front of him, blocking his way forward.","No matter how hard he tried to break through it, he couldn’t.","“Damn it, I’m done with this!”","Xu Yangeng slammed his hand down on the keyboard and leaned back in his chair, thoroughly exasperated.","Just then, the phone on his desk rang.","Xu Yangeng glanced at the caller ID. It was an unfamiliar number.","He was already in a foul mood, so he hung up immediately.","But the number called again and again.","Irritated, he finally pressed the answer button.","“Hello?”","A hoarse voice came from the other end.","“Old Xu, it’s me.”","Xu Yangeng froze for several seconds before suddenly realizing who it was.","“Zhou Ming? Old Zhou? You finally decided to call me, huh?”","“Where the hell have you been these past six months? I couldn’t reach you, and no one could find you. I thought you’d died somewhere!”","Zhou Ming was his high school classmate, and one of the few people over the years who had continued to support him—his “investor,” so to speak.","Though this so-called investor had lent him only fifty thousand yuan in total, spread out over several occasions.","Still, Xu Yangeng had always remembered that friendship.","“Old Xu, listen to me.”","Zhou Ming’s voice was urgent. He had no intention of exchanging pleasantries or reminiscing.","“I don’t have much time. I’ll keep this brief.”","Xu Yangeng’s heart skipped a beat. “What’s wrong? Did something happen?”","“I’m fine, but I need you to do me a favor.”","“Tell me.”","“I have something in my possession. It’s very important. If I stop contacting you, go to the address I’m about to send you and find it.”","The more Xu Yangeng listened, the more uneasy he became.","“Old Zhou, what the hell are you up to? Why does this sound like you’re entrusting someone with your final wishes... No, I mean, making arrangements for after your death? Where are you now?”","“Don’t ask. The less you know, the safer you’ll be.”","“Then I’ll call the police for you.”","“Don’t call the police!”","“It’s not time yet. The waters here are too deep. Calling the police now will only alert them. Listen to me. If I haven’t contacted you after a week, take that thing to the police—and, preferably, make sure it reaches the higher authorities.”","As a university professor and doctoral supervisor, Xu Yangeng still knew a few people, despite having spent the past two years borrowing money everywhere and being avoided like the plague.","“What exactly are you talking about? Why do I have to find someone and pass something on to the higher authorities? Explain it to me clearly—”","“Beep, beep, beep...”","Before he could finish, the line went dead.","Xu Yangeng froze for a second, then immediately called back. A recorded message informed him that the number he had dialed was switched off.","He hung up and tried again. Three or four times in a row, he got the same message.","His unease grew stronger by the second.","Hadn’t Zhou Ming said he was going south to conduct an interview?","Why had he suddenly called with something like this?","Xu Yangeng couldn’t help thinking of the many “insane” things Zhou Ming had done over the years.","When exposing the gutter-oil industry, Zhou Ming had staked out a black-market workshop for seven days and seven nights, nearly getting mauled to death by the owner’s guard dogs.","When investigating a pyramid scheme, he had disguised himself as a new recruit and stayed inside for half a month. He had been brainwashed, beaten, and stripped of his phone. He was given only one meal a day.","In the end, he escaped through a second-floor window with secretly recorded footage, breaking two ribs in the fall.","Xu Yangeng had always felt that he and Zhou Ming were the same at their core—both hopeless idealists.","They were the kind of people others regarded as “madmen,” yet who refused to turn back no matter what.","The difference was that Xu Yangeng had paid the price by burying himself under a mountain of debt he could never repay.","Zhou Ming, on the other hand, might have paid with his life.","The ominous feeling in Xu Yangeng’s heart grew stronger and stronger...","That man had clearly run into trouble unlike anything he had faced before. Or perhaps the people behind the subject of his investigation were simply too powerful—powerful enough that he had to prepare in advance for the worst.","But there was nothing Xu Yangeng could do now.","All he could do was wait...","Wait for Zhou Ming to contact him and let him know he was safe."]},{"number":832,"title":"Chapter 832: 833, Highway Robbery.","paragraphs":["On a provincial highway, a long convoy of buses was making its way slowly along the road.","Most of the passengers were in their forties or fifties, with a small number of elderly people around sixty. This was the fifth group of employees’ family members traveling to BS Province. Everyone on the buses was a parent of one of the company’s employees.","Their destination was a city not far from the area hardest hit by last year’s disaster. They were going there on vacation and, while they were at it, to take a look at the post-disaster recovery efforts.","The driver of the lead bus was a veteran who had spent many years driving passenger routes. There was no denying that Old Li was a steady driver. Even so, the black-clad security officer sitting up front felt a little on edge. From his vantage point, whenever they passed through the mountain roads, it seemed as though the bus was practically scraping the edge of the cliffs. The roads were especially treacherous.","“Old Li, how many years have you been driving this route?” the security officer asked.","“Almost fifteen.”","“You were driving this route before the earthquake too?”","“Yep. I happened to be in Da’nan City when the earthquake struck, so I managed to escape the disaster. Once the roads were repaired, I came back and kept driving this route.”","“Were these mountain roads always this deserted?”","“They were even quieter before. After the earthquake, things actually got lively for a while. Rescue vehicles, reconstruction teams, trucks hauling building materials—they were constantly coming and going. But lately, traffic has thinned out again.”","Old Li paused, as if he had suddenly remembered something. Then he added, “I recently heard from some of the drivers who regularly run this route that this stretch of road may not be safe.”","“Not safe? What do you mean?”","“Apparently, there are people stopping vehicles and demanding money. They set up roadblocks, pull cars over, and ask for tolls. They especially like targeting vehicles with out-of-town license plates.”","The black-clad security officer immediately grew serious. He picked up the radio and relayed the information to the men in the buses behind them.","“Stay alert. The road ahead may not be safe. There could be petty thieves waiting for us.”","“Copy!”","“Copy!”","“...”","Seeing how seriously the security officer was taking things, the driver quickly added with a laugh, “There’s no need to be so tense. I heard there’s been a crackdown lately, so there aren’t many people stopping cars anymore. The previous groups of buses never actually ran into trouble. And even if we do, we can just give them a little money and send them on their way.”","The black-clad security officer nodded. “Let’s hope so.”","The convoy continued forward. After rounding a bend, the view ahead suddenly opened up.","They were less than twenty kilometers from the nearest city when the lead bus suddenly slammed on its brakes.","The elderly passengers were caught off guard and lurched forward in their seats.","“What happened?”","“What’s going on?”","“Ouch! What kind of driving is that?”","“...”","The security officer sitting near the front immediately stood up. While raising a hand to calm the startled elderly passengers, he hurried toward the driver’s cabin.","“Great. I really jinxed us. There really are people blocking the road.” Old Li couldn’t help smacking himself in the mouth.","About forty meters ahead, a pine log thicker than a large bowl lay across the middle of the road.","Standing beside it was a group of people—at least twenty at a rough count.","At the very front was a young man wearing a floral shirt. He had a beer belly, a balding head that shone under the sunlight, and a greasy yet menacing face. With his left hand tucked into his pocket and a cigarette pinched between the fingers of his right, he squinted at the approaching convoy.","Behind him stood more than twenty underlings in a variety of clothes.","Some held steel pipes, while others gripped machetes. Two men were holding leashes attached to a pair of snarling, bared-toothed wolfhounds.","Cheng Gang, the head of security on the lead bus, frowned when he saw the scene. He first reported the situation to the men behind him over the radio, then jumped down from the bus and walked straight toward the group, giving them a careful look.","The balding man in charge carried a hint of ruthlessness about him. He didn’t look like an ordinary petty thief blocking the road.","As for the people behind him, around a dozen looked like ordinary street thugs. Several others were drooling and looked mentally impaired. They even shouted incoherently:","“Rob... rob them!”","“Ro... robbing people is fun!”","“Heh heh heh...”","“...”","Cheng Gang did not immediately make a move. He could tell that several of the men were intellectually disabled, and it was possible that the group had genuinely encountered financial difficulties and was stopping vehicles to collect tolls.","So he politely cupped his fists and said, “Brother, who do you work for? What’s the meaning of blocking the road?”","The balding man casually tossed away his cigarette butt and looked him over. His eyes lingered for a moment on the dragon-shaped insignia on Cheng Gang’s chest before he slowly replied, “Which path we come from isn’t important. What matters is that this road belongs to me. If you want to pass, you pay.”","“How much?”","“Two thousand per vehicle.”","Cheng Gang’s eyes instantly turned cold. This guy certainly knew how to make an outrageous demand.","If he had asked for a few hundred yuan, Cheng Gang might have paid it out of consideration for the disabled men among them. But asking for tens of thousands at the outset made it clear that these people weren’t desperate petty thieves. They were real criminals engaged in illegal activities.","Seeing that Cheng Gang remained silent, the balding man pointed at the convoy behind him.","“Looks like you’ve got quite a few vehicles. How about this? I’ll give you a discount. Fifty thousand yuan, and I’ll have my men move the log. Once you pay, we’ll each go our separate ways. We won’t interfere with each other.”","Cheng Gang glanced back at the buses. Everyone inside was an elderly member of the company’s employees’ families. He didn’t want to escalate the situation and frighten them, so he forced down the anger rising in his chest.","“Everyone on the buses is an elderly tourist. Could you make an exception, just this once? Consider it a favor between friends.”","The greasy, balding man twisted his lips into an ugly smile, revealing several smoke-yellowed teeth.","“I don’t make friends. I only take money.”","“If you don’t pay, you can forget about passing through here.”","The greasy, balding man pointed at one of the drooling young men behind him whose mental state was clearly impaired.","“See them? Every one of these people under me is an idiot, and they don’t know their own strength. If they hurt any of your people, that would be unfortunate.”","Hearing this, Cheng Gang suddenly thought of their boss, Ji Yu, of the Myriad Dragon Society.","He never expected that even these petty thugs would use the same trick. Truly, outlaws everywhere seemed to think alike.","And he had to admit—the tactic was quite effective.","Even if these people were arrested, the police couldn’t do much about it. You couldn’t exactly throw a mentally disabled person in prison, could you?","Seeing that the tour group had no intention of cooperating, the greasy, balding man lost patience. He waved his hand and gave the order to his special underlings behind him.","“Brothers, show them what we can do! Let them see how tough we are!”","At his command, several drooling young men with obvious intellectual disabilities raised their steel pipes and charged forward, howling.","Cheng Gang was just about to shout for everyone to prepare for a counterattack when he witnessed an especially comical scene.","Those dim-witted young men didn’t charge at him. Instead, they rushed toward the fallen pine trunk in the middle of the road and started stabbing it wildly.","“Robbery! Robbery! Hand over your money!”","“Give us your money! If you don’t, I’ll stab you to death!”","“......”","If that pine tree had been sentient, it probably would have felt terribly wronged.","What did I ever do to you?","The greasy bald man’s smile instantly froze.","“Hey, what the hell are you doing? Why are you stabbing the tree? Stab a person! Stab the guy in black! Make a hole in him!”","The few intellectually challenged young men tilted their heads and looked at their leader, then at the pine tree. A look of sudden realization spread across their faces.","“Oh! Make a hole!”","Then three of them really did change direction, grabbed their steel pipes, and charged at Cheng Gang.","A smug, vicious grin returned to the greasy bald man’s face. Only by making an example of someone would this tour group obediently hand over their money.","He turned around, pointed at Cheng Gang, and shouted toward the bus.","“See that? This is what happens to anyone who refuses to—”","He broke off mid-sentence.","Because he suddenly felt a chill on his backside.","More precisely, he felt the cold touch of a steel pipe pressed against it.","He stiffly lowered his head and saw a steel pipe planted precisely against his butt.","Following the pipe upward, he saw a foolishly grinning face. It was Third Fool, one of the intellectually challenged young men under his command.","At some point, Third Fool had crept behind him. Now he was squatting on the ground, gripping the steel pipe with both hands and aiming it at the man’s unmentionable region.","His grin was excited and utterly innocent, like a child who had just discovered a fun new toy.","“Make a hole!”","The greasy bald man’s pupils suddenly contracted.","“Wait! Don’t—”","“I’m stabbing!”","The intellectually challenged young man shouted again and eagerly thrust both hands forward.","The steel pipe struck its target with perfect accuracy, tremendous force, and absolutely no mercy, driving straight into the leader’s unmentionable region.","Even through his trousers, that kind of impact was more than ordinary flesh and blood could withstand!","The next second—","“YAAAGH!!!”","A scream like a slaughtered pig rang out instantly."]},{"number":833,"title":"Chapter 833: 834, Thunder and Wind.","paragraphs":["“Fuck... fuck... FUCK!!!”","The Baldy clutched his butt with both hands and dropped to his knees. The veins on his forehead bulged from the pain, and cold sweat poured down his face.","Cheng Gang and the employees’ families in the several buses behind him all froze at the ridiculous sight. Some of them even instinctively covered their own backsides.","You reap what you sow.","Serves him right!","The intellectually disabled young man, however, seemed completely unaware of what he had just done. He tilted his head, looked at the boss kneeling on the ground, then glanced at the steel pipe in his hand and clapped happily.","“Yay! Yay!”","“I wanna stab him again!”","“N-no... don’t...” The Baldy weakly reached out a hand, trying to stop him.","But the intellectually disabled young man only caught the final word—“don’t”—and picked up the steel pipe again.","“Okay! One more time!”","Grinning cheerfully, he raised the steel pipe even more enthusiastically than before.","“Don’t! I mean, don’t—”","Before he could finish, the intellectually disabled young man brought the pipe down hard again.","“Aaaagh~~~!!!”","The Baldy let out an even more agonized scream than before. He sprawled face-down on the concrete, his butt sticking high into the air as he clutched his rear with both hands. Tears streamed down his face. The pain was excruciating!","The other thugs, who were at least somewhat sane, finally came to their senses. They rushed forward and dragged away the intellectually disabled young man, who was still eager for more and shouting that he wanted to keep stabbing.","“Let go of me! I wanna stab him again! The boss said to do it again!”","“He didn’t! He didn’t say that!”","After finally restraining Third Fool, the Baldy lay on the ground, panting for a long while before he barely managed to recover. When he got up, both legs were still trembling, and he could hardly stand.","He turned around and glared viciously at the intellectually disabled young man being held down by his lackeys.","When Third Fool saw the boss looking at him, he just grinned foolishly.","“Boss! Did I stab him good?”","“Heh-heh...”","The Baldy said nothing. He bent down and picked up the steel pipe lying on the ground.","“Boss?” Third Fool tilted his head, staring at him in confusion.","“You bastard! How dare you stab me!”","“Go to hell!”","The Baldy suddenly raised the steel pipe and brought it crashing down on the intellectually disabled young man’s head.","The pipe struck Third Fool’s skull with a dull thud.","The mentally impaired young man’s eyes widened. His body swayed several times before he fell straight backward. Blood seeped from his hair and trickled down his forehead, dripping one drop at a time onto the gray concrete road.","The entire area fell silent.","The two thugs holding Third Fool unconsciously loosened their grip.","The Baldy clutched the bloodstained steel pipe and panted heavily as he stared at Third Fool lying on the ground. Third Fool’s eyes were still open, staring blankly at the sky. A foolish smile even lingered at the corners of his mouth.","Even as he lost consciousness, he seemed unable to understand why he had suddenly fallen over. He only wanted to take a nice, long nap.","Cheng Gang’s expression darkened at once.","The employees’ families sitting in the buses ahead were also badly frightened.","At first, they had merely been watching the gang of roadblockers make fools of themselves for entertainment.","But the moment the Baldy raised the steel pipe and dealt a lethal blow to a defenseless intellectually disabled man, the nature of the whole incident changed completely.","Using a fool to rob people was one thing.","Beating that fool half to death was another.","Cheng Gang clenched his fist, his knuckles cracking loudly. He stared coldly at the Baldy across from him.","Although the Third Fool lying on the ground had just been using the steel pipe to stab someone in the ass, anyone could see that he had no idea what he was doing.","He was merely a tool for these villains to make money—a pitiful man who lacked even the most basic ability to distinguish right from wrong.","And now, this tool had not only been exploited but beaten until his head was split open.","This gang of thugs had no humanity at all. They were worse than animals!","“What the hell are you looking at?”","The Baldy covered his butt with one hand and pointed the bloodstained steel pipe at Cheng Gang with the other, cursing viciously. “Keep staring and I’ll gouge your eyes out too! Now hurry up and hand over your money, or you’ll end up just like him!”","Cheng Gang looked at him without saying a word. He simply raised his right hand.","It was a signal.","The next instant—","Clatter!","The doors of the dozen or so buses behind him opened simultaneously.","Two young men in black suits stepped down from each bus. Each wore a dragon-shaped insignia on his chest.","One, two, three, four, five...","More and more appeared.","Before long, nearly thirty men in black were standing behind Cheng Gang. With a sharp swish, they all drew their telescopic batons.","The sneer on the Baldy’s face froze.","The thugs behind him instinctively took several steps backward.","Even the two wolfhounds that had been baring their teeth and looking ferocious tucked their tails between their legs and hid behind their owner. They whimpered softly, not daring to bark.","That was the pressure created by sheer presence.","Where the hell had all these gangster-looking men come from?","“You... what do you want?”","“You think you can bully us just because you outnumber us? You people have no honor! Let me tell you, this road belongs to Lord Tiger. Try laying a finger on me and see what happens!”","As he shouted, the Baldy pushed his lackeys in front of him for protection.","“Listen up! I’m warning you, Lord Tiger is somebody important in BS Province!”","“If you touch me, Lord Tiger won’t let you get away with it!”","Cheng Gang could not be bothered to waste any more words on him. He drew his telescopic baton and strode forward. The thirty men in black followed in unison.","Their momentum was like dark clouds pressing down on a city, or a black tide surging toward the Baldy.","The Baldy limped backward, cursing his luck inwardly.","Damn it, they had kicked an iron plate this time!","Who could have guessed that this tour bus convoy from out of town would be carrying a group of gangsters even more intimidating than they were?","“Who... who the hell are you people?”","Cheng Gang finally spoke.","“Which road we walk isn’t important. What matters is that you made three mistakes today.”","“First, you blocked our vehicles.”","“Second, you injured someone.”","“Third, you used a disabled person to commit a crime. You’re worse than animals!”","“People like you deserve to be executed on the spot!”","Although the Baldy was frightened, he still shouted with false bravado, “Stop pretending to be some kind of hero! You’re only relying on your numbers. If you’ve got the guts, fight me one-on-one!”","No one paid him any attention.","“Fine! Fine! You win! You’ve got more people! I’ll take the loss!”","He waved at the thugs shielding him. “What are you standing around for? Let’s go!”","The thugs had wanted to run for a long time. Hearing this, they immediately turned and prepared to flee.","“Stop!” Cheng Gang immediately shouted, bringing them to a halt.","“Did I say you could leave?”","The gangsters froze in fear.","Baldy turned around and glared at him darkly. “Brother, we’ve already admitted defeat. What else do you want?”","Cheng Gang couldn’t be bothered to waste any more words on him. He simply waved his hand.","“Give them a good beating!”","The next moment, all thirty men in black moved at once.","There were no shouts or curses. Aside from the whooshing sound of the batons cutting through the air and the dull thuds as they struck flesh, there was almost no unnecessary noise at all.","Their seriousness and efficiency were on full display!","Thud! Thud! Thud!","Every blow was clean, precise, and vicious.","They struck the gangsters’ thighs, arms, shoulders, backs—in places that wouldn’t damage their internal organs but would still make them suffer indescribable pain.","In less than thirty seconds, all dozen or so gangsters were sprawled on the ground, groaning miserably—including Baldy.","Only the few intellectually disabled young men remained standing off to the side, drooling and clapping their hands as they laughed foolishly.","“Yay! Yay!”","“Good beating!”","“Hehehe... It’s like setting off firecrackers...”","As the gang’s leader, Baldy naturally received some “special attention.”","Cheng Gang had even specifically ordered his men to put a special padded vest on him.","Baldy struggled desperately, shouting nonstop, “They’re beating people! Outsiders are beating people! Is there no law anymore?”","Cheng Gang walked over to him and, without a word, gave him another round of wild punches.","He didn’t stop until Baldy had been beaten into complete submission and was vomiting uncontrollably.","“I’ve got to hand it to that big lawyer—the latest improved version of this vest really works. This guy looks like he’s just drunk, and even a medical examination won’t find any injuries on him.”","“Though it wouldn’t matter even if they did. We were acting in defense of others.”","Cheng Gang muttered this under his breath as he looked at his fists. Then he pulled out his phone and dialed a number.","“Hello, emergency services?”","“I’d like to report a crime.”","Baldy, who was still vomiting nearby, nearly bulged his eyes out of their sockets when he heard those words.","What?","You beat us up and then called the police yourselves?","Aren’t you gangsters?","Do gangsters call the police? Don’t you people have any rules?","“This is a section of Provincial Road XX in XX Province. A group of people blocked the road, robbed passersby, and injured an intellectually disabled person. Yes! The victim is bleeding and needs an ambulance. The attackers have already been subdued. There are twenty-three of them in total—not one got away...”","After hanging up, Cheng Gang turned around and instructed the men behind him, “Clear the roadblocks. Let the bus pass first. Arrange for the families to stay at a hotel in the city. We’ll remain here and keep an eye on these people until the police arrive.”","“Yes!”","Lying on the ground, Baldy watched as the men in black busied themselves—some clearing the roadblocks, some caring for the injured, and others guarding the gangsters. Everyone had a clear assignment, and the whole operation was orderly and efficient.","He suddenly felt a little dazed.","Just what kind of people were these men?","If they were gangsters, why would they dare call the police themselves?","But if they were good people, why were they more ruthless than anyone else?","“You... just who are you people?” Baldy couldn’t help asking again.","Cheng Gang glanced at him and calmly replied with two words:","“Leifeng!”","Baldy: ???"]},{"number":834,"title":"Chapter 834: 835, Qi Tianhu","paragraphs":["On the bus.","Through the windows, the employees’ family members had seen everything that had just happened.","First, the intellectually disabled young man had stabbed Baldy in the butt. Then Baldy, enraged and humiliated, had smashed the young man over the head. After that, Cheng Gang had led his men out of the bus and taken down more than a dozen thugs in twenty seconds.","There hadn’t been a single dull moment. Everyone had watched with their hearts pounding—both terrified and exhilarated.","Their first thought was: Was the company their children worked for actually legitimate?","Why did it feel even more ruthless than the gangs?","But soon, when they saw the gang of roadblock robbers beaten into complete submission, many of them began to see the bright side. They found it deeply satisfying.","“My goodness, those young men are incredible!”","“There were more than twenty of them, and they were all knocked down in the blink of an eye. I didn’t even see how they struck!”","“My Erniu works for the Wanlong Association. He once told me that everyone at his company was really good at fighting. I thought he was just bragging, but it turns out it’s true.”","“‘Good at fighting’? That’s an understatement! They’re unbelievably tough. It feels like each one could take on ten men.”","“Just look at their skills, their presence, those matching black suits... Tsk, tsk, tsk. They look even more like gangsters than the ones on television.”","“What do you mean, ‘like’? They are gangsters! Look at the dragon emblem on their chests. That’s their gang insignia.”","“Isn’t that the company logo?”","“No!”","An elderly man began analyzing the matter with great seriousness.","“When I was young, I spent some time in the provincial capital. I heard the street toughs say that the gangs in Hong Kong all carried themselves like this—matching clothes, matching insignias, and when the order was given, they attacked without hesitation. They weren’t even afraid of the police. That kind of presence was something ordinary gangs simply didn’t have!”","The old woman beside him gave him a smack. “You old fool, what nonsense are you talking about? It’s a legitimate company. What does it have to do with gangs?”","“Could a legitimate company be this good at fighting?”","“That’s called security. Don’t you know anything about security? All major companies have security personnel.”","“I’ve seen security guards too—the kind standing at the gates of residential compounds. They’re either old men or fellows with enormous bellies who can barely run. But look at these young men. Is there a single one of them who’s fat? They’re all lean and wiry. You can tell at a glance that they fight regularly and know what they’re doing.”","“Now that you mention it... you’re right.”","The old man grew more and more enthusiastic. Lowering his voice, he said mysteriously, “Let me tell you all something. I suspect that this Wanlong Association is a legitimate company on the surface, but in reality... Heh heh. You know what I mean.”","“Know what? Stop talking nonsense, you old man.”","“I’m not talking nonsense. Think about it. What legitimate company would call itself the ‘Wanlong Association’? The name alone has a strong underworld flavor. And what legitimate company offers free tours to its employees’ parents? What do you call that? Buying people’s loyalty! That’s exactly how the underworld wins people over.”","The old woman was so angry that her eyes nearly rolled back into her head. “So you’re saying our children have joined a gang?”","“I never said that.”","The old man hurriedly waved his hands, though his mouth was being much more honest than he was.","“But let’s be fair—even if it is a gang, it’s a good gang. Look at them. They saw injustice and stepped in to help. They even protected us elderly people. They have principles. They’re much better than those bullies who only pick on the weak.”","“Of course they are! Could our children’s company really be the sort of gutter-level gang those thugs belong to? If it really is a gang, then it’s the respectable, honorable kind—the orthodox sect of the underworld!”","A middle-aged woman beside them joined in. “I think Uncle is right. Look at those young men. They may look a little intimidating, but they really do seem upright.”","“Put that way... there’s nothing wrong with joining such an honorable gang, is there?”","“Exactly! My son works in Wanlong Association Logistics. He told me their company is extremely legitimate. They even pay into the five kinds of social insurance and the housing fund.”","“My daughter works as a clerk at Wanlong Supermarket. She said their company even provides those benefits to the women who sweep the floors, and there’s a year-end bonus too. She got seven or eight thousand yuan last year.”","“With benefits that good, I’d accept it even if it were a gang!”","“Exactly! Who cares whether it’s a gang or not? As long as it treats our children well and treats us old folks well, then it’s a good organization!”","“And think about it. Our children work for such a powerful company. Who would dare bully us in the future? If we run into some stupid thugs, we just have to mention the Wanlong Association. They’ll be scared stiff!”","“That’s right! I’m going to say exactly that when I go back to the village. My son works for the Wanlong Association! Let’s see who dares steal vegetables from my fields now!”","“Hahaha...”","The bus erupted in laughter. The tension and fear from moments earlier vanished amid the cheerful voices.","Everyone felt much more at ease.","They were even a little proud.","Just look. This was the company their children worked for.","What presence!","What prestige!","What a sense of security!","Before long, several police cars and an ambulance arrived at the scene.","The ambulance carried Third Fool away.","The police, meanwhile, took Baldy and all his men into custody.","Leading the team was a veteran police officer in his forties, a man surnamed Liu. Two bars and two stars adorned his shoulders.","He surveyed the scene, then glanced at the group of men in black standing in neat formation. His brows furrowed slightly.","“Who’s in charge?”","“I am.” Cheng Gang stepped forward.","“Did your people beat these men?”","“Yes.”","“Why?”","“They blocked the road and attempted to rob us. They also injured a mentally disabled person. We were acting in self-defense and intervening to help a victim.”","Officer Liu looked him and the group of men behind him up and down, then glanced at the gangsters sprawled on the ground, their faces swollen and bruised.","Are you really claiming self-defense?","With the way you’re dressed and the numbers you have, who was actually defending themselves from whom?","“Which company are you with?”","“The Security Department of Wanlonghui Group in Pearl City.”","Cheng Gang took his identification card from his pocket and handed it over with both hands.","Officer Liu accepted it and carefully examined it.","The identification was genuine, the company was legitimate, and it even held the proper security qualifications.","What’s more, he had heard of Wanlonghui Group.","During last year’s major earthquake, the company—based in another province—had reportedly donated more than two billion yuan. It was quite well known throughout the province.","He then asked Cheng Gang a few more basic questions, and Cheng Gang answered them clearly and confidently.","“All right. I have a general understanding of the situation. Send a few people back with me to make statements. The rest of you can leave.”","“Thank you, Officer.”","Cheng Gang turned around and gave a few instructions to the men behind him. Then he took two of them and got into the police car with Officer Liu.","Baldy and his men were also forced into the police car.","Before leaving, Baldy glared viciously at Cheng Gang and threatened him in a low voice. “Just you wait! Once I’m out, you’ll regret this. Lord Tiger won’t let you off!”","Cheng Gang wasn’t the least bit intimidated. He merely replied, “Bring it on.”","......","Jinchuan City.","The chairman’s office of Tiger Might Group.","A middle-aged man with a square face, thick eyebrows, and eyes as sharp as an eagle’s was standing before the floor-to-ceiling windows, looking down over the city.","He held a glass of whiskey in his hand, and the authority he had accumulated from years at the top radiated from him like an oppressive force.","This man was the chairman of Tiger Might Group, Qi Tianhu, better known as “Lord Tiger.”","After a secretary-looking man knocked and entered the office, Qi Tianhu did not turn around. With his back to the newcomer, he asked in a deep voice, “General Manager Yang of Wanlonghui Group is coming here tomorrow, isn’t he?”","“Yes, Boss. I hear he’s coming to attend a city investment-promotion seminar. His itinerary has already been confirmed.”","“Perfect. Arrange a meeting with him. Pick a place—I’ll take him out to dinner.”","“Yes, Boss. I’ll arrange it right away.”","After the secretary left, Qi Tianhu remained standing before the floor-to-ceiling windows, his gaze fixed on the enormous new building in the city center not far away.","The main structure of the building was already complete, and a banner hung from its roof.","“Wanlong Plaza Grand Opening Coming Soon—All Major Brands and Businesses Are Welcome to Set Up Shop!”","Qi Tianhu stared at those words for a long while. Then he raised his hand and downed the rest of his whiskey.","“Wanlonghui... I hope this General Manager Yang knows how to play ball. Otherwise...”","Crash!","The glass in his hand dropped straight into the trash can."]},{"number":835,"title":"Chapter 835: 836, Cruel","paragraphs":["Tiger Might Group, Chairman’s Office.","Qi Tianhu had just tossed his wineglass into the trash can when the office door was suddenly shoved open from outside.","“Dad! Something’s happened!”","A young man who looked to be around twenty-four or twenty-five barged in. He was dressed head to toe in designer brands, with dyed blond hair. His handsome features had inherited some of Qi Tianhu’s heroic bearing, but there was an unsettling, sinister look in his eyes.","This was Qi Tianhu’s only son, Qi Licheng.","Qi Tianhu turned around, frowning slightly. “What’s with the panic? Have some composure.”","“I’m not panicking, Dad. I’m furious!”","Qi Licheng dropped heavily onto the sofa, picked up the bottle of wine on the table, and poured himself a glass. After taking a sip, he said, “There’s trouble at the Dawan Coal Mine again. They’re complaining that our offer is too low and saying they’re going to sell the mine to some businessman from out of town.”","“Oh? Is that so?”","Qi Tianhu walked over to the desk and sat down, asking calmly, “How did you handle it?”","Qi Licheng set his glass on the table, a vicious look appearing on his face. “I had someone investigate the outsider’s background. He’s from JZ Province and brought two hundred million with him. He thinks he can come to our territory and grab a bargain? I’ve already sent A Jiu and the others to have a talk with him.”","“I want those outsiders to understand something. Around Jinchuan City, when it comes to coal, anyone who dares to touch it besides Tiger Might Group is looking for death!”","Qi Tianhu nodded. “Are the men you arranged clean?”","“Don’t worry, Dad.”","Qi Licheng thumped his chest confidently. “The people I sent with A Jiu all have clean backgrounds. They’re complete strangers here. Even if the police investigate, they won’t be able to trace anything back to us. Besides, even if something really happens, we can settle it with a little money.”","Qi Tianhu did not respond. He simply stared at him in silence.","Under his father’s gaze, Qi Licheng began to feel uneasy and quickly changed the subject. “Dad, you have no idea. Ever since we took control of Dawan Coal Mine, along with the mines in several surrounding cities, we’ve completely monopolized the local coal market. From now on, we’ll be the ones setting the coal prices. Even the chemical plants have to beg us to sell them coal.”","Qi Tianhu gave a noncommittal grunt before saying, “You’ve done a decent job with the coal mines. But that’s not why I called you here today.”","“Then what is it, Dad?”","Qi Tianhu pointed out the window. “See that building?”","Qi Licheng stood up and followed his father’s finger to the floor-to-ceiling window. His eyes immediately lit up.","“Wanlong Plaza? Dad, are you finally going to make a move against the Wanlonghui?”","Wanlonghui Group was a company that had suddenly emerged the previous year.","The company was unbelievably wealthy. It had reportedly donated two billion yuan to disaster-stricken areas to build schools, and later invested in shopping malls and other projects across several nearby cities. Altogether, it had poured at least five or six billion yuan into the region.","It was a massive piece of low-hanging fruit.","Not to mention anything else, simply securing any one of Wanlonghui Group’s construction projects—earthworks, building materials, or the like—would bring in enormous profits.","The Tiger Might Group had operated in several surrounding cities for many years and was the undisputed local powerhouse. Aside from coal, it had its hands in everything related to construction: building materials, sand and gravel, concrete, transportation...","By their usual standards, they should have been able to secure the contracts for Wanlonghui Group’s projects, including the supply of construction materials.","After all, in the major construction projects across the surrounding cities, at least sixty percent of the real estate developments used building materials supplied by Tiger Might Group.","With such absolute control, the developers basically had to cater to their wishes.","If they said whose sand and gravel to use, that was what got used. If they said whose cement to use, that was what got used.","They were domineering to the extreme!","Wanlonghui, however, was the sole exception. The company simply refused to play along.","Whether it was building plazas or schools, the companies that won the bids were all from out of town. All the construction materials were transported in from elsewhere, completely shutting Tiger Might Group out.","They had sent people to negotiate, but the person in charge had given them only one explanation:","Their qualifications did not meet the requirements.","That had infuriated father and son alike.","In the Jinchuan area, no one had ever dared to show them such disrespect.","But they had held back from taking action—not because they were easygoing, but because they had been waiting for the right opportunity.","Qi Tianhu stood up, clasped his hands behind his back, and walked over to his son. He said slowly, “When the earthquake struck last year, Wanlonghui Group was at the center of attention. The officials were watching them, and the media were watching them too. We couldn’t make a move. But now, more than a year has passed and the spotlight has faded. It’s our turn.”","Qi Licheng immediately grew excited. “Tell me what to do, Dad. How about I gather some men and head straight to their construction sites? We’ll cause a disturbance and force them to shut down.”","“Not yet.”","Qi Tianhu shook his head. “I just received word that Wanlonghui Group has sent a general manager surnamed Yang here to attend the investment promotion conference in Jingchuan. I’ve already had someone invite him. Tomorrow night, we’ll take General Manager Yang out for dinner. You’re coming too.”","“Dinner?”","Qi Licheng’s eyes shifted, and he immediately understood his father’s intention. “You mean we offer them courtesy first, then use force if that doesn’t work?”","Qi Tianhu nodded. “If we can reach an agreement, then we will. If we truly can’t, you’ll know what to do.”","Qi Licheng understood at once. A sinister smile spread across his face.","“Don’t worry, Dad. I know exactly what to do. If that man surnamed Yang knows how to behave and obediently hands those contracts over to us, then everything will be fine. But if he refuses to cooperate, I’ll make sure he learns what it means to regret ever being born!”","Qi Tianhu was just about to say something else when someone suddenly knocked on the office door.","“Come in.”","The door opened, and a young man wearing a black tank top and sporting tattoos on his arms walked inside.","As soon as he entered, he went straight to Qi Licheng, a fawning smile plastered across his face.","“Young Master Cheng, I need to speak with you about something.”","Qi Licheng’s expression changed slightly. He instinctively glanced at his father.","Qi Tianhu’s gaze swept over the bald young man before turning to his son. “Who is this?”","“Dad, this is... this is one of my men. His name is Wumao.” Qi Licheng sounded somewhat uneasy.","Wumao hurriedly bowed and nodded obsequiously at Qi Tianhu. “Greetings, Lord Tiger! Greetings, Lord Tiger! Sorry to disturb you, sir!”","Qi Tianhu waved his hand. “If you have business to attend to, go on.”","“Dad, then we’ll be leaving.”","With that, he took Wumao and left the company, driving to a nightclub they frequented.","The moment they entered a private room and shut the door, Qi Licheng kicked Wumao to the floor, despite the latter still wearing a flattering smile. His expression was frighteningly vicious.","“Who the hell told you to come looking for me at the company?”","“Didn’t I tell you? You’re not allowed to come to the company! You’re not allowed to come to the company! Are you fucking deaf?”","“Hold him down!”","The two underlings who had followed them inside immediately stepped forward and pinned Wumao firmly to the floor.","Qi Licheng pulled a folding knife from his waist, preparing to cut the man’s ear off on the spot as a warning to the others.","Wumao was scared out of his wits and struggled desperately. “I was wrong! Young Master Cheng, I was wrong!”","“I had something urgent to report to you. I tried calling, but I couldn’t get through. I had no choice but to come find you!”","“Young Master Cheng, please spare me this once! Please!”","Qi Licheng stopped and said coldly, “Talk. What’s so urgent?”","“Young Master Cheng, something terrible has happened! The roadblock we set up on the provincial highway was taken out today!”","Qi Licheng’s face instantly turned livid. He grabbed Wumao by the collar and roared, “What the hell did you just say?”","Wumao stammered, “Young... Young Master Cheng, a convoy of long-distance buses from out of town passed through today. Our men stopped them... stopped them to collect a little toll. But then a group of men in black got off the bus. Without saying a word, they beat up all our people and... and called the police.”","“The police came?”","“They... they did.”","Wumao said with a mournful expression, “There were more than twenty of them. They were all taken away, and... and even those idiots were dragged off too.”","Qi Licheng released his collar, his expression dark and terrifying.","There was only one thought in his mind: His father absolutely could not find out about this.","A few months ago, he had gone to the gambling capital for several days and lost nearly fifty million yuan. His father still knew nothing about it.","Although Tiger Might Group was wealthy and powerful, Qi Tianhu kept a very tight rein on his son’s spending. He gave him a fixed allowance of one million yuan a month, and not a penny more.","One million yuan was enough for an ordinary person in Jinchuan City to live on for the rest of his life.","But for a wastrel like Qi Licheng, who spent money like water, it wasn’t even enough to fill the gaps between his teeth.","A single bet at the gambling table could easily run into hundreds of thousands. Losing three to five million in one night was nothing unusual. Adding in his spending elsewhere, his monthly allowance was nowhere near enough.","But with the money running out, he didn’t dare ask his father for more.","Qi Tianhu doted on him, but he wasn’t indulgent without limits. If he found out that his son had gambled away so much money, he could very well beat his legs until they were broken.","That was why Qi Licheng had taken Wumao and his gang under his wing.","These thugs were hardly impressive, but they had plenty of shady ways to make money. Taking a few idiots with them, they set up roadblocks on remote provincial and county roads to extort passing motorists. Even in a single day, they could rake in a considerable sum.","With the addition of other illicit sources of income, Qi Licheng also collected a substantial amount in monthly kickbacks.","Normally, as long as nothing major happened, his father would never find out.","But now this idiot had actually come running to the group headquarters!","Given his father’s shrewdness, if he really started investigating, he would certainly uncover the truth.","And if those men who had been arrested started talking and told the police that the roadblock was connected to him, Qi Licheng would definitely get a beating.","The more Qi Licheng thought about it, the angrier he became. He crouched down again and looked at Wumao, who was being held to the ground. A smile of utterly savage cruelty slowly spread across his face.","“Wumao, although you had a reason for coming, there’s one thing I hate most in this world: a dog that refuses to obey.”","“Since you’ve ignored my orders, there’s no point in keeping this ear.”","“No... No! Young Master Cheng, please! Give me one more chance! I’ll never do it again! Never!”","Wumao shook his head frantically, tears and snot streaming down his face. A dark patch had also spread across the front of his pants.","Qi Licheng frowned and took half a step back in disgust.","“Hold his head down!”","The two underlings immediately pressed Wumao’s head firmly against the ground, leaving him unable to move.","“Young... Young Master Cheng! Don’t! Please...”","“Don’t move. If you do, my hand might slip, and I won’t just cut off your ear.”","Qi Licheng’s voice was ice-cold, sending chills down the spine.","Wumao instantly froze, his entire body trembling like a leaf.","Qi Licheng didn’t hesitate in the slightest. He lowered his wrist and slashed downward with force.","“Ahhh!!!”"]},{"number":836,"title":"Chapter 836: 837, Condolences to Students.","paragraphs":["By the time Liu Yutong arrived at the fifth school, it was already past ten in the morning.","The school was located in a place called Qingyu Town. When an earthquake struck the previous year, half of the town’s elementary school collapsed. Fortunately, the school had been holding its sports day that day, so all the students were outside and no one was injured.","The new school, funded and built by the Wanlong Charity Foundation, stood in the newly developed part of the town.","It was a brand-new, three-story school building with pale yellow walls and a blue roof. The playground had a rubber running track. Although the grounds were not large, they had all the necessary facilities.","Several large characters were embedded above the school building:","WANLONG HOPE ELEMENTARY SCHOOL","As soon as Liu Yutong’s convoy came to a stop, she saw that the school entrance was packed with people.","The principal was a woman in her fifties whose surname was Zhou. Behind her stood all the teachers and students in the school.","The students wore matching uniforms and bright red scarves. They stood perfectly straight, their eyes shining as they watched the convoy slowly approach.","“Welcome, Director Liu! Welcome to our school for an inspection!”","Principal Zhou hurried forward and clasped Liu Yutong’s hands tightly.","After all, this was the first time the chairwoman of Wanlonghui Group had personally come to inspect the school, so Principal Zhou naturally regarded it as a very important occasion. She had begun preparing several days in advance.","Liu Yutong smiled as she held the principal’s hands. “Principal Zhou, you’re too kind. I’m just here to see the children and find out whether the school needs any further assistance.”","“We already have everything we need—more than enough.”","“Director Liu, you have no idea. After last year’s earthquake, all the buildings at our school collapsed. The children could only attend classes in tents. It was only after your company donated money to build this new school that they finally had a proper place to study.”","“Director Liu, on behalf of all the teachers, students, and townspeople, I want to thank you!”","Liu Yutong said, “Principal Zhou, you’re making too much of it. This is simply what we ought to do.”","Principal Zhou wiped the corners of her eyes, then turned to the students and called out, “Children, this is Sister Liu, the person who built this new school for you. Shall we all thank Sister Liu together?”","“Thank you, Sister Liu!” the children shouted in unison.","Looking at those young, innocent faces, Liu Yutong felt a warm current well up inside her.","She bent down and spoke to a little girl standing at the front. “What’s your name?”","The girl was a little shy. Her cheeks flushed as she said softly, “My name is... Zhang Xiaoya.”","“Xiaoya, what a lovely name.”","“Do you like your new school?”","“Yes!”","“The classrooms are so big, and we have new desks and chairs. There’s even air-conditioning, so it doesn’t get hot during class in the summer.”","“That’s good to hear.”","Liu Yutong straightened up and said to Principal Zhou, “Principal Zhou, I brought some gifts for the children. Would you like us to hand them out now or later?”","“Chairman Liu, you really shouldn’t have gone to so much trouble. This is too generous.”","“It’s nothing. It’s just a small token of my appreciation.”","Liu Yutong waved her hand, and her assistant, Yun Cheng, immediately led several people in unloading the gifts from the truck.","There were schoolbags, stationery sets, candy and snacks, as well as a red envelope for every child. Everything was neatly arranged along the edge of the playground.","The moment the children saw the brand-new schoolbags and stationery, their eyes lit up.","“Wow! New schoolbags!”","“There are pencil cases too, with little animals on them!”","“Mine has a bunny!”","“Mine has a red panda!”","“So cute...”","The children chattered excitedly, their faces filled with delight.","Liu Yutong personally handed the gifts to the children one by one. Each time, she would bend down to say a few words to the child and gently pat them on the head.","The last child in line was a thin, undersized boy wearing a school uniform several sizes too large for him. The sleeves had been rolled up several times, revealing his slender wrists, as though his arms were too thin to hold the clothes in place.","“Thank you... Thank you, Sister,” he murmured.","Liu Yutong crouched down and looked at him. “What’s your name?”","“I... My name is Wang Xiaoshu.”","“Xiaoshu, how old are you?”","“I’m ten.”","The boy was ten years old, yet he looked only seven or eight. He was so thin that it broke her heart.","Liu Yutong felt a pang in her chest and asked, “Who else is there in your family?”","Wang Xiaoshu lowered his head and answered quietly, “My grandmother, and... my older brother.”","“What about your parents?”","“My parents... they didn’t make it through the earthquake.”","Seeing the tears glimmering in his eyes, Liu Yutong reached out and gently pulled him into her arms, patting his back.","“Xiaoshu, study hard. If you make it to college one day, you’ll be able to live a better life.”","“Okay!” Wang Xiaoshu nodded vigorously.","After the gifts had been handed out, Principal Zhou took Liu Yutong on a tour of the school’s classrooms, library, dormitories, and computer room.","The computer room contained more than a dozen computers. Their specifications were not particularly impressive, but they were perfectly adequate for the students’ needs.","“All of these were donated by the Wanlong Charity Foundation,” Principal Zhou said with emotion. “The children had never even seen a computer before. Now they have computer classes every week, and they love them. They come running over early every time, just to wait for class to begin.”","Liu Yutong nodded. “Education has to keep pace with the times. It’s good for the children’s development to be exposed to new things from an early age.”","By the time they finished touring the school, it was noon.","Principal Zhou insisted that Liu Yutong stay for lunch.","“Director Liu, the cafeteria is ready. It’s just simple home-style food, so please don’t look down on it.”","Liu Yutong smiled. “Why would I? I love home-style cooking.”","The cafeteria was in a row of bungalows behind the main school building. Inside were more than a dozen long tables.","The children had already lined up and taken their seats. Each had a stainless-steel tray in front of them, and they sat in neat rows.","The day’s dishes were braised potatoes with pork, marinated chicken legs, stir-fried bok choy, and seaweed-and-egg-drop soup.","After getting her food, Liu Yutong carried her tray over and sat among the children.","“Sister Liu, sit here!”","“Sit with me! My spot is clean!”","“...”","The children competed to invite her over.","With a smile, Liu Yutong sat down beside Wang Xiaoshu.","The food on her tray tasted quite good. The potatoes were tender, and the meat was flavorful.","But when she glanced at Wang Xiaoshu’s tray, she froze.","He hadn’t touched the chicken leg or the pork. They were both piled carefully to one side. He was eating only the potatoes and bok choy.","“Xiaoshu, why aren’t you eating your chicken leg? Don’t you like it?”","Wang Xiaoshu quickly shook his head. “No, I like it!”","“Then why aren’t you eating it?”","He lowered his head and whispered, “I... I want to take it home for Grandma. She hasn’t had meat in a long time.”","Liu Yutong’s heart clenched painfully, and her nose began to sting.","She looked at the other children’s trays. Besides Xiaoshu, two girls had also left their chicken legs untouched, carefully wrapping them in plastic bags and setting them aside.","After thinking for a moment, she called Lan Die over.","“Contact our warehouse and see if we can arrange for a shipment of ready-to-eat marinated chicken legs and duck legs. Since these children are reluctant to eat them, let’s prepare some more for them to take home.”","Wanlong Supermarket was extremely strict when it came to selecting products—so strict that it was almost harsh. Although the products were ready-to-eat, every step of the preparation process was fully traceable, and the hygiene standards were exceptionally high. Parents could rest assured that their children would be perfectly safe eating them.","“All right. I’ll call someone right away and have them delivered.”","After finishing their meal, they prepared to leave.","Liu Yutong said to Principal Zhou, “From now on, the school cafeteria’s meals need to be improved. Every meal must include at least two meat dishes, one vegetable dish, and a soup. I’ll cover the cost.”","Principal Zhou was so moved that he hardly knew what to say. He could only thank her repeatedly.","Liu Yutong was just about to get into the car when she suddenly thought of something else and asked, “By the way, Principal Zhou, does our school have any students from especially impoverished families?”","Principal Zhou thought for a moment before replying, “There are a few. The one in the most difficult situation is Wang Xiaoshu’s family. His parents and grandfather are all gone, and his grandmother is in poor health and has to take medicine year-round. The family survives on a few small plots of land and welfare payments. He also has an older brother named Wang Dashu, but there’s something wrong with his mind—his intellectual development isn’t normal. He seems to have gone missing some time ago, and they still haven’t found him.”","Liu Yutong frowned. “Gone missing? Did you report it to the police?”","Principal Zhou replied, “We did, but there hasn’t been any news.”","“For a child with an intellectual disability like his, it’s very difficult to find him once he goes missing. Xiaoshu has had such a hard life. He’s still so young, yet he has to take care of his grandmother while attending school. It’s truly not easy.”","Liu Yutong was silent for a moment before asking, “Principal Zhou, does Xiaoshu’s family live far from here?”","“Not far. They’re in the village behind the school. It’s only a little over ten minutes on foot.”","“Then please take me there to have a look.”","Principal Zhou quickly nodded. “Of course, of course. I’ll take you there.”"]},{"number":837,"title":"Chapter 837: 838, Yang Xin Meets Xu Shishi","paragraphs":["Wang Xiaoshu’s home was in Wangjia Village, below Qingyu Town, about five kilometers away.","The village was small, with only a few dozen households. Most of the residents were elderly people and children, while the younger adults had all gone elsewhere to find work.","Wang Xiaoshu’s house stood at the very back of the village. The original two adobe rooms had collapsed in the earthquake, but the government had allocated funds to rebuild them. The replacement was a two-room bungalow with red-brick walls, white plaster, and concrete floors. It wasn’t anything fancy, but at least it provided shelter from the wind and rain.","When Liu Yutong and the others arrived, Xiaoshu’s grandmother was lying crookedly on a wooden bed against the wall. She was so thin that she looked like skin stretched over bones, with deeply sunken eye sockets. Her eyes were half closed, and she mumbled something indistinctly.","“Xiaoshu’s grandmother is having another episode.”","Principal Zhou sighed from the side and explained in a low voice, “The old lady is lucid sometimes and confused at other times. From the looks of it, she probably only has a few months left.”","Liu Yutong sat down beside the bed and gently took the old woman’s hand.","“Grandma, I’m Xiaoshu’s older sister. I’ve come to see you.”","The old woman’s cloudy eyes shifted slightly. In a slurred voice, she asked, “X... Xiaoshu... Dashu... Has Dashu come back?”","Liu Yutong’s nose stung, and an indescribable sadness welled up inside her.","She took an envelope from her bag and placed it in the old woman’s hand. It contained five thousand yuan.","“This is a little something from me. Use it to buy some nutritious food.”","The old woman seemed to have no idea that she was holding money. She continued mumbling, “Dashu... Has Dashu come back?”","Liu Yutong thought to herself that although the old woman was so confused she could no longer recognize people, she could still remember her grandson’s name.","Not knowing what else to say, Liu Yutong could only explain once again that she wasn’t Xiaoshu.","The old woman’s hand was thin as a withered branch, yet she still clung tightly to Liu Yutong’s hand.","“Dashu, my eldest grandson... W-when did you come back? Why has your hair grown so long?”","“Grandma, Dashu will come back. He went to buy you something delicious. You need to take good care of yourself. If he comes home and sees how thin you’ve become, it will break his heart.”","The old woman seemed to hear her, though perhaps she didn’t. She continued mumbling indistinctly, her voice growing softer and softer, until she gradually closed her eyes and fell asleep.","Liu Yutong gently placed her hand back beneath the quilt, then stood and walked outside.","In the courtyard, Wang Xiaoshu had already been brought home. The moment he saw Liu Yutong, his eyes reddened.","“Sister, does that mean you can’t find my brother?”","Liu Yutong walked over and patted him on the head.","“Xiaoshu, when did your brother go missing?”","Wang Xiaoshu thought for a moment, his voice muffled. “Almost a month ago. My brother was still at home when I went to school that morning, but when I came back in the afternoon, he was gone.”","“Did you report it to the police?”","“We did.”","“The police came and asked us some questions. They also put up missing-person notices in town, but they still haven’t found him.”","“Mm.”","Liu Yutong turned to Yun Cheng. “Go around the village and ask every household if anyone knows what happened before or after Dashu disappeared.”","“Yes.”","Yun Cheng led several people out of the courtyard and split up around the village to gather information.","Liu Yutong continued asking Wang Xiaoshu questions.","“Xiaoshu, where did your brother usually like to go?”","Wang Xiaoshu thought about it, then pointed toward a stream at the foot of the mountain.","“My brother liked playing by the stream. He also liked going to town on market days to watch people play the ring-toss games. But he could always find his way home on his own.”","“Was anything unusual about your brother on the day he went missing?”","“My brother...”","“...”","Liu Yutong spent nearly an hour talking with Wang Xiaoshu before Yun Cheng finally returned.","“Young Lady, we found out a few things.”","“Go on.”","“Two people with intellectual disabilities have gone missing from this village in the past six months. One is Wang Xiaoshu’s brother, Wang Dashu. The other is a twenty-four-year-old named Cheng Erdan, who was born with an intellectual disability. However, Cheng Erdan’s family doesn’t seem willing to talk about it. They appear to be deliberately avoiding the subject.”","“Avoiding it?”","“They seem to think that losing him might actually be a relief—that it would be better if he were gone.”","Liu Yutong furrowed her delicate brows.","The words sounded harsh, but she knew that for many impoverished rural families, a child who was unable to work and needed constant care was indeed a heavy burden.","If the family no longer wanted to search for him, she couldn’t really condemn them.","“Did you find any other leads? For example, whether they came into contact with anyone before disappearing, or whether they rode in any vehicles?”","Yun Cheng shook his head. “The villagers all said they hadn’t noticed anything. Those two were always wandering around on their own, and since the village is mostly populated by elderly people, no one paid particular attention to where the two mentally disabled men went.”","Liu Yutong thought for a moment before saying, “Have the people we have stationed in Jingchuan keep a close watch for any news. Also, find out their physical descriptions and, if possible, get photographs printed on some flyers.”","Two people with intellectual disabilities had disappeared from the same remote village, one after the other.","One family had stopped searching after only a few days, while the other was still waiting for their missing family member to come home.","No matter how she looked at it, something about the situation seemed wrong.","Unfortunately, she had too little information at present. Even if she wanted to investigate, she had no place to begin. For now, she could only have people keep watch.","Hopefully, she was just imagining things.","“All right.”","Yun Cheng nodded and turned to make the arrangements.","Liu Yutong looked back at Wang Xiaoshu and comforted him. “Xiaoshu, your sister will help you find your brother. You need to study hard and take good care of your grandmother, understand?”","Wang Xiaoshu nodded vigorously. “I understand. Thank you, Sister!”","After giving him a few more instructions, Liu Yutong said to Principal Zhou, “Principal Zhou, I’ve seen Xiaoshu’s situation. From now on, I’ll have someone deposit a monthly living allowance into his account. I hope you can help keep an eye on him.”","Principal Zhou hurriedly nodded. “Director Liu, you can rest assured. I’ll personally make sure everything is taken care of.”","“And as for the other students at the school whose families are struggling, please compile a list for me. I’ll sponsor them all at the same time.”","“Of course, of course! Director Liu, you truly have a heart of gold.”","Liu Yutong waved her hand dismissively. She glanced once more at the old woman lying unconscious on the bed, then let out a soft sigh and turned to leave the Wang family home.","...","A hotel suite in Jingchuan City.","Yang Xin stood before the floor-to-ceiling window, a cup of tea in his hand as he gazed out at the unfamiliar city.","He was already in his early thirties, and he increasingly carried the polished air of a successful young executive.","But only he knew that just two years ago, he had been merely a small-time manager in Wushui County, dragged into a car by The Young Lady. Back then, he had spent every day trembling with anxiety, afraid that one careless move might get him stabbed by some local gangster.","Yet in just two short years, he had transformed from a timid little office worker into the president of the Commercial Retail Business Group of Wanlonghui Group, overseeing the conglomerate’s largest business division. Under his command were countless brick-and-mortar outlets, including Wanlong Plaza, Wanlong Commercial Street, Wanlong Supermarkets, Wanlong Convenience Stores, Yuyuefang Restaurants, and more, with tens of thousands of employees under him.","Two years ago, this was something he wouldn’t even have dared dream of—at the very least, he had never imagined he could rise so quickly, or climb so high.","Everything he had was given to him by The Young Lady.","Without The Young Lady’s promotion and trust, he might still be racking his brains over what to do after losing his job.","Yang Xin took a sip of tea, forcing down the emotions stirring in his mind.","This afternoon, he was due to attend Jinchuan City’s investment promotion forum. In the evening, he had a special dinner to attend—an invitation from Qi Tianhu, chairman of Tiger Might Group.","Yang Xin knew a little about Qi Tianhu. The man was a local kingpin in Jinchuan City and certainly no pushover.","Just then, his assistant knocked on the door from outside.","“President Yang, President Xu has arrived.”","“Send her in.”","The door opened, and a sharp, capable-looking woman in her thirties walked in.","She wore a cream-colored business suit. Her features were not breathtaking, but her outstanding bearing more than made up for it. In particular, her alluring, almond-shaped eyes were always slightly narrowed, giving people the impression of a blade concealed within its sheath.","This was Xu Shishi, president of Wanlonghui Group’s Supply Chain and Logistics Business Group.","She was also the only president among the group’s six business divisions who had not risen from within the company’s core ranks. She was a top-tier professional manager whom Liu Yutong had recruited from a multinational logistics giant.","Before joining Wanlonghui, Xu Shishi had already risen to the position of vice president of that multinational company’s Longguo division. With an annual salary in the tens of millions and real authority in her hands, she was renowned throughout the industry as the Iron Lady.","Yang Xin hurriedly set down his teacup and went forward with a smile.","“President Xu, you’re here. Please, have a seat!”","“President Yang, you’re too kind.”"]},{"number":838,"title":"Chapter 838: 839, Attending the Banquet You're Not Qualified Yet","paragraphs":["The two of them took their seats on the sofa in the suite’s living room.","Xu Shishi accepted the tea handed to her by her assistant and thanked her before getting straight to the point. “General Manager Yang, what do you think about Qi Tianhu’s dinner invitation tonight?”","Yang Xin looked slightly surprised. “He invited you too?”","Xu Shishi nodded. “I’m in charge of logistics, after all. We’re going to build several large logistics warehouses in BS Province, and one of them will be in the Jingchuan area. All the transport routes will have to pass through Jinchuan, so it’s hardly strange that he came looking for me.”","Yang Xin nodded as well. They both knew exactly what Qi Tianhu was plotting.","The Wanlonghui Group’s investment projects in BS Province—from Wanlong Plaza and the logistics hub to the agricultural-products processing base they planned to invest in later—would all require massive quantities of construction materials and transportation services.","And the Qiwei Group’s main businesses were construction materials, sand and gravel, concrete, and transportation—all fields related to construction.","Put simply, Qi Tianhu had invited them to dinner because he wanted to tear off a piece of the Wanlonghui Group’s profits.","“So how do you plan to deal with him, Ms. Xu?” Yang Xin asked.","Xu Shishi thought for a moment before replying, “The bidding standards for the Wanlonghui Group were announced long ago. If a company doesn’t meet the requirements, then it doesn’t meet them. That’s an objective fact, not something we’re doing to target him deliberately. Last year, the Qiwei Group was publicly reprimanded for substandard construction materials. Their transport fleet also has serious safety hazards. These are fundamental problems that can’t be ignored. We can’t compromise and gamble with the safety and reputation of so many projects.”","“Besides, General Manager Yang, you know how seriously The Young Lady takes construction safety and quality. Who would dare relax the requirements?”","Yang Xin nodded. “So you mean we should refuse to work with him.”","“There’s no better choice,” Xu Shishi said. “Even if we agreed to cooperate with him, who knows what Qi Tianhu might do later, given his temperament? He could cut corners, raise prices arbitrarily, or even use our supply chain as leverage to force us into making concessions. If the Wanlonghui Group wants to gain a firm foothold in BS Province and smoothly push forward with the projects that follow, then Qi Tianhu—the obstacle in our way—has to be dealt with.”","She paused, then raised one finger. “So simply refusing him isn’t enough. We need to find a way to make him die!”","By “die,” she didn’t mean physically. What she meant was that it would be best to have Qi Tianhu sent to prison.","Yang Xin couldn’t help taking another look at her after hearing that.","No wonder she was the iron lady Brother Ma had recruited at The Young Lady’s request. She was ruthless.","She wanted to take someone down right from the start.","Perhaps only someone this decisive and merciless could hold steady in the position of president.","In some respects, business warfare could be far filthier than fighting with real weapons. A president who wasn’t ruthless enough couldn’t keep people in line, much less crush the competition.","Xu Shishi clearly understood that principle very well.","“All right. I’ll arrange it, then,” Yang Xin said.","After all, aside from being a company president, he also held another identity: he was a core member of the Wanlonghui. It would certainly be more convenient for him than for Xu Shishi to handle matters like this.","...","The afternoon symposium came to an end.","At half past six that evening, a black Mercedes stopped outside Jinchuan Pavilion, the city’s most famous private club.","This was not a place one could enter simply by having money. Membership was required, and the admission standards were extremely high.","Yang Xin and Xu Shishi got out of the car with two assistants. Qi Tianhu’s secretary had been waiting outside for quite some time. The moment he saw them step out, he hurried over with an ingratiating smile.","“General Manager Yang, Ms. Xu, our chairman has already prepared a modest dinner in Private Room One of the Heaven Class. Please allow me to show you the way.”","Yang Xin and Xu Shishi nodded at the same time.","“Thank you for leading us.”","Jinchuan Pavilion was located halfway up a mountain on the outskirts of Jinchuan City. It was Qi Tianhu’s private property, built against the mountains and beside the water. The décor was luxurious, and the security was extremely tight.","Inside Heaven Class Private Room One, sandalwood incense drifted through the air.","Qi Tianhu had arrived long ago and was seated at the head of the table. Dressed in a traditional Chinese tunic suit, he idly rolled two walnuts in his hand, looking completely at ease.","Sitting beside him was his son, Qi Licheng. With his conspicuous dyed-blond hair, he lazily swirled a glass of red wine, his eyes filled with malice.","When Yang Xin and Xu Shishi entered, Qi Tianhu rose and greeted them with a false smile, extending his hand.","“General Manager Yang, Ms. Xu, I’ve long heard of you! Now that I’ve finally met you, I see that you truly are young and capable!”","Yang Xin and Xu Shishi gave him polite smiles.","“Mr. Qi, you’re too kind. Sorry to have kept you waiting.”","“Not at all, not at all. We only just arrived ourselves.”","Qi Tianhu smiled and invited them to sit down, then introduced the son beside him. “This is my son, Qi Licheng. He’s not much good for anything, but I brought him along today to broaden his horizons.”","Qi Licheng rose lazily and nodded at them, which counted as his greeting.","Yang Xin and Xu Shishi nodded back.","Once everyone was seated, Qi Tianhu instructed the servers to bring out the dishes.","The food had been ordered in advance, and every dish was one of Jinchuan Pavilion’s signature specialties: wild soft-shelled turtle, steamed mandarin fish, braised stone frogs, stir-fried venison, and more. The table was soon covered with dishes, and the ingredients alone had probably cost tens of thousands of yuan.","Qi Tianhu personally poured wine for Yang Xin and Xu Shishi before raising his glass.","“General Manager Yang, Ms. Xu, welcome to Jinchuan City. I’ll drink to that first!”","He downed the entire glass, then turned it upside down to show that it was empty.","Yang Xin and Xu Shishi also finished their drinks.","After three rounds of wine and several courses of food, the polite small talk finally came to an end. Only then did Qi Tianhu bring up the real reason he had invited them.","“General Manager Yang, Ms. Xu, let’s speak frankly. The Wanlonghui Group’s investment in Jinchuan is a good thing, and I, Qi Tianhu, welcome it with both hands raised.”","“But Jinchuan has its own rules.”","“All the construction materials, sand and gravel, and concrete for Wanlong Plaza and the logistics warehouse center—as well as every other supporting service required for the projects—must be supplied exclusively by the Qiwei Group. The transport fleet for the logistics warehouses must also use my people. As for security and cleaning at the shopping mall, I’ll arrange those as well.”","“These are all my conditions. In short, we should all make money together. As long as the two of you agree, I guarantee that you’ll have a smooth ride in Jinchuan. No one will dare cause you trouble.”","Yang Xin and Xu Shishi exchanged a glance, the same thought flashing through both their minds.","The tiger had finally bared its fangs.","It sounded like cooperation, but in reality, it was nothing more than naked extortion through monopoly.","They had already looked into the matter. The Qi family’s construction-materials supplies were usually priced thirty percent above market value, while their transport fleet took another thirty percent cut. They also liked to secretly plant idle relatives and hangers-on in companies, paying them for doing nothing. This was the Qi father-and-son duo’s usual method of controlling property developers over the years.","They devoured people without leaving so much as a bone behind. They had driven countless legitimate companies out of business and caused many investments to lose every penny.","Seeing that the two remained silent, Qi Licheng let out a cold laugh.","“You’re both smart people. You should understand the influence our Qi family wields in this area. I can say this without exaggeration: in Jinchuan, my Qi family is the law.”","“Last year, an out-of-town developer refused to show proper respect. Their construction site was surrounded for three months. In the end, they slunk away without earning a single cent and even lost tens of millions more.”","“I assume the Wanlonghui Group doesn’t want to suffer the same fate, does it?”","At that, Yang Xin helplessly spread his hands. “Is your esteemed son threatening us? To be honest, it’s been a long time since anyone threatened me with such sincerity. I have to admit, it feels rather refreshing.”","Qi Licheng slammed his wineglass onto the table. “I’m making myself perfectly clear. In Jinchuan, if you refuse to play by the rules, don’t even think about doing business here! And you’d better watch out for your people, too...”","“Licheng! Is that any way to speak to guests I invited?!” Qi Tianhu cut in. His tone was stern, but it was obvious he was only putting on a show.","He then turned back to Yang Xin and Xu Shishi and said apologetically, “General Manager Yang, Ms. Xu, I’m sorry about this. My son has been spoiled rotten by me. Please don’t take it to heart. I know your Wanlonghui Group is a major enterprise and doesn’t care much about the small businesses here in Jinchuan. But as the saying goes, harmony brings prosperity in business, and having more friends means having more options.”","“I’ve also heard that your group has invested at least several billion yuan in the cities around Jinchuan. If a minor disagreement were to affect your business, the losses could be severe—perhaps even enough to damage your financial stability or drive you into bankruptcy. Wouldn’t you agree?”","Xu Shishi suddenly laughed. Her cool, alluring eyes turned toward Qi Tianhu, filled with sarcasm.","“Chairman Qi, do you know how much revenue our group made last year?”","Qi Tianhu said nothing.","Xu Shishi held up one hand. “More than fifty billion yuan!”","The moment that figure was announced, the pupils of the Qi father-and-son duo contracted slightly. Clearly, they were stunned.","Fifty billion yuan!","What kind of figure was that?","Qi Tianhu had spent nearly twenty years building his empire in Jinchuan, commanding influence in both the legitimate and underworld spheres. Even his entire fortune amounted to no more than three or four billion yuan.","And their annual revenue alone was dozens of times his total net worth. Their strength was indeed formidable.","“Our Wanlonghui Group has invested several billion yuan in Jinchuan, but to us, that amount is merely a drop in the bucket. It would be quite difficult to bankrupt us—unless you can tear a massive hole in the sky itself.” Xu Shishi deliberately allowed a hint of arrogance into her voice, as though she were mocking these two provincial bumpkins who had never seen the wider world.","“Mr. Qi, it’s 2009 now, not the era of your youth, when you could seize territory with your fists.”","“And don’t assume that we’re some powerful outsider deliberately refusing to work with you.”","“The construction materials supplied by your Tiger Might Group have failed three quality inspections. The sand and gravel contain twice the permitted amount of mud, creating serious safety hazards. Several companies in your transport fleet don’t even have operating licenses, and overloading and exceeding weight limits are routine. Last year alone, there were more than thirty traffic accidents, three of them fatal—all covered up with money. Am I wrong?”","“Then there’s the practice of forcing people into positions and paying them for doing nothing, suspected commercial bribery, forced transactions, and manipulating market prices. Any one of those charges would be enough to warrant an official investigation.”","With just a few sentences, Xu Shishi exposed all the dirty secrets of Tiger Might Group. Clearly, she had investigated them thoroughly in advance.","“I’m not saying this to threaten you. I only want to make our Wanlonghui Group’s position clear. We don’t want trouble with you, but you’d be wise not to provoke us either.”","Qi Tianhu’s expression darkened at a visible speed.","It seemed this woman had no intention of letting them share in the profits. In that case, there was no reason for him to show them any courtesy. In Jinchuan, he had never been afraid of anyone.","Ignoring his gloomy expression, Xu Shishi continued.","“Our Wanlonghui Group has only four words as its standard for cooperation: compliance and mutual benefit.”","“We don’t use substandard construction materials. We don’t work with shady transport fleets. And we don’t accept one-sided, coercive contracts.”","“Jinchuan’s market is open and inclusive. We invest based on our strength and operate in accordance with the law. We don’t need to answer to anyone, much less bow our heads to criminal gangs.”","“If Mr. Qi truly wants to work with us, then follow the proper public-bidding process, and we’ll welcome the opportunity. But if you’re planning to use those old-school gangster tactics to force us into buying or selling against our will, then, if I may be frank...”","She paused, then said, “You’re not qualified.”"]},{"number":839,"title":"Chapter 839: 840, Arrogant Lithium Mine (Thank you, \"Half-Baked Literary Master,\" for the Grand Master Recognition)","paragraphs":["“You’re not qualified!”","Those five short words exploded like a thunderclap.","Qi Licheng shot to his feet and slammed his hand on the table. The wineglass in his hand was hurled viciously to the floor, shattering as liquor splashed everywhere.","“You damn woman! You’re really asking for it, aren’t you? How dare you say my father isn’t qualified? You must be tired of living!”","At his roar, the thugs outside the private room came crowding in. Every one of them looked hostile, their faces brimming with menace.","Yang Xin neither panicked nor lost his temper. He slowly rose, straightened his suit, and looked toward the group of rough-looking men at the doorway.","“Young Master Qi, you’re making quite a spectacle. Are you planning to use force against us?”","“Let me warn you now: no one can mess with the Wanlong Association whenever they feel like it!”","“There are people in Pearl City a hundred times more arrogant than you. Every one of them has been driven out. Jinchuan may be far away, but if you push us too far, you won’t like how things turn out!”","The two sides were on the verge of clashing, and the atmosphere grew increasingly oppressive.","Qi Tianhu suddenly threw back his head and laughed. His laughter was dark and sinister.","“Good! Very good, Ms. Xu!”","“I, Qi Tianhu, have been making my way through Jinchuan City for twenty years, and this is the first time anyone has told me I’m not qualified.”","“Since the two of you are determined to oppose me, there’s nothing more to discuss. Someone, see them out!”","“Goodbye!”","Yang Xin and Xu Shishi did not linger. They got up and left.","The dinner ended on an unpleasant note.",".........","Once they stepped out of the club, the cool night breeze brushed against them.","Yang Xin finally could not hold back and said to Xu Shishi, “Ms. Xu, weren’t you being a little too reckless just now?”","“Qi Tianhu is a local tyrant, after all. We’re on his turf. What if we push him too far and he resorts to desperate measures? Wouldn’t that put us in trouble?”","Xu Shishi narrowed her beautiful, almond-shaped eyes slightly and shook her head.","“General Manager Yang, you’re giving him too much credit.”","“Qi Tianhu is nothing more than a crude hooligan. He has a narrow outlook and knows only how to force businesses into submission with violence. He won’t be able to keep jumping around for much longer.”","“Our Wanlong Association’s investment in BS Province is a key investment-attraction project under the province’s watch. It’s officially registered with the authorities. No matter how overbearing Qi Tianhu is, he wouldn’t dare truly lay a hand on us.”","“That may be true, but Qi Tianhu won’t simply let this go. We still need to stay on our guard.”","“Of course we need to be prepared, but I think it would be better to take the initiative. Qi Tianhu is already an obstacle to our plans for expanding into the southwest. If we can eliminate him in one sweep, all the better. It would also help clean up the business environment here, which would greatly benefit our retail operations.”","Yang Xin nodded thoughtfully.","“Ms. Xu, I think I finally understand why The Young Lady went to such lengths to recruit you.”","Xu Shishi smiled faintly.","“It was nothing more than the boss’s trust.”","Yang Xin suddenly felt that Xu Shishi was even more suited than he was to become a core member of the Wanlong Association. She was sharp and decisive, and she never hesitated to draw her sword when the time came.","Just now, she had openly told Qi Tianhu to his face that he was not qualified. Even Yang Xin had been sweating for her. At the very least, he would never have dared to be so blunt on someone else’s turf.","It wasn’t that he was a coward. He simply had a wife and daughter waiting for him at home.","Xu Shishi, however, was exceptionally bold. She had shown no intention of saving the other side’s face, and she had even been certain that they would not dare make a move.","She truly was a woman who could hold her own against any man.","Yang Xin was now completely convinced that she was qualified to become the president of the business group.","It was just that Yu Xin had suddenly gained a powerful competitor.","“Now that we’ve completely fallen out with them, we can’t afford to let our guard down. Let’s all make the necessary preparations in case the Qi family tries to make a move in the dark.”","They both believed that, after the failed negotiations, the Qi family’s domineering style would inevitably lead them to resort to underhanded tactics.","But neither of them was afraid.","When the Wanlong Association had fought its way out of Wuxian County, it had never relied on compromise or retreat. It had always depended on absolute strength.","......","The two got into the car and left the club, heading for the hotel where they were staying.","It was 2009, and Jinchuan City was not particularly lively at night. There were not many cars on the road, so the journey was smooth.","After chatting with Xu Shishi for a while, Yang Xin leaned back in his seat and closed his eyes, thinking about how he should report the matter to The Young Lady.","Xu Shishi, meanwhile, was scrolling through text messages on her phone, apparently dealing with some work-related matters.","They were almost at the hotel when—","Suddenly!","A blinding high beam shone straight through the windshield, followed by the screech of brakes.","The driver slammed on the brakes. The car shook violently, and the phone in Xu Shishi’s hand flew out. Her body lurched forward from the inertia, but the seat belt caught her and pulled her back.","Yang Xin was jolted awake and quickly asked, “What happened?!”","Before the driver could answer, a silver-gray Porsche crossed the double yellow line from the opposite lane, overtook against traffic, and cut directly in front of their car, forcing it to stop.","Fortunately, the driver reacted quickly. Otherwise, they would have crashed into it, and someone would almost certainly have been injured.","The driver had just rolled down his window, preparing to curse the other driver and ask if he even knew how to drive, when the Porsche owner opened his own window and started shouting first.","“Are you blind, you piece of trash?! Didn’t you see me overtaking? How dare you get in my way! Move your damn car!”","The driver’s face instantly turned cold. He was furious enough to drag the man out and beat him, but with Yang Xin and Xu Shishi still in the car, he forcibly held himself back.","“Sir, you crossed the center line and overtook illegally. You also deliberately cut us off. Move your car immediately, or I’ll call the police!”","“Damn it, you’re just a lousy driver, and you think you can lecture me? Believe it or not, I’ll run you over! Move your ass!”","Just then, a motorcycle patrol officer happened to pass by and saw what was happening. He rode directly over to the Porsche and called out to its driver.","“Driver, please show me your license and vehicle registration. You crossed the solid line and overtook in the wrong lane. You’re in violation of traffic laws!”","The Porsche driver, who was wearing a mask and a hat, not only refused to show his documents but arrogantly pulled a thick wad of cash from his wallet and flung it at the traffic officer.","“That enough to cover the fine?!”","The officer was enraged by his contemptuous attitude and shouted sternly, “Pull the car over! Cooperate with law enforcement!”","Yet the man was so arrogant that he ignored the officer’s command entirely. He nudged the car forward, then rolled down the window and shouted toward the back seat:","“You outsiders, remember this! If I run into you again, I’ll run you over and kill you!”","With that, he raised his middle finger at the people in the car, burst out laughing, jerked the steering wheel, stepped on the accelerator, and sped away.","The officer was furious, but he also knew it would be dangerous to chase after him. He could only report the license plate to his superiors first before walking over to Yang Xin and the others’ car and saluting them.","“Are any of you hurt?”","Yang Xin shook his head.","“No. Thank you for your help, officer.”","The officer reminded them to be careful on the road before riding away.","Only then did their car slowly start moving again.","“That was him,” Xu Shishi suddenly said.","Yang Xin nodded.","“Qi Licheng.”","“He was giving us a warning.”","“I know.”","Although the other party was wearing a mask and a hat, they still recognized him at a glance as Qi Tianhu’s son, Qi Licheng.","“Looks like the Qi father-and-son duo will be coming after us very soon.”","“General Manager Yang, if it really comes to a confrontation, this young master is the best breakthrough point.”","“What makes you say that?”","“He’s arrogant, conceited, and completely disregards the law. People like him are usually covered in weaknesses and are the easiest to investigate.”","“That makes sense. I’ll have someone start investigating him, then.”","“Mm.”","Just then, Xu Shishi suddenly remembered some news she had happened to overhear two days earlier while conducting an inspection in the provincial capital.","“General Manager Yang, do you know about lithium ore?”","Yang Xin nodded. “I do. It’s the core raw material used to make lithium batteries, and it’s quite expensive. Why are you suddenly asking about it?”","In 2009, the new-energy sector had yet to take off. Lithium batteries had not yet become the hot commodity everyone was chasing, and lithium ore prices were still relatively low. Still, no matter how you looked at it, lithium was a mineral resource with enormous investment potential.","“It’s like this. Two days ago, while attending an exchange meeting, I overheard someone mention that a large lithium deposit had been discovered in the Qingyan Mountains, roughly sixty kilometers northwest of Jinchuan. Preliminary surveys indicated that its reserves were astonishingly large—it could rank among the largest in the country, or even across the entire East Continent,” Xu Shishi said.","Yang Xin was stunned for a moment. “What does that have to do with us? We don’t mine ore.”","Xu Shishi explained, “It obviously has nothing to do with us directly, but it has everything to do with Qi Tianhu, the head of Tiger Might Group.”","“Lithium is a strategic mineral, so it’s extremely valuable. The Qi father-and-son duo operate several coal mines and have even monopolized the coal market in several cities around Jinchuan. What’s more, this lithium deposit is so close to Jinchuan. Do you really think he’ll let such a tempting prize slip through his fingers?”","Yang Xin immediately understood what she meant. “So we’re going to compete with them for the mining rights.”","Xu Shishi nodded. “But I need to report this to the boss first. After all, I’m only trying to throw a wrench in the Qi father-and-son duo’s plans. We really don’t deal in this kind of business, but I think we could make a profit by selling the mining rights later.”","Yang Xin said, “I’ll ask the Young Lady. She happens to be inspecting the townships under Jingchuan right now.”","“Good!”"]},{"number":840,"title":"Chapter 840: 841, Guessed Half Right.","paragraphs":["Liu Yutong had been racing from city to city around Jingchuan for three or four days straight.","During that time, she visited more than twenty Hope primary and secondary schools built with funding from the Wanlong Charity Foundation. She met tens of thousands of children and handed out tens of thousands of gifts.","The Wanlong Charity Foundation had funded the construction of more than a hundred primary and secondary schools across BS Province. Naturally, it was impossible for her to personally visit every single one, so she could only select a number of schools at random for inspection. In addition to meeting the students, her main focus was checking whether the school buildings had been constructed to the required standards and whether they met the necessary earthquake-resistance ratings.","Fortunately, after completing the rounds of inspections, she found no obvious signs of corner-cutting or the use of substandard materials. This showed that quality control over the construction projects was still quite strict. Her original decision to have Yun Cheng personally oversee the work in BS Province had clearly been the right one.","After all, with a project of such enormous scale, it was inevitable that some people would be tempted to cheat the system and pocket a little money. She could not gamble on every contractor having a conscience. All she could do was issue strict orders and have the supervisory team keep a close eye on every stage of the process.","At the end of her inspections, in addition to an assessment report on the schools as a whole, she also obtained a list of nearly a thousand children in need of financial assistance. The list contained the names of children from exceptionally impoverished families identified during the visits.","Liu Yutong decided to pay for their education out of her own pocket and support them all the way through university.","Aside from inspecting the schools, Liu Yutong had also received a series of reports from her subordinates over the past few days.","The first concerned the disappearance of Wang Xiaoshu’s older brother, Wang Dashu. There had finally been some progress.","While the Wanlong Association Group’s family tour was passing along a certain provincial highway, the convoy had encountered a gang of local thugs who had set up a roadblock to extort tolls. The gang had taken control of several mentally disabled people and used them as enforcers and tools to extort money.","It was an extremely despicable tactic. If anything went wrong, they could simply pin the blame on those mentally impaired individuals. As long as they themselves were not caught, they could walk away completely clean.","Fortunately, the security personnel accompanying the tour had acted decisively, subduing the entire gang and handing them over to the police.","Unfortunately, Wang Dashu was not among the mentally disabled young men who had been rescued.","Still, Liu Yutong’s instincts told her that this lead could not be abandoned. She felt that the two incidents might be connected in some way.","Afterward, she specifically instructed Cheng Gang to keep a close watch on the men who had been arrested and see whether anything useful could be extracted from them.","Cheng Gang was the core member who had been injured and hospitalized the previous year while protecting his brothers. He had since been promoted by one rank. In Ma Da’s words, he was now a bona fide helmsman. He was capable, dependable, and could be counted on to get things done.","The second matter that caught her attention was a report from Yang Xin.","Yang Xin and Xu Shishi’s dinner meeting with Qi Tianhu in Jinchuan City had ended in a complete breakdown.","The Qi father-and-son duo had openly threatened to target the Wanlong Association Group’s projects in the area.","That same evening, Qi Licheng had deliberately driven a luxury car the wrong way down the road, repeatedly cutting them off and issuing personal threats. His attitude had been extremely arrogant.","At the same time, Yang Xin had also relayed Xu Shishi’s attitude toward the matter and her proposed course of action. After hearing it, Liu Yutong approved of both her judgment and her arrangements.","Aside from the conflict itself, the lithium mine Xu Shishi had mentioned had also caught Liu Yutong’s attention.","The Qingyan Mountains contained a large lithium deposit with astonishing proven reserves.","In 2009, the new-energy sector had yet to take off. Lithium prices were still relatively low, and most people had not yet fully recognized the value hidden in this mine.","But Liu Yutong knew very well that within just a few years, as smartphones became ubiquitous and shipments exploded, followed by the rapid rise of the electric-vehicle industry, lithium would become a strategic resource more coveted than gold.","By then, whoever controlled a mine would occupy a firm position on the future map of the new-energy industry.","In short, she was determined to have this mine.","And if the Qi father and son dared to lay their hands on it, she would simply send them to hell.","At the same time, Liu Yutong remembered that Uncle Zhu had briefly mentioned the lithium mine when they parted at the highway toll station.","At the time, she had found it somewhat strange and assumed he had only brought it up in passing. But now, in light of Yang Xin’s report, it was obvious that Uncle Zhu’s words had carried a deeper meaning.","The provincial authorities had certainly known for some time that a major lithium deposit had been discovered in the Qingyan Mountains.","Under normal procedures, a strategic mineral resource of this level would be developed under the leadership of the provincial government. Of course, the most likely arrangement would be a joint venture between state-owned capital and private enterprise.","Something like this could not simply be claimed outright. No one could expect to keep the entire pie for themselves. At the very least, they would have to bring the local state-owned enterprises in on the deal.","When Uncle Zhu had suddenly asked her about it, perhaps he had been inviting her to take a stake—to give her a share of the benefits.","After all, before the projects invested in by the Wanlong Association Group in BS Province—especially the aerospace project—had been fully implemented, Uncle Zhu was probably not entirely at ease. He was just like Uncle Li back then, who had been driven to distraction over the Longxin matter.","So perhaps he wanted to further bind their interests together through this arrangement. By developing the lithium mine in cooperation with local state-owned enterprises, he would essentially be presenting her with a major gift.","It was a case of one good turn earning another—a mutually beneficial exchange.","Apart from that, she could not think of a better explanation.","Could it be that Uncle Zhu also knew what kind of person Qi Tianhu was and wanted to use her hand to eliminate this problem?","That seemed somewhat unnecessary.","Given Uncle Zhu’s position and influence, taking down a local underworld boss would be as easy as saying a few words.","Of course, she could not completely rule out that possibility.","Perhaps Uncle Zhu’s side had already received reports implicating Qi Tianhu and his Tiger Might Group, but had never found the right opportunity to act. There might also be deeply entrenched resistance at the local level, so he wanted this outsider—this powerful dragon crossing into another river—to stir up the stagnant waters.","If that was truly the case, then there was certainly more to it than met the eye.","The Qi family had operated in Jinchuan for nearly twenty years. They monopolized the coal market, controlled the supply of construction materials, meddled in transportation and logistics, and maintained influence in both the legal and criminal worlds. They had long since become a malignant tumor in the business community of BS Province.","But no matter how one looked at it, bringing them down required solid evidence.","Qi Tianhu had a complicated network of connections in the region. The fact that he had managed to establish monopolies across several cities showed that he possessed considerable influence. If they wanted to build an airtight case and take him down in the shortest possible time, they would have to use some special methods.","If Qi Tianhu wanted to bite a chunk out of the Wanlong Association Group, he would inevitably have to make the first move.","Once he acted, he would expose a weakness.","Once he exposed a weakness, it would become much easier to obtain evidence.","At that point, Uncle Zhu’s side would have grounds to move against him—and even to follow the trail and uproot the network of connections behind him.","The more she thought about it, the more reasonable it seemed.","Still, Liu Yutong could not help wondering whether Uncle Zhu had heard some rumors and thought the Wanlong Association Group was becoming a little too much...","After giving it some thought, Liu Yutong decided to call Uncle Zhu and test the waters.","Before long, the secretary put the call through to Uncle Zhu.","“Uncle Zhu, the lithium mine you mentioned last time—is it the newly discovered Qingyan Mountain mine here in Jinchuan?”","A smile colored Uncle Zhu’s voice over the phone. “You’re pretty well-informed. So, are you interested in getting involved?”","“The smartphone market is taking off rapidly, and lithium is a core raw material. I know your side is preparing to make phones too.”","“Nothing gets past you. I do have some ideas, but there are still a few specifics that need to be discussed carefully. Before that, though, could you send an investigation team over? There are some problems that would be difficult for our company to handle on its own.”","Liu Yutong did not say outright what she intended to do. Some things were better left unsaid.","There was a brief silence on the other end before Uncle Zhu spoke again, his voice slightly more serious.","“Here’s what we’ll do. I’ll give you someone’s number. If you run into any problems, you can contact her.”","The moment Liu Yutong heard this, she felt reassured.","It seemed she had been partly mistaken in her earlier assumptions. Uncle Zhu had actually been keeping an eye on the situation here for quite some time—he had simply been waiting for the right opportunity.","After hanging up, Liu Yutong stood by the window, gazing at the undulating green mountains in the distance. Her eyes gradually sharpened.","Since someone wanted to play games, she would be happy to play along—and give them a game to remember."]},{"number":841,"title":"Chapter 841: 842, The Humiliated Fifty-Cent.","paragraphs":["At a bar.","Qi Licheng was drinking and carousing with a group of his good-for-nothing friends amid the deafening music.","After putting on a show of power in front of Yang Xin and Xu Shishi that night, the anger in his heart had not subsided. Instead, it had continued to build.","He had been waiting for an opportunity—an opportunity to properly deal with those two people, especially that woman surnamed Xu.","“Young Master Cheng, what should we do next?” Wumao asked cautiously.","Ever since losing one of his ears the last time, the man had become much more subdued.","He used to occasionally dare to joke around with Qi Licheng, but now he had changed completely, becoming timid and overly careful.","Seeing his cowardly appearance only irritated Qi Licheng further.","“What do you mean, what should we do? How’s the thing I told you to keep an eye on?!” he barked.","“I...I’ve taken care of it.”","“Young Master Cheng, I first had some people cause trouble at the construction sites over in Jingchuan for several days. We even deliberately beat up a few foremen who didn’t know their place, scaring them so badly that they haven’t dared return to work. Now, several of the construction sites have been shut down, and their project manager is frantically calling around trying to find people.”","A faint smile finally appeared on Qi Licheng’s face. “What about the man surnamed Yang and the woman surnamed Xu? How did they react?”","“Well...we don’t know,” Wumao said. “But I think they won’t be able to hold out for long before they give in.”","Qi Licheng let out a cold laugh. “Giving in isn’t enough. I want that woman surnamed Xu to kneel in front of me and apologize personally!”","Wumao nodded and bowed repeatedly. “Yes, yes, Young Master Cheng is absolutely right. That woman is far too insolent! We have to teach that woman surnamed Xu a lesson and show her what Young Master Cheng is capable of!”","“Get lost!”","“Yes!”","Wumao had just turned to leave when a burly man sitting in the booth across from them suddenly called out to him.","The man was called Leopard. He was Qi Licheng’s number-one enforcer and most trusted subordinate. He was broad and muscular, with tattooed sleeves covering both arms from his shoulders to his wrists. His face was a mass of flesh, and he looked exceptionally fierce.","“Wumao, don’t leave yet!”","Hearing someone call him, Wumao turned around with a sycophantic smile. “Brother Leopard, what can I do for you?”","Leopard pointed at his neck. “Hey, Wumao, why are you covering your neck so tightly?”","The smile on Wumao’s face froze for a moment before he explained, “Brother Leopard, I just slept funny and got a stiff neck.”","“Really? If you’ve got a stiff neck, why are you wearing gauze?” Leopard sneered. “Come on, let the brothers have a look. Let’s see whether it’s your neck that’s stiff—or whether your ear has failed to grow back.”","“Hahaha...”","Everyone in the booth burst out laughing.","Wumao’s remaining ear instantly turned bright red, but he still forced a smile. “Brother Leopard is joking. Just joking.”","Leopard refused to let him off so easily. He reached out, grabbed Wumao by the chin, and roughly twisted his head to one side.","Wumao instinctively tried to struggle, but the moment he saw Leopard’s murderous expression, he immediately backed down.","“Bro...Brother Leopard, please, a little gentler.”","Leopard ignored him completely. He had always looked down on petty thugs like Wumao, who knew nothing but how to flatter and curry favor.","“Well, would you look at that? You really are missing an ear.” He turned to the others. “Brothers, come take a look! Our Wumao has turned into One-Ear!”","The people in the booth once again burst into laughter.","“One-Ear? That’s a great nickname!”","“Brother Leopard, you’re a genius.”","“Brother Five Mao, that new look of yours is pretty unique. Which barbershop did you go to? I might get the same cut tomorrow.”","“Hahaha...”","With Leopard gripping his chin, Wumao was forced to remain in that humiliating position while everyone stared at the place where his right ear used to be.","Although he wished he could slaughter every person there, he continued to wear a fawning, ingratiating smile.","“Brother Leopard is right. I’m One-Ear now. One-Ear sounds pretty good, hehe...”","Seeing how spineless he was, Leopard finally released his chin. He patted Wumao’s cheek and said, “One-Ear, let me ask you something. After your ear was cut off, can you still hear clearly when someone talks to you from your left?”","Wumao smiled obsequiously. “Brother Leopard, you wouldn’t believe it. After that ear fell off, the one I have left actually became sharper. I can hear everything perfectly now.”","“Is that so? How amazing.” Leopard grinned. “Then what happened to the ear they cut off? Can you still find it?”","“No, I can’t. It’s long gone.”","“That’s a shame. I was thinking that if you found it, you could bring it to me as a snack with my drinks. I’ve eaten plenty of pig’s ears, but I’ve never tried a human ear.”","The moment Leopard said this, even the girls who had been hired to drink with them began laughing.","One of them—a young woman with dyed red hair and a sequined spaghetti-strap dress—laughed so hard she leaned almost entirely against Leopard.","Wumao knew this woman.","Her name was Xiaomei, and just three days ago, she had been his girlfriend.","Back then, he still had both ears. He had nearly a hundred men under his command and was considered a respectable big shot in the underworld on the western side of Jinchuan City.","Xiaomei was a waitress at the bar. She was quite pretty and had a good figure. He had spent a great deal of money pursuing her.","At the time, Xiaomei had been completely devoted to him, calling him Brother Five Mao at every turn and making him feel warm and pleased with himself.","After his ear was cut off, Xiaomei had been frightened when she saw him with his head wrapped in gauze and had immediately broken up with him.","Later, she became Leopard’s woman.","Leaning against Leopard’s broad shoulder, Xiaomei looked at Wumao and giggled. “Brother Leopard, stop teasing him. Look at him—he’s practically about to cry.”","“Cry?” Leopard said. “Can One-Ear even cry? Come on, come on. Cry for the brothers and let us see.”","The corners of Wumao’s mouth twitched, but he kept his smile in place. He picked up a glass of liquor and held it out to Leopard with both hands, bowing respectfully.","“Brother Leopard, let me toast you. You’re a magnanimous man, so please don’t hold this against me.”","Leopard glanced at the glass, then at Wumao’s petty, obsequious face. He immediately made an outrageous demand.","“You want to drink with me? Fine! Here’s what you’ll do: give us a little dog-crawling performance. Get down on your knees and crawl around like a dog a few times. Weren’t you once in charge of training dogs at a kennel? This is the perfect chance to show off your professional skills.”","The ingratiating smile finally vanished from Wumao’s face.","He first looked at Leopard’s fleshy, intimidating face, then turned toward Qi Licheng, who was seated in the place of honor.","Qi Licheng remained completely unmoved.","Wumao’s heart sank.","Finally, under Leopard’s threatening gaze, he slowly bent down, placed both hands on the floor, dropped to his knees, and began crawling like a dog.","Seeing him in such a degraded and servile posture, Leopard despised him even more and burst into loud laughter.","“Wumao, you’re one hell of a talent!”","Then he turned to Xiaomei and said, “Take a look at your ex-boyfriend. Doesn’t he look just like a dog? Hahaha!”","Xiaomei covered her mouth and said in a coquettish voice, \"Brother Leopard, don't talk about Brother Five Mao like that. After all, Brother Five Mao is one of Young Master Cheng's men.\"","Qi Licheng was leaning on the sofa, watching the show with great interest from beginning to end.","Hearing Xiaomei's words, he then said indifferently, \"A dog? Keep it if it's obedient, and kill it if it's not. For now, it's still obedient.\"","Leopard let out a hearty laugh. Then he picked up a glass of wine, tilted his head and downed it in one gulp. After that, he waved his hand at Wumao.","\"Alright, get out of here and don't be an eyesore.\"","Wumao quickly got up and nodded obsequiously, \"Yes, yes, yes. I'll get out right away, right away!\"","He fled the bar in a sorry state. As the cold outside wind blew, the smile on Wumao's face disappeared instantly, as if it had been ripped off by someone.","He raised his hand, touched his remaining right ear, and then felt the gauze where his left ear used to be. His heart was filled with shame and anger.","It was Qi Licheng who cut it off with a folding knife. It was like cutting off a pig's ear. With one slash and no anesthesia at all, it made him suffer so much that he felt like he was going to die.","Of course, what pained him the most now was not the physical pain, but the disappointment in his heart.","He, Wumao, had been in Jinchuan City for seven or eight years. He had worked his way up from a small hooligan to a boss in charge of nearly a hundred people. Later, he took refuge with Qi Licheng and, thanks to Qi Licheng's connections, his business kept expanding. Moreover, he would honestly offer hundreds of thousands of yuan to Qi Licheng every month.","He once thought that he had finally become Qi Licheng's trusted subordinate...","But what was the result?","Qi Licheng didn't show any mercy when cutting off his ear. Now, he even allowed Leopard to humiliate him like a dog in front of everyone.","Although he really wanted to tear the two of them to pieces, after calming down, that impulse was replaced by a deep sense of powerlessness.","He still knew how powerful the Qi family was in this area of Jinchuan. If he dared to show any resistance, he was afraid that he would disappear from this place tomorrow.","He could only swallow his anger.","Wumao took a deep breath, straightened his collar, covered the gauze more tightly, and then walked towards the back door of the bar.","Behind the bar was a narrow and cramped alley, filled with empty beer crates and stinking trash cans.","At the end of the alley, there was a black car with its lights off. It was probably someone who had parked randomly and blocked the alley entrance.","Wumao was walking towards the depths of the alley with his head down and almost bumped into the black car.","He was about to curse at whoever had parked the car randomly.","Suddenly!","A strange face suddenly appeared in front of him.","\"Wumao?\"","Wumao was greatly startled. \"You...\"","Before he could finish his sentence, three or four black - clothed men flashed out from the side, directly grabbed him and covered his mouth.","At the same time, the door of the black car opened. Without even having a chance to resist, Wumao was stuffed into the back seat.","Then the car started and quickly disappeared into the night."]},{"number":842,"title":"Chapter 842: 843, Jia Egg Released from Prison.","paragraphs":["In a detention center in Jinchuan City, the iron gate clanged open.","Jia Dan, nicknamed \"Rascal Egg\", with a shiny bald head, swaggered out with several of his brothers who had also just been released from the cells.","After being beaten up by the members of the Wanlong Society on the provincial road that day, their whole group was taken away by the police.","They thought they would have to stay inside for at least a year or two this time. Unexpectedly, after being locked up for less than a week, someone bailed them out.","Taking in the free air again, Jia Dan immediately felt much more comfortable all over.","\"Hahaha! I'm out again!\"","\"Alas, why did I say 'again'...\"","\"Boss, did Young Master Cheng bail us out this time so quickly?\" a little brother stepped forward and asked, then lit a cigarette for him.","Jia Dan took the cigarette and put it in his mouth, then raised his hand and gave him a slap, scolding with a smile, \"Nonsense! In this Jinchuan area, besides Young Master Cheng, who else has the face to get us out in groups.","Let's go. First, go to Brother Wumao to find out what those black - clothed bastards who beat us up that day are all about. By the way, see if that stupid guy who stabbed me in the ass is dead. Damn it! How dare he stab me in the ass with a steel pipe. I'll definitely kill him!\"","A group of people headed towards the west of the city in a grand manner.","One of Wumao's main strongholds was in a bathhouse called Grand Splendor in the west of the city. They usually had discussions, divided up the money, and housed their little brothers here.","When Jia Dan arrived, Wumao was lying semi - reclined on the leather sofa in the second - floor office, staring blankly at the ceiling.","\"Brother Wumao! I'm here!\"","Seeing Jia Dan and his group barge in, Wumao then came back to his senses, looked at them, and greeted them with a fake smile.","\"Yo, Brother Jia, out already? Didn't suffer in there, did you?\"","Jia Dan plopped down on the opposite sofa, picked up a beer on the coffee table, opened it, and took a big gulp. Wiping his mouth, he said, \"What could happen to me? It's just a few days inside. Piece of cake!","Brother Wumao, thanks to you talking to Young Master Cheng this time. Otherwise, we brothers wouldn't know how long we'd have to stay in there.\"","Wumao waved his hand, \"It's the right thing to do. We're all brothers. How can we ignore it when something happens.\"","But in fact, his heart was as cold as ice.","Humph!","When my ear was cut off, who the hell cared about me?","Only then did Jia Dan notice something strange about Wumao's ear. Curiously, he asked, \"Hey? Brother Wumao, what's wrong with your ear? Why is it still wrapped in gauze? Did you get into a fight?\"","Wumao subconsciously reached up to touch the gauze and pretended to be nonchalant. \"It's nothing. I just accidentally scratched it the other day. Just a little skin break. It'll be fine in a few days.\"","Jia Dan didn't delve deeper. He nodded and continued indignantly, \"Brother Wumao, you don't know. That day, we were almost successful. Then suddenly, a group of black - clothed men got out of that bus. Damn it, they were so ruthless! But they shouldn't be so proud. Once I find them, I'll make them all kneel on the ground and beg for mercy!\"","\"By the way, Brother Wumao, what's the background of those black - clothed men? You have wide connections. Have you found out?\"","Just as Wumao was about to speak, his phone in his pocket suddenly vibrated.","He looked down and saw a new text message on the screen, just four simple words - \"Follow the plan\".","The only remaining ear of Wumao twitched slightly, and then he nodded.","\"I've found out, Brother Jia. I've not only found out the details of those black - clothed men, but also their backer.\"","Jia Dan immediately perked up, \"Who?\"","Wumao looked around and then whispered, \"Those black - clothed men are from the Wanlong Society Group.\"","\"The Wanlong Society?\"","\"Is it the same Wanlong Society as the one with the Wanlong Plaza downtown? Are they related?\"","\"Right! It's them.\" Wumao nodded.","Hearing that the other side had such a big background, Jia Dan suddenly stammered, \"This... this... ah... this. The Wanlong Society seems to be quite hard to mess with, right?\"","After learning about their background, his idea of revenge immediately faded away.","Jia Dan was brave enough to set up a roadblock on the provincial road with a few idiots and some little brothers to extort tolls. But in the end, he only bullied the weak.","The Wanlong Society Group was different.","Although this company was from outside, it was quite well - known in Jinchuan.","Last year during the earthquake, they donated billions of real money. Many local people were very grateful to them, and even the local leaders attached great importance to this enterprise.","Jia Dan was just a low - level hoodlum. He was okay with stealing, petty thievery, and extorting a little money on the road. But if he really went to provoke the Wanlong Society, it would be like an old man hanging himself - asking for an early death.","Seeing his cowardice, Wumao despised him in his heart, but on the face, he pretended to be nonchalant.","\"Brother Jia, I have a question for you.\"","\"Go ahead.\"","\"Who bailed you out this time when you were arrested?\"","\"Need you ask? Of course, it was Young Master Cheng. Why do you ask?\"","\"Do you know how much money Young Master Cheng spent and how many favors he had to call in to get you out?\"","\"You got out because Young Master Cheng paid a price. Do you think the detention center is a vegetable market, where you can go in and out as you please?\"","The muscles on Jia Dan's face stiffened. \"What exactly are you trying to say?\"","Wumao said, \"Brother Jia, what I'm trying to say is why did Young Master Cheng go to so much trouble to bail you out? It's because he values you. If you were a useless piece of trash in his eyes, would he have bothered?\"","Jia Dan felt a warm feeling in his heart after hearing these words and unconsciously straightened his chest.","Wumao continued, \"I'll tell you. Besides you, Young Master Cheng has also set his eyes on the Wanlong Society.\"","\"Whether the Wanlong Society is easy to mess with or not, Young Master Cheng knows better than you and me. But why does he still want to take on the Wanlong Society? Do you know the reason?\"","Jia Dan shook his head blankly.","\"So stupid!\"","\"It's very simple. This is Jinchuan, our territory! When the Wanlong Society came here, they didn't show any respect and even refused to cooperate with the Tiger - Power Group. Of course, the most important thing is that they dared to beat you. This is like slapping Young Master Cheng in the face! Young Master Cheng said that there's no room for such an arrogant group in Jinchuan!\"","\"If they want to do business and make big money on our turf, they have to follow our rules. Young Master Cheng now wants to make them bow their heads and let them know their place!\"","\"Brother Jia, to be honest, Young Master Cheng has privately said that whoever contributes the most and does the best job in dealing with the Wanlong Society, he will not only take care of everything but also hand over the newly - built entertainment city to that person for management.\"","\"Don't you always want to open your own place in the west of the city? As long as you handle this matter well this time, if Young Master Cheng is in a good mood, that area will be yours. Then, you won't have to take the brothers to stand on the provincial road in the wind and sun to stop cars anymore. Just sit in the office, and the money will flow into your pocket. It'll be so comfortable!\"","Jia Dan was dazed by the big pie Wumao painted. His eyes gradually lit up, \"Really? Did Young Master Cheng really say that?\"","\"Would I lie to you?\"","Wumao pointed at his ear wrapped in gauze. \"Look at this ear of mine. I got injured while doing a favor for Young Master Cheng. But Young Master Cheng gave me two nightclubs right away. Now I'm making at least this much more every month.\"","He held up three fingers, indicating 300,000 yuan.","Jia Dan's breathing immediately became heavy, and his eyes fixed in a daze.","\"Brother Jia, you've been by Young Master Cheng's side for a long time. As long as you work hard, Young Master Cheng won't treat you badly. Fortune favors the bold. You don't need me to tell you this, right?\"","Jia Dan couldn't sit still anymore. He slapped his thigh hard.","\"Let's do it!\"","\"Damn it! So what if it's the Ten-Thousand Dragon Society? They hit me. I must settle this score with them!\""]},{"number":843,"title":"Chapter 843: 844, Conspiracy","paragraphs":["“Brother Five Mao, where is the leader of the men in black who attacked me last time? I’m going to deal with them first!”","Wumao had been waiting for him to say exactly that. He immediately replied, “He’s in Jinchuan City. My people have already been keeping an eye on him. But Brother Jia, there’s something I need to tell you in advance. These outsiders are vicious, and they’ve got a huge appetite. In just the few days you’ve been gone, they’ve already taken over several businesses under Young Master Cheng’s protection.”","“What?!”","Jia Dan was stunned. “They’ve got that much nerve? They even dared to touch businesses protected by Young Master Cheng?”","“Exactly.”","Wumao sighed and said worriedly, “That’s why Young Master Cheng is so furious. Do you think he can tolerate being bullied by people from some out-of-town company?”","Jia Dan’s anger was completely ignited. “Then what are we waiting for? Brother Five Mao, lend me some men. I’ll wipe those bastards out tonight! We’ll make them pay back everything they owe, with interest!”","“Men won’t be a problem. I just took in a new batch of followers. They’re all trained fighters with excellent skills,” Wumao agreed readily.","“However, Brother Jia, those people really are tough. Otherwise, they wouldn’t have taken over several businesses in such a short time. We’ll have to be strategic when we make our move. We can’t just charge in recklessly.”","Jia Dan nodded in complete agreement. After all, he had personally witnessed the skills of those men in black. Their superior numbers had certainly helped them that day, but there was no denying that they knew how to fight.","“Do you have a plan?”","Wumao watched Jia Dan’s expression carefully before revealing his countermeasure. “I thought of one a long time ago. My people have been secretly watching them all this time. I know exactly when those businesses have the fewest people and when their defenses are weakest. As long as we choose the right moment and storm in while they’re undermanned, we can catch them completely off guard. I guarantee it’ll work. Not only will we vent Young Master Cheng’s anger, but once he’s happy, he might even hand all those businesses over to you to manage.”","Jia Dan immediately thought it made perfect sense. “Exactly, exactly! You’re absolutely right! Those useless fools can’t even hold on to their own turf. They deserve to have it taken from them. If I take the businesses back, won’t I be the one managing them from then on?”","The more he spoke, the more excited he became. “Brother, you’re doing me a huge favor this time! Don’t worry. Once I make it big, I definitely won’t forget you.”","He had climbed onto the branch so quickly that he was already calling himself Wumao’s big brother. The thickness of his skin was astonishing.","Wumao waved his hands repeatedly. “Listen to you. From now on, I’ll still be counting on your support, Brother Jia.”","Jia Dan was being flattered into the clouds. He practically wanted to grab a knife and charge out the door that very instant.","At that moment, Wumao changed the subject. “By the way, Brother Jia, I noticed you keep quite a few special talents under your command. Aside from the ones the cops took away after they blocked the road that day, where did the rest go?”","“They were naturally sent to...”","Jia Dan suddenly realized something was wrong and asked warily, “Why are you asking me that?”","Jia Dan might not have been very bright, but after spending so many years in the underworld, he still knew which things could be said and which could not.","Seeing him become cautious, Wumao hurriedly explained, “You misunderstood, Brother Jia. I mean, since you have so many special talents under your command, you should bring a few of them along for the operation.”","“Think about it. If things get out of hand or something goes wrong, we can pin everything on those idiots. Their brains don’t work properly, so even if they’re arrested, they won’t be able to explain themselves clearly. With them taking the heat for us, we’ll be much safer, won’t we?”","Jia Dan found his reasoning convincing, and the wariness on his face gradually faded.","Wumao struck while the iron was hot and gave him a thumbs-up. “Brother Jia, I truly admire your mind. Everyone else looks down on those idiots, but you’ve figured out how to turn them into money-making tools—and even use them as human shields. How did I never think of that? If I’d learned this trick from you sooner, I wouldn’t have suffered so many losses over the years.”","Jia Dan was so flattered by those words that he became completely carried away. He laughed heartily. “Brother, there’s a lot of know-how involved. When we get the chance, I’ll teach you all about it.”","With that, he stood up. “All right, enough of this. I’ll call Young Master Cheng now and report tonight’s operation to him. Then we’ll set out.”","He had just taken out his phone when Wumao reached over and grabbed his wrist.","“Brother Jia, you can’t make that call.”","“Why not?”","Wumao looked at him and said earnestly, “Think about it. What will you do if you call him now and the operation fails? Once words are spoken, they’re like water spilled on the ground—you can’t take them back.","“If you ask me, you should get the job done beautifully first and tell Young Master Cheng afterward. That way, you’ll give him a huge surprise. It’ll not only be safer, but it’ll also show off your abilities and make him think more highly of you.”","“Don’t say I didn’t warn you. You’re not the only one under Young Master Cheng who wants to rise above the rest. Never mind the others—even Brother Leopard is Young Master Cheng’s number-one enforcer and trusted confidant.","“If he finds out you’re going to reclaim those businesses, he might make his move ahead of you. If he steals the credit, all our effort will be for nothing.”","The moment he heard Brother Leopard’s name, Jia Dan’s expression changed.","“You’re right!”","“I’m not making the call! I’ll take the businesses first, then go to Young Master Cheng and claim the credit!”","Wumao looked at Jia Dan’s excited face and laughed coldly to himself.","This idiot was being used as a weapon and still thought he was the one getting the better deal.","The Ten Thousand Dragons Association did have people in Jinchuan City, but they were engaged in legitimate business. They had never intended to seize anyone’s territory—there was no need, and they simply didn’t care about such places.","The story about the mahjong parlor in the western part of the city being taken over, the KTV in the south being seized, and the underground casino being smashed up was all something he had made up on the spot.","But Jia Dan believed every word.","Of course, that wasn’t entirely because Jia Dan was stupid. It was also because the story had come from Wumao.","They had known each other for several years, and officially, they were both men working under Young Master Cheng. It was only natural that Jia Dan wouldn’t suspect him.","“Wumao, which business should we hit first?” Jia Dan asked impatiently.","Wumao pretended to think for a moment before saying, “Let’s start with the casino in the western part of the city. I heard it used to be under Brother Biao’s protection, but recently it was taken over by people from the Ten Thousand Dragons Association. Brother Biao has been having a headache over it. If you can take the place back, wouldn’t that prove you’re more capable than Brother Biao?”","When Jia Dan heard that he could also use this opportunity to get the better of Brother Biao, his eyes lit up even more. He made the decision on the spot.","“All right, we’ll hit that one!”","Wumao reminded him again, “Brother Jia, tonight’s operation needs to be kept discreet. I suggest having all the men wear masks and hats so no one recognizes them. First, it’s for everyone’s safety. Second, if something really goes wrong, the Ten Thousand Dragons Association won’t know who did it and won’t be able to retaliate against us. That way, we can attack or retreat as we please.”","Jia Dan nodded deeply, convinced. “Exactly, exactly. You really have thought this through, Wumao. We’ll do as you say. Everyone covers their faces!”","Seeing how obedient he was, Wumao found the whole thing even more ironic.","Rascal Egg still had no idea that from the moment he was bailed out, everything had already been arranged for him.","“Then I’ll go call them over now.” Wumao stood up and took out his phone to call his men.","In less than twenty minutes, more than thirty young men wearing black T-shirts, black masks, and baseball caps appeared at the bathhouse.","These were all the “underlings” Wumao had recently recruited. Every one of them was muscular and carried an impressive air.","Jia Dan walked around the group once, clicking his tongue. “Brother Five Mao, why do these men of yours look so familiar? I feel like I’ve seen them somewhere before.”","Wumao’s heart skipped a beat, but he kept his expression perfectly composed and laughed it off. “Brother Jia, you’re joking. These men are all elites I went to great lengths to recruit. I usually can’t bear to order them around. I called every one of them out this time to support you.”","Jia Dan had only asked casually, but after hearing Wumao’s explanation, he was even more touched.","“You’re a true brother! I’ll remember this loyalty.”","“Since everyone’s here, let’s go. Time to get to work!”","“Tonight, I’m going to show the Wanlong Society exactly what Jia Dan is made of!”"]},{"number":844,"title":"Chapter 844: 845, Let's Get to Work","paragraphs":["The night was as dark as ink, and the cold wind howled.","Jia Dan brought along seventy or eighty men. Nearly half of them were his own brothers, while the rest had been summoned by Wumao.","The group piled into eight or nine vans and headed straight for the western part of the city, murder in their eyes.","Their first stop was an underground casino in the western district.","The casino was hidden inside an arcade. From the outside, all anyone could see were several rows of flashing game machines. No ordinary person would ever guess that a gambling den was concealed inside.","But Wumao knew where the entrance was. At the very back of the arcade stood a wall plastered with posters. Push it open, and it revealed a concealed door.","One of the underlings lifted his foot and kicked the door in. Sure enough, there was a whole other world behind it. The place was brightly lit and hazy with smoke, while a group of gamblers sat around playing the machines.","“Who’s there?”","The few thugs guarding the place froze for a moment, then flew into a rage.","“What the hell are you doing?!”","Jia Dan had no interest in wasting his breath on them. He simply waved his hand and shouted, “Smash the place!”","His men immediately charged in, howling as they smashed anything they could find and beat anyone who got in their way.","“Don’t move! Get down! Hands behind your heads! Anyone who moves is getting it!”","The casino descended into chaos. The gamblers fled in every direction. A few tried to sneak out through the back door, but Jia Dan’s men grabbed them by the scruffs of their necks and hurled them to the floor, leaving them screaming in pain.","Jia Dan strode into the middle of the casino, kicked down one of the guards who was still trying to resist, then planted a foot on his chest and roared menacingly, “This place is under my management from now on! Anyone who has a problem can step forward and say it to my face!”","The entire casino fell deathly silent. No one dared make a sound.","While Jia Dan and his men were rampaging through the place, the so-called “underlings” Wumao had brought along looked distinctly out of place.","Not only did they refrain from joining the fight, but they also spread out around the casino, each holding a small video camera and filming the chaos from every angle.","They were taking their job extremely seriously—even getting a close-up of Jia Dan’s foot planted on someone.","When Jia Dan saw what they were doing, he frowned and shouted at Wumao, “Wumao, what the hell are your brothers doing? Why are they just filming instead of helping? And what are they taking pictures of everything for?”","Wumao had prepared his explanation long ago. He replied, “Brother Jia, you don’t understand. They’re collecting evidence. Think about it—we’re doing this on behalf of Young Master Cheng. When the time comes, shouldn’t we take these photos and videos to Young Master Cheng and claim credit? We’ve got to let him see how impressive you are, Brother Jia. Once he sees this scene and this kind of presence, he’ll know that you’re a man capable of accomplishing great things!”","Jia Dan was stunned for a moment. Then his face broke into a delighted grin.","“You really thought this through. Exactly! We need to film everything and let Young Master Cheng see how powerful I am!”","What a great partner he had found. Wumao was truly reliable!","Once Jia Dan understood the benefits of being filmed, not only did he stop objecting, he even straightened his clothes and leaned toward the cameras, striking what he considered an incredibly imposing pose so they could capture him more clearly.","“Make sure you get all of me in the shot! I want my heroic image captured!”","“Say cheese!”","The casino’s head guard was a fat man in his thirties. After successfully posing alongside the sole of Jia Dan’s shoe, he finally managed to stammer, “B-Big brother, this place is under Young Master Cheng’s protection. Do you know who Young Master Cheng is? Aren’t you afraid of offending Young Master Cheng—and Lord Tiger?!”","At those words, Jia Dan gave his enormous backside a vicious kick.","“Cut the crap! This place was clearly taken over by the Wanlong Society. You think you can fool me? Do I look like an idiot?!”","“No, no, Big brother, this really is Young Master Cheng’s place. I’m not lying to you...”","“You’re still talking back!”","Jia Dan kicked him twice more, sending the fat man howling until he finally fell silent.","“Listen carefully. From this moment on, this place is under my control! Every month, you’ll deliver the protection money, not a cent short, to the Dazzling Glory Bathhouse in the western district. Miss even one penny, and I’ll rip off one of your arms!”","“Is that clear?!”","The fat man sprawled on the floor and nodded repeatedly. In his heart, however, he was cursing furiously.","Where the hell had this lunatic come from? He actually dared to seize Young Master Cheng’s place. Just wait—you’re going to regret this!","“Come on. Next one!”","Jia Dan waved his hand grandly and led his men away in a mighty procession, leaving nothing behind but a scene of utter devastation.","Their second stop was a KTV in the southern part of the city.","This KTV was fairly large—a three-story standalone building with more than twenty luxurious private rooms. Quite a few expensive cars were parked outside, and business was booming.","When Jia Dan and his men stormed in, the place was already in full swing. The corridors rang with the off-key wailing coming from the private rooms.","“Clear the place! All of you, get the hell out!”","One private-room door after another was kicked open. Before the guests inside could even figure out what was happening, they were dragged out and sent fleeing in terror.","A few of the heavier drinkers tried to put on a tough act, emboldened by the alcohol, cursing and picking fights. Jia Dan’s men promptly surrounded them and gave them a thorough beating. Within moments, they were sprawled on the floor groaning, their drunkenness mostly beaten out of them.","The KTV manager came running out of his office when he heard the commotion. He was shocked by the sight and hurriedly called for help while reaching out to stop Jia Dan and his men.","“Gentlemen, what’s going on? Why don’t we talk this out? This place is...”","Before he could finish, Jia Dan slapped him across the face.","“What is it? This place was taken over by the Wanlong Society, and I’m here today to take it back for Young Master Cheng!”","“Listen carefully. From today onward, the protection money for this place is doubled!”","“D-Doubled?” The manager clutched his face, unable to believe what he was hearing.","They had wrecked his establishment, beaten him up, and now they still wanted him to pay them protection money?","Their nerve was unbelievable!","Then again, why not take off the mask first? He didn’t even know who these people were. How was he supposed to deliver the money to them?","“What? You don’t like that?” Jia Dan glared at him, his eyes filled with menace.","“No, no, Big brother, that’s not what I meant.” The manager hurriedly waved his hands. “I only meant that this place really doesn’t belong to the Wanlong Society. It belongs to Young—”","Smack!","Another resounding slap!","This one was even harder than the first, knocking the manager off balance.","“I say it does, so it does! Say another word and I’ll burn this dump to the ground!”","The manager covered his face and didn’t dare utter another word.","Wumao watched from the side, secretly delighted. Outwardly, however, he fanned the flames.","“Brother Jia, this guy clearly isn’t a good person. Look at him—slick-haired and greasy-faced. He was probably bought off by the Wanlong Society a long time ago.”","“That makes sense!” Jia Dan nodded deeply, convinced.","He walked over and viciously kicked the manager several more times. The man curled up in the corner, clutching his head and not daring to move. Only then did Jia Dan turn around and shout to his men, “Take everything valuable in this place! No matter what, we can’t let the Wanlong Society benefit from it. Consider it interest I’m collecting on behalf of Young Master Cheng!”","His underlings took the order and immediately scattered throughout the building, beginning their looting.","The premium cigarettes and liquor at the front desk, along with the cash in the register drawer—anything that could be carried away was hauled off, and anything too heavy to move was smashed.","Before long, the once-pristine KTV had been reduced to utter chaos.","Wumao’s “underlings” continued taking photos and recording videos, documenting every moment of Jia Dan and his men beating, smashing, and looting the place.","This time, Jia Dan didn’t need anyone to remind him. Instead, he deliberately stepped in front of the camera, smashing things as he shouted at it:","“Young Master Cheng, watch closely! This is Jia Dan venting your anger for you. I’ll smash every Wanlong Society establishment I come across! Just sit back and watch what I do!”","With that, he viciously smashed another speaker, looking incredibly imposing."]},{"number":845,"title":"Chapter 845: 846. Split Personality","paragraphs":["The third place was an underground casino in the northern part of the city.","The casino was hidden inside an abandoned warehouse. From the outside, it looked shabby and run-down, but inside was an entirely different world. It had been decked out like a small gambling resort, with everything from baccarat and roulette to pai gow, along with all kinds of gambling equipment.","When Jia Dan and his men charged in, the place was in full swing. Dozens of gamblers crowded around the tables, shouting and hollering.","“Nobody fucking move! This is a crackdown on prostitution and illegal publications—no, wait! Everybody get down on the ground!”","Jia Dan nearly got his slogans mixed up. He was simply too worked up.","The gamblers were terrified when they suddenly saw dozens of men storm in and immediately scattered in every direction. Several tried to run past Jia Dan and his men, only to get clubbed in the legs and collapse with screams.","The casino was run by a lean man with a crew cut, known in the underworld as Ah Jiu. He was a fairly influential figure in the area.","When Ah Jiu saw Jia Dan throwing his weight around, his anger intensified. He shouted directly at him, “Rascal Egg, have you fucking lost your mind? This is Young Master Cheng’s place! You actually dare hit Young Master Cheng’s territory? You must be tired of living!”","When Jia Dan heard someone call him by his nickname, he blurted out, “How the fuck did you recognize me?”","Ah Jiu glanced at his shiny bald head gleaming under the lights and inwardly muttered, You came to smash up someone else’s place, so the least you could’ve done was wear a hat. With a head like that, it’d be hard not to recognize you. You stick out like a sore thumb.","Jia Dan had lost his hat by accident while wrecking the KTV earlier. Perhaps because everything he had done that night was so thrilling, he had been running on pure adrenaline and hadn’t even noticed that he was missing the hat on his head.","Seeing that someone had recognized Jia Dan, Wumao immediately shouted at him, “Brother Jia, this guy must’ve betrayed Young Master Cheng! Think about it—this is one of the Ten Thousand Dragons Society’s establishments. Why else would he be here?”","His words jolted Jia Dan awake.","Before Jia Dan could figure out what was going on, Wumao had once again led him astray. Jia Dan immediately pointed at Ah Jiu and roared, “So it’s true! Ah Jiu, you actually betrayed Young Master Cheng and joined the Ten Thousand Dragons Society!”","Ah Jiu stared at him in bewilderment. “What Ten Thousand Dragons Society? This place has always belonged to Young Master Cheng! When did I ever join them? Jia Dan, did you get water in your brain?”","Wumao snorted coldly beside them. “Brother Jia, don’t listen to his excuses. One look at him and you can tell he’s bad news—shifty-eyed and suspicious. For all we know, he’s a spy planted by the Ten Thousand Dragons Society beside Young Master Cheng, specifically to pass along information.”","Ah Jiu’s face changed dramatically when he heard Wumao slandering him. “Who the fuck are you? Don’t make wild accusations! I’ve followed Young Master Cheng for five years. How could I possibly betray him?”","Wumao continued fanning the flames. “Brother Jia, we can’t let this man live. He knows too much. If we let him go, everything we’ve done tonight could be exposed.”","Jia Dan nodded, his eyes turning vicious. He waved a hand. “Beat him! Beat him to death!”","Before Ah Jiu could react, several thugs pinned him to the ground and gave him a savage beating. His face was covered in blood, and his nose was broken.","“Ptooey!”","Jia Dan spat at him. “That’s what happens to traitors!”","Ah Jiu, lying on the ground, was so wronged he could barely stand it.","I’m not a traitor!","But the other side refused to listen to his explanation. They didn’t even give him a chance to prove his innocence, just kept beating him relentlessly.","“Search the place! Turn the whole damn place upside down!”","The underlings immediately began looting. Chips, cash, expensive watches, valuable gambling equipment—anything they could carry, they took.","Just then, one of the men suddenly ran out from a back room, holding several small transparent plastic bags. His face was alight with excitement.","“Boss, look what I found.”","Jia Dan took them and looked inside. His expression instantly changed.","It was drugs!","He had committed plenty of crimes in the past—highway robbery, fighting, even human trafficking—but drugs were one thing he truly didn’t dare touch.","Anyone who mixed with the underworld knew that once you got involved with this stuff, it wasn’t merely a matter of spending a few years in prison. You could end up eating a bullet.","“Where did you find these?”","“In the back room. They were hidden at the very back of a cabinet, taped beneath the bottom of a drawer. There are several packets.” The underling spoke excitedly.","Jia Dan turned to look at Ah Jiu, who was sprawled on the floor with blood all over his face. His expression was one of disbelief.","“You even dare touch this stuff? Are you fucking tired of living?!”","Ah Jiu had been beaten so badly that he could barely speak. “N... not mine. It’s... it’s Young Master Cheng’s...”","“Bullshit!”","Jia Dan planted a foot on his face and cursed, “Would Young Master Cheng touch this kind of thing? You got yourself killed, and now you’re trying to pin it on Young Master Cheng? Is he that kind of person?”","Ah Jiu: “...”","For a moment, he couldn’t tell whether this lunatic was on Young Master Cheng’s side or was actually Young Master Cheng’s enemy.","On the one hand, he had brought a crew to raid a place Young Master Cheng had personally looked after. On the other, he was defending Young Master Cheng with all his might.","This guy had to be fucking insane!","As soon as Wumao saw the packets of contraband, he said to Jia Dan, “Brother Jia, we have to keep this somewhere safe. We can hand it over to Young Master Cheng later. It’s solid evidence.”","Jia Dan nodded repeatedly. “Right, right, you’re absolutely right. This stuff is incredibly important. I’ll personally deliver it to Young Master Cheng. Catching him with the goods will definitely earn us a major merit.”","He then carefully placed the packets of drugs into a black bag and tied it tightly. After that, he handed it to one of his most trusted men and solemnly instructed him, “Keep this on you at all times. If you lose it, I’ll take your life. Got that?”","“Don’t worry, Boss. I’ll make sure it reaches Young Master Cheng.” The man accepted the bag with both hands and gave his guarantee.","Jia Dan nodded. He then had his men search the casino one more time. Only after confirming that nothing had been overlooked did he lead them away in triumph.","Before leaving, he looked back at Ah Jiu, who was lying on the floor half-dead, and spat.","“Traitor!”","Ah Jiu: “...”","Fuck you!"]},{"number":846,"title":"Chapter 846: 847, Does Jinfan City Still Belong to the Qi Family","paragraphs":["The fourth place, the fifth place, the sixth place...","Throughout the entire night, Jia Dan seemed to be on drugs as he led his men to sweep through six or seven venues.","What venues were they? There were mahjong parlors, KTVs, bathhouses, underground casinos, arcades... As long as they were the venues that Wumao said had been snatched by the Wanlong Society, he left none untouched and raided them all.","At each venue, he followed the same routine: rush in, clear the place, beat people up, rob money, smash things, and then show off his \"war achievements\" in front of the camera.","This guy was getting more and more excited. He smashed things more and more smoothly, and towards the end, he even seemed unable to stop.","Wumao's little minions filmed the whole process, capturing every detail of Jia Dan's looting and vandalism clearly. Especially the close - ups of him beating up the venue managers, snatching property, and seizing contraband were extremely clear.","At three o'clock in the morning.","Jia Dan led his men to the last venue of the night, a bar in the east of the city.","This bar was the largest and most prosperous one under Young Master Cheng's control. It had two floors. The bar counter alone was more than ten meters long. The dance floor could accommodate over a hundred people dancing at the same time, and there was a circle of VIP booths on the second floor, which were decorated magnificently.","When Jia Dan led his men to rush in, there were still quite a few customers enjoying themselves in the bar.","\"Turn on the lights! Clear the place! Get the hell out of here!\"","The music stopped abruptly, and the lights came on. Only then did the customers notice that the bar had been surrounded by a group of hooligans.","The seven or eight bouncers in the bar didn't even have time to ask about the identity of these masked men before they were knocked down.","Seeing this, the customers finally panicked and started screaming and running around.","Just then, a burly man with a fierce - looking face came down from the second floor and roared at the people downstairs.","\"Who dares to cause trouble on my Leopard's territory? Are you looking for death?\"","When Jia Dan saw Leopard, he was stunned for a moment.","He subconsciously turned to look at Wumao beside him, with a puzzled look on his face.","What's going on?","Wasn't Leopard Young Master Cheng's right - hand man? Why was he here?","When Wumao saw Leopard, his heart skipped a beat, but he reacted very quickly. He immediately pointed at Leopard and shouted loudly, \"Brother Jia, Leopard has defected! He has long since defected to the Wanlong Society! No wonder we couldn't take back this venue. It turns out he's an insider!\"","\"What? Even Leopard has defected?\" Jia Dan was shocked.","After all, Leopard was truly one of Young Master Cheng's most trusted men!","Wumao didn't give Jia Dan any time to think. He quickly started making up reasons: \"Brother Jia, think about it. This venue was clearly snatched by the Wanlong Society. As Young Master Cheng's man and his most trusted and capable subordinate, why is Leopard here?","Originally, I was still wondering how the Wanlong Society had the strength to directly snatch so many of Young Master Cheng's venues. Now I understand. It's all because of Leopard.","If he were really loyal to Young Master Cheng, he should have led his men to take back the venue long ago. But he didn't even make a move, and he didn't even help us when we came to take back the venues for Young Master Cheng tonight. Isn't this a defection?\"","Jia Dan wasn't very smart. After being coaxed by Wumao so plausibly, his thoughts were led astray again.","Right!","This venue was snatched by the Wanlong Society. As the most powerful man under Young Master Cheng, if Leopard were loyal, he should have led the brothers to take back the venue long ago.","But not only did he not make a move, but he also seemed to be having a good time here drinking. Wasn't he a traitor?","It was just a bit strange that the number of \"traitors\" he had seen tonight seemed a bit too large.","There was Ah Jiu before, and now there was Leopard. They had all defected.","Was Young Master Cheng so unpopular now? Were the people around him so unreliable?","Sure enough, a friend in need is a friend indeed!","In critical moments, he, Jia Dan, was the most reliable!","Leopard was extremely angry when he was wrongly labeled as a traitor. \"What the hell are you talking about? When was this venue snatched by the Wanlong Society? I've been in charge of it all along!\"","Wumao continued to fan the flames in Jia Dan's ear, \"Brother Jia, this guy has completely defected. We can't let him go! If we don't take him down today, he'll go to Young Master Cheng later and distort the facts, playing the victim and saying that we're the traitors. Then all the hard - earned merits we've achieved tonight will be in vain!\"","Hearing this, Jia Dan also got anxious.","He had worked so hard to take back seven or eight venues tonight. What for? It was to gain credit in front of Young Master Cheng and show that he, Jia Dan, was also a capable person.","If this traitor, Leopard, went to Young Master Cheng to file a false complaint first, wouldn't he have worked in vain?","After all, on the surface, Young Master Cheng still trusted Leopard and the others more.","No! He couldn't let this traitor play the victim!","Jia Dan immediately pointed at Leopard and roared, \"You still dare to quibble. You betrayed Young Master Cheng and still don't admit it. You're such a despicable person! How could Young Master Cheng have trusted you so much!\"","Leopard was so angry that his face turned green. \"Rascal Egg, stop putting the blame on me. I've been with Young Master Cheng for so many years. When have I ever done anything to let him down? Can't you see that you're being used by this dog, Wumao?\"","Although he was big in size, he wasn't stupid.","Although these two guys were in disguise and had their faces covered, their characteristics were still too obvious.","One had a shiny forehead, and the other had a bandage around his ear.","Who else could they be but Jia Dan and Wumao?","Moreover, he also guessed that it was Wumao who was behind this raid on his venue, just to take revenge on him.","Wumao sneered, \"Leopard, stop pretending. No matter what you say, you defected to the Wanlong Society and betrayed Young Master Cheng. This is a capital crime!","Brother Jia, this guy used to be extremely arrogant just because Young Master Cheng trusted him. He never regarded us brothers who joined later as equals. I'm sure you're aware of this, right? It's just right for us to take down this traitor and settle the score together!\"","Jia Dan also remembered how Leopard used to treat them, the brothers who joined Young Master Cheng later. He either ordered them around like dogs or humiliated them in front of everyone for fun. He never treated them like human beings.","Thinking of this, his eyes instantly turned red, and he immediately gave the order:","\"Damn it, I've long been fed up with you. Brothers, beat him to death!\"","Jia Dan's little minions immediately rushed towards Leopard.","Leopard was really good at fighting. Under normal circumstances, three or five people couldn't even get close to him.","But unfortunately, he was outnumbered. Moreover, there were also the elite men brought by Wumao secretly assisting. Soon, this guy was knocked to the ground and held down by several hooligans.","Jia Dan had gotten addicted to stepping on people's faces. He came in front of Leopard, raised his foot, and stepped on Leopard's face, saying menacingly, \"Leopard, you traitor! I represent... no, I represent Young Master Cheng to punish you!\"","Leopard was almost spitting blood from anger. \"Rascal Egg, you're so stupid. You've been deceived! Young Master Cheng won't let you off!\"","\"Still so stubborn!\"","Jia Dan kicked him several more times hard, but Leopard showed no sign of begging for mercy and kept swearing defiantly.","Wumao stood to one side, watching Leopard, who used to be so high and mighty, forcing him to crawl like a dog and stealing his woman, being beaten to a pulp. He felt an indescribable sense of pleasure in his heart.","Leopard, Leopard, you've finally got your comeuppance.","You forced me to crawl like a dog.","You stole my woman.","This is your retribution!","\"Brother Jia, this guy has a tough bone. The more like this he is, the less we can let him off easily. We must give him a lesson he'll never forget!\"","Jia Dan nodded upon hearing this, then said to his subordinates, \"Strip off his pants and beat him hard for me!\"","Leopard was held down by several people and roughly stripped of his pants in front of the waiters and his little minions.","Then, Jia Dan personally took off the belt around his waist...","Leopard's face instantly changed drastically. \"What... what are you going to do!\"","\"Ah!!!\"","The scene was so cruel that even Wumao felt a bit pity when he saw it.","After Jia Dan whipped Leopard until his skin was torn and his flesh was lacerated, Wumao stepped forward and persuaded, \"Brother Jia, that's enough. That's enough. Our spoils tonight are already great. We've taken over seven or eight venues and those traitors. It's time to go back and rest. We have to go to Young Master Cheng's place to report our achievements tomorrow.\"","Only then did Jia Dan stop reluctantly. He fastened his belt again, then waved his hand, telling his men to drag Leopard away.","This guy definitely couldn't be let go, lest he go to inform someone. They had to send him to a safe place as Wumao suggested.","Before leaving, Jia Dan didn't forget to turn back and strike a domineering pose in front of the camera of the DV held by Wumao's little minion.","\"Young Master Cheng, all the traitors have been purged by me, Jia Dan! You can rest assured. Jinchuan still belongs to the Qi family and is still your world!\""]},{"number":847,"title":"Chapter 847: 848. Kill Three Birds with One Stone.","paragraphs":["The next morning.","Qi Licheng had just woken up in his hotel room. He reached for the phone on the bedside table and turned on the screen. The moment he saw it, he froze.","There were a great many missed calls.","Qi Licheng hated being disturbed while he slept, so he habitually put his phone on silent every night.","Seeing so many missed calls all at once, his heart sank.","“Damn it!”","He sat up abruptly and called one of the numbers back.","“Young Master Cheng! Young Master Cheng! Something terrible has happened!”","“Talk!”","“Young Master Cheng, there’s been a major incident! Our establishments were taken out last night!”","Qi Licheng let out a cold laugh. “What are you talking about? In Jinchuan City, who would dare take out one of my places? Are they tired of living?”","“It’s true! Young Master Cheng, I’m not joking!”","“The bathhouse in the west of the city, the KTV in the south, the mahjong parlor in the east, the foot massage parlor in the north... Even the underground casino personally guarded by Brother Biao—all of them were taken out!”","Qi Licheng’s expression finally changed.","“What did you say? Say that again!”","“All of our places were taken out. Brother Jiu, Brother Biao, and the others have disappeared too. No one knows where they are. The brothers have searched everywhere, but they haven’t found a trace of them.”","“Who did it? Have you figured that out?”","“Not yet. Those people were all wearing masks and hats, so we couldn’t see their faces. But I’m guessing it was probably the Dragon Gang. They’re the only ones who’ve been at odds with us recently.”","Qi Licheng’s face darkened.","He had never expected those bastards from the Dragon Gang to be so bold as to make the first move against him!","“Well... well done, Dragon Gang!”","“If you want to play, then I’ll play with you to the very end!”","The moment he hung up, his phone rang again.","It was Jia Dan.","“Young Master Cheng! Great news! Absolutely fantastic news!”","The moment Qi Licheng heard that, his anger flared. “Every one of my places was wiped out last night, and you’re calling that great news? If you don’t give me a satisfactory explanation today, you can forget about making a living in Jinchuan!”","Jia Dan had not expected such a fierce reaction. It took him several seconds to reply. “Young Master Cheng, please don’t lose your temper. The good news I’m talking about is directly related to what happened last night.”","“What do you mean?”","“Young Master Cheng, it’s hard to explain over the phone. I’ll come over right now and report everything to you in person. I guarantee you’ll feel better after you hear it.”","Qi Licheng said nothing more and hung up.","About half an hour later, Jia Dan appeared in a rush at Qi Licheng’s hotel room.","The man clearly had not slept all night. His eyes were ringed with dark circles, yet he was absurdly energetic, as if someone had injected him with stimulants.","“Young Master Cheng, guess who took out those places last night?”","Qi Licheng stared coldly at him. “Didn’t you say it was the Dragon Gang?”","“No!”","Jia Dan proudly pointed at himself. “It was me!”","“Surprised? Impressed?”","Qi Licheng: “...?”","“You’re saying you did it last night?”","Jia Dan nodded, practically boasting. “That’s right! I did!”","“I led our men to take out all those places last night!”","Qi Licheng narrowed his eyes slightly, and a murderous glint gradually spread across them.","“Oh, really? Very impressive.”","“Jia Dan, you’ve certainly made me see you in a new light.”","Jia Dan failed to notice the murderous intent in Qi Licheng’s voice. Thinking he had rendered a great service, he continued proudly recounting his accomplishments.","“Young Master Cheng, listen. The moment I heard the Dragon Gang had taken your places, I immediately gathered the brothers and went to take them back. We wiped out seven of their establishments in one go. Those Dragon Gang bastards were beaten so badly they were crawling around and begging us to spare them. It was incredibly satisfying, hahaha...”","The murderous look in Qi Licheng’s eyes froze for a moment.","Wait.","Had there been a misunderstanding?","Was Jia Dan saying that he had taken the places back? That he had dealt with the Dragon Gang?","If so, then Qi Licheng might have wronged him. Perhaps he really did need to see Jia Dan in a new light.","Jia Dan had learned about the Dragon Gang’s attack immediately, acted decisively, and led his men in striking back and reclaiming the establishments.","He really was a capable man.","“What about Leopard?” Qi Licheng asked as the murderous intent in his eyes gradually subsided.","“Brother Leopard?”","The smile on Jia Dan’s face faded, replaced by a solemn expression. Following the story Wumao had taught him, he replied, “Young Master Cheng, I was just about to tell you. Brother Leopard has betrayed us!”","“What did you say?!” Qi Licheng shot to his feet, his voice rising sharply.","“It’s true! I saw it with my own eyes.”","“Last night, when I led a team to take out that casino, I personally saw Brother Leopard sitting at a table with people from the Dragon Gang, drinking with them. He even had a woman in his arms. Later, I found out that she was a spy planted by the Dragon Gang. Young Master Cheng, Brother Leopard was bought off by the Dragon Gang a long time ago—with a woman’s charms!”","Qi Licheng’s expression shifted several times, his mood darkening and brightening unpredictably.","Leopard had followed him for nearly ten years. He was one of Qi Licheng’s most trusted right-hand men.","And now someone was telling him that Leopard had betrayed him?","How could that be possible?","But Jia Dan had described everything so convincingly that Qi Licheng had no choice but to believe him.","The most important thing now was to find Leopard and get to the bottom of it.","If it was true...","Suppressing his anger, Qi Licheng said, “I’ll investigate this matter thoroughly. If Leopard really has betrayed me, I won’t let him off.”","Jia Dan put on an expression of unwavering loyalty and flattered him. “Young Master Cheng is wise.”","He then seized the opportunity to report a string of other names, claiming they were traitors as well.","The more Qi Licheng listened, the more alarmed he became. He could hardly believe his ears.","Seriously? He had been making his way through Jinchuan for all these years, only to discover that everyone around him was a traitor?","After Jia Dan finished his report and saw that Qi Licheng looked less than pleased, he tactfully took his leave.","As he was leaving, one of the underlings who had come with him quietly slipped a sealed plastic bag into the inner pocket of the coat hanging on Qi Licheng’s coat rack while no one was looking.","It was not until Jia Dan had left the hotel that he suddenly remembered.","Damn it! He had forgotten to give Young Master Cheng Ah Jiu’s evidence of guilt!","When he learned that his underling had already delivered it to Qi Licheng, he immediately began to waver.","The evidence had already been handed over. Would it look too deliberate if he made a special trip back just to take credit?","Would that cause Young Master Cheng to think less of him?","Forget it. He would not go back.","With Young Master Cheng’s intelligence, he would surely know whose evidence was in the bag. He could deal with the traitors himself.","With that thought, Jia Dan felt relieved. His objective had already been achieved, after all.","Thinking about how he would soon rise to wealth and power, the man happily hummed a tune as he climbed into a van and drove away.","Meanwhile.","After Jia Dan left, Qi Licheng called Wumao.","He was still only half-convinced by what Jia Dan had told him.","It was not that he doubted Jia Dan’s loyalty. Rather, he simply could not bring himself to believe that the men who had followed him for so many years would betray him one after another.","But he had indeed watched Jia Dan’s expression carefully just now. From beginning to end, the man’s gaze had been open and straightforward, and he had spoken with complete confidence. He hadn’t looked like he was lying at all.","Because he couldn’t find any flaws, he had no choice but to ask someone else.","The call connected quickly.","“Wumao, Jia Dan says he was the one who took down those venues last night, and that Leopard betrayed us. Did you know about this?”","Wumao sounded extremely surprised on the other end. “What? Jia Dan took down those venues? I’d always thought it was someone from the Wanlong Society. Young Master Cheng, what exactly is going on?”","Qi Licheng briefly repeated everything Jia Dan had reported to him.","After listening, Wumao fell silent for several seconds before speaking. “Young Master Cheng, I do know a little about what Jia Dan told you. Brother Leopard has indeed been acting somewhat strangely lately. I heard he’s had private contact with people from the Wanlong Society, but I can’t guarantee that he’s really betrayed us.”","“Do you think Jia Dan is telling the truth?”","“Young Master Cheng, Jia Dan may not be the sharpest man around, but he’s absolutely loyal to you. No matter how bold he is, he wouldn’t dare lie to you about something like this. And judging from what I’ve observed recently, Brother Leopard’s behavior has indeed been rather unusual.”","Qi Licheng was silent for a moment before saying in a deep voice, “I understand. I’ll get to the bottom of this. Keep a close eye on Jia Dan’s side for me.”","“Of course, Young Master Cheng.”","After hanging up, Wumao leaned back against the sofa and casually tossed his phone aside. Then he let out a cold laugh.","Everything was proceeding according to plan.","That idiot Jia Dan was still basking in the dream that he had accomplished a great feat.","He had no idea that every venue he’d smashed belonged to Qi Licheng’s operation and was under Young Master Cheng’s protection—not the Wanlong Society’s. And he had successfully pinned the blame on the Wanlong Society as well.","Brother Leopard had also been branded a traitor because of Jia Dan’s outstanding performance. It looked like he would never be able to clear his name, even if he jumped into the Yellow River.","It had been killing three birds with one stone.","Wumao instinctively touched his only remaining right ear. A savage delight and venomous hatred flashed in his eyes.","Qi Licheng, Leopard, Xiaomei...","The humiliation you inflicted on me—I’ll repay it bit by bit, and with interest!","This show has only just begun."]},{"number":848,"title":"Chapter 848: 849, Killing the Dragon to Frighten the Monkey","paragraphs":["Jinchuan City, Wanlong Plaza.","Liu Yutong, wearing a safety helmet, was inspecting the construction site to check on the progress of the resumption of work.","She had only arrived in Jinchuan City last night, yet she had come straight to the site early that morning. She wanted to see whether construction of Wanlong Plaza had been affected.","“Young Lady, Brother Yang and General Manager Xu are here,” Yun Cheng reported as he approached. Yang Xin and Xu Shishi followed behind him.","“Young Lady!”","“Chairwoman!”","The two stepped in front of Liu Yutong and greeted her respectfully.","There was something peculiar about both their expressions, especially Yang Xin’s. He looked as though he wanted to laugh but was embarrassed to let it show.","“What’s with that look? Did you find some money?” Liu Yutong asked with a smile.","“Young Lady, take a look at this first.” Yang Xin stepped forward and handed her a document.","Liu Yutong took it and opened it. Inside was a detailed operation report, with photographs attached to every page—more than a dozen in total.","The subject of the photographs was a bald man.","As she flipped through the pages, Liu Yutong’s expression grew increasingly strange. Finally, she looked up and asked, “Who is this?”","“Jia Dan.”","“He’s one of Qi Licheng’s underlings, a minor gang leader nicknamed Rascal Egg. He was the leader of the group that stopped the tour bus carrying the families of our employees on the provincial highway,” Yang Xin explained.","“Start from the beginning.” Liu Yutong closed the file and motioned for him to continue.","Yang Xin nodded, gathered his thoughts, and recounted the entire story in detail.","“Qi Licheng is an obvious breakthrough point. General Manager Xu told me at the time that we could start our investigation with him. Then...”","“...”","“Wumao had been humiliated by Qi Licheng, so there was no way he didn’t hold a grudge. Once my people found out about it, I immediately had them approach him in secret.”","“He agreed?” Liu Yutong asked.","“He didn’t dare refuse,” Yang Xin said confidently.","“He’s afraid of Qi Licheng. Do you think he wouldn’t be afraid of the Wanlong Society?”","Yun Cheng nodded beside them. That was indeed the truth.","Not to mention a small-time thug like Wumao—even among the young masters of the capital, there were very few who weren’t afraid of the Wanlong Society.","Xu Shishi then continued the account, explaining how they had set the entire trap step by step after turning Wumao.","“Once we had won Wumao over, we began setting the trap. Jia Dan isn’t exactly bright. He’s the kind of hothead who goes off at the slightest provocation. On top of that, he already had a grudge against the Wanlong Society and wanted to show off in front of Qi Licheng. We only had to give him a little push, and he walked right into it.”","After hearing about Jia Dan’s actions, Liu Yutong was reminded of Scarface from Mingzhu City.","Compared with Scarface, Jia Dan was every bit his equal.","One was Zhuge Liang, the other was Pang Tong.","Both of them were incredibly easy to manipulate.","After listening to the entire plan, Liu Yutong regarded Xu Shishi with newfound approval. As expected of an executive who had risen through the ranks of a multinational logistics giant—her methods were ruthless and brilliant.","Subduing the enemy without fighting, making them turn on one another and clean up their own mess, then personally delivering the evidence into their hands afterward...","That kind of skill—using minimal effort to achieve maximum results—was not something an ordinary person could devise. Xu Shishi might be worth developing into a core member.","The plan Xu Shishi had led appeared simple and crude, but in reality, every step had been calculated precisely.","First, they had determined through a few brief interactions that Qi Licheng was the easiest point of entry. Then they had exploited Wumao’s hatred for Qi Licheng and recruited him as an inside man. Finally, they had taken advantage of Jia Dan’s stupidity and eagerness to prove himself in front of Qi Licheng, making him willingly serve as their weapon.","The Wanlong Society members sent in for support had recorded the entire process, gathering evidence of Jia Dan’s and the Qi family’s crimes.","They had even conveniently splashed the blame back onto the Wanlong Society.","That wasn’t a flaw in the plan. It was, in fact, a masterstroke.","If Qi Tianhu wasn’t an idiot, he would definitely use that point to make a major issue of it.","“General Manager Xu, did you work this way at your previous company too?” Yun Cheng couldn’t help asking.","“Not at all.”","Xu Shishi smiled and said, “That company was too conventional. Everything had to follow procedure, so I never had a chance to show what I could do. Working for the Chairwoman is much more interesting. I can finally let loose.”","Yang Xin’s mouth twitched as he listened from the side.","This woman was terrifying!","Then again, the female leaders of the Wanlong Society Group all seemed to be rather frightening. Take Yu Xin, for example. If she were here, her methods would probably be even more ruthless than Xu Shishi’s.","Of course, Little Hui was the sole exception. That girl was innocent and didn’t have much of a scheming mind.","“What about Qi Tianhu? Has there been any movement on his end?” Liu Yutong asked again.","“He should make his move soon.”","“Qi Licheng may be an idiot, but his father, Qi Tianhu, certainly isn’t. I estimate he already knows what happened. He just won’t act against us immediately.”","“The people General Manager Yang sent out have been tracking Qi Tianhu’s recent movements. As expected, he’s set his sights on the lithium mine at Qingyan Mountain.”","“Also, there’s a mining-rights auction in Jinchuan tomorrow, and that lithium mine is on the list. Qi Tianhu will definitely show up. However, quite a few companies are participating in the auction, including several powerful investors from outside the region. If Qi Tianhu wants to secure the mine, he has only two options.”","“The first is to follow their usual methods: sabotage the auction and then take over the mine himself at a low price. The second...”","Xu Shishi paused before continuing, “Kill the chicken to frighten the monkeys—make the other competitors back off before the bidding even begins.”","“Kill the chicken to frighten the monkeys?” Liu Yutong repeated with an amused tone.","Xu Shishi nodded. “Exactly.”","Liu Yutong looked at her. “Since you’ve already anticipated this, you must have a plan to deal with it.”","Xu Shishi nodded again. “Chairwoman, we’ve already obtained quite a bit of hard evidence through the incident involving Jia Dan. Most importantly, I had General Manager Yang assign people to keep an eye on Qi Licheng, and they uncovered something very important. This spoiled second-generation heir actually lost tens of millions gambling in Australia City. His father should know nothing about it. We can use that to our advantage as well.”","After hearing this, Liu Yutong fell silent for a moment, deep in thought. She did not ask for further details and simply said, “The auction is tomorrow?”","“Yes.”","“Then you and General Manager Yang will go. Make sure you secure it.”","“Yes, Chairwoman!”","“Yes, Young Lady!”","Yang Xin and Xu Shishi accepted their orders and left.","After they were gone, Liu Yutong suddenly turned to the Blue Butterfly behind her. “Has Professor Xu sent over the business proposal?”","Blue Butterfly shook her head. “Not yet.”","“Then forget about it...”","Liu Yutong had only just begun speaking when her phone rang.","She took it out and saw that Xu Yi was calling.","“Classmate Liu, does your offer to invest in my parents’ business still stand?” Xu Yi’s voice sounded somewhat nervous.","“Of course it does. But the business proposal...”","“I organized the proposal for my father. I just sent it to the email address you gave me.”","Liu Yutong was slightly surprised to hear that from Xu Yi.","Professor Xu hadn’t organized the materials himself; instead, his daughter had taken care of it. It seemed the girl was truly eager to change the situation.","“All right. I’ll take a look when I get the chance.”","“By the way, where is Professor Xu? Why didn’t he contact me himself?”","“I have no idea where my dad went. I went to his dormitory to look for him, but he wasn’t there, and I couldn’t reach him by phone either. I found the materials he’d only partially organized on his desk, so I finished them up while I was at it. I was worried you might be in a hurry, so I thought I’d send them to you first.”","“Mm, all right. I’ll get back to you as soon as possible.”","“Thank you! Thank you!”","After hanging up, Liu Yutong was reminded of what had happened in her previous life, and an uneasy feeling began to stir within her.","Professor Xu had suddenly disappeared. Could something have happened to him?"]},{"number":849,"title":"Chapter 849: 850, The Conversation Between Father and Son of the Qi Family.","paragraphs":["Jinchuan City, the headquarters of the Tiger Might Group.","Qi Tianhu sat behind the broad mahogany desk, looking impassively at his own good-for-nothing son standing before him.","“Licheng, is there something you’re hiding from me?”","“Dad, no.” Qi Licheng quickly shook his head.","“No?”","Qi Tianhu let out a cold laugh. “Then tell me—how did one of your establishments get taken down?”","The expression on Qi Licheng’s face froze. “Dad... you already know?”","“Of course I know. Have you found out who did it?”","Qi Licheng immediately replied, “It was the Myriad Dragons Society! They sent people to smash up my place. Dad, I was just about to gather our men and hit them back. We have to make them pay!”","“You idiot!”","Qi Tianhu slammed his hand on the desk and rose to his feet.","“This had nothing to do with the Myriad Dragons Society. You’ve been played, understand?!”","Qi Licheng was stunned. “If it wasn’t them, then who was it?”","“I’m asking you—who told you that the Myriad Dragons Society was behind it?”","“One of my men. A guy named Jia Dan.”","“The little punk who used to stop cars on the provincial highway and extort tolls?”","“My son, I really don’t know how you choose your people. You’ll take in any piece of trash. Do you honestly think that guy could take an establishment back from the Myriad Dragons Society?”","“Are you underestimating them?”","“But Dad, I confirmed it with Wumao too.”","“I’m asking you—was that Wumao the guy who came to see you last time?”","“Yes, him!”","“Heh... They’ve already sold you out, and you’re still helping them count the money!”","“Dad, what are you saying? Wumao and Jia Dan—they...”","“Licheng, how many times have I told you? When you’re out in the world, the most important thing is to use your brain.”","Qi Tianhu spoke with exasperation. “You can’t even control the people under you. They’ve made a fool of you, and you’re still standing here swearing that the Myriad Dragons Society did it.”","“You’re hopelessly stupid!”","“I’m telling you, this was definitely Wumao’s doing. He’s trying to drive a wedge between us! I knew the first time I saw that kid that he wasn’t simple. He’s vicious and scheming.”","Qi Licheng’s face flushed red with embarrassment and fury.","He was the young master of the Tiger Might Group, yet he had been completely played by two insignificant nobodies.","At the same time, he realized that his father had probably planted an informant at his side.","Fortunately, the informant probably wasn’t anyone important. Otherwise, everything he had done might have been exposed.","“Dad, I’ll have people drag those two bastards back here right now. I’ll skin them alive myself!” Qi Licheng said murderously.","“Drag them back for what? Sit down!” Qi Tianhu shouted.","Qi Licheng instantly deflated like a punctured balloon and meekly sat back down.","“Now you’re panicking? Where were you before?”","“I’ve told you that when dealing with people, you need to show both kindness and authority. But you? You cut off someone’s ear, let your men humiliate him, and stole his woman. You’ve driven him into a corner without eliminating him completely. Of course he’s going to hate you!”","“Use your brain from now on. Don’t just think about fighting and killing. If you offend someone, either don’t offend them in the first place, or wipe them out completely and leave no loose ends. Don’t put yourself in danger by leaving things half-finished!”","“Yes... I understand, Dad.”","Qi Licheng lowered his head in shame.","Seeing his son’s dejected expression, Qi Tianhu let out a long sigh. His anger had eased somewhat.","“Still, Wumao using the Myriad Dragons Society’s name to set this up has given us an opportunity.”","Qi Licheng raised his head and hurriedly asked, “What opportunity?”","“To borrow their strength.”","Qi Tianhu slowly stood up and walked over to the map of Jinchuan hanging on the wall. He pointed at Qingyan Mountain.","“The auction for the Qingyan Mountain lithium mine is tomorrow. Its confirmed reserves rank among the top three in the country. It’s incredibly valuable, and I’m determined to win it.”","“Besides us, the bidders include the provincial XN Mining Group, Chengyu Group, three major mining companies from other provinces, and possibly the Myriad Dragons Society Group as well. The competition will be intense.”","“If we bid normally, we might not be able to beat those major corporations. So we need to make them withdraw voluntarily.”","Qi Licheng suddenly understood, and his eyes lit up. “So you’re going to use the Myriad Dragons Society as an example—to kill one chicken and scare the monkeys?”","“Exactly.”","Qi Tianhu nodded, a smile spreading across his face. “Whether or not they were responsible for smashing our establishment, from this moment on, they were. I’ve already had people gather evidence and submit it. Then, at the auction, we’ll have them arrested on the spot. We’ll use the authorities to intimidate the other bidders.”","“And once this gets out, the Myriad Dragons Society’s reputation in Jinchuan will be ruined. Their construction sites will have to shut down, and all the money they’ve invested in the Jinchuan area will go down the drain. We won’t even need to act. They’ll be forced to kneel before us on their own.”","“Once the Myriad Dragons Society falls, the other competitors will understand how deep the waters in Jinchuan really are. By then, they’ll withdraw without us having to say a word.”","The more Qi Licheng listened, the more excited he became. The gloom from being reprimanded moments earlier had vanished completely.","“Dad, that’s brilliant! Using borrowed power to strike at them—one move takes care of the Myriad Dragons Society and intimidates everyone else. Two birds with one stone!”","Qi Tianhu gave him a deep look and said earnestly, “Son, Wumao may be vicious, but he does have a bit of cunning. Once we bring down the Myriad Dragons Society Group, you can deal with him however you like.”","“But on one condition: make sure you clean up after yourself. Don’t make me wipe your ass again!”","“I understand, Dad.”","“Dad, if there’s nothing else, I’ll be going.”","Qi Licheng didn’t want to spend another second in that office. His entire body felt uncomfortable.","“Wait.”","Qi Tianhu stopped him, his gaze turning sharp.","“Licheng, I want to ask you something. You’d better answer honestly.”","Qi Licheng’s heart jolted. Bracing himself, he said, “Go ahead, Dad.”","“Someone told me that people have been moving drugs in Jinchuan recently. Do you know anything about it?”","Qi Licheng’s heart sank. He guessed that the report had come from the informant his father had planted, but he still forced himself to remain calm.","“I... I don’t know anything about it.”","“You really don’t?”","“Really!”","Qi Tianhu stared at him for a long while. Only after making Qi Licheng’s back prickle with fear did he slowly speak.","“Licheng, you’re my son. I know you better than anyone. I know exactly how many crooked thoughts are running through your head. I’ll ask you one last time: do you know about this or not?!”","Sweat began to bead on Qi Licheng’s forehead.","Of course he knew.","Not only did he know, but the drugs were being sold throughout Jinchuan from locations he had provided.","Of course, he never touched the stuff himself or handled it directly. He merely used the establishments under his control to provide that man with places to conduct transactions, taking a cut of the profits.","He had kept this matter hidden from his father all along.","Although his father, Qi Tianhu, ran roughshod over Jinchuan and engaged in all kinds of shady dealings, he had one absolute bottom line: he would never touch drugs.","Getting involved with that stuff meant crossing his most forbidden line.","“Dad, I really didn’t know. We’ve already got so much money—why would I deal in that stuff?” Qi Licheng said guiltily.","At last, Qi Tianhu withdrew his gaze. “Hmm. I didn’t think you’d dare.”","“Licheng, remember this. The Qi family can do anything—cheat, swindle, force people into buying or selling, bully and dominate the market. Even if we get caught for those things, the worst that happens is a few years in prison. But drugs are different. Touch them, and you die.”","“If you get pulled in, you won’t be the only one to die. The entire Qi family will be buried alongside you.”","Qi Licheng hurriedly nodded. “Dad, I’ll keep that in mind. I absolutely won’t touch the stuff!”","Qi Tianhu waved a hand. “When you go back later, have someone inspect every establishment under your control. If you find anyone secretly involved in this kind of business, clean them out completely. Even your most trusted aides are not to be spared. Understand?”","“Understood!”","“Go!”","Only then did Qi Licheng breathe a sigh of relief before hurriedly leaving the office.","Watching his son’s departing back, Qi Tianhu sighed inwardly.","Hopefully, he really was unaware of it."]},{"number":850,"title":"Chapter 850: 851, On the Matter of Loyalty.","paragraphs":["Qi Licheng arrived at the company entrance with a dark expression, climbed into his Porsche, and slammed his fist against the steering wheel.","“Ah!!!”","“Wumao, Jia Dan, I’m going to make you wish you were dead!”","After venting his anger, Qi Licheng pulled out his phone and dialed a number.","“A Jiu, find those two bastards, Wumao and Jia Dan. Put out a wanted notice. I want to strip them alive with my own hands!”","A Jiu was one of the two trusted men Qi Licheng had previously sent to handle affairs at the mine. As for the other, Leopard, his whereabouts remained unknown to this day.","After hanging up, Qi Licheng leaned back in his seat and closed his eyes for a moment before dialing another number.","The phone rang for a long time before someone finally answered.","“Young Master Cheng, to what do I owe the call?”","“You can’t use my channels anymore. My father has noticed something. He specifically asked me about the drugs just now. Things have gotten especially tense in Jinchuan recently, so we have to put this on hold for now.”","There was a few seconds of silence on the other end, followed by a mocking laugh.","“Young Master Cheng, you say we stop, and we stop? What am I supposed to do with my shipment?”","“That’s your problem. In any case, you can’t use the venues here in Jinchuan anymore.”","“Young Master Cheng, are you trying to burn the bridge after crossing it?” The other man’s tone turned cold.","“Don’t forget who helped you cover the several tens of millions you lost in Aomen. And I’ve kept all the evidence of you providing venues for me to move your goods. If you dare cut off my source of income, I won’t mind sending it to your father—or...” The other man paused. “Sending it to the police.”","“You fucking dare! Believe it or not, I’ll kill you!”","The man on the other end didn’t take his threat seriously at all.","“Heh heh heh... Young Master Cheng, I’ll pretend I didn’t hear that threat just now. But this is your one and only warning. There won’t be a next time.”","“I’ll say it again: the channel in Jinchuan cannot be stopped. Not only can it not stop, but next month’s shipment has to be doubled.”","“You’re crazy!”","“My father is already suspicious. If we keep this up, something will happen!”","“That’s your problem. It has nothing to do with me.”","“Beep, beep, beep...”","Qi Licheng was about to say something else, but the other man had already hung up.","Furious, he slammed his fist against the steering wheel again.","He had actually known for a long time that he’d been set up.","That kind-hearted big brother who had taken the initiative to lend him money to turn his luck around at the casino in Aomen had never been kind at all. The whole thing had been a carefully designed trap—a damn pig-butchering scam!","The man’s purpose was to deceive him and use his venues as cover for selling contraband.","But it was too late for Qi Licheng to do anything now. All he could do was grit his teeth, swallow his anger, and follow the man’s demands.","...","Jia Dan had been living very comfortably these past few days.","After all, he had taken down seven of the Wanlong Society’s venues in one night. Overnight, he had become a legendary figure in the western part of Jinchuan.","His exploits were being passed around by every street thug in the city.","“Did you hear? Rascal Egg led his men and took down seven of the Wanlong Society’s venues in one night!”","“Seven? I heard it was more than that—at least thirteen.”","“Holy shit, he’s that tough? What was Young Master Cheng’s reaction?”","“What else could it be? He must be planning to give him more responsibility! I heard Young Master Cheng is handing all those venues over to him. Jia Dan has really risen to power this time.”","“Rascal Egg is badass!”","“...”","The rumors became more exaggerated with every retelling, and Jia Dan’s status rose along with the praise.","These days, he walked through the streets with his chest puffed out. Even the local bosses who had previously ignored him now took out cigarettes the moment they spotted him from a distance, greeting him with flattering smiles.","Many people also came to join him of their own accord, hoping to make something of themselves alongside him.","Jia Dan naturally accepted everyone without exception.","In just a few days, the number of men under him had skyrocketed from a little over thirty to more than a hundred.","Of course, most of them were only there for the reputation. They weren’t truly loyal to him.","At the Great Splendor Bathhouse.","After taking a bath, Jia Dan lay on a sofa in the lounge wearing a bathrobe, his legs crossed and a cigarette between his fingers as he puffed away contentedly.","A local boss was sitting beside him. In reality, he was nothing more than the leader of a small gang with a little influence. Now that Jia Dan had risen to prominence, he wanted to curry favor with this powerful new ally.","“Brother Jia, you’re incredible! Absolutely incredible!”","“From now on, Brother Jia, you’ll be Young Master Cheng’s right-hand man. Don’t forget to look after your brothers. You eat the meat, and just leave me a little soup.”","The flattery sent Jia Dan soaring. His entire body practically floated toward the ceiling, and for a moment, he even felt as if he were the underground emperor of Jinchuan.","With a grand wave of his hand, he declared, “Of course, of course. We’re all brothers here. Whenever there’s a big deal in the future, I’ll definitely bring you in. You can count on that.”","“Not to brag, but these days, I’ve got people and venues. If there’s anything you need, just ask. In Jinchuan, apart from Young Master Cheng, my word carries the most weight!”","The local boss immediately showered him with praise. “Brother Jia, you’re a true friend!”","“Since Brother Jia treats me with such loyalty, I’ll make this promise today: whenever you need something, just call me. I, Big Brother Crooked Mouth, won’t hesitate. I’d climb mountains of blades or plunge into seas of fire for you. If I even frown, then I’m no son of a human being!”","“What if someone comes after me with a knife?” Jia Dan asked jokingly.","Big Brother Crooked Mouth pounded his chest and swore, “Then I, Crooked Mouth, will be the first one to charge in! I may not be as brave as you, Brother Jia, but I’ve been out here for many years, and I know that loyalty is the most important thing. If Brother Jia ever gets into trouble, I’ll definitely help!”","Jia Dan was pleased with his declaration. He reached out and patted Crooked Mouth on the shoulder.","“Good. Since you’ve put it that way, we’re brothers from now on. We’ll make money together, drink together, and sleep with women together—”","Before he could finish, the door was suddenly kicked open from outside, and more than a dozen men stormed in.","The man leading them was lean and had a buzz cut.","It was Qi Licheng’s subordinate, A Jiu.","Behind him were more than a dozen men, each carrying a steel pipe or a baseball bat. Every one of them wore a murderous expression.","The moment they entered, they shouted, “Who’s Jia Dan?”","Jia Dan turned toward the commotion. The sight of the men startled him, and he instinctively sat up to look at the newcomers.","The leader looked vaguely familiar, but Jia Dan couldn’t immediately remember where he had seen him before.","“I’m Jia Dan. What can I do for you, brother?”","A Jiu sneered. “Who I am isn’t important. What matters is that someone sent me to take you somewhere.”","“Who?”","“Young Master Cheng.”","When Jia Dan heard those words, he froze for a moment before visibly relaxing.","“So you’re brothers sent by Young Master Cheng! You scared me for a second. I thought you were someone else.”","“Brother, what does Young Master Cheng want with me? Is he giving me more territory? Come on, let’s go. I’ll even bring a couple of bottles of good liquor so I can have a proper drink with him.”","A Jiu shook his head expressionlessly.","“No need to bring liquor. Young Master Cheng isn’t inviting you for a drink.”","“Then what does he want me for?” Jia Dan asked.","“Young Master Cheng says he wants to strip your skin off with his own hands.”","???","The flesh on Jia Dan’s face twitched as he stammered, “B-Brother, this has to be a misunderstanding, right? I’m absolutely loyal to Young Master Cheng...”","A Jiu couldn’t be bothered to waste his breath on him. He raised a hand and waved. “Take him.”","The dozen or so men behind him immediately raised their weapons and charged at Jia Dan.","Terrified, Jia Dan turned and fled, but it was already too late. He had barely reached the doorway when someone kicked him from behind, sending him sprawling to the floor. A savage beating followed.","“Don’t hit me! Don’t hit me! I’m one of you!”","“Ahhh!”","Jia Dan clutched his head and screamed. Just as he was nearing despair, he looked toward Crooked Mouth, who was still sitting there obediently, and cried for help, “Crooked Mouth, we’re brothers! Save me!”","The moment Crooked Mouth heard his name, his heart lurched and his scalp prickled. All he could do was lower his head and pretend he hadn’t seen a thing.","At the same time, he cursed Jia Dan and his ancestors to the eighteenth generation in his heart.","What a load of crap about being Young Master Cheng’s trusted aide! He was nothing but a con man!","Crooked Mouth had actually treated this bastard like a brother just moments ago, and now the man even had the nerve to ask him for help.","As if that were ever going to happen!","Jia Dan’s shout also drew A Jiu’s attention to Crooked Mouth.","A Jiu sauntered over and stood in front of him, looking down from above. “Hey, he’s asking you to save him.”","Crooked Mouth hurriedly waved his hands. “I don’t know him! I’m just here to take a bath!”","A Jiu looked amused. “Wasn’t he your brother?”","Crooked Mouth deliberately played dumb. “What brother? Don’t make things up! I’ve been making my way in Jinchuan for years, and the person I respect most is Young Master Cheng. If I’d known this bastard had offended Young Master Cheng, I would’ve been the first to take him out!”","Hearing this, Jia Dan was so furious he nearly spat up blood. “Crooked Mouth, fuck you!”","After cursing him viciously, he added mournfully, “People these days are so damn disloyal. What happened to brotherly loyalty? I’m ashamed of all of you!”","Then he suddenly remembered something. Raising his head, he shouted at A Jiu, “Brother Jiu! Brother Jiu! Stop hitting me! I have important information! I know where Wumao is. I’ll take you to him!”","A Jiu’s eyes narrowed slightly. “You know where Wumao is?”","“I do! I do!”","Crooked Mouth nodded frantically. “That bastard called me this morning. Brother Jiu, give me a chance. I’ll take you to capture him and make up for my crimes! But I do have one small request...”","“Speak!”","“Um... if someone’s going to be skinned, could you skin Wumao first?”","A Jiu glanced at him with an ambiguous smile.","“Sure.”"]},{"number":851,"title":"Chapter 851: 852, I Want to Be a Human Being.","paragraphs":["The southern outskirts of the city, in an urban village.","Inside an old residential building, Wumao was sprawled on a worn-out sofa. An old-fashioned television sat on the coffee table in front of him, broadcasting the midday news.","To his right lay a cellphone. To his left was an opened bottle of beer, still fizzing.","The room was small, and the curtains had been drawn tightly shut. The only light came from the television, flickering across his gloomy face.","After watching the news for a while, Wumao picked up the beer and took a long gulp. He wiped the foam from the corner of his mouth with the back of his hand and muttered to himself, “That idiot Jia Dan should’ve been caught by Young Master Cheng’s men by now.”","Jia Dan had smashed so many of Qi Licheng’s establishments and beaten Leopard’s trusted lieutenants into cripples. No matter how stupid Qi Licheng was, it wouldn’t take him long to figure things out. And once he did, there was no way he would let Jia Dan off.","After Jia Dan was caught, with that spineless coward’s personality, he would definitely sell Wumao out.","But Wumao wasn’t worried in the slightest.","He had prepared a way out for himself long ago.","When the people from the Wanlong Association first approached him, they gave him two choices.","The first was to continue being Qi Licheng’s dog and wait for the day Young Master Cheng was in a bad mood and cut off his other ear as well. Once both ears were gone, he would be worse off than a dog.","The second was to work for the Wanlong Association. Once the job was done, they promised to send him somewhere safe to lie low for a few years, along with enough money to settle down and live a peaceful life.","He had chosen the second option without the slightest hesitation.","As for whether that idiot Jia Dan lived or died, Wumao had never cared.","Someone who would help count the money after being sold was nothing but a waste of food, even if he stayed alive.","Wumao picked up the remote and was just about to change the channel when his thumb pressed the button. Suddenly, he heard a rush of hurried footsteps outside the door.","His expression changed. He shot up from the sofa, grabbed the cellphone from the coffee table, quickly dialed a number, and stuffed the phone into the inner pocket of his clothes.","The instant he finished, a tremendous bang rang out. The door was violently kicked open from outside.","“Wumao! We finally found you!”","Wumao’s body stiffened. He slowly turned around and saw A Jiu leading seven or eight men into the room.","Behind A Jiu stood a familiar figure.","Jia Dan.","“Wumao, you son of a bitch!”","The moment Jia Dan saw him, his eyes turned bloodshot.","After questioning him, Jia Dan now knew that he had been used by Wumao from beginning to end—and that this bastard had ruined his life.","“What are you getting so worked up about?” A Jiu shot him a cold look.","Jia Dan forced down his rage and glared at Wumao through clenched teeth.","Seeing the murderous look on Jia Dan’s face actually calmed Wumao down. He slowly raised both hands and smiled.","“Well, Brother Jiu, what brings you here? And Brother Jia, you don’t look so good. Didn’t sleep well last night?”","“How dare you laugh!” Jia Dan pointed at him and began cursing. “You bastard! You’ve ruined me! I treated you like a brother, but you used me as a weapon. Are you even human?!”","Wumao tilted his head and looked at him as though he were an idiot.","“Brother Jia, I have no idea what you’re talking about. When did I ever use you as a weapon? You were the one who insisted on taking men to smash those places last night. I even kindly lent you more than thirty of my men. How can you turn around and blame me?”","“You still dare to deny it?”","“You said those establishments had been taken by the Wanlong Association! You said Leopard and the others were traitors! It was all made-up nonsense! You lied to me and played me for a fool. Now Young Master Cheng has put a price on my head! I hope you die a horrible death!”","Wumao sighed and said in an utterly sincere tone, “Brother Jia, I was deceived too. I only repeated what I heard from someone else. Who knew the information was fake? I’m a victim too.”","He paused, then changed tack.","“And don’t blame me. You kept preaching about brotherhood, but didn’t you sell me out too?”","Jia Dan’s face stiffened.","“I...I only did that because you forced me into it.”","A Jiu couldn’t be bothered to watch them tear into each other. He waved his hand.","“Enough nonsense. Take them away!”","Two of his men immediately stepped forward and restrained Wumao from either side.","Wumao didn’t resist. He cooperated fully as they escorted him outside. But when he passed Jia Dan, he suddenly stopped and whispered something into his ear.","“Brother Jia, did you know that the reason I lost one of my ears was actually because of you?”","“We’re even now.”","The anger gradually faded from Jia Dan’s face.","What did he mean?","Why was Wumao saying he had lost his ear because of him?","What the hell was this bastard talking about? He couldn’t understand a word of it!","Before he could ask, A Jiu’s men roughly dragged him away.","...","On the outskirts of Jinchuan City stood a warehouse that had long since been abandoned.","Qi Licheng had specifically chosen it as the perfect place to settle things privately. He intended to deal with these two traitors here.","After Jia Dan and Wumao were brought in, they were each tied to a chair, unable to move.","In front of them, Qi Licheng sat in an old leather chair that had seemingly been dragged in from somewhere. He had one leg crossed over the other, a folding knife glinting coldly in his hand.","It was the same knife he had used to cut off Jia Dan’s ear that day.","“Well, well. Long time no see.”","Qi Licheng wore a smile, but there was something chilling about it that made their spines prickle.","When Jia Dan saw the knife in his hand, he was terrified. He cried out, “Young...Young Master Cheng, I’m innocent! I was really tricked by that bastard Wumao! My loyalty to you is as clear as the heavens and earth!”","“Hahaha...Loyalty?”","Qi Licheng laughed. He rose and walked over to Jia Dan, tapping his face with the back of the knife.","“You smashed seven or eight of my establishments and injured dozens of my brothers, and now you’re talking to me about loyalty? Jia Dan, do you really think I’m that easy to fool?!”","“No, no! Young Master Cheng, I really...”","“That’s enough.”","Qi Licheng cut him off and turned his attention to Wumao.","Compared with that idiotic dog Jia Dan, he was far more interested in Wumao.","This was the useless wretch whose ear Qi Licheng had personally cut off, and whom Leopard had publicly humiliated and forced to crawl like a dog. Yet somehow, he had managed to lay out such an elaborate scheme to retaliate against him.","To be honest, if they weren’t on opposing sides now, Qi Licheng might even have admired him a little.","“Wumao, you really are something.”","Qi Licheng walked over and crouched in front of him. He used the tip of the knife to lift Wumao’s chin, forcing him to look up.","“I cut off one of your ears, and you set up such a massive scheme to come after me? Not bad. You’ve got guts!”","“Do you hate me that much?”","With the knife tip pressed against his chin, Wumao showed no trace of fear. He smiled.","“You flatter me, Young Master Cheng. When you cut off my ear, that was a reward from you. How could I possibly resent you?”","“Then what was the point of all this?”","“To find a way to survive.”","Wumao looked at him calmly. “Young Master Cheng, I’ve worked under you for years, paying you hundreds of thousands every month. I may not have made great contributions, but I’ve certainly put in the effort. And yet what did you do? You let Leopard force me to crawl like a dog in front of all those people and steal my woman from me. You sat there watching the show without saying a single word on my behalf.”","“That was when I realized that, in your eyes, I’m nothing but a dog. When you’re pleased, you toss me a bone. When you’re displeased, you can butcher me whenever you want.”","“I don’t want to be a dog anymore. I want to be a man.”","The smile gradually faded from Qi Licheng’s face.","“Fine. You want to be a man, do you? I’ll make that happen.”","He turned and ordered A Jiu, “Hold him down.”","A Jiu immediately led his men forward. They pulled Wumao out of the chair and pinned him firmly to the floor.","Qi Licheng crouched down and pressed the folding knife against Wumao’s other ear. The cold blade rested against his skin, and Wumao could feel its bone-chilling edge.","“Wumao, you set a trap for me. By the rules of the underworld, I’d be justified in slicing you into a thousand pieces and dumping you in the river to feed the fish. But I’m in a good mood today. I only want your other ear.”","“You want to be a man, don’t you? Let’s see how you’ll manage that without either ear!”","Pinned to the floor, Wumao’s forehead broke out in a fine sheen of sweat, but he clenched his teeth and refused to make a sound.","Jia Dan watched from the side, his heart pounding with terror. His legs trembled nonstop beneath the chair.","Just as Qi Licheng tightened his grip on the knife and was about to press down—","BANG!!!","The warehouse door was violently blasted open from outside and crashed to the ground, sending clouds of dust billowing through the air.","A black-clad figure strode in through the dust. Backlit by the sunlight, his face was impossible to make out, but the dragon-shaped insignia on his chest stood out sharply.","Nearly a hundred men dressed in black rushed in behind him, instantly surrounding the entire warehouse.","“Well, well, well. What’s going on here? Carrying out private punishment in broad daylight? That’s a crime, you know. Not a good idea!”"]},{"number":852,"title":"Chapter 852: 853, Zhao Tianyi: Teaching Me About the Law","paragraphs":["Everyone in the warehouse turned toward the entrance in unison.","Qi Licheng’s hand, still gripping the knife, froze in midair. The expression on his face shifted from shock to anger, then from anger to wariness.","“Who the hell are you? How dare you barge into my territory!”","Zhao Tianyi adjusted the gold-rimmed glasses on the bridge of his nose and walked in unhurriedly. The group of men in black behind him streamed inside like a black tide.","Nearly a hundred men, all dressed in black suits and wearing dragon-shaped badges.","The aura. The oppressive presence. It was every bit as intimidating as a gang shootout in a movie.","No—it was even more frightening than anything in a movie.","Qi Licheng’s men swallowed nervously one after another at the sight.","It wasn’t that they were cowards. The other side’s show of force was simply too damn terrifying.","A Jiu swallowed and leaned close to Qi Licheng’s ear, whispering, “Young Master Cheng, they’re from the Ten Thousand Dragons Society.”","Although Qi Licheng was a little slow to react, he recognized them soon enough.","The man surnamed Yang he had met at Jinchuan Pavilion that day had been dressed exactly like this.","Black suits, dragon-shaped badges, the same intimidating style.","What he never would have expected was that the Ten Thousand Dragons Society would dare barge directly into his territory—and bring nearly a hundred men with them.","They had hidden their strength well.","Most importantly, he had brought too few men today. For now, he could only swallow his pride.","“What exactly do you want? Don’t tell me you’re planning to make a move against me. I’m warning you, that’s illegal! This is a society governed by law!”","When Qi Licheng said this, not only Zhao Tianyi but even the underlings behind him almost failed to react.","Seriously, Young Master Cheng? Those are words you can say with a straight face?","Have you even looked at what you’re doing?","Zhao Tianyi laughed when he heard that.","“Young Master Qi, you want to talk to me about the law?”","He slowly pulled his lawyer’s license from the inner pocket of his suit, opened it, and waved it gently in front of Qi Licheng.","“Take a good look. This is my license. Zhao Tianyi, Tianyi Law Firm. Completely legal.”","“By the looks of it, I’m actually more qualified than you to talk about the law, aren’t I?”","“Since I’m in a good mood, I’ll explain it to you. Based on the evidence we have, you’re suspected of unlawful detention, intentional assault, provoking trouble, organizing a criminal gang, and...” He paused. “Oh, right. Drug-related offenses as well.”","“You’ll probably be eating peanuts before long.”","Qi Licheng’s expression changed dramatically. “You’re talking out of your ass! When the hell have I ever been involved with drugs?”","Zhao Tianyi pointed at Wumao and Jia Dan, who were tied to chairs.","“Young Master Qi, you really went all out on them. Unlawful detention and intentional assault are both serious crimes. Add drug-related offenses and organizing a criminal gang on top of that, and with all the charges combined...” He stroked his chin thoughtfully. “I’d estimate the metal content in your cremated remains will be quite high.”","“You...”","Qi Licheng wanted nothing more than to tear this lawyer apart, but when he saw the nearly hundred men in black behind him, he forcibly suppressed his rage.","One who cannot bear the small troubles will never accomplish great things.","More importantly, he had no confidence that he could beat them.","“Fine. So you’re the Ten Thousand Dragons Society? You’re ruthless!”","“But don’t forget, this is Jinchuan. This is the Qi family’s territory! If you dare lay a finger on me today, my father will never let you get away with it!”","Zhao Tianyi smiled again.","“Young Master Qi, you’ve misunderstood.”","“We’re legitimate businessmen. We never do anything illegal. We simply enjoy helping those in need and following the example of Lei Feng by doing good deeds.”","As he spoke, he suddenly seemed to remember something and smacked his forehead.","“Oh, right. I almost forgot to tell you—the police should be here any minute. You can tell them whatever you have to say.”","Qi Licheng’s face instantly turned pale.","“You... You called the police?”","“Of course.” Zhao Tianyi nodded solemnly. “When you encounter illegal activity, you report it to the police at once. It’s every citizen’s duty. Young Master Qi, don’t tell me you don’t even know that. They taught it in elementary-school civics.”","Qi Licheng: “...”","You barged into my territory with over a hundred men in black, then had the nerve to tell me you’re law-abiding citizens?","You people look even more like gangsters than I do!","But now wasn’t the time to worry about that.","The police would arrive any moment, and he had to get out of there immediately.","If the police caught him on the spot—and if the evidence the other side mentioned really existed—he might actually end up with several pounds of peanuts before being sent to the crematorium.","Qi Licheng secretly gave A Jiu a look, signaling for him to lead the men out through the back door. Once they were outside, he was to find his father and report everything.","As long as the old man stepped in, any problem could be solved.","A Jiu understood at once and nodded. He was a professional when it came to running away. Otherwise, after all the vile things he had done, he would have been behind bars long ago.","However, he had barely turned around and taken a few steps when a dark figure blocked his path.","“Move!”","A Jiu instinctively tried to attack.","Then...","Crack!","In an instant, his wrist was twisted behind his back. It felt as though his entire arm might have been torn right out of its socket.","“Ahhh!”","A Jiu doubled over like a shrimp, howling in pain.","“Assaulting a police officer... Ah, no, my mistake. Assaulting a law-abiding citizen carrying out a mission of civic heroism is also a crime,” Zhao Tianyi added lazily from across the room.","A Jiu, drenched in cold sweat: “...”","Damn it, why was this lawyer’s mouth so vicious?","He could turn black into white! My arm is practically broken, for crying out loud!","But all A Jiu could do was curse him silently in his heart.","Qi Licheng’s expression had become uglier than ever.","In Jinchuan, Qi Licheng had always been the one bringing men to surround others. Since when had anyone dared surround him instead? And these people were outsiders—a group of dragons crossing the river—who had broken one of his men’s arms right in front of him, on his own turf.","If word got out, how was he supposed to keep his standing in Jinchuan’s underworld?","“Damn it, this is going too far!”","He spun around and roared at the dozens of men behind him, “What are you waiting for? Get them! Take these outsiders down!”","“Whoever knocks one of them down gets a hundred thousand! Whoever kills the leader gets five hundred thousand!”","With enough money on the line, even cowards became brave.","The men who had been glancing uneasily at one another suddenly had greed shining in their eyes. Then, as if injected with adrenaline, they charged toward the men in black at the entrance, shouting wildly.","Five hundred thousand!","That was enough to let them spend freely in Jinchuan for years!","Taking advantage of the chaos, Qi Licheng quietly began retreating.","He didn’t expect his useless underlings to defeat the Ten Thousand Dragons Society.","All he needed was for them to hold the enemy off. Even one or two minutes would be enough. As long as he could escape, he would still have a chance to turn things around.","Zhao Tianyi watched the gangsters charging toward him, shouting at the tops of their lungs. There wasn’t the slightest trace of tension on his face.","He calmly took one step backward, pulled a cigarette from his pocket, and placed it between his lips. Then he lit it with a lighter, took a deep drag, and slowly exhaled a cloud of smoke.","After that, he raised his right hand and gave it a slight wave.","“Move!”","“Yes!”","Swish! Swish! Swish!","Nearly a hundred men in black drew their batons in perfect unison.","Then they moved.","The thug leading the charge had just raised his baseball bat when his wrist suddenly went numb. The bat flew from his hand, and before he could react, a kick struck the back of his knee. Then blows rained down on him with sharp smacks until he collapsed to the ground, screaming.","Just as he was about to get back up, a large hand pressed down on the back of his head.","“Holy shit!”","The thug instinctively tried to struggle, but both his arms were already twisted behind his back. A moment later, a pair of handcuffs snapped shut around his wrists.","Wait.","Handcuffs?","The thug was stunned.","Were these people gangsters or cops? Why the hell were they carrying handcuffs?","Could they be police officers in disguise?","Before he could figure it out, his fellow gang members had already started dropping one after another.","They fell in all sorts of positions, but the result was the same: every one of them was pinned to the ground and handcuffed.","The whole thing took less than thirty seconds.","The dozens of men brought by A Jiu had all been taken down.","Not one of them was still standing, yet not a single one was bleeding.","These men in black knew exactly how much force to use. Every blow landed in a place that caused excruciating pain without resulting in any serious injury that would show up on an examination.","And their movements were unbelievably clean and efficient!","Jia Dan had witnessed everything from start to finish, his mouth hanging open wide enough to fit an egg.","He recognized them.","These men in black were the exact same group of underlings Wumao had lent him that night!","They were wearing the same black suits; the only difference was that they weren’t wearing the dragon-shaped badges.","That night, they had merely taken photos and videos without actually lifting a finger. Today, Jia Dan finally got to see what they were truly capable of.","Dozens of men—wiped out in less than thirty seconds.","What the hell kind of combat ability was that?","Zhao Tianyi glanced at the gangsters groaning across the ground and nodded in satisfaction.","“All right. Hand them over to the police later.”","“Yes, sir!”","The men in black immediately began wrapping things up and collecting evidence."]},{"number":853,"title":"Chapter 853: 854. Where the Fools Go.","paragraphs":["After they finished cleaning up the battlefield, a man in black came over to Zhao Tianyi and reported, “Lawyer Zhao, Qi Licheng escaped through the back door.”","Zhao Tianyi flicked the ash from his cigarette, completely unbothered. “Let him go. There’s no need to chase a cornered enemy.”","With that, he raised a hand and pointed at Wumao and Jia Dan, who were still tied to chairs. “Untie them.”","The man in black acknowledged the order, then gave a signal to the two men behind him, indicating that they should step forward and release the captives.","The two men immediately went over and undid their restraints.","Wumao rubbed his wrists, which had gone numb from the tight bindings, and said to Zhao Tianyi, “Thank you!”","Zhao Tianyi waved a hand. “Don’t thank me. If you hadn’t made that call, we couldn’t have arrived so quickly.”","As it turned out, the number Wumao had dialed when A Jiu and his men kicked down the door belonged to one of the men in black from the Wanlong Society.","The man had certainly reacted quickly.","Zhao Tianyi then turned his attention to Jia Dan, who was trembling beside them.","“As for you, choose how you want to die.”","The moment those words left his mouth, Jia Dan was scared out of his wits. With a thud, he dropped to his knees.","“Please spare me! Big brother, please spare me! I have elderly parents to support and children to raise...”","He shouted while frantically banging his head against the floor.","Zhao Tianyi looked at him coldly. “I’m not an unreasonable man. But who gave you the guts to stop the Wanlong Society’s convoy? And then smear our name? Didn’t you bother asking around? Plenty of so-called big shots in the underworld who offended the Wanlong Society have already ended up dead. You’re just a nobody. Where did you get the nerve?”","Jia Dan stammered, “I... I really didn’t know that was the Wanlong Society’s convoy! If I had known, I wouldn’t have dared to touch it even if you gave me a hundred lives, big brother... Please, I beg you, show mercy and let me go!”","Just then, Wumao suddenly stepped forward and said to Zhao Tianyi, “Lawyer Zhao, Brother Jia didn’t know this was the Wanlong Society’s convoy. If he had known, he never would have dared to do anything. Could you give him a chance?”","“He’s not exactly a good man, but he isn’t completely useless either.”","When Jia Dan heard that, he hurriedly nodded. “That’s right, that’s right! Wumao is telling the truth! I, Jia Dan, may not be a good person, but I’m useful! I really am useful!”","Zhao Tianyi pushed his glasses up the bridge of his nose and looked Jia Dan over again before asking Wumao, “Is he really useful?”","“He is.”","Wumao nodded, then turned back to Jia Dan, who was kneeling on the floor.","“Brother Jia, I’m going to give you a way to stay alive.”","“I can plead with Lawyer Zhao to spare your life. I can even have you sent somewhere safe. But in return, you have to answer one question.”","Jia Dan said, “What question? Ask me anything! I... I’ll tell you everything I know!”","Wumao asked, “Where did you send those young people with intellectual disabilities?”","Jia Dan’s expression changed instantly.","The desperation to survive gradually vanished from his face, replaced by panic and guilt.","“Why... why are you asking about that?”","“Brother Jia, you were born to parents too. The young people with intellectual disabilities under your control are living, breathing human beings. You tricked them into leaving their homes, used them as tools to make money and as scapegoats, then discarded them when you were finished. Do you really think that’s acceptable?”","Jia Dan’s lips moved, but his voice came out hoarse. “I had no choice. If I didn’t do that, how was I supposed to support all my brothers?”","“Stop using your ‘brothers’ as an excuse.”","“Your life is in the hands of the Wanlong Society’s boss now. If you want to live, then tell us everything honestly!”","“If you confess, I’ll guarantee your life. If you refuse, then I’m sorry, but there’s nothing I can do for you. You’ve already seen what the Wanlong Society’s boss is capable of.”","“Think it over carefully.”","Sweat began to bead on Jia Dan’s forehead.","He knew better than anyone how serious the crimes he had committed were.","Some of those intellectually disabled young people had been lured from the countryside. Some had been bought from human traffickers. Others had been handed over by their own families. Those impoverished families couldn’t afford to raise a mentally disabled son, and when they heard that someone could arrange work and provide food and lodging, they were practically eager to send him away.","Regardless of how they had ended up in his hands, they all became nothing more than tools for making money.","Those who were obedient were trained and taken to the highways to stop cars and collect tolls. Whenever the authorities came to arrest them, Jia Dan would push the young people forward to take the blame.","Those who refused to cooperate were sent to coal mines to work as slaves.","Even a normal person would come out of a coal mine half-dead, let alone someone with an intellectual disability.","Going hungry and lacking proper clothing were everyday occurrences. They had to work at least ten hours a day, and the moment they slacked off, they were beaten with a whip. If they fell ill or were injured, no one cared. They were simply dumped in the mountains and left to fend for themselves.","After working for several years, it was considered a miracle if half of them were still alive.","When their families came looking, Jia Dan would tell them that the person had run away and that he had no idea where they had gone.","After all, they were idiots. Wasn’t it perfectly normal for an idiot to get lost?","Who would risk crossing Jia the Big Thug over someone like that?","He had done this more than once.","He also knew that for crimes like these alone, ten lives wouldn’t be enough to save him from execution.","That was why he had still refused to speak when Wumao brought it up. Saying it aloud would very likely get him killed.","Otherwise, given what a coward he was, he would have confessed everything long ago.","“I... If I tell you, can you really keep me safe?”","Wumao turned to Zhao Tianyi.","Zhao Tianyi nodded. “I keep my word. As long as you confess everything you know and cooperate with us in gathering evidence, we won’t touch you. We’ll even send you somewhere completely safe. The Wanlong Society has been around for a long time, and we’ve never broken our word over something like this.”","Wumao said, “I can vouch for that. Brother Jia, we’ve known each other for so long. You know what I’ve done, yet I’m still alive and well, aren’t I? The boss of the Wanlong Society made me the same promise. What are you still hesitating over?”","Jia Dan gritted his teeth, seemingly engaged in one last internal struggle.","But when he saw Zhao Tianyi’s eyes, which seemed capable of seeing straight through him, and the men in black surrounding him—men even more intimidating than ordinary gangsters—his final psychological defenses collapsed completely.","“I’ll talk! I’ll tell you everything!”","“Most of those idiots are actually in the coal mines around Qingyan Mountain.”","“The Qi family owns several coal mines in the Jinchuan area. Besides the few that operate legally on the surface, they also have several illegal mines. Those mines have no permits and no safety inspections. They rely entirely on slave labor to keep them running.”","“Intellectually disabled young people are perfect for the job. They don’t know how to file complaints, they don’t run away, and they’ll work as long as you give them a little food. If they can’t keep working, or if they fall ill and can’t be cured, they’re thrown into abandoned mine shafts in the rear mountains and left to die...”","As Jia Dan finished confessing everything, even the usually gentle smile on Zhao Tianyi’s face vanished, replaced by a chilling gloom. He had already guessed some of it, but hearing Jia Dan say it aloud still sent a cold shiver down his spine.","“Give me the exact location.”","“Northwest of Qingyan Mountain is a place called Eagle’s Beak. There’s an abandoned mine there. From the outside, it looks like nothing more than a patch of wasteland, and the entrance is covered with branches and rocks. Most people would never notice it.”","After saying this last sentence, Jia Dan completely lost all strength and slumped to the ground.","Zhao Tianyi asked another question. “Let me ask you this, then. Have you ever seen a man named Wang Dashu? He’s in his twenties, mentally disabled, short, and very dark-skinned.”","Jia Dan thought for a moment, then shook his head. “I don’t remember. I’ve handled too many idiots. How could I remember every one of their names?”","“Um... You said earlier that you’d guarantee my safety and send me somewhere safe. Does that... still count?”","Wumao also looked at Zhao Tianyi. “Lawyer Zhao, Brother Jia has probably told you everything he knows. What do you think...?”","Zhao Tianyi stubbed out his cigarette and nodded. “Fine. I keep my word.”","He waved his hand, and two men in black immediately stepped forward.","“Take him somewhere safe.”","The two men answered in unison, “Yes!”","But there was now a chilling, meaningful look on their faces, as though they were looking at a dead man.","Wumao noticed their expressions too, and his heart gave a jolt. A vague sense of unease crept over him.","“Um... May I ask whether Jia Dan is really going to be safe? I mean, will he still be able to live a normal life from now on?”","He was actually asking on his own behalf as well. After all, they had promised to send him somewhere safe too.","Zhao Tianyi glanced at him, then suddenly broke into laughter.","“If he’s lucky, he’ll have a chance to start over.”","Wumao had just begun to relax when Zhao Tianyi added:","“Just in his next life.”","Wumao was struck as if by lightning, every hair on his body standing on end.","The Wanlong Society really was a criminal organization!","Oh no!"]},{"number":854,"title":"Chapter 854: 855, Suicide Note.","paragraphs":["In a sparsely populated street somewhere in the new district of Jinchuan City.","Qi Licheng pulled his car over in an inconspicuous spot by the roadside. The designer shirt he was wearing had been ripped, and there was a cut on his neck from a tree branch, burning with pain.","“Damn it! Damn it!”","Qi Licheng slammed his fists against the steering wheel again and again, venting his rage.","It had been two hours since he had fled the warehouse in a panic.","For those two hours, he had been hiding and dodging pursuit, driving all the way to this remote street. Only after making sure no one was following him had he dared to stop and catch his breath.","A Jiu had been captured, and the dozens of men he had taken to the warehouse had all been wiped out.","At that moment, he was no different from a stray dog driven from its home.","“Dragon Alliance! Dragon Alliance! I’ll kill every last one of you!”","Qi Licheng roared through clenched teeth, punching the steering wheel once again.","He had never suffered such humiliation in his entire life.","In Jinchuan, he had always been the one bringing people to surround and beat others. When had anyone ever dared to turn the tables on him?","If he hadn’t reacted quickly and slipped away amid the chaos when both sides began fighting, he would probably have been captured by the Dragon Alliance along with that useless bunch led by A Jiu.","Yet whenever he thought of Zhao Tianyi’s smiling, treacherous face behind those gold-rimmed glasses, and the group of Dragon Alliance enforcers dressed in black standing behind him, Qi Licheng felt a chill spread through his heart.","He had always thought the Dragon Alliance was merely an outsider trying to muscle in. No matter how much money or manpower they had, they shouldn’t have been able to make waves on his territory in Jinchuan.","Only now did he realize that they weren’t some outsider trying to cross the river into his territory. They were a pack of despicable schemers!","“No. I can’t let this go!”","Gnashing his teeth, Qi Licheng pulled out his phone and dialed another number.","At that moment, there was only one thought in his mind:","Revenge! Revenge! And more revenge!","He would make the Dragon Alliance pay!","Yang Xin, Xu Shishi, and the lawyer surnamed Zhao would all pay as well!","Qi Licheng called Akun, a minor boss at one of his establishments.","The moment the call connected, he began screaming into the phone like a madman.","“Akun! Get everyone together immediately. Bring weapons and go to the Dragon Plaza construction site. Smash the place up! Break the workers’ legs! I’ll take responsibility for whatever happens!”","To his surprise, Akun began crying on the other end of the line.","“Young Master Cheng, we can’t! We can’t get out at all. There are police everywhere, checkpoints all over the roads, and they’re searching for you one by one.”","“What did you say?!”","“The police are looking for me? Why the hell are they looking for me?”","“Young Master Cheng, you’ve been put on the wanted list.”","“The police just issued a notice asking for assistance in your capture. They say you’re suspected of unlawful imprisonment, intentional assault, provoking trouble, and... and drug trafficking. The entire city is searching for you. The train station, bus station, and highway entrances have all been sealed off. The brothers are hiding in the wooden cabins at the mine and don’t dare go outside!”","Buzz!","Qi Licheng’s mind instantly went blank.","A wanted notice?","He was wanted?","Clatter!","The phone slipped from his hand and fell beneath the car seat.","How could this be?","How had it happened so quickly?","He had escaped the warehouse less than two hours ago. How had the police already issued a wanted notice? And how had they even uncovered the drug charges?","It had to be the Dragon Alliance!","It had to be that damn lawyer, Zhao Tianyi!","So the evidence he had claimed to possess was all real.","Qi Licheng’s teeth ground together with a harsh clicking sound. Even now, he still couldn’t figure out where things had gone wrong or how he had ended up being wanted by the police.","“No. I have to call my father. My father can definitely handle this. He practically rules Jinchuan. He can make this go away!”","“That’s right, that’s right! I have to call him! He’s the only one who can save me!”","Qi Licheng hurriedly bent down and groped beneath the seat for his phone. It took him quite a while to retrieve it.","He opened his contacts and found his father Qi Tianhu’s number. His finger hovered over the call button, but he hesitated and couldn’t bring himself to press it.","His father had warned him long ago that he absolutely must not touch that powder. Once he did, it would be a dead end. He had also warned him to wait until they had secured the lithium mine before dealing with those insignificant nobodies, and not to create unnecessary complications for now.","But Qi Licheng hadn’t listened to a word.","He had treated all those warnings as if they were nothing. He had touched everything he shouldn’t have touched, and provoked everyone he shouldn’t have provoked.","Now he had backed himself into a corner and even ended up on the police’s wanted list.","He didn’t dare imagine what his father would do once he found out.","In the end, Qi Licheng still didn’t make the call. Instead, he hugged his legs and curled up in the driver’s seat, trembling all over. He looked like a little dog that had lost its fangs and been left with nothing but fear.","He was surrounded on all sides, and he couldn’t even run.","Just as Qi Licheng sank into despair, his phone suddenly rang. His entire body jolted, and he thought the police were calling.","But when he looked closely, he saw that it was the person in charge at the mine.","He let out a sigh of relief.","“Hello? What is it?”","“Young Master Cheng, something’s happened! Something huge has happened! There’s been an incident at the mine!”","Qi Licheng’s heart sank again, and the ominous feeling in his chest grew stronger.","“Why are you panicking? Take it slow. What exactly happened?”","“It’s that idiot. It’s... it’s about that idiot! The new idiot at our mine—he was pretending! He’s a journalist! An undercover reporter!”","“That guy spent more than three months undercover at the mine and filmed everything that was happening there. We only discovered him this morning.”","Boom!","Qi Licheng’s vision darkened. It felt as though a massive hammer had slammed into his chest, leaving him gasping for breath.","One disaster after another! Disaster after disaster!","He was already in trouble himself, and now something had gone wrong at the mine as well.","Apart from several legitimate mines operated openly by the Qi family, they also had several illegal coal mines.","Those illegal mines had no extraction permits, no safety certifications, and no protective measures of any kind. They relied on intellectually disabled young men and vagrants as illegal laborers, exploiting them ruthlessly.","Over the years, at least eight or ten people had died in those mines. Every one of them had been quietly disposed of.","If this came to light, not only would Qi Licheng be sentenced to death, but his father, Qi Tianhu, would be in serious trouble as well.","The entire Qi family might even be destroyed.","“Did... did you catch him?” Qi Licheng asked in a trembling voice.","“We caught him, but we searched him from head to toe and found nothing. He didn’t have anything on him. He must have already sent the evidence out. And he’s incredibly tight-lipped. Even after we used force, he still refuses to tell us where the evidence is.”","“You useless bunch! You’re all completely useless!”","Qi Licheng finally broke down.","“What the hell am I paying you for? You actually let a journalist infiltrate the mine!”","“Young Master Cheng, we never expected it. He played an idiot too convincingly.”","“I don’t care what method you use. Force the truth out of him. You absolutely cannot let him reveal where the evidence is. Do you hear me?!”","“Yes, yes, we understand!”","“...”","Qi Licheng viciously ended the call, then began pounding the steering wheel like a madman once more.","“Ahhh!”","He threw back his head and let out a hysterical roar.","Half an hour later.","Qi Licheng finally stopped, resting his forehead against the steering wheel as he forced himself to calm down and think of a way out.","Yet the more he thought about it, the more desperate he became.","The wanted notice, the drug allegations, the illegal mines, the undercover reporter... Any one of these would have been enough to ruin him. Now, they had all exploded at once.","It was a completely hopeless situation—a certain death sentence with no way out.","At that moment, he finally saw the truth clearly. From the very beginning, he had fallen into the trap laid by the Wanlong Society.","Wumao was a mole, Jia Dan was a pawn, and even he himself was nothing more than a piece on the other side’s chessboard, used to bring down the entire Qi family.","He had thought he was the hunter, only to discover that he was merely the prey—a useless fool!","He remained silent for a very long time, so long that darkness had fallen outside the car window.","At last, Qi Licheng made a decision.","He started the car and drove to a small supermarket at the end of the street. Lowering his head, he went inside and bought some paper and a pen.","When he returned to the car and locked the doors, he spread the sheet of paper across the steering wheel. Then he picked up the pen and, with trembling hands, wrote two words at the very top of the blank page.","—Suicide Note!"]},{"number":855,"title":"Chapter 855: 856, Mineral Auction.","paragraphs":["Nine o’clock the next morning, at the Jinchuan Auction Hall.","Today was the public auction for the exploration and mining rights to the Qingyan Mountain lithium deposit.","The Qingyan Mountain lithium deposit had an initially verified lithium oxide resource volume of more than one million tons, making it a super-large deposit that ranked among the most significant in the entire East Continent.","Even in 2009, when smartphones had yet to become widespread and electric vehicles had not yet taken off, anyone with a bit of strategic vision could see that the mine was immensely valuable.","Whoever secured it would gain the upper hand in the new-energy sector of the future.","The auction hall was packed.","The VIP seats in the front row were occupied by all the heavyweights of the domestic mining industry.","XN Mining and Chengyu Group, both long-established and powerful companies in the southwest, sat on the local side. They had operated in the region for many years.","Beside them sat representatives from three major mining companies from other provinces. All were well-known enterprises in China’s lithium-mining industry and had come to Jinchuan specifically to compete for the super-large deposit.","At the very center of the front row sat Qi Tianhu, chairman of Tiger Might Group.","Jinchuan was his territory, and Qingyan Mountain was practically right under his nose. Naturally, he was determined to win the mine.","A few seats to his left sat Yang Xin and Xu Shishi of the Wanlong Association Group.","Once everyone had taken their seats, many of the company representatives and media reporters present kept glancing in their direction, either openly or discreetly.","“Those are the people from Wanlong Association Group? They have such an imposing presence.”","“Exactly. I heard the company came from Pearl City and that its strength is unfathomable. After last year’s earthquake, they donated more than two billion yuan in one go. They’re incredibly powerful.”","“But I heard the company isn’t exactly clean. There are rumors that they’re involved in some shady business.”","“It should be fake news. Their company name is certainly easy to misinterpret, but I think those are just baseless rumors. They can’t be true.”","“Still, I heard Wanlong Association Group has some bad blood with Lord Tiger. Apparently, Lord Tiger suffered a loss at their hands.”","“Seriously? Is that true? Looks like today’s auction is going to be quite a show.”","“...”","Yang Xin and Xu Shishi could vaguely hear people discussing Wanlong Association Group, but neither of them paid it any mind.","“President Xu, do you think Qi Tianhu will make a move?” Yang Xin asked.","“He probably will.”","“Didn’t you hear? People have already started saying that Wanlong Association Group is involved in criminal business. That kind of rumor doesn’t appear out of nowhere. It means someone has been building momentum behind the scenes.”","“Otherwise, how would everyone here have heard about it?”","Yang Xin nodded thoughtfully.","That made sense.","Someone had suddenly begun spreading those rumors, which meant there had to be someone behind the scenes fanning the flames. As for who was pulling the strings, even a fool could figure it out.","But they weren’t afraid. They had prepared a contingency plan long ago.","Just as they changed the subject and began discussing their bidding strategy, two middle-aged men in sharply tailored suits entered through the auction hall doors.","Judging by their attire and their distinctly Cantonese-accented speech, they appeared to be from Hong Kong.","“They’re Mr. Zhang and Mr. Xie from Hong Kong!”","“Zhang Ting of Zhang Mining and Xie Jichuan of the Xie Group? What are they doing here?”","“My god, these two are major figures! The Zhang family has mines across the East Continent and Africa, while the Xie family is a venerable Hong Kong clan with an incredibly deep foundation. Have they set their sights on this mine too?”","“This is getting exciting! The competition was already fierce, and now two more tycoons have arrived. The price is going to skyrocket!”","“...”","Under the astonished gazes of the crowd, Zhang Ting and Xie Jichuan followed the staff’s guidance, smiling as they walked straight through the crowd and took their seats in the empty places at the front.","Xu Shishi and Yang Xin looked at them simultaneously.","Qi Tianhu also stopped rolling the walnuts in his hand and frowned.","None of them had expected anyone from Hong Kong to show up.","This was going to be difficult.","In those days, Hong Kong businessmen were practically synonymous with deep pockets on the mainland.","It seemed they would have to reconsider their budget for today.","At half past nine in the morning, the auction officially began.","The auctioneer, dressed in a crisp formal suit, strode onto the stage. He first read out the auction rules and the basic information about the Qingyan Mountain lithium deposit, then picked up the gavel and brought it down hard.","“Exploration and mining rights to the Qingyan Mountain lithium deposit. Opening bid: 800 million yuan. Each bid must be at least 5 million yuan higher than the previous one!”","“Let the bidding begin!”","The moment the auctioneer finished speaking, someone in the hall raised a bidding paddle.","“805 million!”","“810 million!”","“850 million!”","“...”","The price shot upward without pause.","Within just a few minutes, it had broken through the one-billion-yuan mark.","The atmosphere in the hall instantly caught fire.","Before long, however, the representatives of the smaller companies wisely fell silent and stopped raising their paddles.","The price had already exceeded what they could afford.","By the time it reached 1.2 billion yuan, only four parties were still bidding: XN Mining, Chengyu Group, Wanlong Association Group, and Qi Tianhu’s Tiger Might Group.","The two men from Hong Kong had yet to place a single bid. They simply sat there with cups of coffee in hand, watching the spectacle like outsiders.","“1.3 billion!”","The representative from XN Mining raised his paddle again, though his expression had already grown tense.","The price was now very close to the upper limit of what his company had expected to pay.","After he called out 1.3 billion, no one else bid for more than ten seconds.","Just as the representative of XN Mining began to think the mine was his, Qi Tianhu finally made his move.","“1.4 billion!”","The entire hall erupted.","He had raised the price by a full 100 million yuan in one go!","Tiger Qi was making it crystal clear to everyone present: I am determined to win this mine. No one is taking it from me.","The representatives from XN Mining and Chengyu Group looked utterly defeated and ultimately chose to withdraw.","At that moment, Xu Shishi finally entered the bidding as well. Without the slightest hint of panic, she raised her paddle and called out, “1.5 billion!”","Whoosh!","The eyes of the entire hall instantly focused on her.","Qi Tianhu finally turned his head and looked directly at Xu Shishi for the first time, his expression filled with meaning.","Wanlong Association Group actually dared to challenge him head-on.","“1.6 billion!” Qi Tianhu raised his paddle again, still completely unfazed as he increased the bid by another 100 million yuan.","The crowd collectively drew a sharp breath.","They were insane!","Every last one of them!","The auction had been underway for less than ten minutes, yet the price had already climbed from 800 million to 1.6 billion yuan—doubling outright.","Just as everyone assumed Xu Shishi would continue bidding, she lowered her paddle and stopped.","Yang Xin grew anxious and said in a low voice, “President Xu, why aren’t we bidding anymore? The young lady specifically said we had to secure it.”","Xu Shishi shook her head slightly, then glanced toward the two men from Hong Kong.","“Don’t rush. Those two old foxes from Hong Kong haven’t made a move yet. Let’s make them show their hand first.”","Sure enough, the moment she finished speaking—","The Hong Kong businessman, Zhang Ting, who had remained silent all this time finally lowered his coffee cup after seeing that no one else was bidding. Without the slightest rush, he raised his bidding paddle.","“Two billion!”","Boom!","The entire auction hall erupted.","He had just raised the bid by four hundred million in one go!","He was insane—completely insane!","Even the auctioneer froze for a moment before coming to his senses and hurriedly shouting, “Two billion! Mr. Zhang has bid two billion! Is there anyone willing to go higher?”","Qi Tianhu’s expression darkened.","Damn it, so what if he was from Hong Kong?","What a show-off!","He opens his mouth and adds four hundred million at once—who is he trying to scare?","He was determined to win this mine today!","Since these Hong Kong businessmen wanted to put on a show, he would start by striking down this dragon to intimidate the monkeys!","Weren’t Hong Kong businessmen supposed to be loaded?","He wanted to see whether their nerve was as big as their wallets."]},{"number":856,"title":"Chapter 856: 857, Fierce Bidding, Report","paragraphs":["“Two billion!”","The moment that number was called out, the auction hall fell silent.","Zhang Ting turned to Xie Jichuan and said something in a low voice in Cantonese, smiling. Huo Zhenting also replied with a smile. Both of them looked completely relaxed.","Judging by their demeanor, the two sides had probably reached some kind of agreement.","The representatives of Chengyu Group and XN Mining finally lowered their bidding paddles and shook their heads with bitter smiles.","The price had already far exceeded the maximum budget they had set before coming. They were prepared to give up.","“Two billion and fifty million!” Qi Tianhu raised his paddle again.","This figure was already close to the limit of the cash flow Tiger Might Group could mobilize.","If he still couldn’t win the mine, he would have to resort to some measures outside the auction.","Make an example of someone!","Qi Tianhu hadn’t even fully lowered his hand when Zhang Ting raised his paddle again.","“Two billion two hundred million!”","2.2 billion!","That was nearly three times the starting price.","Yang Xin’s expression also grew serious. He turned slightly and said in a low voice to Xu Shishi, “President Xu, it’s 2.2 billion now. That’s already beyond our original expectations.”","When they had initially appraised the lithium mine, they had set the upper limit at 1.8 billion. Now that the price had been pushed directly to 2.2 billion, it had indeed exceeded their expectations.","Xu Shishi’s brows drew together slightly.","Although they both knew that Liu Yutong’s side must have made preparations in advance, the price had reached this point, so it was still best to ask for instructions.","Yang Xin took out his phone and sent Liu Yutong a text message, briefly reporting the situation at the auction.","Less than ten seconds later, Liu Yutong replied.","There were only four words on the screen:","[Bid with confidence.]","After reading the message, Yang Xin and Xu Shishi felt the tight string in their hearts instantly relax.","Then, without the slightest hesitation, Xu Shishi raised her bidding paddle again.","“2.3 billion!”","The entire hall erupted once more.","The Wanlong Association had joined in! Faced with the aggressive Hong Kong capital, they had actually chosen to keep bidding!","2.3 billion!","No wonder they were a major company that had donated two billion in a single stroke the previous year. They certainly had deep pockets.","Surprise flashed through Zhang Ting and Xie Jichuan’s eyes.","They had originally thought that their earlier psychological tactics would suppress these mainland companies. They had even believed victory was within reach. They hadn’t expected this previously unknown Wanlong Association to follow their bid.","Zhang Ting didn’t think much of it and raised his paddle again.","“2.4 billion!”","“2.5 billion!” Xu Shishi followed almost without hesitation.","Everyone in the auction hall felt their heartbeats quicken at the sight.","This was a spectacle!","Mainland capital was going head-to-head with Hong Kong capital.","“2.6 billion!”","“2.7 billion!”","“2.8 billion!”","“......”","The two sides went back and forth, raising the price by one hundred million each time without any sign of stopping. The people present cried out in astonishment one after another.","Just as the price reached 2.8 billion, Zhang Ting suddenly turned around and looked toward Xu Shishi and Yang Xin with a genial smile.","“Your mainland economy has certainly developed rapidly. However, I’ve heard that most of it revolves around real estate. I imagine the Wanlong Association got its start in that line of business too, didn’t it?”","“But I have to remind you that mining is completely different from real estate. It isn’t something you can manage simply by throwing money at it.”","Xie Jichuan smiled as well. “That’s right. Between our two companies, we have numerous mines around the world. We’ve invested more than five billion just in exploration equipment. Young people, don’t act on impulse. 2.8 billion is already a lot. If you keep raising the price, I’m afraid you’ll have a hard time explaining it to your boss when you go back.”","His words sounded polite, but everyone could hear the underlying message:","You don’t understand this industry. Don’t force yourselves. You might not be able to clean up the mess afterward.","Xu Shishi naturally understood that the two men were deliberately trying to pressure them into backing down, but she wasn’t intimidated in the slightest.","“Thank you both for your concern. You’re right. The Wanlong Association really doesn’t have much equipment or any experience in mining.”","She raised her bidding paddle once again.","“But we do have plenty of money!”","“Three billion!”","The smiles vanished from Zhang Ting and Xie Jichuan’s faces.","These mainlanders were unbelievably arrogant!","But just as they were considering whether to continue raising the bid, something unexpected happened.","Suddenly, a middle-aged man sitting in the back row stood up.","He was Wang Fei, the owner of a local entertainment venue in Jinchuan. He was also a pawn Qi Tianhu had arranged in advance.","The moment Wang Fei stood up, he pointed at Yang Xin and Xu Shishi.","“I want to report them! The Wanlong Association isn’t a legitimate company at all. They’re gangsters! They’re a criminal organization!”","“They have no right to participate in this auction!”","The hall erupted.","Everyone’s eyes immediately turned toward Xu Shishi and Yang Xin.","Sitting in his chair, Qi Tianhu smiled.","Here it comes.","The time to make an example of someone had arrived!","Wang Fei immediately raised the USB drive in his hand and shouted, “Everyone, take a look. This contains evidence. It clearly records all the things the Wanlong Association has done! Just the day before yesterday, they brought more than a hundred gang members into Jinchuan City, armed with weapons. They smashed, looted, and set things on fire, assaulting people with violence. They even wrecked and robbed my KTV!”","“They may look like a legitimate company on the surface, but in reality, they throw their weight around and stop at nothing! What right does a company with criminal connections like this have to participate in an auction?!”","The entire hall erupted into an uproar.","Those who had already heard vague rumors that the Wanlong Association had ties to criminal forces now believed them without a doubt.","“Damn, the Wanlong Association really is a criminal organization?”","“No wonder they dared to go head-to-head with Tiger Qi. So this is what they do behind the scenes.”","“A company like that should have its bidding qualifications revoked immediately. How can we let a criminal enterprise mine the country’s resources?”","“That’s terrifying. I thought they seemed pretty legitimate just now. Who would’ve guessed they were so ruthless behind closed doors?”","“......”","Even the two Hong Kong businessmen’s expressions changed. Their faces became uncertain.","As Hong Kongers, they were no strangers to criminal gangs.","Many years ago, there had even been a kidnapping case that shocked the entire world.","Precisely because they knew how dark and ruthless those organizations could be, they were wary of them.","They hadn’t expected such groups to exist on the mainland as well.","Wasn’t the mainland known for cracking down extremely hard on organized crime and maintaining a very safe environment?","Then what was going on here?","Qi Tianhu watched the crowd’s reaction, and the smile on his face deepened.","This was exactly the effect he wanted.","Even if this tactic couldn’t directly drive the Wanlong Association out of the auction, it would make everyone present wary of them. They would be afraid to continue bidding, and perhaps even afraid to have anything to do with them.","In the end, the mine would still belong to Qi Tianhu.","Wang Fei continued fanning the flames from the floor, portraying the Wanlong Association as a ruthless criminal organization that could kill without blinking and stop at nothing. His words sent shivers through the people below.","Yang Xin and Xu Shishi had been prepared for this, but they were still furious.","Who were they insulting?!","Who were they insulting?!","The Wanlong Association either didn’t make a move at all, or, once they did, they wiped out the opposition completely. If that were really what they had done, how could Wang Fei still be standing there in one piece?","He would have been taken care of long ago.","Because the incident had happened so suddenly, the auction, which had been proceeding normally, was forced to come to an abrupt end.","Just then, Qi Tianhu stood up and put on a righteous, indignant expression. He pressed down on the air with one hand and said, “Everyone! Everyone, please be quiet! Listen to me!”","Everyone present turned to look at him.","In fact, some of them had already guessed what was going on. This was probably Tiger Qi’s doing. That man was no cleaner than the Wanlong Association.","But no one dared say it aloud. After all, this was Jinchuan.","Qi Tianhu raised his hand and pointed at Yang Xin and Xu Shishi, declaring sternly, “In light of the Wanlong Association Group’s involvement in organized crime, I have already notified the police. They will be here shortly and will bring all relevant parties to justice!”","The room erupted.","Several local small-business owners seated in the back immediately began whispering among themselves, their expressions growing more animated by the second.","“Here we go. Tiger Qi is making his move.”","“I knew it. How could Qi Tianhu possibly let an out-of-town company lord it over him on his own turf? There it is—the killing blow.”","“I know this Wang Fei fellow. He’s one of Tiger Qi’s lackeys. He was ordered to make the attack.”","“Whether he’s attacking them or not is beside the point. The real issue is that he stripped the Wanlong Association bare in front of everyone. That’s like putting them over a fire to roast. What a ruthless move. If you ask me, the Wanlong Association is in for a world of trouble today.”","“I heard Tiger Qi has been established in the Jinchuan area for many years and has connections with people higher up.”","“Keep your voice down. Just know what’s going on.”","“This is a clash between immortals. We small fry should just watch the show and make sure we don’t get involved.”","“But look at those two from the Wanlong Association. They seem pretty calm. Could they have another card up their sleeves?”","“Calm my ass. They’re just pretending to keep their composure. Going up against Tiger Qi in Jinchuan—isn’t that just asking to die?”","“Exactly. They’re outsiders. How could they possibly match the Qi family’s foundation?”","“...”"]},{"number":857,"title":"Chapter 857: 858, These Are Solid Now.","paragraphs":["In the VIP seats at the front.","Zhang Ting and Xie Jichuan exchanged a glance, both seeing the schadenfreude in the other’s eyes.","That woman surnamed Xu from the Wanlong Society had opened with, “Our Wanlong Society may have nothing else, but we have plenty of money.” Her arrogance had nearly put the two of them in an impossible position.","But now things had taken an interesting turn. The mantis stalked the cicada, unaware of the oriole behind it.","A man named Wang Fei had suddenly appeared at the auction and, in front of everyone present, completely exposed the Wanlong Society.","“Mr. Zhang, did you hear that? They’re gangsters,” Xie Jichuan said, deliberately teasing him in Cantonese.","Zhang Ting laughed as well. “I heard. Robbery, looting, arson—the whole package. How impressive. But Old Xie, don’t you think there’s something strange about this?”","“What’s strange?” Xie Jichuan asked.","“Think about it. If the Wanlong Society really is a criminal organization, as he claims, what gives this Wang Fei the nerve to expose them in public?”","“In Harbor City, would you dare point at the head of Hing Kee in front of several hundred people and accuse him of being a gangster? You wouldn’t, would you? I’m afraid you wouldn’t even finish speaking today before ending up at the bottom of the sea tomorrow.”","After hearing this, Xie Jichuan nodded thoughtfully. “You mean someone is directing Wang Fei from behind the scenes?”","Zhang Ting jerked his chin toward Qi Tianhu’s direction. “Isn’t it obvious?”","“Chairman of Tiger Might Group, the local kingpin of Jinchuan—anyone with eyes can see that he has a grudge against the Wanlong Society. The whole ‘criminal organization’ accusation is probably just an attempt to smear his opponent.”","Xie Jichuan followed his gaze and happened to see Qi Tianhu rising to his feet, declaring with righteous indignation that he had already called the police.","“Good point.”","“But this is good news for us.”","“Of course it is.”","The two of them had flown all the way from Harbor City to Jinchuan specifically for the massive lithium deposit at Qingyan Mountain.","Originally, they had not taken the mainland companies seriously at all. But they had never expected the Wanlong Society to appear out of nowhere, seemingly loaded with money, raising the bid by hundreds of millions at a time until it reached three billion yuan.","Now Qi Tianhu and the Wanlong Society were fighting each other. That was unquestionably beneficial to them.","“That woman surnamed Xu was acting so arrogantly earlier, bragging that the Wanlong Society had plenty of money. She must be dumbfounded now, huh? No matter how much money they have, it’s useless now,” Xie Jichuan said gleefully.","But the smile on Zhang Ting’s face gradually faded.","He stared at Xu Shishi and Yang Xin, his brows drawing together slightly. Something about the situation felt wrong.","The two of them were far too calm.","This was not how normal people would react.","If ordinary people were publicly branded as gangsters in a setting like this—especially with several officials present—their first response would surely be to stand up and defend themselves, clarifying that they were innocent.","Yet from the moment Wang Fei had appeared until now, the two had remained quietly seated, acting as though it had nothing to do with them.","That reaction meant either they were completely prepared, or they simply did not care.","Or perhaps the informant was telling the truth—the Wanlong Society really was a criminal organization.","That would make things troublesome.","They were not afraid of competing with others financially, but they were genuinely wary of people from the underworld.","“Old Xie, how much do you know about the Wanlong Society?” Zhang Ting suddenly asked.","Xie Jichuan thought for a moment. “If you’re asking whether I know anything, I do have some information. Mr. Zhang, do you remember what happened to the Jiang family?”","“You mean Jiang Yuan?” Zhang Ting asked.","Xie Jichuan nodded. “Yes.”","“Jiang Yuan was arrested in the capital, and the Jiang family was practically uprooted overnight. I heard some rumors in Harbor City that the mainland’s Wanlong Society was involved.”","Zhang Ting’s expression changed slightly. “Why didn’t you tell me that earlier?”","“I didn’t think much of it at first.”","Xie Jichuan spread his hands. “Jiang Yuan had plenty of dirt on him. Smuggling, hiring hitmen—he was involved in every kind of shady business. It was only a matter of time before someone found the evidence. Still, that kid Jiang Ximing was quick. He got out of the country in advance, and nobody knows where he’s hiding now.”","“But with his vengeful personality, I doubt he’ll let this go.”","“So what if he doesn’t? Does he dare come back to the country?”","“True.”","Zhang Ting suddenly remembered something else. “Old Xie, you held quite a few shares in those publicly listed companies under Jiang Yuan’s name, didn’t you?”","The smile on Xie Jichuan’s face instantly froze.","Of all things, why bring that up?","After Jiang Yuan’s case came to light, the police in Harbor City, together with the mainland authorities, had comprehensively frozen all the assets under Jiang Yuan’s name.","Several listed companies under the Jiang Group had plummeted overnight. He and Zhang Ting both held substantial amounts of stock, which had been rotting in their accounts ever since. Even if they were willing to cut their losses, they could not find anyone to take them off their hands. Their losses amounted to at least double-digit billions.","And those “double digits” were measured in hundreds of millions of yuan.","At the time, they had simply assumed that Jiang Yuan’s own recklessness had dragged down everyone who had done business with him.","But now, if the Wanlong Society really had been behind Jiang Yuan’s downfall, should the money they had lost also be charged to the Wanlong Society?","“If that’s really the case, then the Wanlong Society is no pushover.”","“What are you afraid of?”","“Someone else is sticking their neck out for us now. Let Qi Tianhu deal with the Wanlong Society. If he succeeds, we lose one competitor. If he fails, the Wanlong Society will still take a beating. Either way, we don’t lose anything. We can just sit back and watch the show.”","Zhang Ting considered this. His expression gradually eased, and he nodded. “That’s true.”","As the two spoke in low voices, a burst of hurried footsteps suddenly came from the entrance to the auction hall.","Everyone turned their heads in unison, all eyes fixed on the doorway.","A moment later, a middle-aged police officer walked in at the head of the group. More than twenty uniformed officers followed behind him.","“Is that Chief Wu from headquarters?” someone whispered in surprise.","When Qi Tianhu saw who had arrived, the smile on his face grew even wider.","Chief Wu had actually come in person.","It seemed the connections he had called upon had arranged everything perfectly. With such a large show of force, victory was practically guaranteed!"]},{"number":858,"title":"Chapter 858: 859, Two-Level Reversal","paragraphs":["“Chief Wu, you’re here.”","Qi Tianhu hurried over and extended a hand to shake his.","Chief Wu merely glanced at him and gave a slight nod. He didn’t reach out.","Qi Tianhu awkwardly withdrew his hand, and a faint sense of unease immediately rose in his heart.","What was going on?","It wasn’t as though he had never dealt with Chief Wu before. Their relationship was not particularly close, but whenever they met, they had always been polite to each other and exchanged the usual pleasantries.","Yet today, in front of so many prominent figures from Jinchuan, Chief Wu wasn’t even willing to give him that much face.","Qi Tianhu quickly came up with an explanation. Perhaps with so many people watching, Chief Wu simply couldn’t afford to appear too friendly.","After all, he was a police officer. In a public setting like this, he had to maintain an official, businesslike demeanor. That was understandable.","Seeing the police arrive, Wang Fei in the back became even more excited. He raised the USB drive in his hand and waved it toward them, shouting, “Officer! Officer! The evidence is here with me! The Wanlong Association is a criminal organization! I have video evidence of them smashing things, looting, and setting fires!”","As he shouted, he jogged toward the officers, afraid that no one would know he was the righteous man who had stood up to fight evil on behalf of the people.","When the others in the hall saw the police arrive, they began whispering among themselves.","“It’s over, it’s over. The Wanlong Association is really finished today. Chief Wu personally brought people here. With this kind of show of force, it’s obviously not a minor matter.”","“Look at the man surnamed Yang and the woman surnamed Xu. They’re still sitting there without moving. Do you think they’re scared senseless?”","“That would be normal. Who would’ve thought they’d be taken away by the police while attending an auction?”","“I told you. Outsiders can’t expect things to go smoothly here. Challenging Tiger Qi in Jinchuan is practically suicide.”","“That was a ruthless move by Tiger Qi—cutting off their support at the roots. Not only did he ruin their reputation, he’s even sending them to prison. Even if the Wanlong Association gets out of this in the end, today’s auction will have been a complete waste of time for them.”","“...”","Zhang Ting and Xie Jichuan had witnessed the scene as well. They exchanged a smile.","If the situation had been more appropriate, they would have poured themselves two glasses of champagne and raised a toast.","Once the Wanlong Association fell, their biggest competitor would be gone.","Judging purely by financial strength, no one else among the companies present should be able to compete with them. The mine would ultimately end up in their hands.","Chief Wu led his officers through the crowd and headed straight into the hall.","A smile returned to Qi Tianhu’s face as he looked toward Yang Xin and the others. He wanted to personally witness the grand spectacle of the police arresting them.","However, that smile vanished after only a few seconds.","When Chief Wu and his team passed in front of him, they didn’t even spare Yang Xin or Xu Shishi a glance.","They walked straight past them and stopped in front of Wang Fei.","“Take Wang Fei into custody!”","The order was crisp and decisive, utterly devoid of emotion.","Wang Fei: “???”","Before he could react, two officers immediately stepped forward, seized him by both arms, and restrained him.","Click!","A pair of silver handcuffs was locked tightly around Wang Fei’s wrists.","Wang Fei stood there in a daze, completely questioning reality.","Something was wrong! Something was very wrong!","Had they gotten the script mixed up? Had they arrested the wrong person?","“Wait, Officer! Have you made a mistake?”","“I’m the one who reported this! I’m the informant! The Wanlong Association is the criminal organization! They’re the ones you should be arresting!”","“It’s a misunderstanding! This is definitely a misunderstanding!”","Chief Wu had no interest in wasting words on him. He simply took out a document, unfolded it, and held it up in front of Wang Fei.","“Wang Fei, this is your arrest warrant. Take a good look.”","“Take him away!”","Without offering a single unnecessary explanation, the officers dragged the stunned Wang Fei out of the auction hall.","The people who had been whispering and enjoying the spectacle fell silent in an instant.","Within just a few seconds, their expressions changed from schadenfreude to shock, then from shock to confusion, and finally to a kind of indescribable terror.","Wasn’t the police here to arrest the Wanlong Association? Why had they taken the informant away instead?","What on earth was going on?","The smile on Qi Tianhu’s face disappeared the moment Chief Wu displayed the arrest warrant.","What was happening? What had gone wrong?","He had clearly made arrangements in advance.","Even if Chief Wu refused to do him a favor, he should at least have tried to smooth things over. There was no reason for him to turn around and arrest the man Qi Tianhu had planted there.","But Qi Tianhu had spent more than twenty years navigating the underworld. He quickly regained his composure, his face darkening as he demanded, “Chief Wu, what do you mean by this? Wang Fei is clearly the informant. Instead of arresting anyone from the Wanlong Association, you’ve arrested him. Don’t you think that’s a little hard to justify? Everyone here witnessed it—he came to report them.”","After he finished speaking, quite a few local businessmen in the back nodded instinctively.","That was true. Even if the report was false, the police shouldn’t have put him in handcuffs without asking a single question.","But in the next moment, Chief Wu turned his attention to Qi Tianhu.","“Qi Tianhu, please come with us as well. There’s a case at the station that requires your assistance with the investigation.”","As he spoke, he took out another document. This one was an official order requiring Qi Tianhu to cooperate with the investigation.","Boom!","The entire hall erupted.","Qi Tianhu was being taken away too?","What did that mean?","Tiger Qi had ruled Jinchuan unchecked for twenty years. How many officials had come and gone without being able to touch him? Yet today, not only had one of his lackeys been arrested, but Qi Tianhu himself was being taken in.","All because he had questioned the police.","This...","Zhang Ting and Xie Jichuan were both stunned.","What kind of background did the Wanlong Association have?","Only moments ago, they had been celebrating internally, convinced that the Wanlong Association was about to be finished—or, at the very least, would suffer a serious blow.","Yet in less than two minutes, the tide had completely turned.","The one who was finished wasn’t the Wanlong Association. It was Qi Tianhu.","Clearly, the Wanlong Association had an even more powerful backing.","Although Qi Tianhu himself hadn’t expected to be summoned as well, he remained relatively calm.","He quickly guessed the reason. It probably had something to do with his son, Qi Licheng, being wanted by the police.","He had received word the previous night that his son was wanted. Although he found the situation troublesome, he had spent twenty years building connections throughout Jinchuan. He believed that if he personally intervened, spent enough money, and called in enough favors, he could somehow suppress the matter.","Even in the worst-case scenario, he could first send his son away to lie low.","That was why he had attended the auction as usual today. His plan had been to secure the mine first, then devote all his attention to dealing with his son’s problems.","What he had never expected was that the other side seemed to have prepared in advance.","Or perhaps they had already captured his son.","If that was the case, then one wrong move could bring ruin not only upon him, but upon the entire Qi family.","Seeing that he still hadn’t moved, Chief Wu urged him again. “Qi Tianhu, please cooperate with the investigation.”","Two officers approached Qi Tianhu from either side, forming a pincer. If he dared make any sudden move, they would immediately restrain him.","Qi Tianhu remained silent for several seconds before slowly nodding.","“All right. I’ll go with you.”","For now, he could only hope that his son would keep his mouth shut and withstand the interrogation. Once he got out, he would find a way to clean up every loose end.","The police had not issued an arrest warrant directly. Instead, they were using an investigative warrant, which meant they still needed more evidence proving his connection to the case.","After he got out, he had to use this window of time to seal off every possible point of failure.","As long as he could make it through this crisis, he would find a way to save his son afterward.","Before leaving, Qi Tianhu turned to look at the two members of the Wanlong Society sitting in the front row. With a sinister look in his eyes, he mouthed a few words.","“You two just wait!”","Yang Xin refused to back down and mouthed three words in reply.","“Who’s afraid of you?”"]},{"number":859,"title":"Chapter 859: 860, Is the Sky Over Jinchuan Getting Darker","paragraphs":["The hall was so quiet you could hear a pin drop.","Everyone stared in shock and disbelief as Qi Tianhu, the local kingpin of Jinchuan, was led away by the police.","No one had expected the grand spectacle to end this way.","They had all seen that Tiger Qi was trying to set a trap for the Wanlong Association.","He had spread rumors, filed reports, called the police, and more...","In the end, the police really did show up—but the ones they arrested weren’t members of the Wanlong Association. They were Tiger Qi himself and his lackey, Wang Fei.","The reversal had come so quickly and violently that no one had been able to react.","“What exactly is the Wanlong Association’s background?”","“I have no idea, but it must be incredibly powerful. Otherwise, how could even Tiger Qi have ended up getting taken down?”","“My God, didn’t that Chief Wu just cuff him and take him away without even bothering to explain? He couldn’t even be bothered to come up with a reason.”","“Exactly! Shouldn’t the police normally tell people what crime they committed before arresting them?”","“Then I guess they didn’t have a reason...”","“Whew... When you put it that way, it’s kind of terrifying!”","“...”","Zhang Ting and Xie Jichuan began whispering among themselves as well. Neither of them had expected things to turn out this way.","“Mr. Xie, do you think we should keep competing with the Wanlong Association? This company may not be involved in organized crime, but its connections are truly extraordinary.”","“Why wouldn’t we keep competing?”","“If we give up, why did the two of us fly all the way from Hong Kong to Jinchuan? To watch them put on a show? The reserves of this Qingyan Mountain lithium mine rank among the top three in the country. You know how rapidly the smart-phone industry is developing overseas. Demand for lithium from batteries and other downstream industries will only continue to grow. I’m very optimistic about the future value of lithium mines. In fact, I would never simply hand it over just because the other side has powerful connections.”","He paused, then added, “Besides, how many projects have we invested in on the mainland? The officials we know are no fewer than theirs. If the Wanlong Association can make arrangements in advance, so can we. As long as everyone plays by the rules, it’s still anyone’s game.”","His words gradually restored Zhang Ting’s confidence.","Thinking it over carefully, he realized that Xie Jichuan was right.","The Wanlong Association had not used any illegal means from beginning to end. The police had arrested people in accordance with the law, which showed that the other side played by the rules.","And when people played by the rules, things were much easier to handle. In a business competition, the final contest was still one of strength.","What the two of them had feared most at the beginning was that the other side was involved in organized crime and that they would provoke a ruthless gang. For businessmen who valued their lives, that was the greatest risk of all.","But now, it seemed that the Wanlong Association was not in that line of business after all. The one who truly belonged to the underworld might have been Qi Tianhu.","If that was the case, then let them compete on the strength of their businesses!","“Fine. Let’s keep bidding!”","After the interruption had passed, the auctioneer onstage finally continued, “The Wanlong Association Group’s Ms. Xu has just bid three billion yuan. Three billion once...”","“Three point one billion!”","Xie Jichuan immediately raised his bidding paddle.","The entire hall erupted once again.","Those two men from Hong Kong actually dared to keep bidding?","Hadn’t they seen what happened to Tiger Qi? Their courage was unbelievable!","Xu Shishi turned and glanced at Xie Jichuan.","These two men from Hong Kong were far bolder than she had expected.","She had originally assumed that after such a dramatic reversal, none of the bidders present would dare compete with the Wanlong Association anymore. She hadn’t expected these two men from Hong Kong to be willing to give up just yet.","But the boss had already made it clear that they were determined to acquire the lithium mine, so she had no intention of showing them any mercy.","However, just as she was about to raise her paddle...","Something unexpected happened!","A heavy thud suddenly came from the street outside the auction hall, as if some massive object had fallen from a great height and slammed into the ground.","The next moment, a wave of screams rang out from outside.","“Someone jumped!”","“Oh my God! Someone just fell from the building!”","“A human flying through the air!”","“Someone’s dead! Someone’s dead!”","“...”","When the people in the auction hall heard the commotion, their hearts inexplicably tightened. One after another, they rose from their seats and rushed toward the entrance.","Across the street stood a commercial building more than twenty stories high. At its foot, a person lay motionless on the cold asphalt. A glaring pool of crimson was slowly spreading out from beneath him.","The police immediately moved in to secure the scene.","Qi Tianhu, who was just about to be put into a police car, heard the commotion and instinctively looked over. When he recognized the clothes of the person on the ground, it was as if he had been struck by lightning. He let out a heart-rending roar.","“Qi Licheng!!!”","Qi Tianhu struggled desperately, trying to break free from the officers beside him and rush over. But several officers held him back firmly, refusing to let him approach the scene.","All he could do was stare at the body, his eyes bulging with rage, and howl in anguish:","“Licheng! My son!!!”","“Ahhh!!!”","In that instant, the notorious Jinchuan kingpin seemed to age ten years. He could barely remain standing.","After spending his whole life hunting wild geese, he had finally been blinded by one himself.","For twenty years, he had ruled Jinchuan. No one in the city had dared provoke him. He had even come to believe that he was the emperor of this land, its absolute master.","Yet in the end, he had been left to suffer the tragedy of a white-haired parent mourning a dead child.","Qi Tianhu suddenly whipped around. His bloodshot eyes locked onto the entrance of the auction hall, and he roared in a voice filled with near-curse-like hatred:","“Wanlong Association!!!”","“I’m going to war with you bastards! It won’t end until one of us is dead!!!”","His agonized voice carried into the auction hall, making many people’s hearts jolt.","That man’s gaze was terrifying!","Then, almost in unison, they turned to look at the two Wanlong Association representatives standing at the entrance and watching the spectacle as well. Their eyes were filled with fear.","Damn it, this confirmed it, didn’t it? You really are criminals!","You actually forced the man’s only son to jump from a building right in front of the police!","When Yang Xin saw the looks on everyone’s faces, his first thought was:","We’re screwed! The company’s reputation has taken another hit!","Wait—why “another”?","Yang Xin and Xu Shishi truly hadn’t expected Qi Licheng to jump from the building in front of so many people.","They had originally thought that once they dealt with the nuisance known as Qi Tianhu, they could focus on bidding for the lithium mine in peace.","But in the blink of an eye, Qi Tianhu’s son, Qi Licheng, had put on a spectacular display of human flight for everyone.","What were the odds?","Regardless of what had actually happened, at least in the minds of everyone present, the Wanlong Association had now been branded as a criminal organization.","And it was the kind of label that could not be shaken off, no matter what they did!","The local businessmen, in particular, couldn’t help but arrive at the same thought.","“The sky over Jinchuan is even darker now.”"]},{"number":860,"title":"Chapter 860: 861, Hidden Currents Surging","paragraphs":["Zhang Ting had no idea when it started, but his legs suddenly felt as though they were no longer under his control. They kept trembling, no matter how hard he tried to stop them.","“Mr. Xie, do you think we’ve... offended someone we really shouldn’t have?”","The color had drained from Xie Jichuan’s face as well. His lips moved twice, but he didn’t know how to respond.","What they had just witnessed had shaken them to the core.","Qi Tianhu had been taken away by the police, and then, right in front of those same police officers, his son had leaped from the roof of a building more than twenty stories high, putting on an aerial performance.","Even in the familiar streets of Hong Kong, back in the days when criminal organizations ran rampant, few people would have dared to act so brazenly.","They truly should never have held on to any illusions!","They had actually thought about going head-to-head with the Wanlong Association in the bidding. Now, they regretted it more than anything.","They regretted it so much they could have slapped their thighs raw!","Inside the auction hall, the others were whispering among themselves as well.","“Are we still bidding?”","“What’s the point? Didn’t you see Tiger Qi’s son fly off the building?”","“Do you think Qi Licheng jumped of his own accord, or...”","“Shh! Do you have a death wish? How dare you say things like that?”","“Anyway, I’m not going to compete with the Wanlong Association. I wouldn’t fight them over any amount of money. I still want to make it home alive.”","“They’re untouchable, absolutely untouchable. This isn’t doing business—it’s risking your life!”","“Exactly. When the gods fight, ordinary people suffer. We really can’t afford to provoke them.”","“...”","The auctioneer stood alone on the stage, his expression impossible to describe.","Normally, after something this serious happened, the auction should have been suspended immediately, or even postponed altogether. But the higher-ups had yet to issue any instructions, and he didn’t dare make the decision on his own. All he could do was stand there and wait.","Just then, Zhang Ting and Xie Jichuan returned through the entrance.","Instead of going back to their seats, they walked straight over to Yang Xin and Xu Shishi, adopting an extremely deferential attitude.","“General Manager Yang, Ms. Xu, could we have a word in private?”","Yang Xin and Xu Shishi exchanged a glance, then nodded.","The four of them went to the lounge area in a corner of the hall.","Zhang Ting and Xie Jichuan didn’t waste any time with pleasantries. They got straight to the point.","“General Manager Yang, Ms. Xu, we’ve just discussed the matter carefully. Regarding the Qingyan Mountain lithium mine, why don’t we work together?”","“In what way?”","“Joint development.”","“Let’s be frank. We have the utmost respect for the Wanlong Association’s strength. We don’t want to compete for this lithium mine anymore, and we couldn’t win even if we did. But Zhang Mining is one of the top companies in Eastland when it comes to lithium mining and processing technology. We already have the equipment, technical teams, and downstream channels in place. If we cooperate, the Wanlong Association can provide the capital and resources, while we provide the technology and equipment. We’d complement each other’s strengths, making it a highly profitable arrangement for everyone.”","Xie Jichuan quickly nodded. “The Xie family also has a very deep presence in the new-energy sector. Our downstream customer base can be connected directly and seamlessly. Between our two families, we may not be number one in the world when it comes to technology and the market, but at least in Eastland, we have no rivals.”","Yang Xin remained expressionless, but he secretly approved of their proposal.","What they had said was indeed true.","The Wanlong Association had the money and would soon obtain the mining rights, but the technical threshold and experience required for mining could not be overcome overnight simply by throwing money at them.","Although The Young Lady had said that they could slowly build their own technical team, directly partnering with an established mining company would undoubtedly make things far more efficient. It could save them at least three to five years of trial and error.","“How will the shares be divided?”","Zhang Ting gritted his teeth and held up three fingers.","“Together, our two companies will take thirty percent. We’ll advance the funds for the auction. The Wanlong Association will hold seventy percent, while our two companies will provide all the technical support and equipment. We won’t participate in day-to-day management; we’ll only collect dividends. All we ask is to be allowed to take a sip from the pot.”","His offer could be regarded as a complete surrender—one made on his knees. He was practically begging Yang Xin and Xu Shishi for a chance.","Of course, from a business perspective, they were taking a tremendous loss. But they were genuinely frightened.","They were afraid of being targeted by the Wanlong Association. They were afraid that the next person to jump from a building would be one of them.","Their compromise was less a partnership than a protection payment—a way to buy their own safety.","Yang Xin did not answer immediately. Instead, he took out his phone, walked a short distance away, and called Liu Yutong. He briefly reported Zhang Ting and Xie Jichuan’s proposal.","After listening, Liu Yutong said only two words:","“Accept it.”","Yang Xin hung up and returned to the lounge area. He extended his hand toward Zhang Ting and Xie Jichuan.","“The Young Lady agrees. I look forward to working with you.”","Hearing this, Zhang Ting and Xie Jichuan released a long, simultaneous sigh of relief. They hurriedly extended their hands in return.","“Likewise! Likewise!”","After returning to the auction hall, Yang Xin announced publicly that the Wanlong Association was withdrawing from the bidding.","The auctioneer was somewhat surprised, but he still followed procedure and asked whether anyone else wished to raise their paddle.","The entire hall fell silent. Not a single person dared to raise a hand.","Who would be insane enough to challenge the Wanlong Association over something it had set its sights on?","The auctioneer took a deep breath. He raised the gavel high, then brought it down with a heavy thud.","“Three point one billion! Sold!”","“Congratulations to Mr. Zhang on successfully acquiring the exploration and mining rights to the Qingyan Mountain lithium mine!”","With the fall of the gavel, the development rights to the Qingyan Mountain lithium mine officially landed in Zhang Ting’s hands.","Of course, on the surface, he was the one who had purchased it. But everyone knew that the mine’s true owner was only one entity: the Wanlong Association.","Thunderous applause broke out. As they looked at Xu Shishi and Yang Xin, everyone present was left with the same thought:","The Wanlong Association had truly established an unshakable foothold in Jinchuan this time. From now on, the city’s mining industry would probably be monopolized by the Wanlong Association.","Anyone could see that the two businessmen from Hong Kong had been forced into compromising. Otherwise, even if they had ten times the courage, they would never have dared to raise their paddles under those circumstances.","“Joint development” might have sounded pleasant, but in reality, they had simply handed over control in exchange for a talisman of safety.","After the event ended, Zhang Ting and Xie Jichuan—men who were considered important figures by many—followed closely behind Yang Xin and Xu Shishi with ingratiating smiles. Their obsequious, subservient manner left everyone present sighing inwardly.","At the same time, it further confirmed their suspicions:","The power behind the Wanlong Association was indeed both formidable and ruthless.","...","Three days later.","In a top-floor suite at a hotel in Jinchuan, Liu Yutong sat on the sofa, listening as Yun Cheng gave her a full report on the investigation into the Qi Licheng incident.","Every detail had been recounted, from the moment Qi Licheng escaped the warehouse to the moment he jumped to his death.","“Qi Licheng probably reached the rooftop at around five in the morning. The surveillance cameras on the roof of the commercial building opposite captured the final part of his movements in full. He stayed on the roof for nearly five hours, smoking and pacing back and forth. At one point, he even crouched down and cried for a while.”","“It wasn’t until after ten in the morning, when the crowd below had grown dense, that he climbed over the railing and jumped. Before doing so, he left behind a lengthy suicide note, taking all the blame upon himself.”","“What did it say?”","“In essence, it said that he was responsible for the drug trafficking, the organization of the criminal gang, the unlawful imprisonment, and the illegal mining operation. He claimed that he had handled everything himself and that his father, Qi Tianhu, had known nothing about it.","“He also provided a detailed list of the businesses under his control, his drug-trafficking network, the exact locations of the illegal mines, and the enormous gambling debts he had personally accumulated in Aocheng. He confessed to everything in detail, and the chain of evidence was remarkably complete.”","“Looks like he intended to take all the charges upon himself and trade his life for a chance to get his father off the hook.”","“Yes. At the end of the suicide note, he even included a passage aimed at our Wanlong Association. He claimed that all of this had been forced on him by the Wanlong Association—that we had driven him into a corner. He also emphasized that there were problems within our organization, implying that the Wanlong Association was a criminal organization as well.”","Hearing this, Liu Yutong let out a humorless laugh.","That bastard was still trying to smear them even with death staring him in the face.","The Wanlong Association had always been a legitimate, law-abiding company!","But after calming down and thinking it over, she had to admit that what Qi Licheng had done was indeed a clever move.","While alive, he had been arrogant, conceited, foolish, and vicious... His faults were too numerous to count. Yet, at the very last moment of his life, he had done something absolutely right.","He had used his own life to buy his father a chance to escape.","“What’s the police’s reaction?”","“They’re still investigating. However, Qi Licheng took all the blame in his suicide note and provided a large amount of verifiable evidence to support his claims. So far, the police haven’t found any conclusive evidence directly implicating Qi Tianhu. Besides, Qi Tianhu’s lawyers are pulling every string they can. It probably won’t be long before he gets out.”","“Understood. We need to make every possible preparation as well.”","“Yes, The Young Lady!”","Liu Yutong was still somewhat worried about how Qi Tianhu would retaliate once he was released. After all, his only son had leaped from the roof of a building more than twenty stories high right in front of him.","Qi Tianhu would certainly blame the Wanlong Association for this blood feud and make them pay."]},{"number":861,"title":"Chapter 861: 862, The Young Lady's Command","paragraphs":["Sure enough!","Just one day later, Qi Tianhu was released on bail.","The result came as no surprise.","Qi Tianhu had been running things in Jinchuan for twenty years. It was hardly unexpected that he could get out so quickly.","But after Liu Yutong received the news, the tension in her heart only tightened.","Her main concern was that someone under her command might suffer unnecessary casualties. If that happened, things would become truly troublesome.","Less than a day after she heard that Qi Tianhu had been released, Lan Die hurried into the room.","“Young Lady, I have four pieces of news.”","“Go ahead.”","“First, before Qi Licheng jumped to his death, we had already sent people to investigate the illegal coal mine on Qingyan Mountain. But by the time our people and the police arrived, the workers with intellectual disabilities had already been transferred, and the entire site had been cleaned out. We found nothing.","“However, the police later made a major discovery in an abandoned mine shaft mentioned in Qi Licheng’s suicide note. A large number of human remains were found there—at least a dozen, according to the preliminary assessment.”","Liu Yutong’s heart sank.","More than a dozen sets of remains.","She immediately thought of Wang Xiaoshu and his grandmother. She was truly afraid that Dashu’s remains might be among them.","If Dashu was really gone, Xiaoshu’s grandmother would surely be unable to withstand the blow.","The old woman had held on for so long because of that last shred of hope.","If even that hope were snuffed out, she might very well give up on life then and there.","Liu Yutong made a silent decision at once. No matter what it cost, she had to send Qi Tianhu to prison—and make sure the case against him was airtight, leaving him no chance to turn things around!","“Second, while our people were following up on the illegal coal mine lead, they received some unexpected information. A normal person had infiltrated that group of intellectually disabled workers—and he was a journalist.”","“A journalist?”","“Yes. According to what we’ve learned, the journalist disguised himself as someone with an intellectual disability and infiltrated the illegal mine. He had been undercover there for more than three months, secretly filming everything. But the day before our people and the police arrived at the mine, his identity was discovered. He was probably captured.”","“Have you found out who the journalist is?”","“We have. His name is Zhou Ming. He’s an investigative journalist for a newspaper in northern China, specializing in undercover investigations and exposés. He’s fairly well-known in the industry. In the past, he reported on illegal cooking-oil operations, pyramid schemes, and gangs controlling homeless children. Several sensational cases that made national headlines were first exposed by him. But because of that, he also made a lot of enemies.","“I’ve also heard that he hasn’t dared to return home for many years.","“Besides that, our people discovered that Zhou Ming was a high school classmate of Professor Xu at BS University. The two of them seem to have been very close.”","When Liu Yutong heard this, she abruptly raised her head. “What? He and Professor Xu were classmates?!”","The moment she heard that, countless pieces fell into place.","It all matched! Every last detail!","In her previous life, she had only learned from others that Professor Xu had died suddenly. She had never known the exact reason.","Now, everything was connected!","Professor Xu must have gotten involved because of his old classmate Zhou Ming. He might even have obtained the evidence Zhou Ming had hidden away.","Otherwise, how could an elderly professor who preferred staying in his laboratory and rarely ever went out have suddenly died a violent death?","“Continue!”","“Third, we have information on Qi Tianhu’s movements. He appears to be gathering people, possibly preparing to retaliate against us.”","Liu Yutong wasn’t surprised by this news.","After being released, the first thing Qi Tianhu did was go to the funeral home and claim his son’s body. He then held an extraordinarily grand funeral.","At that funeral, the local kingpin who had dominated Jinchuan for twenty years said nothing. He stood before his son’s portrait for three full hours.","He didn’t say a word or shed a single tear. He simply stood there.","That kind of silence was the most frightening of all. The man was clearly plotting something.","Sure enough, after the funeral ended, Qi Tianhu began to take action.","Qi Tianhu’s retaliation was most likely to target three areas.","The first target would probably be Professor Xu. If Qi Tianhu intended to eliminate loose ends and silence everyone who knew the truth, Professor Xu would certainly be on his list.","The second target would be their Wanlong Association.","The Wanlong Association had numerous businesses throughout Jinchuan: construction sites, supermarkets, logistics parks, Internet cafés, and more. If Qi Tianhu ignored all restraint and targeted ordinary workers and managers, the resulting impact and casualties would put Liu Yutong and the others in an extremely difficult position.","The third target would most likely be the Qingyan Mountain lithium mine they had just acquired.","Lan Die had already received reports that unfamiliar faces had recently been seen near the lithium mine. They couldn’t afford to let their guard down.","Besides, Zhang Ting and Xie Jichuan, the two businessmen from Hong Kong City, were scheduled to visit the lithium mine in person within the next couple of days for their first on-site inspection.","If anything happened to them at the mine, the matter would truly spiral out of control. With the safety of businessmen from Hong Kong City involved, the entire direction of public opinion would become impossible to control.","“Fourth, Qi Tianhu is selling off his assets at rock-bottom prices in large quantities—coal mines, property developments, hotels, building-materials factories... He’s dumping everything. He’s raising money like a madman, and according to the information we’ve obtained, he also seems to have contacted people overseas.”","After hearing this final piece of news, Liu Yutong’s first thought was: He’s going to flee!","Or rather, before fleeing, he intended to retaliate like a rabid dog, then disappear with a fortune.","Liu Yutong immediately had someone bring her a map of the Jinchuan area and spread it across the table.","Then she picked up a red marker and marked the locations of every Wanlong Association business in Jinchuan one by one.","The Wanlong Plaza construction site, the supermarkets, the logistics and storage center, Phoenix Authority Internet Café... and the Qingyan Mountain lithium mine they had just acquired in partnership with the Hong Kong City businessmen.","After circling all the locations, Liu Yutong suddenly asked, “Yun Cheng, how many of our core members are in Jinchuan?”","“A little over a hundred.”","“If we spread them across more than a dozen business sites, each location can have at most seven or eight people. But if Qi Tianhu really attacks more than a dozen of our targets at the same time, he could concentrate his forces and launch a surprise attack on any one of them. We simply don’t have enough people to hold them off.”","“What about the entire BS Province?”","“Roughly five or six hundred.”","Liu Yutong made her decision immediately. “Call in reinforcements. We need to be prepared in case anyone makes a desperate move!”","They could call the police, of course, but the police couldn’t stand guard over all their businesses indefinitely before anything actually happened. In the end, they would still have to rely on themselves.","Their top priorities were to mobilize reinforcements to protect their businesses and find Professor Xu and the journalist Zhou Ming as quickly as possible. Once they obtained the evidence in their possession, Qi Tianhu would never be able to recover.","Yun Cheng nodded heavily. “Yes, Young Lady!”","Then he turned and walked to the side, took out his phone, and opened the Wanlong Association Group’s internal communications app.","The app’s interface was extremely simple, featuring only a contact list, a group chat list, and a module for posting announcements.","It was a newly developed app from the Digital Business Group, similar to QQ on a cellphone, except that it had limited functionality and was intended solely for internal communication within the company.","The app had also been developed with the company’s information security in mind.","After opening the app, Yun Cheng quickly tapped a few buttons.","Before long, the same four words appeared simultaneously in the announcement sections of all the major group chats:","[The Young Lady’s Order!]","The four words were displayed in red and pinned to the top. The instant the announcement was posted, nearly all the major groups for core members began vibrating at once.","JH Province Group.","BS Province Group.","HS Province Group.","Imperial Capital Group.","Pearl City General Group.","...","More than a dozen large groups, comprising over five thousand core members of the Wanlong Association, received the message at almost exactly the same time.","[The Young Lady’s Order!]","The announcement contained no unnecessary explanation. There was no reason, no description of the mission—not even a single additional word.","Yet the moment everyone saw those four words, they instinctively put down whatever they were doing and became serious.","In the more than two years since the Wanlong Association had been founded, The Young Lady had never issued a cross-regional mobilization order of this kind. This was the first time ever.","Everyone understood what it meant. Something major was about to happen.","Someone had crossed the Wanlong Association’s bottom line. Someone was trying to test The Young Lady’s limits again and again.","Before long, messages began flooding the major core groups.","“Received! Pearl City members standing by!”","“BS Province members standing by!”","“Imperial Capital members standing by!”","“HS Province members standing by!”","“JH Province members standing by!”","“...”","After countless confirmation messages filled the screens, a new line of text appeared repeatedly across all the groups:","“Please issue your instructions, Young Lady!”"]},{"number":862,"title":"Chapter 862: 863, Gathering","paragraphs":["HS Province, Pearl City.","Ma Da was leading a group of new recruits from the Human Resources Department through orientation in the conference room. Just as he reached the point about company culture and was talking himself hoarse, his phone suddenly vibrated in his pocket.","He casually pulled it out and glanced at the screen. The instant he saw the message, the expression on his face changed.","The next second, he tore the employee ID hanging around his neck, tossed it onto the table, and turned to the deputy beside him. “You take over here. Finish the rest of the training.”","With that, he hurried out of the conference room.","As he walked down the corridor, Ma Da made a call. “Taozi, book me the soonest flight to Jinchuan. I don’t care what class it is—as long as there’s a seat. Everyone in Pearl City who doesn’t have an urgent assignment, bring them all. Every last one.”","“Brother Ma, apart from those we have to leave behind to guard the city, we can probably mobilize around a thousand people. You want all of them sent over?”","“All of them!”","“If there aren’t enough plane tickets, charter a flight. If that won’t work, drive!”","“In short, I want to see everyone standing on Jinchuan’s turf within one day. Not a single person missing!”","“Yes! Understood, Brother Ma. I’ll arrange it right away!”","At the same time, in the provincial capital—","Yu Xin was sitting in a conference room in the Mobile Business Division, discussing the antenna design for the company’s first engineering handset with the technical team.","She, too, received a message during the meeting. When she opened it, a red pinned announcement from a group chat appeared on the screen.","She only had to glance at it before immediately ending the meeting. “That’s all for today. I have an urgent matter to deal with. Organize the follow-up proposals and send them to my email.”","Half an hour later, a convoy of more than a dozen black Mercedes-Benz vehicles left the provincial capital.","Scenes like this were unfolding almost simultaneously in cities across multiple provinces throughout the Dragon Kingdom.","Within just a few hours, flights bound for BS Province were being booked in huge numbers.","Large numbers of vehicles bearing license plates from different provinces took to the highways heading southwest at nearly the same time.","Countless people dressed in black suits were making their way to Jinchuan by every means available.","At the same time, messages were flooding more than a dozen major group chats in the capital, Pearl City, BS Province, and elsewhere.","“Received! Departing immediately!”","“On the way to the assembly point!”","“Booked the earliest flight. Expected to land in BS Province in four hours!”","“The self-driving convoy is on the highway. Estimated arrival in Jinchuan: ten hours!”","“The first group of three hundred has departed!”","“...”","Not a single message asked what had happened or whether the trip could be delayed for a couple of days.","To them, if The Young Lady summoned them, they had to appear where they were needed. No explanation was necessary.","Viewed from a purely rational perspective, such almost fanatical obedience was utterly incomprehensible.","But if you truly understood the history of the Wanlong Society from its founding to the present, if you understood how Liu Yutong had gathered these people—once scattered across street corners and pushed to the fringes of society—and given them jobs, dignity, and a place they could call home, then you would understand where this terrifying unity came from.","The most difficult kind of loyalty to buy in this world sometimes required only two things: sincerity.","That afternoon, unfamiliar faces began appearing in large numbers at Jinchuan’s long-distance bus station and railway station.","Most of them were between twenty and thirty years old. Every one of them looked energetic and particularly fit.","In Jinchuan, this was highly unusual.","It wasn’t the New Year, nor was it a holiday. Normally, most of the city’s young people had already left for work in the big cities by this time of year. More people went out than came back.","For so many young people to arrive in Jinchuan in wave after wave was clearly abnormal.","What was especially strange was that nearly all of them spoke with out-of-town accents.","The highways were attracting attention too, particularly at the exits.","Jinchuan was no provincial capital or major metropolis. The city normally saw very little outside traffic, and foreign license plates were rare sights on its streets.","Yet starting at noon, vehicles with out-of-town plates began streaming off the highway one after another. Almost all of them were black Mercedes-Benz sedans, occasionally mixed with dark-colored commercial vans or buses. They emerged from the toll station in a long line.","Some local taxi drivers noticed the unusual scene as well and began chatting about it whenever business slowed down.","“Holy crap, what’s going on today? I picked up seven or eight young people with out-of-town accents at the bus station in one go. They were all headed downtown, and none of them had much luggage. Doesn’t feel like they’re here to sightsee. Anyone know what’s happening?”","“I picked up more than a dozen at the railway station too. Normally, I’m lucky if I get three or five passengers around this time. Business is incredible today! Does anyone know what’s going on?”","“I’ll tell you what—I was waiting for passengers at the rest area near the highway exit earlier. I hadn’t even been there half an hour when I saw at least twenty black Mercedes-Benz cars come through the toll station. All had out-of-town plates, and none of them stopped. I’ve been driving a taxi for five years, and this is the first time I’ve ever seen a spectacle like this in our little city.”","“Why are all these rich people suddenly descending on Jinchuan?”","“Could they have discovered a gold mine here and come to strike it rich?”","“Not that I’ve heard! But I did hear something else. Things haven’t been very peaceful in Jinchuan lately.”","“What do you mean by ‘not peaceful’? Come on, tell us more.”","“You haven’t heard? A few days ago, that guy from Jinchuan—the son of Tiger Qi—jumped from a building. He died on the spot.”","“Holy crap! Seriously? You mean the one from Tiger Group?”","“Who else could it be? How many Tiger Qis are there in Jinchuan?”","“My cousin works as a security guard in that building. He saw it with his own eyes. You have no idea how horrible it was. Tiger Qi had just been put into a police car downstairs when he watched helplessly as his son came crashing down from the roof!”","“Damn... Then could all these outsiders be here for Qi Tiger’s son’s funeral?”","“Don’t rule it out. In Jinchuan, only the Qi family has that kind of clout.”","“But it doesn’t feel like that to me. Who wears suits and doesn’t even put on mourning clothes when attending a funeral? I think they look more like they’re here to pick a fight...”","“Whatever. It has nothing to do with ordinary people like us. Let’s just keep our heads down and work.”","“Exactly. Making money is what matters. Come on, let’s get moving!”"]},{"number":863,"title":"Chapter 863: 864, Storm Clouds Rising","paragraphs":["Elsewhere.","Liu Yutong had also been waiting for news about Professor Xu.","“Lan Die, have you heard anything from Professor Xu’s side?”","“Our people went to Professor Xu’s residence, but no one was home. We also asked around at the university. His colleagues said they last saw him five days ago, and he hasn’t appeared since. His phone is unreachable as well. In addition, his daughter, Xu Yi, has been unable to contact him.”","“Also, our people spotted traces near BS University that appear to belong to Qi Tianhu’s men. They’re asking around about Professor Xu’s whereabouts too.”","Liu Yutong’s expression grew grave.","Qi Tianhu had moved faster than they had anticipated. He had already traced Professor Xu’s whereabouts to BS University.","“As for that reporter, Zhou Ming, we’ve been tracking him constantly. We’ve used every channel available to us, but so far, we still have no reliable information. If he’s still alive, then the only person who probably knows where he is now is Qi Tianhu himself.”","Liu Yutong fell silent for a moment, considering the various possibilities. Then she looked up at Yun Cheng.","“How many people have we assembled so far?”","“More than five hundred are already in place. At this rate, we expect the number to exceed three thousand by tomorrow evening.”","Three thousand people. That was enough!","Just as Liu Yutong was about to issue the next order, Lan Die received a new message.","“Miss!”","“We’ve just received word that someone may have spotted Professor Xu Yangen!”","“Where?”","“In the old district. According to the description, the person believed to be Professor Xu was walking in a hurry and looked panicked. He also seemed to have suffered a minor injury.”","“Yun Cheng!”","“Here!”","“Notify all our men near the old district immediately. They must find Professor Xu before Qi Tianhu’s people do! Use force if necessary!”","“Yes, Miss!”","......","At the same time.","At a private club halfway up the mountain, Qi Tianhu was meeting with a group of old comrades.","In just a few days, this Jinchuan’s underworld emperor seemed to have aged ten years. The gray in his temples had become noticeably more pronounced.","His entire aura had changed as well.","If Qi Tianhu had once been a mighty tiger ruling over the mountains and forests, he was now a wounded beast that had lost its cub.","An icy, dangerous presence radiated from him.","“Is everyone here?”","“Lord Tiger, everyone’s here.”","Standing before him were seven or eight men. They had all been old brothers who had followed him in his early days as he fought to build his empire. None of them were young anymore, and some even had gray at their temples.","Most of them had gradually stepped back from the front lines, leaving their operations and businesses to their subordinates while enjoying a semi-retired life.","Now, a single call from Qi Tianhu had brought them all back.","“I called you here today for one reason only.”","“Every one of you knows how my son, Li Cheng, died.”","“The Wanlong Association is the murderer!”","“They drove my son to his death! If I, Qi Tianhu, don’t avenge this blood debt, I’m no father!”","The expressions of everyone present grew solemn.","“My plan has three steps.”","“First, I’m going to completely destroy the Wanlong Association’s reputation in Jinchuan. I’ll make them utterly rotten, so they can never clear their name!”","“Second, I want those two businessmen from Hong Kong dead!”","The moment he said this, everyone’s faces changed.","A man seated at the front, a street boss wearing a thick gold chain, couldn’t help saying, “Lord Tiger, isn’t attacking Hong Kong businessmen too risky? You know what the relationship between Hong Kong and the mainland is like. If something happens to Hong Kong businessmen on the mainland, it will immediately alarm the higher-ups. Once this blows up, we...”","What he meant was that none of them might be able to escape.","But Qi Tianhu cut him off without the slightest concern.","“That’s exactly what I want. I want it to blow up!”","“I’ve already contacted someone and paid them three million. On the day of the groundbreaking ceremony for the Qingyan Mountain lithium mine, they’ll disguise themselves as members of the Wanlong Association and attack.”","“When that happens, every major media outlet in the country will report on it!”","“No matter how fake it looks, once public opinion catches fire, the Wanlong Association won’t be able to explain itself even with a hundred mouths.”","“I want these waters as muddy as possible! So muddy that even the people above can’t suppress it, so muddy that the Wanlong Association won’t be able to clear its name even if it jumps into the Yellow River!”","The room fell silent.","Everyone had been stunned by Qi Tianhu’s vicious scheme.","Framing someone else, killing with a borrowed knife, and then using the blade of public opinion to drive the enemy into the ground for good—","It was truly ruthless!","But taking the lives of Hong Kong businessmen and pinning the blame on the Wanlong Association would cause an enormous stir once exposed.","If the authorities investigated, every single one of them would be finished.","Some had already begun reconsidering their involvement, wondering whether they should flee to another city as soon as the meeting ended.","They had all fought alongside their boss in the past, but who would be willing to risk their lives at an age when they were nearly retired?","Of course, they could only keep such thoughts hidden. Anyone could see that Qi Tianhu was in an utterly irrational state, and no one dared provoke him now.","“Third, I want every business the Wanlong Association owns in Jinchuan brought to a complete standstill!”","“Old Sun!”","Old Sun gave a slight start and hurriedly straightened up.","“Lord Tiger, what are your orders?”","“How many men can you mobilize right now?”","“I can bring out a little over two hundred brothers. If we count the security staff at several of our establishments, gathering three hundred won’t be a problem.”","“Good.”","Qi Tianhu turned to the next man.","“What about the East District?”","Another burly man, two blue dragons tattooed on his arm, immediately replied, “Lord Tiger, I can provide one hundred and fifty men.”","“What about the South District?”","“I can bring two hundred.”","“And the North District?”","“One hundred and eighty. They can be assembled at any time.”","The seven or eight men reported their numbers one after another. In the end, they could mobilize roughly a thousand people.","That was the maximum force Jinchuan’s underworld could muster.","Qi Tianhu slowly nodded after hearing the total.","“That’s enough.”","“The Wanlong Association has, at most, a hundred men in Jinchuan. They have to spread themselves across more than a dozen businesses, so each location will have only a handful of people. Send all one thousand of our men out and have them strike simultaneously in separate groups. I want to see how those few men plan to defend more than a dozen sites!”","“Lord Tiger, when we hit the Wanlong Association’s businesses, do we attack their people directly, or...”","“No.”","Qi Tianhu waved a hand. Although he desperately wanted revenge, he understood that, at a time like this, if anyone died, the police would pursue the matter relentlessly. Then not only would he fail to get his revenge, he might even lose every possible escape route.","“Your main targets aren’t their people. They’re their businesses. In short, smash them hard! As long as you bring every one of the Wanlong Association’s businesses in Jinchuan to a halt, that’s all that matters.”","“Remember, have all the brothers wear black clothes and cover their faces with masks. There are already plenty of people saying that the Wanlong Society is a criminal organization, so let’s make that accusation a fact!”","“Understood, Lord Tiger!”","“Go. I want to see the results within three days.”","“Yes, sir!”","Seven or eight men rose from their seats and left the clubhouse.","Only one man remained behind. A centipede tattoo crawled along his arm.","His nickname was Centipede, and he was Qi Tianhu’s most trusted subordinate.","For years, he had handled all the dirty, underhanded work that could never see the light of day.","“Little Centipede, has that reporter talked yet?”","Centipede shook his head. “That bastard’s got one hell of a stubborn mouth. We’ve had him hanging in the basement for two days and two nights, and we’ve tried every method there is, but he still hasn’t said a word. I’ve broken plenty of tough nuts in my time, but I’ve never seen anyone this hard.”","Qi Tianhu’s expression darkened at once, killing intent spreading through his eyes.","“Don’t kill him yet.”","“He must have handed those hidden pieces of evidence to his classmate. We need to keep him alive so we can use him to draw that person out.”","“Yes, Lord Tiger!”","“By the way, Lord Tiger, according to reports from our men on the streets, a group of people from the Wanlong Society has made its way into the old district. They look like they’re searching for someone. I suspect they may have also discovered the whereabouts of that professor.”","“If you suspect it, then capture them! No matter the cost, we absolutely cannot let the evidence hidden by that reporter be sent out! You know what will happen if it falls into the hands of the Wanlong Society!”","“Understood! I’ll take care of it right away!”","After Centipede left as well, Qi Tianhu was the only person remaining in the clubhouse.","He stood alone before the square table, staring at the black-and-white memorial portrait of his son resting on it.","In the photograph, Qi Licheng was still very young. His hair was dyed an obnoxious shade of yellow, and he was flashing the camera an especially arrogant hand gesture.","Qi Tianhu reached out and gently brushed his finger across his son’s face in the photograph. His hand trembled faintly.","“Li Cheng, your father is sorry. I failed to discipline you properly, and that’s what led you to this point. But I promise you, every single person responsible for your death will pay. Not one of them will get away.”","“You just watch over it all from heaven.”"]},{"number":864,"title":"Chapter 864: 865, Collision","paragraphs":["The Old City, evening.","The sky had already darkened considerably, but the streetlights in the alley had yet to come on.","Xu Yangeng was hunched in the innermost corner of a shabby hole-in-the-wall restaurant, head lowered as he wolfed down the dan dan noodles in his bowl, picking at them with his chopsticks.","After only a few mouthfuls, he would raise his head to glance toward the entrance, checking whether anyone had followed him.","His current situation could be summed up in four words: surrounded on all sides.","No—more accurately, surrounded by thugs on all sides.","To understand how things had come to this, they had to go back to the previous week.","That day, following the address his childhood friend Zhou Ming had given him, Xu Yangeng found a kraft-paper envelope taped beneath a windowsill at a rented apartment in an old tube-shaped residential building in the Old City.","Inside the envelope was a USB drive and seven or eight developed photographs.","The photos showed scenes deep inside a mine.","In them, emaciated miners with vacant, dazed eyes dug for coal in the darkness like walking corpses.","With only a single glance, Xu Yangeng understood everything.","That bastard Zhou Ming had stirred up another hornet’s nest—an enormous one.","And this time, he probably really wasn’t getting out.","Xu Yangeng’s first reaction upon seeing the evidence was to call the police.","But at the last moment, he stopped.","He remembered the final words Zhou Ming had said to him over the phone: “The waters here run too deep. Don’t just hand this stuff over to anyone. Find someone familiar—someone you can trust.”","So he changed his mind. He planned to return to the provincial capital first, then find a police officer he knew and trusted and hand the evidence over in person.","However, the moment he arrived at the bus station, he realized something was wrong.","There were large numbers of tough-looking men loitering around the station plaza. They weren’t lining up or buying tickets. They simply stood there, studying the faces of everyone entering or leaving the station.","For his own safety, he had no choice but to abandon his original plan and hide temporarily in Jinchuan’s Old City.","Over the past few days, he had changed hotels three or four times and even removed the SIM card from his phone. Like a frightened rabbit, he had scurried from place to place through Jinchuan’s streets and alleys.","He could finally understand why Zhou Ming had not dared return home for so many years. The feeling of being watched was truly suffocating.","It was as though someone had pulled a plastic bag over your head and slowly tightened it, making you feel fear, then despair.","And just as he feared, the worst came to pass.","Xu Yangeng had just set down his chopsticks and was preparing to leave when he noticed two men in black through the greasy glass window of the restaurant.","The two young men in black were standing across the street, looking around as if searching for something.","“Damn it. They still found me.”","Xu Yangeng quickly pulled his cap lower and silently told himself, Don’t panic. Maybe it’s just a coincidence. Maybe they’re only a couple of salesmen.","But in the next second, his last shred of wishful thinking was shattered.","He saw two more men in black appear across the street. After the four of them regrouped, one pointed toward the noodle shop, and the other three immediately turned their heads in unison to look at the little restaurant where Xu Yangeng was sitting.","His mind exploded with a buzz.","He hurriedly lowered his head, flipped up the hood at the back of his jacket, and pulled it over his head, covering himself as thoroughly as possible.","“I can’t just sit here waiting to die. Run!”","He slapped a ten-yuan bill onto the table, turned around, and dashed toward the restaurant’s kitchen.","This was something he had learned during the past few days of hiding. Small eateries in old neighborhoods usually had a back door leading to the rear alley, which was used for deliveries. At critical moments, it could double as an escape route.","Xu Yangeng swept aside the plastic curtain leading into the kitchen. Under the astonished gazes of several older women sitting on little stools and sorting vegetables or washing dishes, he squeezed through the narrow passageway, shoved open the metal back door, and fled into the alley behind the building.","He ran as fast as he could, taking several turns before finally making it back to the residential building where he was staying temporarily.","He raced up to the fourth floor, pushed open the door, locked it from the inside, and leaned against the door panel, gasping for breath.","But before he had even caught his breath, he glanced down through the window, and his heart instantly sank halfway into his stomach.","Several more young men dressed in black had appeared in the narrow alley below. They were spreading out in pairs and groups, searching for someone. One of them even looked up toward the building, sweeping his gaze across the upper floors while pointing here and there. Xu Yangeng couldn’t make out what he was saying.","Xu Yangeng hurriedly pulled his head back inside, his spine pressed tightly against the wall, cursing under his breath.","Black clothes again!","Damn it, why were there people in black everywhere?!","Countless men in black had suddenly appeared throughout Jinchuan over the past two days. Wherever he went, he ran into them, like they were swarming flies.","There were some at the railway station, some at the bus station, and even some around this rundown residential building where he was hiding.","What was more, all of them wore the same style of black clothing. Anyone could tell they belonged to the same group.","“Oh no, oh no. They’ve mobilized the entire criminal underworld of Jinchuan to hunt me down!”","“I’m a dead man!”","Leaning against the wall, Xu Yangeng closed his eyes in despair.","His mind was filled with images of Old Zhou being tortured in every way imaginable.","He had never actually witnessed any of it, but he couldn’t stop himself from imagining it.","The more he thought about it, the more frightened he became; the more frightened he became, the more he thought about it. The cycle went on and on.","“Old Zhou, you really went and made a mess of things this time!”","“You’re going to get me killed too!”","After crouching in the corner for quite some time, Xu Yangeng vigorously rubbed his face with both hands, forcing himself to pull it together.","“No. I can’t wait here to die.”","He stood up, quietly turned the lock, and crept toward the stairwell.","There were no lights in the corridor. It was pitch-black, save for a motion-activated light at the far end that flickered on and off.","He had barely taken a few steps when a dense chorus of footsteps suddenly rose from below.","He looked down and saw seven or eight men in black running up the stairs. Startled, he quickly pulled back, turned around, and ran in the opposite direction.","This tube-shaped residential building had an old-fashioned ring-shaped layout, with two stairwells at opposite ends—one on the east side and one on the west.","The men in black were coming up from the east, so he ran toward the west.","But just as he reached the western stairwell, he heard another burst of hurried footsteps coming from below.","Xu Yangeng slammed on the brakes, nearly tumbling down the stairs.","There were people on the west side too!","He was trapped in the middle!","“After living for more than forty years, I, Xu Yangeng, have conducted research, published papers, and even won a National Science and Technology Progress Award. Am I really going to meet my end in some dilapidated residential building today?”","Xu Yangeng looked left and right. Gritting his teeth, he pushed open the half-closed door of a nearby apartment and slipped inside.","The family that had lived there had moved out long ago. All that remained in the room was a broken bed with one leg collapsed and an old wardrobe missing half its door.","Without a second thought, Xu Yangeng pulled open the wardrobe door and climbed inside. He pulled the door shut behind him, held his breath, and sat perfectly still.","The wardrobe was thick with dust, making his nose sting repeatedly. He almost sneezed.","But all he could do was clamp his hand over his mouth and nose and force himself to endure the discomfort.","The footsteps outside drew closer and closer, finally stopping at the doorway.","Soon, voices drifted in from outside.","“I clearly saw someone run this way just now.”","“Split up and search. Check every room—don’t miss anything.”","“Move it! We can’t let that bunch get there first!”","“...”","Hearing the exchange, Xu Yangeng’s heart sank once again.","That bunch?","What did they mean?","Had different gangs put a bounty on him?","Yes! That had to be it!","That mob boss must have put out a hit on him, sending every gang in Jinchuan out to search for him. Whoever found him first would collect the money.","No wonder he kept running into men in black wherever he went.","This was bad. He really wasn’t going to get away now!","Outside the wardrobe, the footsteps had already entered the room. He could even hear them rummaging through things.","Xu Yangeng shut his eyes and began frantically reciting in his mind: “Prosperity, democracy, civility, harmony... rule of law...”","Just as he reached “rule of law”—","Bang!","Someone yanked the wardrobe door open from the outside.","Xu Yangeng came face-to-face with the man in black who had opened it.","The man was clearly stunned as well. He obviously hadn’t expected a living person to be hiding inside that battered wardrobe.","The two of them stared at each other, wide-eyed, for several seconds before the man finally came to his senses. He turned toward the hallway and shouted, “Found him! He’s with me!”","“It’s over.” Xu Yangeng was utterly despairing.","At that critical moment, another burst of rapid footsteps came from the doorway. Yet another group had arrived.","“Who are you? Hand him over!”","“Hand him over? Why should we? We found him first!”","“Cut the crap. Lord Tiger said whoever captures him gets double the reward. We’re taking him!”","“Double? What do you mean, double? You’re not with that bunch?”","“What bunch? Which side are you with?”","“We’re Lord Tiger’s men. Who are you?”","“The Wanlong Society!”","The air suddenly fell silent.","The two groups of men in black faced each other in a standoff in the hallway.","The next second, both sides attacked at once.","Crouched inside the wardrobe, Xu Yangeng could only hear a chaotic burst of banging and crashing from outside. People screamed, cursed, and shouted as everything descended into pandemonium."]},{"number":865,"title":"Chapter 865: 866, What Exactly Does Your Ten Thousand Dragons Society Do","paragraphs":["The fight lasted less than a minute before the sounds of struggle outside suddenly came to an abrupt halt.","Professor Xu had just started to stick his head out to see what was happening when the wardrobe door was pulled open from the outside once again.","This time, three men in black stood before him. Each of them wore a dragon-shaped badge on his chest.","The man in the lead bent slightly toward Professor Xu, who was curled up in the corner of the wardrobe, and said politely, “Professor Xu, please don’t be afraid. We’re here to protect you.”","Professor Xu looked at them, then glanced at the black-clad thugs sprawled all over the floor behind them. He had only one thought in mind.","You guys look even more like gangsters than the people outside!","Protect me? Who are you trying to fool?","“Who... who sent you?”","“We’re with the Wanlong Society.”","The moment Professor Xu heard those three words, his heart sank.","Wanlong Society. Even the name sounded like some serious criminal organization!","Professor Xu slowly closed his eyes, stiffened his neck, and said, “Just get it over with! Kill me! I won’t tell you anything!”","But the pain he had imagined never came.","No one pulled out a knife. No one put a sack over his head. No one even laid a finger on him.","Instead, the men in black escorted him into a black Mercedes-Benz waiting downstairs.","Once they were in the car, the leader took the front passenger seat. He turned around and looked at Professor Xu, who was still trembling, before finally explaining, “Professor Xu, please don’t be nervous. The Young Lady sent us to protect you.”","“The Young Lady? Which Young Lady?”","“You’ve met her before—Liu Yutong, Miss Liu.”","Professor Xu froze for several seconds before a figure finally emerged in his mind.","Liu Yutong?","The wealthy young woman who had been sitting with his daughter, Xu Yi, in the BS University cafeteria that day, and had chatted with him for quite a while about her business plans?","Wait—she was the daughter of a crime boss?","“Just who exactly is your Young Lady?”","“She’s the chairwoman of the Wanlong Society Group.”","Professor Xu was stunned. “Chairwoman? Isn’t she a student at the University of Finance?”","The man in black nodded proudly. “That’s right. Our Young Lady just started her third year this year. You knew she was still in school?”","Professor Xu’s head began to buzz.","Everything was a mess. Completely unbelievable!","A third-year female university student was actually the chairwoman of some Wanlong Society?","And she had so many men in black working for her, all of them frighteningly skilled fighters.","What kind of person was she?","“Where are we going?”","“To the hotel. The Young Lady is waiting for you there.”","About twenty minutes later, the car stopped in front of a luxury hotel.","Professor Xu was helped out of the car. He looked up at the hotel entrance, and the small amount of relief he had begun to feel immediately vanished.","A huge number of men in black stood in the hotel lobby. At a rough estimate, there were at least fifty of them. They all wore identical black suits and identical dragon-shaped badges, looking exactly like a scene from a movie where a gang was gathering for a meeting.","“Professor Xu, this way, please.”","Professor Xu was led into the building, through the lobby, and into an elevator.","His legs kept trembling. With men in black surrounding him on both sides, there was nowhere to run even if he wanted to. All he could do was steel himself and follow them.","Before long, they arrived in front of the banquet hall.","When the men in black standing by the entrance saw them approaching, they pushed the doors open from either side.","It was an enormous banquet hall, at least a thousand square meters in size.","Even though Professor Xu felt he had prepared himself mentally, the scene before him still left him terrified the moment the doors opened.","The vast banquet hall was packed wall to wall with men in black.","Not five. Not fifty. Not even five hundred.","As far as the eye could see, there was nothing but a sea of black. There had to be at least a thousand people.","The instant he stepped into the hall, more than a thousand pairs of eyes turned toward him in unison. The sight nearly scared the old professor into a heart attack.","Where on earth had he come?","What exactly were these people?","With this kind of force, even the police wouldn’t be enough. It looked like they would need to send in the army to wipe them out.","While he stood there in a daze, a black-clad figure at the front of the banquet hall rose from her chair and turned around.","It was the young woman he had met in the university cafeteria that day.","At this moment, she was completely different from the female student he had seen in the cafeteria. Her presence was far more commanding.","Several core members, all dressed in black and radiating an imposing air, stood behind her.","“Professor Xu, we meet again,” Liu Yutong said with a smile.","Professor Xu instinctively took half a step backward.","He had imagined meeting this young woman again countless times—in his office, perhaps, or at a restaurant...","But he had never imagined it would happen under circumstances like these.","A third-year female university student, with more than a thousand men in black standing behind her.","The contrast was simply too overwhelming!","It was terrifying!","“Professor Xu, please don’t be nervous. I asked you here because I’d like to discuss something with you.”","“You... what do you want with me?”","“I’ll get straight to the point. Professor Xu, you have something in your possession that one of your classmates gave you, don’t you?”","Professor Xu’s heart gave a jolt.","Here it was. She really had come for that thing!","“I have no idea what you’re talking about.”","It wasn’t that he didn’t want to cooperate. He simply didn’t dare hand it over so casually.","His old classmate, Zhou Ming, had risked his life to obtain that item. If he handed it over, and the other side turned around and used it to strike a deal with that crime lord, wouldn’t Old Zhou’s sacrifice have been for nothing?","“Professor Xu, are you worried that I’ll use the evidence to make a deal with Qi Tianhu?” Liu Yutong asked.","Professor Xu said nothing, but the expression on his face—an expression of defiance, as if he had already resigned himself to death—had given her the answer.","Liu Yutong naturally saw through him. “I can assure you that I’m not on the same side as Qi Tianhu.”","“I’m asking you for the evidence not to destroy it. I want to save your classmate.”","“Who did you say you want to save?”","“Your classmate, Zhou Ming.”","“You... you know Old Zhou?”","“I don’t know him personally, but I know he must still be alive. He’s currently in Qi Tianhu’s hands. The only reason Qi Tianhu has kept him alive until now is because he hasn’t found the item yet. Once the item is gone, he’ll have no reason to keep Zhou Ming alive.”","As she spoke, Liu Yutong raised two slender fingers.","“I’ll give you two choices.”","“First, give the item to me. I’ll use it to exchange for Zhou Ming’s life.”","“Second, continue hiding it. I’ll call the police and have them search Qi Tianhu’s hideout. But if that happens, Qi Tianhu will certainly kill Zhou Ming immediately. Even if you eventually manage to bring him to justice, Zhou Ming won’t survive.”","Professor Xu’s eyes immediately turned red.","It wasn’t because Liu Yutong had convinced him. It was because he had imagined what his old classmate might be suffering at that very moment—perhaps being tortured by those people—and the thought filled him with pain and anguish.","At the same time, two voices began fighting wildly inside his mind.","One voice screamed: Don’t be fooled by her appearance! This is clearly an extremely vicious criminal organization!","The other desperately reminded him: This might truly be the only chance to save Old Zhou.","“What guarantee do I have?” Professor Xu’s emotions had finally defeated his reason.","“I can’t give you any guarantee at all.”","“But you can take a gamble—gamble that I truly want to save people, or gamble that I’m lying to you,” Liu Yutong said.","Xu Yangeng slowly lowered his head.","He kept it lowered for a long time.","Under the gaze of more than a thousand people, he finally raised his head again and looked at Liu Yutong, telling her where the item was:","“In a supermarket in the north of Jinchuan City. Locker No. 17 in the third row. The key is hidden under the second brick in the flower bed outside the supermarket.”","Liu Yutong nodded, then turned to Lan Die behind her and ordered, “Send someone to retrieve it immediately.”","“Yes!”","Watching Liu Yutong’s swift and decisive manner, Xu Yangeng felt a jumble of emotions.","His fear had lessened somewhat, but his doubts had only deepened.","In the end, he couldn’t hold back and asked her one question: “What exactly does your Wanlong Society... do?”","Hearing this, Liu Yutong turned and glanced at the packed hall full of men in black before answering:","“We’re a legitimate, law-abiding private company!”","Xu Yangeng: “???”"]},{"number":866,"title":"Chapter 866: 867, Trading People for Evidence.","paragraphs":["The outskirts of Jinchuan City. A private club.","Qi Tianhu sat there with a dark expression as he listened to his men report.","His son, Qi Licheng, had jumped from a building and died a horrible death. The family business had suffered a devastating blow, and nearly all the coal mines, property developments, building-material factories, and other assets under his name had been sold off at rock-bottom prices. In other words, he had practically thrown away the foundation he had spent half his life building.","Although he now had more cash in hand, he had also become increasingly irritable and irrational.","His latest failed operation against the Wanlong Association had pushed his anger to the limit.","He had gathered more than a thousand street toughs and sent them to launch simultaneous attacks on all of the Wanlong Association’s businesses throughout Jinchuan. Their sole objective was to bring the association’s operations in the city to a complete standstill.","But they had all been soundly defeated. It was utterly ridiculous!","More than a thousand men!","He had sent them to wreak havoc on the Wanlong Association’s territory, yet the other side hadn’t even lost a hair. Instead, his men had been beaten so badly they were crying for their mothers.","Even if a thousand pigs had charged in and trampled around, they should at least have managed to smash a few floors, shouldn’t they?","“Lord Tiger, something’s gone wrong! The supermarket operation failed. Our men had just rushed into the sales area and were preparing to smash the shelves when more than twenty men in black suddenly charged out from the warehouse and fire exits. They took down all our brothers in a matter of moments, then called the police. Every one of our men was taken to the station. Most of them didn’t even get away.”","“Lord Tiger, the construction site operation failed too. We had scouted the place beforehand and thought there were only a few security guards on duty. Who could have known that nearly a hundred men in black were hiding behind the surrounding walls? The moment our men climbed in, they were surrounded and beaten. Quite a few were injured.”","“Lord Tiger, the same thing happened at Huangquan Internet Café. We hadn’t even entered the building when two rows of men in black were already standing outside. They outnumbered us...”","“Lord Tiger...”","Report after report of failure came in, and Qi Tianhu’s face gradually turned ashen.","“Useless!”","“Useless!”","“You’re all fucking useless!”","“Who the hell can tell me what’s going on?!”","“Tell me!”","“Even a thousand pigs could have taken down at least one location! What the hell have you been doing all this time?”","The old associates who had been urgently summoned all lowered their heads, not daring to say a word.","They hadn’t expected this result either.","Their boss had clearly told them that the Wanlong Association had, at most, a hundred or so people in Jinchuan. Those men were spread across more than a dozen business locations, with only a few assigned to each one.","According to that intelligence, more than a thousand people attacking simultaneously from different directions should have completely overwhelmed them.","But reality had turned out the exact opposite.","Wherever their men went, they were greeted by groups of men in black—more numerous than them and far more capable. They had been crushed in return. It made no sense at all.","It felt as though the Wanlong Association didn’t have a hundred men in Jinchuan, but at least a thousand—perhaps even more.","Before long, a wild thought occurred to several of the underworld bosses present.","Could the Wanlong Association have brought in reinforcements from outside the city?","The moment that thought surfaced, their expressions changed.","If that was true, then the Wanlong Association’s strength was terrifying.","To mobilize so many people from elsewhere and bring them into Jinchuan in such a short time required extraordinary organizational ability. An ordinary person could never have pulled it off.","Their guess was correct.","The Wanlong Association had not only brought in reinforcements—it had mobilized nearly four thousand men in one move, spreading them throughout every corner of Jinchuan.","No matter which direction Qi Tianhu’s men attacked from or what time they chose, they could not possibly break through a defensive force of that scale.","Besides, those random street punks were only useful for putting on a show and making up the numbers. When it came to a real fight, their combat ability was worlds apart from that of the Wanlong Association’s rigorously trained core members.","The more they thought about it, the more frightened they became. Yet none of them dared to explain anything to Qi Tianhu at a time like this.","Everyone could see that Qi Tianhu’s mental state had already become somewhat unstable.","Seeing them all sitting there with their heads lowered and refusing to speak, suspicion in Qi Tianhu’s eyes grew stronger and stronger.","Someone among them had definitely been brushing him off. There might even be a traitor.","Otherwise, there was no way the Wanlong Association could have learned of his operation in advance and mobilized its forces ahead of time.","The Wanlong Association only had around a hundred men in Jinchuan. Even if it had temporarily called in reinforcements from elsewhere, it should have been impossible to form such an overwhelming numerical advantage in such a short period.","Unless someone had leaked his plans beforehand.","Qi Tianhu’s sinister gaze swept across the old associates seated before him, trying to read something from their faces.","Under his stare, several of the underworld bosses began to feel their hearts tremble, and sweat started forming on their foreheads.","But the more nervous they looked, the more convinced Qi Tianhu became that they were hiding something. He grew increasingly certain that there was a traitor among them—someone who had revealed his plans to the Wanlong Association and given it time to gather its men and prepare.","Yes, that had to be it!","Otherwise, there was no way to explain why all the operations at more than a dozen locations had failed.","Just as Qi Tianhu was preparing to pressure them into exposing the mole, his phone suddenly rang.","He glanced at the incoming number, and his eyes immediately sharpened. Then he answered the call.","A somewhat familiar voice came from the other end. It was the Dragon Society president surnamed Yang.","“Qi Tianhu, The Young Lady asked me to pass a few words on to you.”","“Speak!”","A murderous glint appeared in Qi Tianhu’s eyes.","Although he currently wanted nothing more than to grind everyone in the Wanlong Association to dust, the other side had taken the initiative to call him, which meant there had to be a reason.","He temporarily suppressed the murderous rage surging through his heart, wanting to hear what kind of trick they were trying to play.","“First, the thing you wanted is in The Young Lady’s hands now—the original copy.”","Qi Tianhu’s heart sank when he heard that.","The thing he had feared most had happened after all.","Still, he couldn’t understand it. If the other side had obtained the evidence, why hadn’t they simply joined forces with the police and taken him down in one sweep?","Why call and warn him instead?","The answer came quickly from the other end.","“Second, The Young Lady knows you’re holding a reporter captive. She wants to make a deal with you. Tomorrow at noon, at the construction site in the northern suburbs. Bring the reporter there, and the two of you can negotiate face-to-face.”","“The Young Lady you mentioned is your boss, right? She wants to meet with me personally?”","Qi Tianhu vaguely remembered the president surnamed Yang mentioning something about The Young Lady before. Judging from his tone and attitude at the time, this Young Lady was probably the true leader of the Wanlong Association.","To this day, Qi Tianhu still had no idea who this mysterious Young Lady was, what she looked like, or how old she was.","But for a woman to rise to the position of head of an organization of this caliber, she clearly had to possess some ability.","Now, this mysterious Young Lady of the Wanlong Association actually wanted to meet with him in person. There seemed to be something suspicious about it.","“That’s right. President Qi, please bring the reporter to the meeting tomorrow at noon. If you are late, The Young Lady will hand the evidence directly to the police.”","“Beep... beep... beep...”","The call ended.","Qi Tianhu stared at his phone. Then, without warning, he began to laugh. The smile on his face was sinister.","“Heh... hehehe... hahaha!”","After searching high and low for so long, he had finally found what he was looking for!","He had been worrying that he couldn’t find an opportunity to wipe out the Wanlong Association in one fell swoop, and now The Young Lady of the Wanlong Association had actually dared to show herself. In that case, she could hardly blame him for showing no mercy!","Of course, he had also guessed that the other side might be setting a trap for him, but so what?","As long as they didn’t call the police and came at him head-on, there was no one he feared!","He was also certain that they wouldn’t dare call the police. Otherwise, they wouldn’t have made this call in the first place—unless they actually wanted that reporter dead.","Qi Tianhu laughed for a while before gradually sobering up and turning once again to the old brothers seated around him.","He no longer had the time or inclination to investigate who the mole was. For now, he still needed to rely on these men to avenge his son.","“I won’t pursue what happened earlier.”","The moment they heard this, everyone felt as though they had been pardoned, and they all breathed a sigh of relief.","They had genuinely feared that Qi Tianhu would lose his temper on the spot. Given his current state of mind, no one knew what he might do.","“Thank you, Lord Tiger! Thank you, Lord Tiger! We’ll certainly atone for our mistakes by rendering meritorious service!”","“That’s right! Lord Tiger, just give the word. We brothers will go through fire and water without hesitation!”","Qi Tianhu nodded. “I want you to gather all the men under your command. Then go find more people. By noon tomorrow, bring me at least another thousand men.”","“The Eldest Miss of the Wanlong Association has arranged to meet me tomorrow at the construction site in the north of the city. I’m going to wipe them all out!”","“No one is allowed to mess this up. You must get it done. Do you hear me?”","“Yes!”","“Don’t worry. I, Qi Tianhu, have never mistreated my brothers. Once this is over, each of you will receive ten million.”","“Thank you, Lord Tiger!”","Everyone accepted their orders and left.","Watching their retreating figures, Qi Tianhu revealed a cruel smile.","By then, he wanted to see what the Eldest Miss of the Wanlong Association could possibly use to withstand the assault of a thousand men when she showed up for the meeting with barely a hundred people.","Last time, she had gotten lucky. Someone had tipped her off, allowing her to mobilize reinforcements quickly.","This time, he wanted to see how she would call in help!","At the same time, he had already made up his mind: the moment this job was done, he would flee.","Following the plan he had drawn up earlier, he would first hide in the mountains, then use a smuggler at the border to take a black-market vehicle out of the country. Once abroad, he would assume a new identity and start over.","The money he had raised by frantically selling off his assets at rock-bottom prices would be more than enough to let him live in comfort for the rest of his life.","But before he ran, he had to send the Eldest Miss of the Wanlong Association down to accompany his son in death!"]},{"number":867,"title":"Chapter 867: 868, Drinking Mung Bean Soup.","paragraphs":["At eleven in the morning, the sky was dim, with layers of dark clouds pressing down over the mountaintops as if rain were about to fall.","Two kilometers from a construction site in the northern suburbs of the city, at a fork in the road, a small food stall had been set up by the roadside.","It was a tricycle converted into a mobile food stand. On it were insulated containers filled with hot rice, braised meats, several home-style dishes, and chilled mung bean soup.","The vendor was a middle-aged man in his forties or fifties named Uncle Wang. He was a local villager who made a living by riding this tricycle around construction sites on the outskirts of the city and selling boxed lunches.","Recently, Uncle Wang had been showing up at the construction site entrance every day without fail. He could sell dozens of boxed lunches in a day, which was enough to make a living.","Today, as lunchtime approached, he pedaled toward the construction site as usual.","But just after turning a bend, before he even reached the entrance, he slammed on the brakes and immediately turned around, pedaling back the way he had come.","He had not seen the workers waiting for lunch. Instead, he had seen large numbers of idle gangsters streaming toward the construction site from the direction of Jinchuan City.","Many of them were covered in tattoos, with brightly dyed hair, and were carrying steel pipes or machetes. They gathered in groups of three or five, cursing and swearing, their hostility palpable.","Before long, the abandoned construction site was packed with a sea of gang members—at least several hundred of them.","Uncle Wang had lived through most of his life and had seen his fair share of major incidents.","Back in the day, when people from Qi Tianhu’s generation were carving out their territory, street clashes and brawls had been commonplace.","But this was the first time he had ever seen so many gangsters gathered in one place.","There was no need to guess. Something major was clearly about to happen here.","Uncle Wang did not dare stay another moment. He pedaled his tricycle for dear life, covering the two kilometers back to the fork in one breath before stopping and setting up his stall again.","Business at the roadside was not as good as at the construction site, but at least passing truck drivers would buy a few meals.","While Uncle Wang squatted beside his tricycle, holding a steaming boxed lunch and shoveling rice into his mouth with braised dried tofu, two black luxury cars pulled over on the opposite side of the road.","The doors opened, and five people stepped out in succession—three women and two men, each of them carrying an extraordinary air.","Uncle Wang instinctively looked over.","The girl standing at the front looked barely twenty, yet the aura surrounding her was so imposing that people instinctively felt intimidated and dared not look directly at her.","She definitely wasn’t an ordinary person. She must be the daughter of some powerful family, he thought.","“The Young Lady, all of Qi Tianhu’s people have entered the abandoned construction site. There should be at least eight hundred of them—somewhere between eight hundred and a thousand by our estimate. They’re all carrying weapons.”","“I didn’t expect him to be able to gather so many people in such a short time, even after we sent so many of his men to the hospital over the past few days. Qi Tianhu’s foundation in Jinchuan really is quite deep.”","“They’re probably mostly small-time gangsters paid to make up the numbers. We’ve looked into the going rate around here. It’s only fifty yuan for showing up once.”","“Fifty? That’s a little cheap.”","“The Young Lady, should we head over now?”","“Zhou Ming seems to have been brought there as well. He’s apparently being held upstairs at the construction site and isn’t in any immediate danger.”","“No rush. We’ll wait until our people have all arrived.”","“Yes!”","Just then, the slightly chubby young man on the opposite side suddenly noticed the small food stall by the roadside.","His eyes lit up.","“The Young Lady, they have chilled mung bean soup!”","Only then did the girl look toward the opposite side and see the sign hanging from the stall: Chilled Mung Bean Soup.","“Then let’s go have a bowl of mung bean soup and make Qi Tianhu wait a little longer.”","“Coming right up!”","The chubby young man scampered across the road first.","The others followed.","Uncle Wang had been secretly sizing up these five extraordinary young people all along. When he saw them approaching, he quickly stood up, set down his half-eaten boxed lunch, and greeted them warmly.","“Welcome, folks! I’ve got hot rice, braised meats, home-style dishes, and chilled mung bean soup. It’s awfully hot today—how about a bowl of mung bean soup to cool you down?”","“Five bowls of mung bean soup to start!” the chubby young man said eagerly.","“Sure thing!”","Uncle Wang wiped down the two folding tables beside him with a rag, then gestured toward the stools.","“You can sit over here if you don’t mind the humble surroundings.”","“Thank you,” the girl said. She did not seem to mind at all and led the others over to sit down.","Soon, Uncle Wang brought out five bowls of chilled mung bean soup one after another.","“Enjoy, everyone. I’ve been simmering these mung beans since early this morning, and I used old-fashioned rock sugar. They’re nice and sweet.”","“Thank you, Uncle,” the girl said again.","She picked up the disposable bowl in front of her and used the spoon to take a mouthful. The air was still hot and heavy, so the cool, sweet soup felt wonderfully refreshing.","All of them drank slowly, except for the chubby young man. The moment the bowl was placed in his hands, he tipped it back and drained it in one go. Then he called out to the vendor.","“Boss, another bowl of mung bean soup!”","“And bring me two portions of that braised-meat platter too. No rice.”","Uncle Wang: “...?”","It took him a few seconds to process what the young man meant.","He only wanted the meat.","Rich people really were something else!","When the second bowl of mung bean soup and the braised-meat platter arrived, the chubby young man could hardly wait to dig in.","But just as he was about to pick up his chopsticks, a woman’s voice came from the neighboring table.","“In a moment, you’re going to run over to the construction site.”","The chubby young man’s face immediately fell.","“No, please, The Young Lady!”","“Hahaha...”"]},{"number":868,"title":"Chapter 868: 869, Oh My God","paragraphs":["After that little interlude,","the five of them chatted over bowls of mung bean soup, discussing what they would do once they entered the site.","Uncle Wang didn’t have many customers either. Selling food by the roadside was an unpredictable business, after all.","With nothing better to do, he couldn’t help pricking up his ears and listening in.","But when he heard that the five of them were planning to head to the construction site, he finally couldn’t resist offering a word of warning.","“Miss, are you girls heading to the construction site up ahead?”","The girl leading the group looked over and nodded. “Yes. Why?”","“Oh, dear, I’d advise you not to go. Things aren’t safe over there today.”","“What do you mean?”","Uncle Wang glanced around. Only after making sure no one else was nearby did he lower his voice and say, “Haven’t you noticed? A whole lot of rough-looking men have shown up today—several hundred at least. They’re all here for a fight! I’ve been selling boxed meals around here for several months, and this is the first time I’ve ever seen anything like it. Something major must be going down!”","“You young people should listen to your uncle. Don’t go looking for trouble. Finish your mung bean soup and leave as quickly as you can. If you wait too long, you may not be able to leave at all.”","The girl exchanged a glance with the others before asking curiously, “Uncle, you said there’s going to be a fight here. Which two groups are involved?”","At that, Uncle Wang’s spirits immediately lifted.","For a street vendor who roamed from place to place, his greatest hobby was chatting with people about gossip. And when it came to underworld gossip, he had plenty to share.","“Miss, judging by your accent, you’re not from around here, are you?”","“No. This is my first time in Jinchuan.”","“Then let me tell you, Jinchuan has been quite lively these past few days!”","“I heard an outside gang called the Wanlong Society came to Jinchuan to seize territory.”","“The Wanlong Society?”","“That’s right, the Wanlong Society! I’m telling you, they’re no ordinary gang. They’re an outside power—a dragon crossing the river—and they’re vicious, absolutely ruthless! A few days ago, Tiger Qi’s son—the son of the Underground Emperor of our city—well, guess what happened to him?”","“What happened?”","“He went flying out of a building! Smack! He hit the ground and became a pancake right on the spot!”","“.........”","“Is it possible the story is fake? Maybe the Wanlong Society wasn’t responsible.”","“How could it be fake? Everyone outside is saying it was the Wanlong Society! They forced him to perform a midair stunt right in front of the police. Just imagine how ruthless they must be! Who wouldn’t be terrified?”","“If the rumors are true, they do sound pretty ruthless.”","“Pretty ruthless? They’re downright vicious!”","“I’m telling you, I heard the leader of the Wanlong Society is a young woman, called The Young Lady. Tsk, tsk, tsk... For a young woman to control so many roughnecks, she must be some kind of terrifying monster!”","“I bet she has a hideous face, with blue skin, fangs, and three heads and six arms—the kind of monster that eats people without even spitting out the bones. Otherwise, how could those murderous thugs obey her?”","The girl: “.......”","The others all lowered their heads at the same time, pretending to drink their mung bean soup, while their shoulders trembled uncontrollably.","The Young Lady’s reputation was getting worse and worse!","Uncle Wang was far too engrossed in his story to notice the strange expression on the girl’s face. He continued speaking enthusiastically.","“I’m telling you, these days you can find people dressed in black all over Jinchuan. No matter where you go, you’re liable to run into them. They’re like locusts—enough to make your skin crawl. My wife sells tea eggs near the bus station, and she saw several groups of people from the Wanlong Society in just one morning. Every one of them was big and muscular, with a dragon emblem hanging on their chests. Tsk, tsk, tsk... In all my years, I’ve never seen a gang this ruthless. They’re even worse than Tiger Qi!”","“Have the people from the Wanlong Society ever bullied ordinary people like you?” the girl asked.","Uncle Wang thought for a moment, then shook his head. “Actually, they haven’t. That’s the strange part. They look like a bunch of vicious thugs, but they’ve never really harmed ordinary folks. My wife told me that while she was selling tea eggs at the bus station, a few local punks came looking for trouble. They ate all her eggs, refused to pay, and even tried to overturn her stall. Then, guess what happened? A few people from the Wanlong Society nearby came over, knocked those punks flat in no time, and afterward even asked her whether she wanted to call the police.”","“Honestly, how can they be gangsters and still act like Lei Feng and do good deeds? Now even I can’t tell whether they’re good people or bad people.”","“Maybe they aren’t gangsters at all,” the girl said.","“How could they not be?” Uncle Wang exclaimed.","“If they weren’t a gang, how could they have so many people? If they weren’t a gang, how could they have forced Qi Tiger's son to his death? Miss, you’re still too young. You don’t understand how these things work in the underworld. I heard the Wanlong Society has a powerful backer behind them—someone with an even greater background than Tiger Qi.","“Tiger Qi ruled Jinchuan for twenty years, and no one dared cross him. But the moment the Wanlong Society arrived, they took care of his son without a second thought. That’s not something an ordinary power could accomplish.”","The girl: “......”","While they were talking, a convoy appeared in the distance near the construction site.","Uncle Wang glanced toward the site and suddenly let out a surprised cry. “That’s strange. Another group has arrived. They’re wearing black, and it looks like they have badges pinned to their chests. Could they be people from the Wanlong Society?”","“Could it be that Tiger Qi and the Wanlong Society are going to fight here today?”","The convoy drove into the open area at the entrance of the construction site and came to a stop.","The car doors opened in perfect unison, and a group of young men in black suits filed out. There were quite a few of them, and they were clearly better trained than the ragtag thugs standing opposite them. The two sides weren’t even in the same league.","Uncle Wang clicked his tongue in amazement. “My goodness, that looks even more intimidating than something out of a movie. But aren’t they a little short on numbers? There are several hundred people on the other side, while this group seems to have only seventy or eighty. If they really start fighting, won’t the smaller side be at a disadvantage?”","The standoff at the construction site had already begun.","Qi Tianhu stood at the very front with several old comrades. Behind them was a dense crowd of thugs he had summoned at great expense—at least a thousand men.","Every one of them was holding a weapon: steel pipes, machetes, baseball bats, and the like.","Qi Tianhu swept his gaze over the group of men in black opposite him, a contemptuous smile curling at the corner of his mouth.","That was it?","That Yang fellow had said The Young Lady wanted to meet with him in person, yet she had brought only seventy or eighty men?","Looks like the Wanlong Society was nothing special after all!","Meanwhile, after seeing the Wanlong Society’s people arrive, Uncle Wang finally realized that a large-scale brawl was definitely about to break out.","He hurriedly began packing up his stall. As he worked, he anxiously called out to the young people beside him, “Quick, quick, quick! Miss! You need to leave right now! You can’t stay here any longer! Those two groups are about to start fighting. When this many people clash, it won’t be a joke. You could get caught in the crossfire and be seriously hurt! I need to pack up and run too!”","But just as Uncle Wang was halfway through packing up, he suddenly felt the ground beneath his feet trembling faintly.","The sound was muffled and heavy, like some enormous beast growling under its breath.","Uncle Wang instinctively turned toward the source of the noise.","A vehicle appeared on the asphalt road in the distance.","It was a black Mercedes-Benz.","Then came a second, a third, a fourth... More and more vehicles poured out from around the bend in the road, one after another.","Nearly all of them were black Mercedes-Benzes, along with a few buses. The convoy was so enormous that it stretched out like a long dragon, its tail disappearing beyond sight.","Uncle Wang’s mouth slowly fell open.","He had never seen so many expensive cars in his life. No—if he added together every luxury car he had ever seen on the streets, there still wouldn’t be as many as there were in this convoy.","Just as he stood there, stunned by the sight, the convoy stopped not far from the stall.","The doors opened in perfect unison, and large numbers of young men in black suits filed out.","Ten, fifty, a hundred, five hundred, a thousand...","A sea of black-clad figures advanced toward them, making it feel as though they had wandered into some gangster movie. Their terrifying presence weighed down on everyone so heavily that they couldn’t stop trembling, and even breathing became difficult.","Uncle Wang was scared senseless. His legs felt as though they had been filled with lead, making it nearly impossible to lift them.","When he finally came to his senses, he immediately shouted anxiously at the few customers, “Miss! Run! Hurry! If you don’t leave now, it’ll be too—”","Before he could finish, the mass of black-clad men arrived in front of his stall. In perfect unison, they bent at the waist and respectfully called out:","“Good day, Young Lady!”","“Good day, Young Lady!” × three or four thousand.","Uncle Wang felt as though the top of his skull was about to explode. He stiffly turned to look at the beautiful girl, his face filled with terror.","“You... you...”","For the life of him, he couldn’t force out another word.","Only then did he notice that the girl and the other four people all wore dragon-shaped badges on their chests, though their materials differed from those worn by the black-clad men.","The black-clad men wore mainly silver badges, while the other four wore gold-edged platinum badges. Only the girl’s badge was pure gold.","Because he had never seen badges of that color before, it had never occurred to him that they might be connected to the Ten Thousand Dragons Society.","“Uncle, your mung bean soup is delicious.”","The girl rose to her feet and gave him a slight nod before turning toward the vehicles.","The black-clad men quickly split into two lines, leaving a straight passage between them.","When the girl reached the car, one of the men had already opened the door and respectfully welcomed her inside.","Soon afterward, all the vehicles started up one after another. The black dragon began moving again, heading toward the construction site.","Uncle Wang stood as motionless as a stone statue, watching the convoy disappear into the distance.","The chubby young man carried his half-finished bowl of braised food over to Uncle Wang and joked, “Uncle, do you think our Young Lady looks like a man-eating demon?”","Uncle Wang’s inner thoughts: I was wrong! I shouldn’t have run my mouth! Please spare me!","Ma Da didn’t give him any trouble. Seeing that the convoy was getting farther and farther away without the slightest intention of stopping for him, he hurriedly grabbed his lunchbox and chased after it.","“Wait for me! I haven’t gotten in yet!”","After a while, when the convoy had finally disappeared into the distance, Uncle Wang gradually came back to his senses.","He dropped heavily onto the ground, then raised his hand and slapped himself across the face.","It was real. He wasn’t dreaming.","“Oh, my God!”"]},{"number":869,"title":"Chapter 869: 870, Both Sides Meet","paragraphs":["“Miss, all our men are in position. We can move in at any time.”","“Not yet.”","“Have everyone wait where they is. No one is to rush in without my signal. Qi Tianhu has a hostage, so we’ll get him back first.”","“Understood!”","With that, Liu Yutong got out of the vehicle with Yun Cheng, Lan Die, Yu Xin, and the others, then headed toward the construction site on foot.","The more than three thousand men behind them remained where they were.","By then, the two sides at the construction site had already been locked in a standoff for quite some time.","The first group, consisting of more than eighty men in black led by Zhao Tianyi, stood glaring at the men Qi Tianhu had brought.","The moment Liu Yutong and the others entered the construction site, more than a thousand pairs of eyes turned toward them in unison.","Judging by the situation, Qi Tianhu clearly had the numbers. Nearly a thousand men stood packed together in a dark mass, at least eight or nine hundred of them. Each carried a steel pipe, machete, or baseball bat, and every one of them looked ready for bloodshed.","At the very front of the open space sat a large square table. A copper hot pot rested on top of it, its spicy red broth bubbling and sending clouds of steam into the air.","Qi Tianhu sat behind the hot pot, casually swishing slices of mutton in the broth.","Kneeling at his feet was a man who had been bound tightly and beaten until he was covered in wounds.","It was Zhou Ming, the investigative journalist who had spent more than three months undercover at a black-coal mine. After being discovered, he had been beaten within an inch of his life.","Qi Tianhu was still dipping meat into the hot pot when he saw the group of men in black part to form a passage. Several young men and women emerged from within.","When he saw the young woman at the front, dressed in a black suit with a golden dragon emblem pinned to her chest and carrying herself with extraordinary poise, he finally set down his chopsticks and looked at her.","“You’re the Dragon Society’s Young Mistress?”","She was completely different from what he had imagined.","He had assumed that the head of the Dragon Society would be, if not some terrifying harridan, then at least a broad-faced, heavily built woman. Otherwise, how could she possibly keep all those arrogant and unruly subordinates in line?","Yet the woman standing before him looked barely twenty. Her features were delicate, and her bearing was refined. She looked nothing like a crime boss—instead, she resembled the young mistress of some wealthy, powerful family.","Liu Yutong nodded. “That’s right.”","Yun Cheng and Lan Die stood half a step behind her, guarding her on either side.","“Did you bring the things?” Qi Tianhu picked up the towel on the table, wiped his mouth, and got straight to the point.","“I did.” Liu Yutong lifted her chin slightly.","Yun Cheng stepped forward, pulled a brown paper envelope from inside his coat, and took out its contents: a stack of photographs and a USB drive. He held them up so Qi Tianhu could see them clearly.","“These are the originals. I didn’t keep any copies.”","“How do I know you didn’t make backups?” Qi Tianhu asked.","“You don’t have to believe me, but you have no choice.”","“Either release the man and I’ll give you the evidence, or I’ll hand everything over to the police and call them right now.”","The instant she said that, the entire site fell silent.","The two locked eyes, neither showing the slightest intention of backing down.","After a moment, Qi Tianhu suddenly laughed and clapped his hands.","“Good! Good! As expected of the Dragon Society’s leader. You’ve got guts!”","He then motioned directly for his men to untie the journalist.","Zhou Ming, who had been kneeling on the ground, suddenly began struggling violently. Summoning every ounce of strength he had left, he shouted toward Liu Yutong, “Don’t give it to them! The worst they can do is kill me! Take the evidence and leave! Hurry! Don’t worry about me!”","Centipede kicked him hard in the back.","Zhou Ming went sprawling, his chin striking the concrete floor. Blood sprayed from his mouth.","He let out a muffled groan, his body twitching twice as he nearly lost consciousness.","The sight instantly sent Yun Cheng and the others into a fury. They were about to attack when Liu Yutong raised a hand to stop them.","“Don’t be impulsive!”","Seeing their reaction, Qi Tianhu’s smile grew wider.","The more desperately the journalist tried to stop them, the more it proved that the evidence was genuine.","“Reporter Zhou, save your breath. You spent three months undercover and took all those pictures, but in the end, you still have to hand them over to me. If you’d known this would happen, why did you do it in the first place?”","Qi Tianhu rose to his feet and gestured toward Liu Yutong. “Miss Liu, please.”","“Untie him,” Liu Yutong said coldly.","“Untie him,” Qi Tianhu repeated.","Centipede crouched down, pulled out a knife, and cut through the ropes binding Zhou Ming.","At the same time, Yun Cheng stepped forward and placed the brown paper envelope on the square table before retreating to his original position.","Two men in black helped Zhou Ming to his feet and carried him toward the exit.","As he passed Liu Yutong, she lowered her voice and said to him, “Don’t worry. I’ll make sure every one of these men is brought to justice.”","Zhou Ming froze for a moment.","With great difficulty, he raised his battered, bloodied face and took a long look at her. His cracked lips formed two words:","“Thank you.”","Then the two men carried him out through the construction site’s entrance.","After confirming that Zhou Ming had left safely, Liu Yutong turned around and prepared to lead her people away.","“Stop!”","Qi Tianhu’s sudden shout brought them to a halt.","Liu Yutong stopped without turning around, though the corners of her lips lifted slightly in a cold smile.","“Our transaction is complete, isn’t it? Is there something else, Chairman Qi?”","“The transaction is complete, but my son’s debt still hasn’t been settled!” Qi Tianhu suddenly waved his hand.","Whoosh!","A large number of thugs poured in from all directions, surrounding Liu Yutong and the more than eighty men in black at the site.","Nearly a thousand men surrounded fewer than a hundred, leaving them no room to escape.","Liu Yutong turned around and glanced at the vicious-looking thugs before finally saying to Qi Tianhu, “You want a fight?”","“That’s right.”","Qi Tianhu spoke through clenched teeth, his voice filled with hatred. “Today, neither you nor a single one of your men will leave this place alive! The Dragon Society must pay for my son’s life in blood!”","The veteran associates behind him also revealed sinister smiles, pulling out their weapons one after another.","A thousand men against eighty. The odds were roughly fifteen to one. No matter how anyone looked at it, this was an overwhelming advantage.","They had absolute superiority.","Yet no fear appeared on Liu Yutong’s face or on the faces of the people with her. Every one of them remained perfectly calm.","That made several of Qi Tianhu’s men uneasy.","Could it be that they still had another card to play?","Liu Yutong said calmly, “You’re planning to use your numbers to bully the outnumbered, aren’t you?”","“That’s right!” Qi Tianhu replied resentfully. “I’m going to use my numbers to crush you!”","“I’m going to make sure none of you leave this place alive!”","“Qi Tianhu, are you certain you want to take this all the way?”","“You’re the one who went too far first! You killed my son!”","Liu Yutong stopped looking at him. She turned her head slightly and nodded at Yun Cheng.","Yun Cheng understood. He turned to face the entrance of the construction site and raised his right arm, making a hand signal.","Outside the entrance, everything remained quiet for roughly five seconds.","There was no reaction at all.","The thugs exchanged puzzled glances. A few even laughed, their faces full of disdain.","“He’s on the verge of death and still putting on an act—”","The sentence was cut short.","Suddenly, a voice blared through a loudspeaker from the construction site’s entrance, loud and clear.","“Everyone inside, listen up!”","“You’ve been surrounded by the Dragon Society!”","At the unexpected sound, the thugs instinctively turned toward the entrance.","The moment they looked over, every one of them was stunned.","Even Qi Tianhu, who had been certain of victory, froze with his sinister smile still plastered across his face.","Outside the construction site’s gate, the once-empty dirt road was suddenly covered by a sea of black.","Looking closely, they were all young men dressed in black suits, each wearing a silver dragon-shaped insignia on his chest. There were so many of them that their ranks stretched beyond the eye’s ability to take in.","Although it was noon, the arrival of this crowd seemed to dim the sky itself, creating the eerie impression that night was about to fall.","At the very front of the group, a chubby young man stood atop a black Mercedes-Benz. He held a megaphone in one hand and a bowl of half-finished braised-meat rice in the other as he shouted at the top of his lungs:","“Let me repeat myself! You have been surrounded by the Dragon Society!”","“Please do not put up any pointless resistance! Put your hands on your heads and squat down! The Dragon Society is a legitimate company that obeys the law. We won’t make things difficult for you. We’ll even provide you with a job that includes food and lodging!”","All the thugs at the construction site were stunned for a full second.","Obeys the law?","A legitimate company?","You’ve got at least three or four thousand men in black blocking the entrance, and you expect us to believe that? Who the hell would buy that?","Still, a job with food and lodging did sound rather tempting.","When Qi Tianhu finally came to his senses, he spun around and glared at Liu Yutong.","“What the hell are you playing at?”","Liu Yutong tilted her chin toward the construction site’s gate.","“Isn’t it obvious? It’s a matter of strength in numbers! That’s what you said just now, wasn’t it?”","“Only now, I’m the one with the numbers!”"]},{"number":870,"title":"Chapter 870: 871, Battle, Gunfire","paragraphs":["The fat on Qi Tianhu’s face twitched twice. He was left speechless.","He had always assumed that the Wanlong Association had, at most, a hundred or so men in Jinchuan. Even if they brought in reinforcements from elsewhere, he was certain they couldn’t have more than two hundred.","He had even suspected that one of his own men had betrayed him.","But now it was clear that betrayal had nothing to do with it. He had simply underestimated the Wanlong Association.","The sea of black before him contained at least three or four thousand people.","Three or four thousand!","What kind of organization was the Wanlong Association? How could it possibly have such terrifying numbers?","The old brothers behind him looked even more shaken than he did.","Some had already begun trembling uncontrollably. The knives in their hands shook, and their palms were slick with cold sweat.","“Lord Tiger, h-how the hell are we supposed to fight this?”","Qi Tianhu stared fixedly at the young woman across from him. The expression on his face gradually twisted into something vicious and crazed.","He suddenly turned around and roared at the nearly thousand thugs behind him, “Listen up! Anyone who takes down one of the Wanlong Association’s men gets a hundred thousand! Whoever cuts down that woman gets a hundred million!”","A hundred million!","The figure hit the mob like a shot of adrenaline, finally rekindling some of their fighting spirit.","Although most of them were still afraid, some had been driven half-mad by the bounty.","As the old saying went, people would die for money.","“Let’s fucking do this!”","“Charge! Cut them down!”","“That hundred million is mine!”","“...”","A chaotic roar erupted from the crowd. Some of the men raised their weapons and surged toward the mass of black-clad figures opposite them.","Yun Cheng immediately stepped half a pace forward and shielded Liu Yutong behind him. At the same time, he raised his right arm and sharply swung it down toward the entrance of the construction site.","“Go!”","One word. Clean and decisive.","At that exact moment, the more than three thousand men in black outside the gate moved.","The scene was like a black flood bursting through a breached dam, sweeping into the construction site with overwhelming force!","The thug at the very front raised his machete and brought it down. With a clang, the blade struck a black wall.","No—that wasn’t a wall. It was something resembling a riot shield, with row after row locked together to form an impenetrable barrier.","Before the attackers could react, telescopic batons came crashing down on them through the gaps between the shields.","One, two, three, fifty...","More and more thugs fell under the black-clad men’s tight coordination and relentless assault.","The battle instantly became a one-sided massacre.","Standing at the rear, Qi Tianhu watched the thousand men he had recruited at great expense collapse in heaps as if they were made of paper. His face turned green.","Then he suddenly remembered something. He grabbed Centipent’s collar and urged him, “Go! Get the thing ready!”","Centipede’s face went deathly pale. “Lord Tiger, once that thing goes off, we’ll be caught in it too...”","“I said go!”","Qi Tianhu’s eyes were bloodshot, and he had completely lost control. “If I can’t get out of here, then neither can they! At the very least, I’ll take a few of them with me!”","Seeing the almost lunatic ruthlessness in his eyes, Centipede knew there was no point trying to persuade him.","He gritted his teeth and turned toward the rear of the construction site.","At the back of the site stood an unfinished building. On the seventh floor, inside two bare-concrete rooms, five or six SWAT officers in dark blue uniforms were lying prone by the windows. Two high-precision sniper rifles and a spotting scope were set up in front of them.","“Sniper One has the target.”","“Sniper Two has the target.”","“Spotter confirms. Target has no cover.”","Commander Old Lin held up his binoculars, but his eyes were not fixed on Qi Tianhu. Instead, he was staring at the densely packed crowd outside the construction-site entrance, the corner of his mouth twitching.","“Old Li.”","“Yeah?”","“What exactly is the Wanlong Association?”","Old Li lowered his binoculars. His expression was just as difficult to describe. “The higher-ups told me it’s a legitimate private enterprise.”","“Seriously? You call this a legitimate company? What legitimate company has this many people?”","“Maybe their corporate culture is... particularly hardcore?”","“...”","“But the more I look at it, the more something feels off. Look at how badly those thugs are getting beaten. For a moment, I almost thought the thugs were the vulnerable ones. The black-clad men look more like the villains.”","“So tell me—are these people good or bad?”","Old Li looked out the window. The black-clad men were pinning the thugs to the ground one by one, expertly binding their wrists with zip ties. They even searched the men as they went, confiscating their illegal knives and arranging them in a pile nearby.","The entire cleanup operation was frighteningly efficient, almost as efficient as a SWAT operation.","The SWAT team’s appearance here today had been coordinated with the Wanlong Association in advance. They had two main objectives.","First, rescue the reporter.","They were worried that sending the police in directly might trigger a desperate reaction. If the kidnappers knew they were going to die, they might kill the hostage. So in the end, they went with the plan proposed by Lawyer Zhao of the Wanlong Association: exchange counterfeit evidence for the reporter.","Why did they think this rescue method had a higher chance of success? Because compared with the reporter, Qi Tianhu cared more about the Wanlong Association.","That was how today’s situation had come about.","Second, restrain Qi Tianhu and capture him alive if possible.","Originally, when these SWAT officers saw Qi Tianhu’s forces, they had been extremely shocked. They had even contacted the armed police to come in and finish the operation.","There were simply too many people. Ordinary police officers would never have been enough.","But unexpectedly, the Wanlong Association turned out to be the truly ruthless side!","They had brought several times the manpower of the gangsters—more intimidating than an actual criminal organization.","A moment later, Old Li finally spoke.","“I’m not sure whether they’re good people, but there’s one thing I know for certain now.”","“What’s that?”","“From now on, in BS Province, never provoke the Wanlong Association.”","Old Lin nodded in deep agreement.","Just then, the spotter’s voice suddenly came through the earpiece.","“Report! Qi Tianhu’s trusted aide, Centipede, is moving toward the unfinished building on the west side of the construction site. His movements are suspicious!”","Old Lin immediately raised his binoculars and scanned the western side.","A man with a centipede tattoo on his arm was crouching as he slipped away from the melee. Keeping close to the base of the wall, he ran toward the unfinished building.","He was moving quickly, glancing back from time to time as if checking whether anyone was following him.","“Keep him under close watch,” Old Lin ordered in a low voice.","“Yes, sir!”","The spotter’s camera locked tightly onto Centipede.","When the man reached the rear of the unfinished building, he crouched down and pulled a dark green canvas bag from beneath a pile of broken bricks. He unzipped it, revealing bundle after bundle of explosive tubes and detonators.","“Report! Suspected explosives discovered! Repeat, suspected explosives discovered! Large quantities of industrial explosives and detonators located behind the unfinished building on the west side. Target is at the scene!”","Old Lin’s heart sank. He cursed, “That bastard Qi has gone insane! He’s planning to take everyone down with him!”","“Snipers One and Two, prepare to fire! Do not let him detonate them!”","“Sniper One copies!”","“Position Two, I’m in position!”","Centipede crouched on the ground, his hands trembling as he connected the detonator wires.","He didn’t want to die, but he didn’t dare disobey orders. After all, he and Qi Tianhu were in the same boat now. If he refused, he knew he would meet a terrible end.","But just as he connected the final wire and was about to get up and leave with the detonator...","Bang! Bang!","Two gunshots rang out across the construction site.","Without warning, Centipede’s hand froze in midair. A bloody hole appeared in his chest.","The next second, the detonator slipped from his grasp and hit the ground, rolling a long way away.","He touched the blood running from his forehead, then slowly lowered his head to look at the fresh hole in his chest. His lips moved a few times, as if he wanted to say something.","Then his entire body pitched forward, face-first onto the ground. He lay motionless, completely devoid of life."]},{"number":871,"title":"Chapter 871: 872, The Dragon Alliance Got Blacklisted Again","paragraphs":["The gunshot came far too suddenly.","Before anyone had time to react—","Bang!","Another shot rang out.","The sniper’s bullet once again struck Qi Tianhu’s right shoulder with pinpoint accuracy.","The Underground Emperor who had ruled Jin River’s underworld for twenty years jerked backward. He staggered two steps and crashed into the Eight Immortals table behind him.","The copper hot pot flipped over, spilling scalding red oil all over him. White smoke hissed up from his skin.","“Ahhh!”","Qi Tianhu let out a heart-rending scream and rolled desperately across the ground.","The sniper had been ordered to wound, not kill. A living Qi Tianhu was far more valuable than a dead one. There were still countless unsolved crimes tied to him, and once he was dead, no one would be able to get anything out of him.","The hundreds of thugs at the construction site heard the three consecutive gunshots. When they saw their boss shot and knocked down, panic instantly spread through their ranks, and their morale completely collapsed.","A gun!","They had a gun!","That bunch from the Wanlong Society actually had a sniper rifle!","Damn it, how were they supposed to fight that?","Everyone in the underworld knew how strictly guns were controlled in this country.","Even a big shot like Qi Tianhu, who dominated an entire region, didn’t possess a firearm. He had merely acquired some industrial explosives through his coal-mine connections. He had originally planned to use them to take everyone down with him if he couldn’t escape.","But those thugs had never imagined that, in broad daylight and in front of nearly a thousand people, the Wanlong Society would actually shoot their boss with a sniper rifle.","A sniper rifle! That wasn’t some handgun!","Just how powerful was the backing of the Wanlong Society?","They had connections all the way to the top, didn’t they?","After a brief moment of panic, someone suddenly shouted:","“Don’t kill me! Don’t kill me! I surrender!”","The entire construction site immediately descended into chaos.","The thugs who were still standing threw down whatever weapons they had. Steel pipes, machetes, baseball bats—all of them clattered onto the ground.","Everyone hurriedly crouched down with their hands over their heads. Some were so terrified that they dropped to their knees, wailing and begging for mercy.","“Please spare me, boss! Please! I was only paid to stand around and make up the numbers. This has nothing to do with me!”","“Don’t kill me! I was forced into this! Tiger Qi made us come! I’ve got an eighty-year-old mother and a three-year-old kid to support!”","“I was wrong! I really was! I’ll never get involved with society again! I’ll turn over a new leaf, reform myself, and become a good person!”","“Exactly! Me too! We’ll all turn over a new leaf!”","“.........”","One of the gang leaders kneeling at the very front looked up at the black-clad man before him with tears streaming down his face. He begged sincerely, “Big brother, to be honest, I’ve had a dream since I was a kid—to join the Wanlong Society and make my way in the underworld alongside you....”","The black-clad man: “.....”","“Big brother, I’ve always wanted to find a respectable job. That job you mentioned just now—the one that provides food and lodging—is it still available?”","“I... I want a job with food and lodging too!”","“Please take me in! I don’t mind cleaning toilets!”","“Plus one!”","“Plus a thousand!”","“.....”","Liu Yutong stood where she was, the corner of her mouth twitching.","Ma Da came trotting over to her, carrying the bowl of braised-meat rice that had nearly gone cold. With a grin, he asked, “Miss, what should we do with these people?”","Liu Yutong said, “Naturally, we’ll fulfill their requests and send them somewhere with food and lodging.”","“Yes, miss!”","Ma Da set the lunch box aside, turned around, and grabbed a loudspeaker. He shouted at the group of thugs, “Quiet down, all of you! We heard your requests! The Wanlong Society always keeps its word. Since we said we’d provide you with food and lodging, then that’s exactly what we’ll do! Not a single one of you will be left out!”","The thugs were instantly moved to tears by their good fortune.","“Thank you, brothers of the Wanlong Society!”","“Long live the Wanlong Society!”","“Long live Miss!”","“.....”","Ma Da nodded in satisfaction, then turned back to Liu Yutong. “See, miss? They’re even thanking us.”","Liu Yutong: “...”","...........","At the fork in the road.","Uncle Wang hadn’t gone far. His three-wheeled cart was still parked behind the crooked tree by the roadside.","Actually, he had wanted to run just now. But when that terrifying convoy of black vehicles passed right in front of him, his legs had felt as if they’d been filled with cement. He couldn’t move at all.","After the convoy had disappeared into the distance, he crouched behind his cart for a long while before finally coming to his senses.","Run?","What was he running for? The people from the Wanlong Society hadn’t done anything to him.","Their miss had even praised his mung bean soup.","Although Uncle Wang was still somewhat shaken, his curiosity eventually overcame his fear.","He pushed his three-wheeled cart behind the crooked tree and hid it there, then crept toward the battlefield and began secretly observing from nearby.","He was too far away to make out the details, but he could see the mass of dark figures surging into the construction site. He could also hear faint cries of battle and screams drifting over.","The fight must have been spectacular—and brutal.","“My goodness, they’re really going at it.”","Uncle Wang nervously swallowed as he watched, completely absorbed. Suddenly, he heard two muffled booms.","The sounds were dull and brief, like something had exploded—or someone had set off an especially loud firecracker.","Then another one followed.","After that, the construction site fell silent.","The silence was unnaturally complete.","Uncle Wang pricked up his ears and listened for a moment. Then he suddenly realized what he had heard, and his face went deathly pale.","A gun!","Damn it, those were gunshots!","Back when Uncle Wang was young, guns hadn’t been so strictly controlled. In fact, he himself had used a gun to hunt when he was younger.","But that had been many years ago. These days, how many people in the country dared to use a gun?","Yet today, he had not only witnessed a massive battle involving thousands of people—he had also heard gunshots. And they hadn’t come from an ordinary handgun or hunting rifle.","They sounded somewhat like the sniper rifles he had heard on television.","The realization terrified him. He immediately shrank back behind a large tree and didn’t dare poke his head out again.","It wasn’t long before dozens of police cars came racing over in the distance, sirens blaring, and stopped at the entrance to the construction site.","Several military-green trucks arrived right behind them. A group of armed paramilitary police jumped out and quickly cordoned off the entire perimeter.","Uncle Wang finally dared to stick his head out again. He felt somewhat relieved as well. With the police and paramilitary officers there, at least he didn’t have to worry about his safety.","But his curiosity began stirring once more. He simply couldn’t hold it back. He quietly slipped out from behind the tree, hunched low, and followed the ditch along the roadside for more than a hundred meters. Finally, he lay down at the edge of the ditch and peered toward the construction site.","What he saw next was astonishing. By sheer coincidence, he witnessed the two most crucial scenes.","The first scene: A group of bruised and battered thugs were being marched out of the construction site by the Wanlong Society’s black-clad men. Their hands were bound with plastic zip ties, one after another, like candied hawthorn skewered on a stick. They were then handed over to the police waiting at the entrance.","As the black-clad leader handed them over to the officer in charge, the officer even nodded at him and seemed to say something.","Based on their lip movements, expressions, and the direction of the conversation, Uncle Wang made a rough guess.","Police: “You’ve worked hard. We’ll take it from here.”","Man in Black: We’re all on the same side. No need to be so formal.","The second scene: Two armed police officers carried a stretcher out of the construction site. A white sheet covered it, concealing the shape of a person beneath.","Uncle Wang lay facedown in the ditch, his head buzzing.","He was dead.","Someone had really died.","And he still hadn’t seen any sign of Qi Tianhu. Could it be that he...","“My God!”","..........","That evening, at a teahouse in Jinchuan’s old town, Uncle Wang sat surrounded by more than a dozen old buddies, spittle flying as he recounted everything he had seen that day.","His friends gasped in astonishment as they listened.","Before long, those embellished stories sprouted wings and spread through every street and alley in Jinchuan.","The Wanlong Society had opened fire. Tiger Qi and his centipede-tattooed lieutenant were both dead.","Tiger Qi and his son were all gone, and nearly every notable thug in Jin​​chuan’s underworld had been wiped out in one fell swoop.","The Wanlong Society had connections with the police. Of course, those who understood, understood.","But most importantly, the Wanlong Society was absolutely untouchable. They were the true Underground Emperor!","That was dark!"]},{"number":872,"title":"Chapter 872: 873, Dust Settles (Thanks to Jin Pengshi's Great God Certification.)","paragraphs":["The situation in BS Province had finally been brought to a complete close after the heart-stopping battle at the construction site.","Qi Tianhu had been captured after taking a bullet to the right shoulder. His trusted lieutenant, Centipede, was shot dead on the spot by a sniper who had been lying in wait at a commanding position when he attempted to detonate the industrial explosives.","The man who had ruled Jinchuan with an iron fist for twenty years—the Underground Emperor—had ultimately brought his reign to a brutal end.","Following the trail, the police sealed all the illegal coal mines under the Qi family’s name in one fell swoop and rescued dozens of people with intellectual disabilities who had been illegally detained and enslaved as forced laborers.","Unfortunately, Wang Xiaoshu’s older brother, Wang Dashu, was still missing, with his fate unknown.","That was the only regret Liu Yutong carried in her heart throughout the entire affair.","Over the following week, Liu Yutong represented the Wanlong Association Group in signing several in-depth cooperation agreements with the authorities of BS Province.","The mining rights to Qingyan Mountain’s lithium deposits were formally finalized. The Wanlong Association Group, Zhang Mining, Xie Group, and the state-owned assets of BS Province would jointly invest in and establish a company called Longchuan Lithium.","The first phase of investment would reach five billion yuan, with mass production expected to begin within two years.","Wanlong Aerospace also officially finalized the location of an assembly and launch base somewhere in BS Province.","Construction on Wanlong Plaza projects in Jinchuan, Jingchuan, and several other prefecture-level cities resumed in full. In addition, two major projects—a logistics hub and an agricultural products deep-processing base—were added to the plans. The local government held three special coordination meetings for them, clearing every possible obstacle and giving the projects the green light all the way.","Before leaving, Liu Yutong arranged a private meeting with Professor Xu Yangeng.","The elderly professor, who had been frightened half to death in the apartment blocks, seemed to have shed an entire layer of himself after everything he had been through. He had grown noticeably thinner, yet his spirits were better than ever.","Liu Yutong kept her promise. On the spot, she signed an eight-million-yuan check to provide the initial funding for his battery project.","She also made her requirements clear: he was to begin with smartphone battery research and proceed step by step. He could not expect to swallow the whole elephant in one bite. In scientific research, the greatest taboo was aiming too high without a solid foundation.","She further required Xu Yangeng to produce a viable business plan and a report on his progress within two months. As long as the work was solid, she would provide at least another fifty million yuan in funding.","Xu Yangeng’s hands trembled as he accepted the check.","But this time, it was not out of fear. It was excitement.","His wife, Zhou Wanqing, and their daughter, Xu Yi, were moved to tears as well.","Their years of suffering had finally come to an end.","As for Zhou Ming, the investigative journalist who had spent three months undercover in the illegal coal mines, he was sent to the best hospital in Jinchuan, with all his medical expenses covered by the government.","This had been a directive from the higher authorities, who wanted to hold him up as an exemplary figure.","Liu Yutong even offered him five million yuan in recognition under her personal name, but he refused without the slightest hesitation.","Instead, he made a request that both surprised Liu Yutong and did not surprise her at all: he wanted his family relocated to Pearl City.","Liu Yutong immediately understood his intentions.","Zhou Ming was clearly afraid of retaliation. He had offended too many people. Even though many of them had been arrested, there was no guarantee that they—or their associates—would not seek revenge after being released. And they might target not only him, but his family as well.","The headquarters of the Wanlong Association Group was in Pearl City. People like the intimidating men in black Zhou Ming had seen were everywhere there, making it a much safer place.","He did not want money. He only wanted to exchange it for his family’s safety.","Liu Yutong agreed without a second thought.","Not only did she agree, but she also promised to provide his family with a four-bedroom apartment worth roughly one million yuan and guarantee their safety.","She even told him that he was not allowed to refuse again.","In the end, the tough-as-nails journalist accepted the kindness with tears streaming down his face.","With that, the cleanup work in BS Province was finally complete.","In late September, Liu Yutong flew back to Pearl City with Yun Cheng, Lan Die, and the others.","More than a thousand core members of the Wanlong Association who had distinguished themselves in the Battle of Jinchuan returned with her.","The group booked out Pearl City’s largest hotel for a grand welcome banquet for everyone who had taken part in the battle.","Ma Da drank until his face was bright red. Standing on a chair with a glass in hand, he regaled the newly inducted brothers with every detail of the Battle of Jinchuan, spraying spittle everywhere as he spoke. At the most exciting part of the story, he misstepped and nearly fell off the chair. Wine splashed all over him, prompting a roar of laughter from the entire banquet hall.","After returning to Pearl City, Liu Yutong rested for only one day before throwing herself back into her studies and work.","Her junior year had already begun. Although she held the titles of honorary professor and distinguished alumnus at the University of Finance and Economics, she still had to attend her classes. Fortunately, the university president had made a special exception, allowing her to arrange her schedule flexibly.","Thankfully, the structures of the six major business groups were already operating smoothly. Each group’s president was handling their own responsibilities, and there were far fewer matters requiring Liu Yutong’s personal approval than before.","During the National Day holiday, Liu Yutong took her grandparents and Yaya to the capital, fulfilling the two elderly people’s long-held wishes to see Tiananmen Square and climb the Great Wall.","Yaya had now started first grade. She was doing extremely well in school, especially in mathematics, where she displayed astonishing talent.","First-grade problems had long since ceased to pose any challenge to her. She could already solve complicated word problems normally taught in third or fourth grade, and she performed multiplication and division faster than many third- and fourth-graders.","This unexpected discovery strengthened Liu Yutong’s resolve to nurture the little girl’s mathematical abilities.","After spending several relaxing days in the capital, Liu Yutong once again settled into the rhythm of school and work, moving between the two with unwavering consistency.","The Wanlong Association Group continued to grow steadily and rapidly at the same pace.","Time flew by. Before anyone knew it, the end of 2009 had arrived.","Before the annual meeting officially began, Liu Yutong summoned the presidents and core executives of the various business groups to the large conference room on the forty-eighth floor of Shunchang Tower. There, she held a product strategy meeting to prepare for the market battles ahead.","More than three months had passed since the group’s last restructuring conference. During that time, the Wanlong Association Group’s six major business groups had completed an intensive period of integration. Their various business lines were gradually getting on track, and the benefits of cooperation were beginning to emerge. Meetings and administrative affairs were also being handled more efficiently.","Liu Yutong sat at the head of the conference table.","Present were Yang Xin, president of the Commercial Consumer Retail Group; Yu Xin, president of the Technology Group; Zhang Dalong, president of the Digital Group; Lin Muyang, president of the Entertainment and Media Group; Xu Shishi, president of the Supply Chain and Logistics Group; and Su Mansu, vice president of the Finance and Investment Group.","All six leaders were present, along with Ma Da, head of human resources; Chu Yang, head of security; Yun Cheng and Lan Die, Liu Yutong’s special assistants; Qiu Ciyun, CEO of Longxin Semiconductor; Zhao Tianyi, head of Tianyi Law Firm; and the other attendees.","Everyone was there.","“I called everyone here today mainly to bring you up to date on the progress of each division and discuss our key plans for the coming year.”","“Yu Xin, you go first.” Liu Yutong gestured to Yu Xin.","Yu Xin stood up and opened the laptop in front of her, projecting its display onto the large screen behind her.","A rendering of a mobile phone appeared on the screen.","The phone’s black body featured clean, angular lines, with subtly rounded corners that softened its otherwise crisp, businesslike look.","Its screen-to-body ratio couldn’t match the razor-thin bezels of the full-screen era that would come later, but in 2009, the display was already impressive enough to turn heads.","The most eye-catching detail was the circular physical button beneath the screen—smooth, prominent, and unmistakable. On the upper center of the back sat the camera and flash, along with an especially striking dragon logo.","The dragon had been adapted from a Chinese character. It looked both imposing and beautiful.","Apart from the few people who had known about it in advance, everyone present froze for a moment when they saw the design.","Not because it was ugly, but because it looked strangely familiar."]},{"number":873,"title":"Chapter 873: 874, Patent Advantage. (Thanks to Raiden Ei, a senior homebody from Inazuma, for the Grandmaster certification)","paragraphs":["“Sister Yutong, everyone, this is the finalized exterior design for the first-generation prototype of Longyao Mobile.” As she spoke, Yu Xin advanced through the PPT, displaying more details of the phone.","“Isn’t this design a little too similar to... well, you know?” Yang Xin hesitated before voicing the question on everyone’s mind.","“You mean an iPhone?”","Yang Xin nodded.","“A few days ago, I saw some leaks online. Aside from the logo, our phone looks almost exactly like the new iPhone shown in the leaked photos. General Manager Yu, can you explain that?”","Yu Xin smiled. “It’s very simple. The exterior design patent for Longyao’s first-generation phone was registered before the iPhone 4’s exterior design patent.”","Her words were shocking.","For a moment, everyone in the meeting room thought they had misheard her.","What did she mean, their phone’s exterior design patent had been registered before the iPhone 4?","Did she mean what they thought she meant?","Seeing the confusion on everyone’s faces, Yu Xin smiled and said, “Yes, it means exactly what you think it means. Literally.”","“Hiss...”","Everyone’s eyes lit up.","Now this was interesting. Very interesting.","Back when Liu Yutong had chosen to have someone register the phone’s exterior design patent, she hadn’t told anyone about it.","Yu Xin had only found out after taking over the phone project. Sister Yutong had actually prepared the phone’s design drawings long in advance.","At first, Yu Xin hadn’t paid much attention. She had assumed Sister Yutong simply wanted to give the first-generation phone a distinctive appearance.","That was, until the leaked photos of the iPhone 4 began circulating online.","She was stunned.","Sister Yutong really was something else. She had somehow known the iPhone 4’s exterior design ahead of time.","Even more astonishingly, when had Sister Yutong planted a mole inside Apple? Not a single member of the Wanlong Society, including those close to Yu Xin, had known about it.","It was simply incredible.","What was even more amazing was that they had managed to register the exterior design patent before Apple had even finalized its own design.","It was nothing short of a divine move.","Yu Xin could already imagine the enormous media storm that would erupt next year when the iPhone 4 was officially released and collided head-on with Longyao’s first-generation phone.","“Holy crap! Our phone’s exterior design patent was registered before the iPhone 4’s! That’s insane!”","“I’m suddenly looking forward to Apple’s launch event next year.”","“Same here!”","“Plus one...”","The meeting room erupted with excitement.","This was Apple they were talking about—one of the hottest technology companies in the world in recent years. Ever since the release of its first-generation phone, the company had attracted countless eyes. The entire industry was holding its breath, waiting for the next revolutionary product.","After leaks of the iPhone 4’s exterior design surfaced, who knew how many people had already prepared their money and were waiting for the phone to be released?","Everyone present was an experienced businessperson. They all knew what this exterior design patent meant.","It meant that if Apple wanted to enter the domestic market, it would have to either obediently pay licensing fees, change the phone’s design and start over, or face Apple’s day in court and risk having the phone forcibly banned from sale.","Any of those options would be a devastating blow to Apple.","Paying licensing fees would mean admitting that it had copied someone else’s design.","Changing the exterior would mean that an entire year of preparation had gone to waste. There would also be the problem of what to do with all the phones that had already been manufactured.","And if the phones were banned from sale, the losses would be equally enormous.","“General Manager Yu, did you only register the basic shell design, or did you also...” Yang Xin couldn’t help pressing for details.","“Domestically, we registered every exterior design element we could think of. That includes the rounded-rectangle body, the single physical button on the front, the arrangement of the rear camera and flash, the layout of the side buttons, the symmetrical openings on the bottom, and even the flip-top structure of the packaging box. We registered all of it.”","“Overseas, we also applied for exterior design patents through offshore companies in the major markets, covering the key countries and regions across both the Eastern and Western continents.”","“How much did it cost?”","“The patent application fees themselves weren’t particularly high. The real expense came from the breadth of the patent strategy and from defining the scope of protection for every individual detail. That required the legal and design teams to repeatedly discuss and refine everything.”","“The total cost was roughly twenty million.”","When they heard that it had cost only twenty million, everyone in the room could no longer sit still. They began exclaiming that the money had been incredibly well spent.","What was twenty million?","Once the iPhone 4 was released, the licensing fees or compensation alone could amount to tens of billions.","To give everyone a more direct sense of the differences—or rather, the similarities—between the iPhone 4 and Longyao’s first-generation phone, Yu Xin switched the presentation to a comparison image.","On the left was a rendering of the Longyao phone. On the right were several leaked photos of Apple’s new phone, collected from various sources.","The two images were placed side by side. They couldn’t simply be described as similar. Once the logos were covered, they were practically identical—even the curvature of the buttons and the number, spacing, and arrangement of the openings on the bottom matched perfectly.","“Interesting. This is really interesting.”","“Then can’t we strike first? The moment Apple dares to release its new phone, we can sue them for infringement. We’d have the upper hand in the court of public opinion from the very beginning.” Lin Muyang was visibly eager to make a move.","Zhao Tianyi nodded. “It’s not just a matter of suing them for infringement. Exterior design patents fall under the category of industrial design patents, and their protection period is roughly ten years. If Apple releases a product with an exterior design that substantially overlaps with our patent without knowing about it, we can apply to the court for an injunction prohibiting them from selling the infringing product in the relevant markets. If that injunction is granted, it will deal them a devastating blow.”","“Most importantly, Apple’s great myth will be shattered overnight. Jobs would never tolerate having his reputation ruined.”","“I’m really looking forward to seeing the expression on his face when he finds out he copied someone else’s design! Hahaha...”","In China, exterior design patents generally undergo only a preliminary examination. They are not subjected to a substantive search. As long as the application meets the formal requirements, it is approved.","Only when two patents come into conflict do the authorities go back and determine which one was filed first. For exterior design patents, priority is determined by the application date. The rights of the patent filed earlier take precedence.","Even in the West, there is a patent examination period during which related patents cannot be found through searches.","Liu Yutong had also made arrangements in this regard. Not only had she arranged for the patent examination period to be extended, she had deliberately filed the exterior design patent under other classifications rather than under mobile phones.","It was an especially underhanded move.","When Apple’s lawyers handled patent registration, they would normally search databases related to mobile-phone patents. But if the design patent wasn’t filed under the mobile-phone category, they could turn the database upside down and still never find it.","They would have to search in completely unrelated fields before they had any chance of uncovering this exterior-design “bomb.”","So Apple was bound to step on the land mine.","Of course, even if Liu Yutong had registered the patent overseas in advance, that did not necessarily mean they would be able to do anything to Apple.","After all, things are different at home and abroad.","“Domestic matters are easy enough to handle, but what about overseas?” Yang Xin happened to raise the key question.","“The rules overseas are different. When it comes down to it, the intellectual property litigation environment in those countries is influenced by politics, and they’re experts at playing dirty. My suggestion is that we enforce the restrictions domestically for the short term, while completely opening things up overseas. Unless they stop suppressing our products and chips, we can freely license the design patents to them as a bargaining chip.”","“That’s what you call making progress together!” Zhao Tianyi said with a laugh.","“I think that works.” Zhang Dalong was the first to voice his support.","“I agree,” Ma Da said with a nod.","“Agreed!”","“Agreed +1.”","“...”"]},{"number":874,"title":"Chapter 874: 875. Progress of Various Business Operations.","paragraphs":["Liu Yutong nodded slightly and continued, “Yu Xin, go on with the phone itself.”","Yu Xin acknowledged her. She tapped a key on her laptop, and the projected presentation switched to the next slide.","“In terms of specifications, the first-generation Longyao phone is positioned in the mid- to high-end market. It uses a 3.7-inch capacitive touchscreen with a resolution of 480×800, and is powered by the LX-A1 chip developed by Longxin. Based on the ARM architecture, it has a clock speed of 800 MHz and integrates a PowerVR SGX530 graphics processor. It comes with 512 MB of RAM and starts with 8 GB of storage.”","“The operating system is Long OS, a heavily customized system based on the Android 2.2 kernel. We redesigned the entire user interface and added several signature features, including smart dialing, spam-call blocking, data-usage monitoring, and app-permission management. None of these features are available in stock Android at present.”","“As for the cameras, the rear camera has five megapixels and autofocus, while the front camera has 0.3 megapixels and supports video calls.”","“The battery has a capacity of 1,800 milliamp-hours. We got a late start in the battery sector, so we still need to catch up. For now, we’re using a new type of imported polymer lithium battery from overseas. Under normal use, it can last up to a day and a half.”","“We’ve kept the total manufacturing cost to around 2,000 yuan, and the preliminary retail price is set at 2,999 yuan.”","“2,999?”","Yang Xin looked surprised. “That’s much cheaper than Fruit’s phone. Will the profit margin be enough?”","“Absolutely.”","Yu Xin nodded confidently. “We developed the chip ourselves, and Longxin is supplying it to us at cost plus five percent. The screens and camera modules are being purchased in bulk through our supply chain, and we’ve already established good relationships with the suppliers. At a price of 2,999 yuan, our gross margin should be around twenty percent. If sales pick up later, we’ll be able to push the cost down even further.”","Liu Yutong was quite satisfied with the pricing.","In her memory, the mainland version of the Fruit 4 had started at 4,999 yuan. It had been nearly impossible to get hold of one, and scalpers routinely sold them for seven or eight thousand yuan.","If the Longyao phone could launch before the Fruit 4, offer comparable hardware at nearly half the price, and—most importantly—if Fruit was the one copying their design, what kind of reaction would the market have?","The answer was obvious.","The only weakness might be that its system experience would be slightly inferior.","But the system could be improved through updates. The most important thing was to seize the window of opportunity by launching first.","“Have we set a date for the launch event?”","“Provisionally, it’s scheduled for the day after Fruit’s launch event. The domestic event will be held at the National Convention Center in the Imperial Capital, while the overseas launch will take place in Silicon Valley, Beautiful Country.”","“Also, we’ve already finalized our overseas distribution channels. In the Western markets, we’ll distribute through Voda’s partner network. In the Eastern Continent markets, we’ll be working with the Xie family’s conglomerate in Harbor City, which has highly developed distribution channels throughout the surrounding countries.”","“Good work.”","Liu Yutong nodded approvingly, then turned her attention to Qiu Ciyun. “President Qiu, how are things progressing on the chip side?”","Qiu Ciyun was the CEO of Longxin Semiconductor.","Strictly speaking, Longxin was an independent company outside the Wanlong Group. However, because the two sides needed to cooperate closely in areas such as custom development for mobile-phone chips and production-capacity coordination, Liu Yutong had simply invited him to this meeting. It would also give him a more comprehensive understanding of the resources currently under the Wanlong Association Group’s control.","“Chairwoman, development of the 65-nanometer process is about a month ahead of schedule.”","“We completed our first wafer-fabrication test last month, achieving a yield rate of seventy-one percent. Although that’s still a long way from the yield rate of our 90-nanometer line, it’s an excellent start. We expect the yield to exceed eighty-five percent by the second half of next year, at which point we’ll be able to begin small-scale production.”","“That fast?”","“It’s all thanks to the talent you recruited from overseas, Chairwoman.”","“Especially the few lithography experts brought in from Mudland. Their experience with immersion lithography has been an enormous help to our R&D team.”","The matter traced back several months. Through Wei Xiao’s overseas security channels, she had secretly recruited a group of top chip-manufacturing experts from the West and Taiwan Province.","Some had come from ASML, some from Applied Materials, and others from Taiji Electronics and Two-Star. Without exception, they were seasoned experts in their respective fields.","As for how they had been recruited, naturally, it had not been through the usual work-visa channels.","Some things simply weren’t suitable for discussion in public.","Besides the talent, Jesse had also played a major role.","Using his identity, Liu Yutong had acquired two lithography-machine component companies overseas. Although neither company was particularly large, both possessed several core patents related to immersion lithography. They had played a crucial role in Longxin’s technological breakthroughs.","“I’m sure everyone here understands what achieving 65-nanometer technology means.”","“With a 65-nanometer process, we can achieve greater chip integration, lower power consumption, and stronger performance. The chips for the second- and third-generation Longyao phones can be designed using 65-nanometer—or even more advanced—processes. By then, the gap between us and the international leaders will shrink even further.”","“What about 45 nanometers?”","“Preliminary research into the 45-nanometer process has already begun, but progress will be slow for now because of limitations on core equipment such as lithography machines.”","“The most advanced lithography machines currently in our possession can only handle 65 nanometers. To break through to 45 nanometers, we’ll need more advanced equipment, and that kind of equipment is currently subject to a comprehensive embargo against us,” Qiu Ciyun said honestly.","Liu Yutong nodded. “We’ll find a way to deal with the equipment situation. There’s no need to rush.”","She knew full well that, in the field of lithography, it was unrealistic to rely entirely on independent research and development to overtake the world through a shortcut in such a short period of time. Merely keeping pace and avoiding falling behind would already be a blessing.","But Liu Yutong had never been the type to obediently stand in line and wait for others to offer her charity.","If the normal channels wouldn’t work, she would continue using unconventional methods.","The lithography-machine manufacturing company she had originally acquired was already being transferred bit by bit through an “ants moving a mountain” strategy. Before long, its core technologies and equipment would be moved entirely into the country.","At the same time, after Jesse joined the Dark Phoenix Society, he received nearly ten billion yuan in funding from her. By continually pouring money into the effort, he helped her acquire the relevant technology and equipment.","But all of this had to be done in secret, and the window of opportunity was limited.","She had estimated that this route would be completely cut off within at most three or four years.","So she could only remain patient and move as much as possible back home before relations deteriorated further on every front.","“Next, Zhang Dalong, Digital Business Group.”","“Understood, Chairwoman!”","Zhang Dalong immediately opened his PowerPoint presentation.","As a former top talent from Big Goose, Zhang Dalong’s experience and capabilities in the field of instant messaging were unquestionably among the top three in the country.","Liu Yutong had recruited him in the first place precisely because of his deep understanding of mobile internet communication tools.","“Chairwoman, everyone, WeChat’s internal testing has now completed two rounds. At present, thirty thousand employees across the Wanlong Group are conducting hands-on testing, and the feedback has been excellent.”","As Zhang Dalong spoke, he projected screenshots of WeChat’s interface onto the large screen.","The interface was extremely simple, with only three tabs at the bottom: Chats, Contacts, and Discover.","Compared with the flashy QQ from Goose Inc., WeChat was practically a breath of fresh air.","There were no splash-screen advertisements, no confusing collection of value-added services, no forced system notifications—not even a membership-level system. He had cut all of that out.","“We’ve focused on developing several core features for WeChat.”","“First, a social network built around users’ existing mobile contacts. After registering for WeChat, users can add friends directly through their phone numbers instead of having to memorize a string of digits. The experience is far better than QQ.”","“Second, voice messages. This is WeChat’s biggest innovation. Users can press a button to record and send a voice message of up to sixty seconds. There’s no need to type, which frees up both hands. During internal testing, voice messages accounted for more than forty percent of all messages sent, making them the most popular feature so far.”","“Of course, this feature has its drawbacks as well. It consumes a considerable amount of data, and many users may not be able to accept a sudden surge in their phone bills. We’ll need the chairwoman to negotiate with the country’s three major telecom operators and see whether they can launch dedicated data plans.”","Liu Yutong said, “Don’t worry about that. I’ve already started working on it through my connections. It won’t take long to resolve.”","In 2009, and even for several years afterward, as smartphones gradually became more widespread, mobile data fees were indeed a major pain point. Without a data package, one megabyte of data could cost around ten yuan—an outrageously high price.","If that issue wasn’t resolved, WeChat would be seriously affected later on.","Fortunately, it was no longer a particularly difficult problem for Liu Yutong. She only needed to reach an agreement with one of the three major telecom operators. Naturally, she would also consider subsidizing users’ data costs. It would burn a great deal of money in the short term, but once economies of scale took effect, and data prices eventually fell, it would no longer be a concern.","“Good. Then I’ll continue with the next feature.”","“Third, we’ve also experimented with social entertainment features. We’ve added Drift Bottle and Shake. Users can shake their phones to match with strangers who happen to be shaking theirs at the same time, or they can meet people at random by tossing out a virtual drift bottle. During internal testing, the usage rates of these two features weren’t particularly high, but user retention was impressive. Most people who tried them once came back for a second time.”","“Besides that, we’re also exploring a mini-program ecosystem within WeChat. We plan to port the popular farm-stealing game from Weibo onto the platform, using lightweight games to increase the amount of time users spend on WeChat and strengthen their engagement.”","“.........”"]},{"number":875,"title":"Chapter 875: 876, This Is the Young Lady of the Dragon Alliance (Thanks to Matcha Little Cake ♪ for the Great God Certification)","paragraphs":["As Liu Yutong listened to Zhang Dalong’s report, she rapidly calculated the timeline in her head.","According to her memories, Big Goose’s WeChat would not officially launch until early 2011. In other words, she was a full year ahead of Pony Ma.","In the world of internet products, a one-year lead was incredibly valuable—more than enough time for WeChat to grow from zero to hundreds of millions of users.","Once its user base took shape and social connections became deeply embedded, even if Big Goose realized what was happening and tried to catch up, it would not be easy.","That was because the moat of a social app had never been the technology itself, but the network of relationships between its users.","When all your family and friends were on WeChat, you could hardly abandon it alone for another app that nobody used.","That was the logic of winner-take-all.","“What about the promotion plan?” Liu Yutong asked.","Zhang Dalong had clearly come prepared. He laid out his proposal in a clear and orderly manner.","“We plan to proceed in four stages.”","“First, we’ll use the more than one hundred thousand employees within the Wanlonghui Group to get the app off the ground. Every employee will be required to install WeChat and invite at least five relatives or friends to register and use it. Those who complete the invitation task will receive phone-credit subsidies. We estimate that this step alone will bring in at least one million initial users within a month.”","“Second, I’ve already discussed this in depth with Mr. Yu. When Longyao unveils its first-generation phone, WeChat will be presented as a core preinstalled application. We’ll use the phone’s rapidly growing sales to drive user growth. In addition to Longyao phones, Mr. Lei of Xiaomi has also indicated that he’ll showcase WeChat alongside Xiaomi’s first phone, which is scheduled to launch next year. He was full of praise for the voice-messaging feature we developed, and we’ve already signed a preinstallation agreement.”","“Third, we’ll promote it by leveraging the continuing popularity of The Voice of Longguo. Preparations for the second season are already underway. We plan to incorporate interactive WeChat features into the program—for example, allowing viewers to vote for contestants through WeChat, scanning a QR code displayed on the television screen to download the app, and so on.”","“Fourth, we’ll fully integrate with Weibo and Wanhui Youxuan. Weibo will direct traffic straight to us, and Weibo accounts can also be used as WeChat accounts. On the Wanhui Youxuan side, couriers and merchants will be required to use WeChat for certain types of communication. We’ll provide corresponding subsidies to couriers, merchants, and users. After placing an order, users will also receive message notifications through WeChat. This single use case will cover more than ten million users.”","“At the same time, we plan to launch a PC version of WeChat by the end of the year, enabling seamless synchronization between phones and computers and further expanding its range of applications.”","“......”","Zhang Dalong’s proposal was clear and well organized. Every step had a specific timeline and target, down to the estimated conversion rates for each channel.","After listening, Liu Yutong praised him. “Very good. Proceed according to this plan. Remember, within the next year, I want WeChat’s user base to exceed one hundred million.”","“Yes, Chairwoman!”","Zhang Dalong had just sat down when Su Mansu took over. “Chairwoman, regarding the payment license for Longfutong, our discussions with the central bank have made substantial progress.”","“There are dozens of institutions currently waiting to apply for licenses, but our documentation and qualifications are among the most complete. In addition, the disaster-relief donations and charitable contributions we made in BS Province earned us an excellent social reputation. We expect to receive the official license early next year.”","“Once we obtain the license, Longfutong will be fully integrated into every consumer scenario under the Wanlonghui Group, including Wanlong Plaza, Wanlong Supermarkets, Yuyuefang, Huangquan Internet Cafés, Qingyin Tea Drinks, Wanhui Youxuan, and more. Our goal is to cover one million offline merchants within a year.”","Liu Yutong nodded.","Payment was the infrastructure of the digital economy. Its importance could never be overstated.","She knew very well that in her previous life, Alibaba and Big Goose had burned hundreds of billions fighting for the mobile-payment market, engaging in a subsidy war that lasted for years. What she had to do now was enter the battlefield before the two companies completely took control of it and teach them a good lesson.","She would show them that a latecomer could still crush them in an instant.","“Lin Muyang, is there anything that needs to be coordinated with the entertainment and media division?” Liu Yutong turned her gaze to the other side of the room.","Lin Muyang stood and reported, “The first season finale of The Voice of Longguo achieved a ratings share of over four percent, setting a historic record for domestic variety shows. Preparations for the second season are already underway, and it is expected to air during next year’s summer vacation.”","“Also, Chu Junlin’s The Most Musical of Longguo has essentially stopped airing. Xingyao Media’s stock price has fallen from over seven yuan before we shorted it to just 3.2 yuan now. There hasn’t been any meaningful rebound along the way, and investor confidence is extremely difficult to restore. It probably won’t recover anytime soon.”","“What about Chu Junlin?”","“Young Master Chu has become much more subdued. He has discreetly expressed several times that he wants to join the Chairwoman’s Yunshan Club. I estimate that he’s growing anxious because he can’t get the stock price back up.”","Liu Yutong said, “Ignore him for now. Wait until he comes to me personally.”","“Understood!”","After nearly two hours, the meeting was drawing to a close.","Liu Yutong rose to her feet and placed both hands on the edge of the conference table. Her gaze slowly swept across every face in the room.","“Everyone, in addition to reviewing the progress of each division today, I have one more announcement to make.”","“Next year—in other words, 2010—will be the year the Wanlonghui Group launches its full-scale offensive.”","“Longyao’s phones must fight a beautiful sniper campaign. We’re not only going to seize the domestic market; we’re also going to break into overseas markets and let those international giants know that Longguo can build world-class phones too.”","“WeChat must grow from zero to one hundred million users within a year, securing our ticket to the mobile-social era ahead of everyone else.”","“Longfutong must connect every online and offline payment scenario and completely establish the infrastructure for mobile payments.”","“Longxin must continue tackling advanced process technology, striving to complete the preliminary research for the 45-nanometer process by the end of next year.”","“At the same time, Wanlong Aerospace will also be making a major move.”","As Liu Yutong said this, she deliberately looked toward Yun Cheng.","Yun Cheng understood at once. He opened his laptop and projected the display onto the large screen.","“Wanlong Aerospace Technology’s first medium-lift launch vehicle, the Wanlong-1, has completed its preliminary design review and officially entered the engineering-development phase. Professor Zhou Yingpei’s liquid-oxygen kerosene staged-combustion-cycle engine has successfully completed its first full-system simulated firing. Its thrust reached 105 percent of the design target, with every parameter meeting requirements. This marks a substantial breakthrough for us in the core field of rocket engines.”","“According to the current schedule, the Wanlong-1 is expected to make its maiden launch around 2012. Its first payload has tentatively been designated as Wanlong Aerospace’s first experimental communications satellite, which will also serve as the first verification satellite for the Longchain Initiative.”","A collective gasp swept through the conference room.","Although everyone knew that Liu Yutong was serious about aerospace, it still felt unbelievable when they actually heard the news that the rocket engine had ignited successfully and that the rocket had entered the engineering development stage.","They were really building a rocket.","And judging by the way things were progressing, this was no small-time project. They were clearly aiming to send actual payloads into space.","“Where will the first launch of the Wanlong-1 take place?”","“We’ve already signed a cooperation agreement with BS Province. The launch site will be built at an abandoned military testing range there, which is currently being renovated.”","“That area is at a relatively low latitude, giving it certain advantages for launching satellites into low-Earth orbit. However, if we want to launch high-orbit satellites or deep-space probes, we’ll still need to rely on a large coastal launch facility.”","“The launch site in BS Province is only the first step. Once Wanlong Aerospace obtains more licenses and resources, we’ll consider building a new commercial launch site along the coast. It won’t be used exclusively by Wanlong Aerospace. We’ll also open it to other domestic commercial aerospace companies and turn space launches into an open platform.”","Her words once again showed everyone the breadth of Liu Yutong’s vision.","She wasn’t trying to turn Wanlong Aerospace into a closed-off personal toy. She wanted to build an open ecosystem.","Just like SX overseas, she intended to use commercial thinking to drive the advancement of aerospace technology and ultimately realize humanity’s dream of reaching the stars and exploring the sea of space.","Of course, dreams of the stars and the sea required money—an astronomical amount of money.","Fortunately, Liu Yutong no longer lacked the ability to make money.","Not to mention the profits of more than thirty billion yuan she had made this year by short-selling Xingyao Media, the steady cash flow from her other businesses alone had left the Wanlonghui Group with more than ten billion yuan in cash on hand. The funds in the accounts of the major investment companies under her control were even more substantial, totaling over one hundred billion yuan—and that didn’t include the money that had already been invested.","Over the next five years, Liu Yutong planned to transform all that money into technology, products, and market share, ultimately building a super-empire spanning semiconductors, smartphones, social media, payment services, aerospace, and numerous other fields.","“Everyone.”","Liu Yutong rose to her feet.","Everyone else in the conference room immediately stood as well.","“Next year, we’re going to be extremely busy.”","“In fact, we’ll be busy throughout the next five years.”","“We have no way back, and we don’t need one.”","“Since we’ve chosen this path, we’ll give it everything we have.”","“I’ll say only one thing: when Wanlonghui takes on a project, we either don’t do it at all, or we do it better than anyone else!”","The moment those words were spoken, a fire ignited in everyone’s chest.","Not because the words themselves were particularly rousing, but because every single person present had personally witnessed how this twenty-year-old girl had built the group from nothing into the terrifying giant it was today.","From selling lobsters to creating a hundred-billion-yuan business empire; from mass-producing 90-nanometer chips to successfully completing rocket-engine ignition tests; from a small local enterprise to a supergroup spanning multiple industries.","Not one of the things she had ever said was empty talk.","Not one of the things she had set out to accomplish had failed.","This was the Young Lady of Wanlonghui.","This was the person they were willing to follow to the death!"]},{"number":876,"title":"Chapter 876: 877, Dragon Soars Cup, All-Staff Health Management Fund.","paragraphs":["January 28, Pearl City.","The annual meeting of the Wanlonghui Group was held as scheduled.","This year, the venue was changed to the newly completed stadium—the same stadium that had hosted the finals of The Voice of Dragon Kingdom.","There was simply no other choice. Too many people were attending.","This year’s annual meeting attracted more than ten thousand employees. Nearly all the core members were present, and they alone accounted for almost half of the attendees. Holding the event in a stadium was therefore the most practical option.","Employees from other provinces and non-core members organized their own annual meetings. The group provided the benefits packages, all of which followed exactly the same standards.","On the day of the annual meeting, luxury cars filled the area outside the stadium. Mercedes-Benz vehicles were especially numerous, making up nearly ninety percent of the total. The sight was nothing short of spectacular.","The citizens passing by the stadium got a firsthand look at Wanlonghui’s strength and extravagance. The group bought luxury cars as casually as other people bought vegetables.","The massive impact of the scene inspired even more people to rack their brains for a way to join Wanlonghui Group.","After all, Wanlonghui’s employee benefits were simply too generous. Five types of social insurance and the housing provident fund were only the basics. Its income levels were especially impressive, standing far above those offered by companies in the same industry. Social insurance and provident fund contributions were paid in full, and holiday benefits were never an afterthought.","Wanlonghui also had an almost domineering mechanism for forcing its partners to raise their standards.","Because of Wanlonghui Group’s meteoric rise, every company that worked with it—from upstream suppliers to downstream distributors—had been forced to improve its employees’ benefits by a considerable margin.","Although their packages still could not match those offered by Wanlonghui Group, they were certainly better than what their competitors provided.","They had been forced to do this by Wanlonghui.","Want to work with us?","Then if you refuse to pay social insurance for your employees, or if you treat them too poorly, I’m sorry. No matter how good your products are or how competitive your prices may be, I won’t work with you. I’ll put you on the blacklist as well.","And if I really take a dislike to you, I may even take direct action against you, support a competitor of similar strength, and keep going until I drive you completely out of the supply chain.","Given Wanlonghui Group’s current size, it was absurdly easy for it to sanction its partners.","In truth, Liu Yutong’s logic had always been simple.","Only when employees’ incomes genuinely increased would consumption be stimulated and the market become more prosperous.","Wanlonghui Group could not force every company to adopt its own benefits standards, but any company that wanted to work with Wanlonghui had to follow these rules.","At present, Wanlonghui’s own employees, together with the various upstream and downstream partners in its network, represented an employment population of at least several million people directly affected by these policies.","In other words, in their respective regions, these millions of people enjoyed salaries, social insurance, and benefits that were reliably above the industry average.","Their families numbered more than ten million altogether. Because Wanlonghui existed, their quality of life and spending power had genuinely improved.","Once the annual meeting officially began, senior executives from all six business groups took their places.","Liu Yutong stood at the center of the stage as a massive screen behind her displayed the group’s key figures from the past year.","Over the course of the year, the number of Wanlonghui’s core members had grown from fewer than four thousand to more than six thousand, including the new members promoted at this annual meeting.","The more than one thousand new members had all passed rigorous legal and physical fitness assessments. Their average age was under twenty-four. The highest educational qualification among them was a bachelor’s degree, while the lowest was only junior middle school.","The gap in education was substantial, but it also reflected Wanlonghui Group’s willingness to recognize talent regardless of background.","The total number of official group employees had surpassed eighty thousand. Including full-time delivery riders and couriers, the overall headcount was approaching two hundred thousand.","The revenue figures for each business were then displayed on the screen one after another.","The Commercial Retail Business Group generated annual revenue of more than twenty billion yuan.","Wanlong Plaza currently had two operating locations: the flagship store in Pearl City and another in Dannan City. The two malls had maintained an average daily footfall of more than thirty thousand, with combined annual sales exceeding four billion yuan.","Apart from its presence in the home province, Wanlong Supermarkets had generally been opened alongside Wanlong Plaza malls. Following a strategy focused on carefully selected products and improved service, its expansion had not been fast. There were fewer than thirty branches in total, most of them concentrated in the home province and BS Province.","By the standards of any supermarket chain, this pace was exceptionally inefficient.","Even so, the company continued to refuse blind expansion. Every new store had to ensure that its operating team was fully in place, service quality was up to standard, and the supply chain was completely functional before it could officially open to customers.","The advantages of this approach were obvious. Customer satisfaction and word of mouth continued to rise, while the member repurchase rate had reached an astonishing seventy-eight percent. In other words, nearly eight out of every ten members returned to shop again.","In addition, the main structures of Wanlong Plaza’s projects in Jinchuan and Jingchuan, BS Province, had already been topped out. They were expected to officially open in the first half of 2010.","Nearly ten other Wanlong Plaza projects were also under construction in provincial capitals across the country. Land acquisition, design, and tenant recruitment were all progressing simultaneously, and the projects were expected to open one after another in the second half of 2011.","The Technology Business Group was still in its investment phase. The Longxin Semiconductor 90-nanometer production line had maintained stable mass production throughout the year. Thanks to cooperation with companies such as Qiming Electronics, its revenue had approached 1.2 billion yuan. It had already begun generating enough cash to sustain itself and no longer needed unlimited funding from Liu Yutong.","The Digital Business Group’s Weibo had surpassed three hundred million registered users, with daily active users holding steady at more than fifty million. It firmly occupied the leading position in the social media sector.","As an aside, Big Goose’s Weibo had been operating for nearly half a year by then, but had already fallen into a development bottleneck.","Riding on the explosive success of the first season of The Voice of Dragon Kingdom, the Entertainment and Media Business Group had generated more than three billion yuan in annual revenue, becoming one of the group’s strongest sources of cash flow.","In addition, toward the end of the year, the Entertainment and Media Business Group had incubated an entirely new video website—Long Dimension.","The platform was built around a bullet-comment video format and targeted younger users. Its content covered anime, games, fan-made film and television edits, music, and exclusive behind-the-scenes footage from The Voice of Dragon Kingdom. It also opened a creator submission system, allowing users to upload original videos of their own.","Just one month after launch, the platform had already surpassed three million registered users, with daily active users holding steady at more than four hundred thousand. Although it could not yet be considered a major platform, its growth had been astonishingly rapid, and user engagement had far exceeded expectations.","The Supply Chain and Logistics Business Group had established four regional hub centers across the country, covering East China, South China, and Southwest China. Both delivery times and fulfillment rates had entered the industry’s top five.","After the data report concluded, the lights throughout the stadium dimmed slightly for a moment. Everyone’s attention focused on the slender figure dressed in black at the center of the stage.","Liu Yutong took two steps forward and swept her gaze across the audience. Then she suddenly announced something that no one had expected.","“I’m planning to organize an internal group competition once our core membership surpasses ten thousand.”","The moment those words left her mouth, everyone’s interest was piqued. They began discussing excitedly, wondering what kind of competition the Young Lady had in mind.","She revealed the answer soon enough.","“Longguo has been known as the home of martial arts since ancient times. All of you are always boasting about how tough you are, so why not put your real abilities to the test? You’ll form teams according to your respective districts and compete in combat, physical fitness, and legal knowledge. I’ll personally present awards to the top three teams and individuals. We’ll call it—the Dragon Soaring Cup!”","“The total prize money will be no less than fifty million!”","Boom!","The core members sitting below, who had been wearing stern expressions just moments before, instantly erupted with excitement.","They hadn’t done anything major in the past six months, and no one had dared to provoke them. They were practically unused to the peaceful routine.","Now, at last, they had a chance to show what they could do.","Ma Da, seated in the front row, was especially excited. He sprang to his feet, the flesh on his chubby face trembling as he shouted, “This is great! Pearl City has to take first place!”","“Absolutely!”","“...”","“Besides the Dragon Soaring Cup, I’m also planning to establish an organization-wide Health Management Fund. Those who keep exercising and continue studying legal knowledge will be assessed based on changes in their body-fat percentage, physical fitness test results, and progress in preparing for the bar exam. Anyone who meets the standards or shows significant improvement will receive a special bonus. The fund will start with one hundred million yuan, and additional money will be added every year.”","“That’s all I have to say. I hope that at next year’s annual meeting, every one of you will present a report card more impressive than this year’s. Meeting adjourned!”","There was no emotional appeal, nor any long-winded motivational speech.","As soon as she finished speaking, she walked straight off the stage.","But her announcement completely set the entire room ablaze.","In the days that followed, the core members of the Wanlong Association seemed to go completely mad. Those studying law worked even harder, and the legal study rooms were packed every day. The intensity of physical training also shot up by an entire level. From dawn until late at night, the track was always filled with runners, while people in the strength-training area lifted weights without pause.","The money wasn’t what mattered.","What mattered was the honor—and the chance to earn the Young Lady’s approval.","Being personally presented with an award by the Young Lady, having her remember your name— that sense of honor was worth more than any amount of money.","There were still roughly six months left in the current lull. At the current rate of expansion, the number of core members would exceed ten thousand by the middle of the year at the earliest, and certainly no later than the third quarter.","That didn’t leave them much time.","At first, the ordinary employees thought the Dragon Soaring Cup had nothing to do with them. But once they heard the rules of the Health Management Fund, they too sprang into action as if injected with adrenaline.","Body fat too high? Train!","Don’t understand the law? Study!","From top to bottom, the entire group was swept up in an unprecedented frenzy of self-improvement.","For a while, Pearl City became home to a remarkable sight.","People stopped taking cars to work. Many didn’t even ride bicycles. Instead, they ran to and from work, turning the streets into a sea of young people in sportswear, panting as they jogged along.","The study rooms of the city’s major law firms were packed as well. The materials normally used to prepare for the bar exam were borrowed until not a single copy remained, and the lights in those rooms stayed on deeper into the night than those in the libraries.","The spring of Year Ten quietly passed amid this feverish atmosphere of restlessness and determined effort."]},{"number":877,"title":"Chapter 877: 878, Crazy Fruits 4, Crazy Buyers.","paragraphs":["The spring of 2010 slipped quietly away amid this feverish atmosphere.","Longyao’s first-generation mobile phones officially entered mass production in Lancang. The first batch of 100,000 phones had already rolled off the assembly line, and Yu Xin had spent an entire month stationed at the factory with her team, making sure nothing went wrong with the initial production run.","After confirming that the mass-produced phones were working properly, she flew straight to the United States to prepare for the launch event.","The number of users participating in WeChat’s closed beta had expanded from 30,000 to 300,000 in one go. The product’s stability continued to improve through round after round of repeated testing and iteration.","Longxin’s yield rate for its 65-nanometer process had finally climbed steadily to 78%. At the same time, a research team for the 45-nanometer process was officially formed. A group of younger engineers were transferred to the team and began tackling the next process node.","Wanlong Aerospace’s rocket engine was about to undergo its second full-system test.","Construction of the infrastructure at the Qingyan Mountain lithium mine had begun in full swing. Excavators and fleets of transport trucks worked day and night, steadily pushing deeper into the mountains.","The two businessmen from Harbor City, Zhang Ting and Xie Jichuan, flew to Jinchuan almost every month, eager to get their projects into production as soon as possible.","The two Wanlong Plazas in Jinchuan had also entered the stages of interior finishing and tenant move-in. The construction barriers around the sites were already covered with advertisements seeking potential businesses.","On Weibo, discussion of Apple’s next-generation phone began heating up rapidly.","Overseas technology media outlets successively leaked spy shots and detailed specifications of Apple’s new phone. Everything from its dimensions to its camera specifications was exposed in exhaustive detail.","Each new leak sparked an enormous wave of discussion on domestic tech forums.","Across major Baidu Tieba communities and online forums, searches for the keyword “iPhone 4” were climbing rapidly. Unboxing predictions, price-guessing threads, and related discussions were multiplying by the day.","Everything was progressing according to plan.","May 7, San Francisco, across the Pacific Ocean—the Moscone Center.","Apple’s Worldwide Developers Conference.","The date appeared to be about a month earlier than it had been in his previous life.","When Jobs stepped onto the stage wearing his trademark black turtleneck and blue jeans, technology media outlets around the world turned their cameras toward him. The sound of camera shutters filled the livestream.","A phone slowly appeared on the giant screen.","It had a rounded-rectangle body, with only a single circular physical button on the front. The back was made of glass, with the camera and flash arranged in the upper-left corner.","The phone’s design was so clean and simple that it bordered on severe. Even the number of buttons along the sides had been reduced to a minimum.","“Today, we’re introducing a revolutionary product—one that will change everything all over again!”","Jobs began introducing the iPhone 4’s various features: a Retina display with a resolution of 960 by 640, a 5-megapixel high-definition camera, a brand-new video-calling feature, and the powerful A4 processor.","With every feature he unveiled, the applause from the audience grew more enthusiastic. It barely stopped throughout the presentation.","The launch event was livestreamed across the world over the internet.","In China, even though the presentation took place in the middle of the night, more than a million people still stayed up in front of their computers to watch it.","The servers of major technology forums were nearly overwhelmed. On Tieba and Weibo, new discussion threads about the iPhone 4 appeared at a rate of dozens every second.","“The design is way too gorgeous! Apple’s design really is in a league of its own.”","“A Retina display and a 5-megapixel camera? This configuration is incredible. I heard the mainland version starts at 4,999 yuan. It’s definitely expensive, but after watching the launch, I think it’s worth it.”","“4,999? I’m going to throw all the money I make from my summer job into it. If that’s not enough, I’ll ask my parents for more.”","“I only make a little over a thousand yuan a month. I’d have to go four months without eating or spending anything just to afford it.”","“I make only eight hundred a month. I don’t think I’ll ever be able to own this phone.”","“Does anyone know when the mainland version goes on sale? I’m already preparing to spend the night lining up.”","“...”","Several days later, in front of an Apple store in the capital.","A girl wearing a blouse and with long, straight hair stood anxiously at the edge of the crowd, making a phone call.","“Xiaoyan? Why are you calling at a time like this? Aren’t you supposed to be in class?”","“Mom, I need some money.”","“How much?”","“Five thousand.”","The girl named a figure that was exactly enough to buy an iPhone 4.","There was a brief silence on the other end.","Xiaoyan could hear her mother speaking quietly to someone, as though they were discussing something. Her mother kept her voice low.","After a long while, her mother finally spoke again.","“What do you need that much money for?”","“I’m preparing for the graduate school entrance exam. The prep classes and study materials are really expensive.”","“All right. Your mother will figure something out. Don’t worry. Your father and I don’t earn much, but we can still manage to scrape together five thousand yuan.”","Xiaoyan gave a quiet acknowledgment and hung up.","She felt a little guilty, but this was hardly the first time she had told her parents a similar lie, so she wasn’t particularly nervous.","By the time the money arrived, it was already afternoon.","Xiaoyan pooled the newly transferred money with her living expenses. After setting aside enough for her train ticket home, two days of meals, and a small emergency fund, she had exactly enough to pay the official price of the iPhone 4—not a yuan more, not a yuan less.","Fortunately, she didn’t have many classes during her junior year, and taking leave was easy. She casually made up an excuse for her counselor, then hurried to the flagship store before dawn to join the line.","Only after arriving did she discover that more than a hundred people had already lined up at five in the morning. The line stretched around two corners of the sidewalk, and quite a few people had brought small folding stools and were dozing off where they sat.","After waiting all day, the line had barely moved.","Someone near the front turned around and said that they probably wouldn’t have any luck that day either. The store had brought in too few units, and only sold a small number at a time. Every time customers were allowed inside, it took less than ten minutes for the store to put up the “Sold Out” sign again.","Xiaoyan stood in the crowd, her legs numb from waiting.","But the moment she heard that scalpers were already selling the phone for 6,000 yuan, her spirits lifted.","Six thousand!","If she managed to buy one, she could make a thousand yuan in pure profit right away!","And judging by the situation, the price might climb even higher.","At the thought of that, Xiaoyan began to grow restless.","What if she bought two phones? Wouldn’t she make even more money?","Xiaoyan had bought her train ticket and rushed overnight to the capital on the second day after the iPhone 4 launch.","She had learned that the capital was the site of the phone’s mainland debut, while other cities would not receive it for at least another month.","This timeline was also several months earlier than Liu Yutong remembered from her previous life.","When Xiaoyan arrived outside the flagship store two nights earlier, that day’s stock had already sold out. All she could do was wait for the next shipment.","While waiting, she had also taken the opportunity to find out what the scalpers were offering, giving herself a reference point before asking her parents for money.","She had always been proud and ambitious. Put kindly, she had a strong sense of self-respect; put less kindly, she was somewhat vain.","Her family was clearly ordinary, yet she wanted to surpass everyone else in every possible way. Since high school, she had liked presenting herself as a wealthy heiress, someone whose family had deep pockets.","But after entering university, she had been crushed mercilessly.","Her classmate, Liu Yutong, could outshine her in every respect.","She was prettier than Yu Xin, scored better than Yu Xin, and used more expensive things than Yu Xin. She had even been the first one in the dorm to buy an electric scooter at the start of the school year.","Yu Xin had eventually gritted her teeth and bought one too, but after riding it for only a few days, she discovered that Liu Yutong was actually being driven around in a Mercedes-Benz. Later, Liu Yutong upgraded to a Maybach.","After that, she became the most famous person on campus. Her net worth was said to exceed ten billion yuan.","Yu Xin didn’t understand.","They had all lived in the same dormitory. So why was the gap between them so enormous?","What made it worse was that Lin Lele and the others had joined Liu Yutong’s company before even graduating. They all had stable sources of income, and their lives began improving as well. The things they ate and used were no worse than Yu Xin’s—sometimes even better.","It was impossible for her not to feel jealous.","But because she and Liu Yutong had clashed in the past, there was no way she could join Liu Yutong’s company. She could only rely on the living expenses her family sent her, occasionally working as a private tutor to make ends meet and barely keep up with the others’ standard of living.","Even so, she had never lowered her head in front of Lin Lele and the others. She had even made up a story, claiming that a major company had recruited her early, before she had graduated, all to protect that pitiful shred of self-esteem.","She accepted that she couldn’t compare with Liu Yutong.","Liu Yutong simply wasn’t an ordinary person. There was no way to compare herself with her—the gap was far too great.","But there was absolutely no way she could allow herself to live worse than the others.","After Fruit 4 was released, every student on campus was talking about it. Wealthier students had even hired people to purchase the phone overseas and bring it back for them. They had all switched to the new device, which was being hailed as a revolutionary smartphone.","Yu Xin wanted one too. Its appearance and cutting-edge features had opened her eyes.","So phones could actually have fully edge-to-edge screens.","So unlocking a phone could be done with nothing more than a light swipe.","From that night onward, her desire for a Fruit 4 became impossible to suppress.","That was why she had decisively requested leave and come to the capital.","Of course, she couldn’t possibly afford to buy one at the inflated price scalpers were charging. Her only option was to queue at an official store.","But waiting in line was excruciating. She had stood there for two days without managing to buy a phone, forced to watch helplessly as the scalpers’ prices continued to climb.","Yet the experience also made her realize there was money to be made.","A person could earn one or two thousand yuan by reselling a single phone. What if she bought two more when her turn came?","Then she could make an even bigger profit.","Once the thought occurred to her, she couldn’t suppress it. The more she thought about it, the more tempted she became. In the end, even she felt that after enduring two full days crouched outside the flagship store, she deserved to seize this opportunity and make a substantial amount of money.","On the third day, just before dawn, she called her family again.","This time, she called her father.","“Dad, I need another sum of money for my postgraduate entrance exam. It’s mainly for a prep course—fifteen thousand yuan.”","“Why do you need money again? We’ve already sent you money twice this month.”","“The exam is expensive, and I can’t help it. As long as I pass, it’ll all be worth it.”","“...All right. I’ll find a way to get it. Don’t worry.”","After hanging up, the girl spent five hundred yuan to hire someone to stand in line for her. She hurried to the bank, withdrew the money, and paid the person.","The going rate for hiring someone to queue was extremely high these days. Otherwise, no one would be willing to spend hours baking under the blazing sun.","A little over an hour later, she finally got the money and rushed back.","There was now more than enough in her account to buy three phones. She would keep one for herself and resell the other two, earning a considerable profit from the price difference.","She then began planning what she would do once she had made the money. She would treat herself to a delicious meal and take a proper shower.","For the past three days, her skin had been sticky with sweat, and she had begun to smell sour.","But the other people in line were no better. For example, the bespectacled young man standing beside her smelled even more strongly of sweat and sourness.","Yet for the sake of a phone, all of them seemed possessed. Each one stubbornly endured it.","“Hey, bro, do you think we’ll make it to the front today?” A fat man in a basketball jersey turned around and asked the bespectacled man beside her.","“How would I know? I didn’t make it yesterday either. Those scalpers at the front were cutting in line like crazy.”","“I heard they stocked more phones today. We should have a chance.”","“A chance, my ass. They said the same thing yesterday.”","“...”","The girl listened to their intermittent conversation while watching the store entrance draw closer and closer. Her excitement grew with every passing moment.","She would have the phone soon.","If she hadn’t been short on money, she would have bought out every Fruit 4 in the store.","Just as the girl was lost in her thoughts, a sudden commotion broke out near the front of the line.","A convoy of black cars was slowly approaching from the end of the street.","The people waiting in line turned to look.","Leading the convoy was a black Maybach, followed by five identical black Mercedes-Benz vehicles. All six cars stopped conspicuously in front of the flagship store.","The doors opened at the same time.","The first to step out were the men in black from the five cars behind. They were all dressed in black suits, with muscular builds. After getting out, they quickly formed a line in front of the flagship store, separating the waiting crowd from the entrance.","Their imposing presence instinctively caused everyone in line to hold their breath.","“Holy crap, what kind of entrance is this? Five Mercedes-Benzes and a Maybach—and the license plates are all consecutive numbers.”","“Look at what those guys are wearing. All black suits. That’s obviously no ordinary person.”","“Let me count... More than twenty bodyguards. What kind of person needs more than twenty bodyguards every time they leave the house?”","“I think I’ve seen that emblem somewhere before... I can’t remember clearly, but it looks familiar.”","“Is that a Maybach in the middle? I’ve seen it in magazines. It must cost at least seven or eight million yuan after everything.”","“Seven or eight million? I couldn’t earn enough in my entire life to buy one of its tires.”","“...”","Before long, the convoy came to a stop. A man in black opened the rear door of the Maybach parked in the middle.","A stunningly young and beautiful girl stepped out.","She was also wearing a black suit. Her features were delicate, and she wore no heavy makeup or unnecessary jewelry. The only adornment on her was a watch on her left wrist that was clearly worth a fortune.","What drew the most attention, however, was the badge pinned to her chest.","Unlike the silver badges worn by the men in black beside her, hers was pure gold, with a vividly detailed dragon engraved across it.","The moment she appeared, a powerful aura swept over the area. The people who had been whispering instinctively fell silent.","Soon, the manager of the Fruit flagship store and several employees hurried outside to greet her.","The manager was a man in his forties, wearing the standard blue polo shirt of a Fruit company employee. As an employee of such a major corporation, he should have been calm and composed, but at that moment, his expression was extremely nervous and awkward.","“Miss Liu, you’re here. Please, come inside! This way, please!”","Liu Yutong gave a slight nod. With the manager leading the way, she walked straight into the store.","The men in black followed closely behind. Some remained outside to guard the entrance, while the others accompanied her inside.","Their movements were highly professional, and their execution was exceptionally efficient.","Only after her figure disappeared from view outside the shop did the invisible pressure gradually lift.","Only then did the people waiting in line dare to start chatting again.","“Whoa! That girl’s presence was terrifying. I didn’t even dare breathe when she showed up.”","“The store manager practically knelt before her. She must come from a seriously powerful background.”","“Could she be some huge celebrity? But even celebrities don’t put on that kind of show when they go out, do they?”","“No celebrity has that kind of aura. Not even close.”","“I bet she’s some big shot. Anyway, she’s definitely not someone ordinary people like us can afford to offend.”","“Did you notice? She didn’t look at us even once the whole time.”","“Well, obviously. Why would someone that important look at a bunch of lowlifes like us?”","“True...”","The girl standing among the crowd also waited until that figure had completely entered the shop before she dared raise her head.","At the same time, feelings of envy, jealousy, inferiority, and unwillingness surged through her.","She had never expected to run into her classmate, Liu Yutong, here."]},{"number":878,"title":"Chapter 878: 879. Breaking Mobile Phones Banned from Sale","paragraphs":["Liu Yutong’s sudden appearance made the girl extremely uneasy. She was terrified that the other woman might spot her and recognize her.","About half an hour later, Liu Yutong finally came out of the store, got into her car, and drove away.","The girl secretly breathed a sigh of relief, but a vague sense of irritation soon welled up inside her.","Why did she keep running into that woman everywhere?","Still, she had no time to dwell on it. The line began moving forward again.","“It’s moving! They’re letting people in!”","The crowd stirred, and the girl quickly perked up, rising onto her tiptoes to look ahead.","Through the glass doors of the Fruit flagship store, employees were letting customers inside in groups of a dozen or so at a time. The long line outside was finally getting visibly shorter.","She did a quick calculation. At this rate, she would have to wait less than an hour at most.","Just one hour. She could handle that.","She had already endured three whole days. What was one more hour?","Time passed minute by minute.","The number of people ahead of her dwindled, and she drew closer and closer to the store entrance. Her excitement rose with every step.","It was almost her turn. Almost!","The girl reached into her bag and felt the cash inside. It was everything she had—roughly twenty-two thousand yuan in total.","Once she got inside, she would buy four phones outright.","She would keep one for herself and resell the other three at a premium, earning a sizeable profit.","At the thought, the corners of her mouth lifted involuntarily.","“Next!”","At last, it was her turn.","A smile spread across the girl’s face as she stepped toward the entrance. But just as she was about to go inside—","Suddenly!","A store employee wearing a blue polo shirt rushed out and stopped her at the door. Then he called loudly to the people outside:","“Everyone, we sincerely apologize! We’ve just received notice from our superiors that, due to special circumstances, this store is suspending sales of the Fruit 4 effective immediately. We’ll announce a reopening date separately. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause!”","The air fell silent.","Then the crowd exploded.","“What the hell? You’re suspending sales? I’ve been in line for two days, and now you’re telling me you’re not selling them anymore?” A burly man flew into a rage on the spot.","“Exactly! How is that fair? We’ve waited this long, and you can just stop selling them whenever you feel like it? Is this how the Fruit company treats its customers?”","“Fuck this! I’ve been waiting since yesterday afternoon. I haven’t even dared to use the bathroom, and now you’re telling me you’re not selling them?”","“Did you save all the stock for the scalpers? I knew it! You’re in league with them!”","“Rip-off! This place is a rip-off!”","The crowd descended into complete chaos.","Some people pounded on the crowd-control barriers. Others threw mineral-water bottles at the store doors. A few even tried to cross the barriers and charge inside, only to be held back by the security guards.","The employee braced himself and tried to explain.","“No, that’s not it. We just received the notice ourselves. It’s not that we don’t want to sell them—the higher-ups said the Fruit 4 has been banned from sale.”","Boom!","Those words sent shock waves through the crowd.","“Banned from sale? What kind of joke is that? Who banned it? And on what grounds?”","“Exactly! Who the hell has the authority to ban a Fruit phone? It’s an international brand! Who’s powerful enough to do that?”","“I don’t believe it! You’re just making excuses! Get the manager out here!”","“Right! Bring out the manager! Get the store director!”","But no matter how much the crowd shouted, cursed, and demanded answers, they received only one response:","The Fruit 4 really had been banned from sale.","The moment she heard the final confirmation, the girl’s heart sank completely.","She had spent three days waiting in line, lied to her parents to get twenty thousand yuan, and barely eaten a proper meal in days. She even smelled awful from not being able to wash properly.","And after all that, this was what she got?","A sales ban?","Then what had all her suffering, lies, and sacrifices been for?","For a moment, the world spun around her. Her vision went black, and she nearly collapsed.","Then, suddenly, a thought flashed through her mind.","Liu Yutong.","Liu Yutong had been here just now.","And after she left, the Fruit phone had been banned from sale.","Was it really a coincidence?","Although the girl had no idea what Liu Yutong had come here to do, there was one thing she knew for certain:","Wherever that woman appeared, nothing good ever came of it.","At least, that was always the case for her.","The ban on the Fruit phone probably had something to do with Liu Yutong.","The crowd continued shouting angrily, but for all their yelling, no one truly intended to do anything to the store.","The commotion lasted nearly an hour. It was only after the police arrived to maintain order that the people in line gradually dispersed.","The girl, however, remained where she was, staring blankly at the store’s doors, now closed for the night.","Then her phone vibrated.","She looked down and saw a text message from her mother.","“Xiaoyan, do you have enough money? If you don’t, I’ll discuss it with your dad and send you more. Don’t try to save too much, and take care of yourself.”","She stared at the message for a long time. Her eyes suddenly stung, and tears nearly spilled over.","She was just hesitating over whether to return the money to her parents when a thought occurred to her.","The Fruit flagship store might have stopped selling the phones, but the scalpers must still have stock.","She abruptly raised her head and looked to the side.","Sure enough, the middle-aged scalper who had been squatting by the roadside with a cigarette between his lips looked even more delighted after hearing that sales had been suspended. He was not panicking in the slightest.","The girl hurried over and asked, “Big brother, do you still have any Fruit 4s?”","The scalper looked her up and down, then held up one finger.","“Twelve thousand. No bargaining.”","“Twelve thousand?”","The girl sucked in a sharp breath. “Weren’t they only seven thousand before? How did the price jump so much?”","“Miss, that’s old news.”","The scalper jerked his chin toward the flagship store. “See that? They’re not selling them anymore. Right now, the only people with stock are channels like us. Twelve thousand is already a bargain. If you don’t believe me, wait until tomorrow and see. The price will only go up.”","“Besides, they’ve said the phone is banned from sale. Who knows how long that’ll last? If the ban continues for ten days or half a month, the price could climb to twenty thousand. By then, you’ll regret not buying one today.”","The girl bit her lip, rapidly weighing her options.","Twelve thousand yuan.","She had twenty-two thousand on her, but she had originally planned to buy three phones, maybe even four.","Now she could afford only one.","One would have to do. She could buy a single phone first, then resell it when the price rose and still make a little money.","She wouldn’t earn as much as she had originally expected, but at least she wouldn’t lose money.","Finally, she gritted her teeth.","“I’ll take one!”","“Coming right up!”","The scalper immediately pulled a brand-new white box from the black backpack behind him and handed it to her.","“Good choice, miss! Here you go. Genuine merchandise. You can inspect it on the spot.”","The girl took the phone and carefully opened the packaging. After confirming that everything was in order, she pulled out twelve thousand yuan and handed it to him.","Cradling the white Fruit 4 in her hands, she squatted by the roadside like all the strength had drained out of her and panted for quite a while.","To be honest, she had no idea what was wrong with her. The moment the phone was finally hers, she didn’t feel the excitement she had imagined.","Instead, she felt a pang of regret. Maybe she had acted too impulsively.","The girl quickly shook her head and forced herself to stop thinking about it.","Impulsive or not, the important thing was that she had finally managed to buy one.","Even if she used the phone for a while, she could still make a profit by reselling it a few days later.","She had just finished putting the phone away and was about to leave when another person came running over, panting heavily.","“Bro, I’ll give you fifteen thousand for that one! Sell it to me!”","The scalper spread his hands. “Sorry, it’s gone. That was the last phone, and I just sold it to her.” He pointed toward the girl nearby.","The man immediately turned to the girl and said anxiously, “Miss, will you sell me yours? Fifteen thousand! I’ll pay fifteen thousand!”","Her heart began to race when she heard the offer.","Fifteen thousand!","She had only just paid twelve thousand for it, and in the blink of an eye, its value had risen by three thousand.","If she waited another couple of days, it might really climb to twenty thousand!","“Not selling!” she refused decisively, clutching the phone tightly to her chest as she turned and walked away.","The man continued shouting after her, “Sixteen thousand! I’ll give you sixteen thousand!”","The girl didn’t stop. She quickened her pace and left the area.","She couldn’t sell it.","Selling it now would be foolish.","The supply restriction definitely wouldn’t end anytime soon. During that period, the scalpers’ prices could only continue rising. It might even break twenty thousand.","By then, she could use the phone for a few days, take some pictures, and share them on her QQ Space to make her classmates jealous. After that, she could sell it and pocket nearly ten thousand yuan in pure profit. Not only would she be able to repay the money she had tricked her parents into giving her, she would still have a sizeable sum left over.","At the thought of this, the girl’s mood finally improved a little. It felt as though all the hardship of the past few days had finally paid off.","Then she caught a whiff of the sour odor coming from her own body and remembered that she hadn’t showered in three days.","First, she would take a shower, then find somewhere to stay and get a good rest. Tomorrow, she would take the train straight back to school.","She found a very cheap youth hostel, the kind with tiny private rooms that cost only eighty yuan a night.","After showering, she lay on the hard mattress, still hugging the white iPhone 4 in her arms.","She turned on the phone and played with its smooth screen, feeling delighted. She was convinced that refusing the offer earlier had been the wisest decision.","Just wait. The price would definitely be even higher tomorrow.","Carrying this wonderful fantasy with her, the girl fell into a deep sleep.","She had no idea that something major would happen outside that very night—an event that would send shock waves through the tech world.","The scalpers’ price for the iPhone 4 plunged from nearly twenty thousand yuan to around six thousand, suffering a spectacular collapse."]},{"number":879,"title":"Chapter 879: 880, The Dragon Glory mobile phone launch event begins.","paragraphs":["That evening, at the National Convention Center in the imperial capital.","While countless people were still lining up outside, desperately begging for an iPhone 4 but unable to get one, a press conference that was destined to go down in the history of Long Kingdom’s mobile-phone industry was being held here.","The media reporters who arrived first had assumed they were merely attending an ordinary product launch for a domestic mobile-phone brand. After all, there were plenty of homegrown phone companies these days. Most of them were just knockoff phones with new casings and different labels, offering little in the way of genuine technology. The reporters had planned to take a few photos, see what all the fuss was about, and go home to finish their assignments.","But when the invited guests began entering the venue, every one of those reporters was left utterly stunned.","“Isn’t that Ma Yunyun? The one from Ali Group?”","“And that’s not all! Look over there. That’s Li Yanhong from Baidu, and beside him is Ding Sanshi from NetEase. There’s Cao Wei from Xinlang, Chen Sheng from Shengda Entertainment, and Zhang Yang from Souhu... My God! Almost every internet heavyweight in the country is here!”","“Pony Ma is here too? Doesn’t he never attend events like this?”","“Holy crap, aren’t those people from Hong Kong? That’s Zhang Ting, and beside him is Xie Jichuan. They’re both scions of old-established Hong Kong families.”","“What... what kind of phone launch is this? How did they manage to invite so many big names?”","“...”","These reporters had seen lavish product launches before, but never one on this scale.","Nearly every major figure in the domestic internet industry had shown up.","Besides the internet tycoons, the reporters also spotted a number of famous investors, including Ji Zhe of Qixing Capital and Chu Hai of AEG Capital.","The representatives of Hong Kong’s business world were naturally Zhang Ting and Xie Jichuan. The two tycoons had flown in from Hong Kong specifically to lend their support.","The reporters’ cameras began flashing wildly. After all, it was rare to see so many influential figures gathered in one place. If they didn’t take as many pictures as possible, when would they ever get another chance?","Ten minutes before the press conference was about to begin, another commotion erupted at the entrance.","Everyone turned in unison and saw a group of young men and women enter the venue. Each of them carried an extraordinary air, and sharp-eyed observers quickly recognized them.","“Holy crap! That’s Chu Junlin of the Chu family!”","“And there’s someone from the Shen family...”","“...”","“They’re all young masters and heiresses from the most powerful families!”","“...”","Most of these people were members of the Yunshan Society, along with several scions of prominent families from the imperial capital.","“This phone launch has connections that are practically against the heavens! It’s a brand-new company, yet it managed to invite all these people.”","“...”","In addition to business leaders and scions of aristocratic families, more and more familiar faces from the entertainment industry began arriving. Every one of them was a major celebrity.","“J Lun!”","“It’s J Lun! Oh my God, Xue Qian is here too!”","“They’re actually appearing together!”","“This is way too impressive!”","“...”","The reporters hurriedly readied their equipment and began snapping photos. The entertainment reporters were especially excited. This was guaranteed to make tomorrow’s headlines.","Once all the invited guests had taken their seats, many people stared at the lineup in the first few rows in a daze.","The guest list for this press conference could no longer be described as luxurious. It was a gathering of the stars.","The internet industry, Hong Kong’s business community, the investment world, the children of the country’s most powerful families, and the biggest names in entertainment were all represented.","This was unquestionably the most impressive lineup at a domestic phone launch in more than a decade. In fact, even across the entire technology sector of Long Kingdom, it would be difficult to find another event with such an extraordinary gathering of guests.","As the start of the press conference drew nearer, however, many people noticed one detail: the seat at the exact center of the first row remained empty.","Was there still someone who hadn’t arrived?","Was this person deliberately putting on airs?","Of course, some people speculated that the owner of the seat must have an incredibly powerful background. Otherwise, they wouldn’t dare arrive so late and make everyone wait.","“Could there really be someone even more important who hasn’t arrived yet?”","“That can’t be. Every major figure in the domestic internet industry is already here. Who could possibly have a bigger presence than them?”","“Could it be someone from the government?”","“No, that seat is clearly reserved for someone from the business world. But I honestly can’t think of anyone else.”","“...”","The reporters whispered among themselves, offering one guess after another.","Some said it might be the head of a state-owned enterprise. Others suggested a mysterious overseas investor. A few even joked that perhaps Jobs had flown over from Apple.","The reporter who made that remark received a withering look from a colleague. Everyone laughed, but afterward they still couldn’t help glancing at the empty seat.","As the reporters continued their quiet speculation, the rear of the venue suddenly fell silent.","Every reporter instinctively turned around.","The doors at the back of the hall had been pushed open.","A group of men in black filed in. They were all dressed in identical black suits, with silver dragon-shaped badges pinned to their chests. Their presence created an overwhelming sense of pressure.","A straight passage had been left open between the two lines of men.","Then a slender figure dressed in black appeared at the far end of the passage and walked toward them.","It was a woman.","No—more accurately, she was a girl.","She appeared to be barely twenty. She wore a tailored black suit and had delicate, exquisite features. Her bearing was cool and aloof, and she radiated an imposing authority that made people instinctively wary.","A golden dragon-shaped badge was pinned to her chest.","As she approached the first row, everyone in the hall turned their attention to her.","What happened next left even the reporters, who were accustomed to witnessing grand occasions, utterly astonished.","In the first row, the business magnates whose every move could send tremors through the entire internet industry—including Ma Yunyun, Pony Ma, Li Yanhong, Ding Sanshi, Cao Wei, Chen Sheng, and Zhang Yang—rose from their seats almost in perfect unison the moment they saw her.","It gave the strange impression of a classroom when the homeroom teacher walked in and all the students instinctively stood to attention.","Next, the representatives of Hong Kong’s business community, Zhang Ting and Xie Jichuan, stood as well.","The investment heavyweights—Ji Zhe, Chu Hai, Lei Yun, and the others—rose to their feet.","The entertainment celebrities stood too.","Even the young heirs and heiresses of the imperial capital’s most powerful families stood up. Chu Junlin led the way, followed by the young masters and young ladies of the Shen, Lin, and Gu families.","Once the influential figures in the front rows had all risen, the people from the technology media and the ordinary attendees followed suit.","After all, if the big shots were standing, remaining seated would seem rude and out of place.","At that moment, everyone in the hall was on their feet.","The reporters were completely shaken.","Although some of them had guessed from the insignia on the girl’s clothing that she was probably the chairwoman of the Wanlong Group, they had never actually seen her before. There were no photographs of her anywhere online—at most, one could find a few basic details about her.","One rookie reporter instinctively raised his camera, hoping to capture a close-up of the girl. But before he could press the shutter, a man in black stepped in front of the lens and raised a hand to block it.","“Sorry. Photography is prohibited.”","The rookie reporter’s hand trembled. He hurriedly lowered the camera, his face pale with fright.","The other reporters and audience members who had been about to raise their equipment were stopped as well.","Every camera in the room was blocked.","No filming was allowed.","No images could be recorded.","The reporters could only etch the sight before them—one so shocking it left them speechless—into their memories.","After reaching the front row, the girl shook hands and exchanged pleasantries with each of the industry heavyweights standing there.","With every handshake, the executives bowed slightly, adopting an exceptionally deferential posture.","Was this the legendary chairwoman of the Wanlong Group?","She was... she was incredible!","The reporters were at a loss for words. The first phrase that came to mind was the only one that seemed fitting:","Absolutely badass!","And why did they think she was so impressive? It was simple.","If, at the age of twenty, you could make so many business tycoons stand to welcome you—and be so respectful while doing it—you’d be pretty incredible too.","Once the girl sat down in the middle of the front row, the executives standing behind her finally took their seats as well.","The lights gradually dimmed, and the enormous screen slowly lit up.","Amid the eager anticipation of everyone present, a highly distinctive dragon emblem appeared on the screen.","The press conference officially began."]},{"number":880,"title":"Chapter 880: 881. A Smartphone Launch Event That Doesn't Follow the Script.","paragraphs":["According to the usual format of a product launch, the company typically spends a long time introducing the product first—its appearance, specifications, features, and user experience—going through everything point by point before finally announcing the price and saving the suspense for last.","However, what happened next took everyone completely by surprise.","At the start of Longyao’s launch event, a young man wearing black-rimmed glasses and exuding a refined, scholarly air walked onto the stage.","He was Qing Yuan, the man in charge of Longyao’s smartphone system development.","Yu Xin had personally recruited him back from Silicon Valley. He would be the keynote speaker at the Imperial Capital launch.","After taking the stage, Qing Yuan first thanked the guests who had come to attend the event, as was customary. Then, the first thing he said was:","“I know what everyone is most curious about.”","“So I’ve decided to announce the price first.”","The entire venue fell silent for a moment before erupting into an uproar.","“???”","“Announce the price first?”","“What kind of strategy is this? Who announces the price before we’ve even seen what the phone looks like?”","“Could it be that they lack confidence in their own product and want to keep people around with a low price?”","“Maybe. But if the product is no good, even a dirt-cheap price won’t help.”","“...”","The audience began whispering among themselves. Even the internet tycoons seated in the front rows wore intrigued expressions.","Only a young reporter in the corner, filming while muttering under his breath, seemed thrilled.","“Holy crap! This is bold! I’ve never seen a phone launch announce the price first!”","Qing Yuan didn’t waste any time. He lightly pressed the remote control in his hand, and a gigantic number appeared on the screen:","[3,999!]","The entire venue went quiet.","Not from surprise, but disappointment.","“3,999? A new domestic brand actually dares to charge that much?”","“Fruit 4 is around that price. Why would anyone buy yours?”","“I thought there’d be some kind of surprise. Announcing a price like that right off the bat—you’re a little too confident, aren’t you?”","“...”","The murmurs from the audience grew louder. Many reporters and invited members of the tech community wore disappointed expressions.","Looks like this was just another company chasing hype. No wonder they had invited so many big names to lend their presence—it was all for publicity.","A price of 3,999 yuan did have its market in China in 2010, and the potential customer base was hardly small. But this was a domestic brand—and a brand-new one at that.","To dare set the price so high was a little too arrogant.","Qing Yuan didn’t panic in the slightest at the audience’s reaction.","“This is merely the suggested retail price for this phone. Customers purchasing from the first batch will receive a certain discount.”","As he spoke, he pressed the remote again.","A red X appeared on the screen, striking through the previous number. A new figure then popped up:","[2,999!]","The entire venue fell silent once more.","Then, a burst of applause mixed with surprise and laughter erupted throughout the hall.","“2,999? That’s a full thousand less than 3,999!”","“That price is a lot more acceptable.”","“Yeah, 2,999 sounds much more reasonable than 3,999.”","“But the price alone doesn’t mean anything. We still have to see the specs.”","“...”","With nothing more than a change in price, they had instantly broken through the audience’s psychological barrier against an expensive domestic phone.","A price of 2,999 yuan was considered mainstream in the current smartphone market. It was nearly half the price of Fruit 4. If the specifications were decent as well, the phone was definitely worth looking forward to.","Clearly, Qing Yuan had no intention of stopping there. He smiled faintly and pressed the remote control again.","This time, the number on the screen disappeared, replaced by a line of bold, eye-catching text:","[We’ve prepared more than just a great price.]","A door at the side of the stage, which had been dark until then, suddenly opened. A spotlight snapped on and shone toward it.","A man in a tailored suit, his signature slicked-back pompadour unmistakable, walked out through the door.","The audience stared blankly for a moment before erupting into deafening screams.","“It’s Hua Shao!”","“Hua Shao from Dragon Nation’s Got Talent! What’s he doing here?”","“Wait, what’s he here for? He’s a host, not a product manager...”","Hua Shao took the microphone handed to him by a staff member and walked to the center of the stage. He gave the audience a playful wink.","“Didn’t see this coming, did you? I’m not here to host today. I’m here to give you some amazing freebies.”","He cleared his throat and took a deep breath.","Over the next thirty seconds, he rattled off a long list of perks at astonishing speed.","“Customers who purchase a Longyao phone from the first batch will receive a 200-yuan cash card for Wanlong Supermarket, 200 yuan’s worth of membership time at Fengquan Internet Cafés, 380 yuan’s worth of Longkan Vision services, an annual membership to Long Dimension Video, eligibility for a lottery to win VIP-section tickets to the season-two finale of Dragon Nation’s Got Talent, free delivery for an entire year from Wanhui Select, twelve complimentary drinks from Qingyin Tea, two discount vouchers from Yuyue House, one free screen protector application every six months, and one free replacement in the event of accidental screen damage within the first year! The total value of all these benefits exceeds 3,000 yuan! They’re available only to first-batch customers, and supplies are limited—act fast!”","The entire venue fell completely silent.","Wait—what had Hua Shao just said? Nobody had caught it all!","Qing Yuan deliberately joked, “Hua Shao, we prepared so many benefits, and you finished listing them in thirty seconds. Aren’t we going to lose a fortune?”","The audience burst into laughter.","“Would everyone like to hear it again?” Qing Yuan asked, turning toward the audience.","“Yes!”","This time, the response was remarkably loud and unified.","Hua Shao shrugged helplessly, raised the microphone again, and repeated the entire list of benefits at an even faster pace.","When he finished, he added deliberately, “That time only took twenty-five seconds.”","The audience immediately roared with laughter.","Qing Yuan put on an exaggeratedly troubled expression and asked, “Did everyone hear all that clearly?”","“No!”","The audience deliberately began to heckle him.","Qing Yuan shrugged. “Then there’s nothing I can do. If you didn’t hear it clearly, I can’t say it again. We haven’t even shown you the phone yet.”","In reality, some people might genuinely not have heard everything, but everyone certainly knew what the benefits were—the entire list was displayed on the giant screen behind them.","The exchange was simply meant to liven up the atmosphere and make the audience remember the perks more clearly.","The big names seated in the front rows were the first to react. They began whispering among themselves.","Lei Yun leaned toward Ji Zhe and murmured something. The two of them laughed at the same time.","Pony Ma, meanwhile, stared thoughtfully at Qing Yuan onstage, seemingly lost in thought.","Perhaps he was thinking about what Liu Yutong had said to him earlier when she shook his hand—asking why he had come.","Could there be any downside to his being here?","The internet tycoons, whose fortunes ranged from tens of billions to well over a hundred billion yuan, were the first to start applauding.","Then the media section joined in, followed by the entire venue.","“I just did the math. If you convert all those benefits into cash, it’s basically like getting the phone for free!”","“That’s insane! At this price, with all these benefits, they’re practically giving it away!”","“I just want to know when it goes on sale. I want those perks too!”","“You haven’t even seen the phone yet, and you’re already eager to buy it?”","“...”","At the very beginning, when the phone’s price was announced, most people’s first reaction had been that it was expensive.","Even after the thousand-yuan discount, it still seemed expensive.","It wasn’t because of the product itself. People simply felt that this was a domestic phone from a new brand.","Deep down, many people believed that only foreign giants—Apple, Samsung, Nokia, and the like—were worth buying at this price point. Although domestic brands such as Lenovo existed, they still hadn’t done much to change the public’s perception. “Made in China” was still synonymous with cheap, off-brand products—brands that could only make feature phones costing a few hundred yuan. Smartphones were a different matter altogether; they simply weren’t good enough to be taken seriously.","Unfortunately, that kind of ingrained prejudice couldn’t be overturned overnight. It would take time.","That was why no one thought the iPhone 4 was expensive, even when it sold for 5,000 yuan—or when scalpers drove the price up to 10,000 or even 20,000 yuan.","But when the first-generation Dragon Glory phone, the Dragon Glory S1, was priced at the same level, everyone thought it was too expensive.","Who in their right mind would spend 3,000 yuan on a domestic phone?","But now that they had seen all these benefits, people suddenly began to look at things differently.","Some had even started doing the math in their heads.","Hmm, these perks are actually pretty generous. If the specifications aren’t too bad, then this could be well worth buying.","Before long, once the applause had died down, Qing Yuan picked up the microphone again.","“I’m sure everyone is eager to see what our phone looks like and what kind of specifications it has.”","“So next, our president of the Technology Business Group, President Yu Xin, will introduce it to you.”","“Incidentally, this launch event is being held simultaneously around the world. President Yu Xin is currently holding a launch event in the United States. What you’re seeing here is a live broadcast, so you can see for yourselves what kind of reaction the Dragon Glory S1 receives in the Western market.”","The lights dimmed once again, and the large screen switched to a satellite broadcast.","The screen showed the Dragon Glory S1 launch event taking place in the United States.","Dressed in a black suit, Yu Xin stood on the stage at the Moscone Center in San Francisco, speaking confidently in a foreign language. Behind her was the same enormous dragon logo."]},{"number":881,"title":"Chapter 881: 882. Breaking News: Fruit Plagiarism","paragraphs":["The capital’s press conference venue.","On the giant screen, a live broadcast of the Longyao S1 launch event in the United States appeared.","Yu Xin, dressed in a black suit, stood at the center of the stage inside San Francisco’s Moscone Convention Center, speaking fluently in a foreign language.","Behind her was another enormous dragon-shaped logo.","“Now, let us witness the true face of the Longyao S1 together.”","Yu Xin smiled faintly and gently pressed the remote in her hand.","The image changed, and a 360-degree rendering of the Longyao S1 slowly appeared on the giant screen.","It had a black body, clean, angular lines, and subtly rounded corners. The front featured a 3.7-inch capacitive touchscreen, with a circular physical Home button embedded beneath it. The back was made of glass, with a camera and flash arranged in the upper-left corner and a delicate dragon-shaped logo in the exact center.","The entire venue fell silent.","Almost everyone stared wide-eyed at the Longyao S1 displayed on the screen.","A few seconds later, the entire hall erupted in an uproar as deafening as a tsunami.","“Holy crap! Am I seeing this right?!”","“How does this phone look exactly like the Fruit 4?”","“Other than the dragon logo on the back, the exterior, frame, buttons, and screen layout are all exact copies!”","“This is insane!”","“They’re selling a knockoff for 2,999?”","“Jobs is probably laughing his head off. He just launched a new phone, and someone’s already replicated it for free.”","“This is hilarious. They actually have the nerve to copy Fruit so blatantly.”","“...”","Inside the capital’s venue, chaos erupted. Countless reporters abruptly rose to their feet as camera shutters flashed furiously, and the entire scene instantly spiraled out of control.","Many of the big names from the tech industry seated below the stage frowned, unable to stop themselves from complaining inwardly.","That’s it?","Domestic phone manufacturers really never fail to disappoint.","At this point in 2010, the Fruit 4 was the pinnacle of smartphones—the absolute benchmark of technological aesthetics.","The revolutionary phone design personally defined by Jobs was considered unique and impossible to replicate.","Now, a brand-new domestic company had suddenly appeared with a phone that copied the design outright. In everyone’s eyes, it was cheap, shameless opportunism with absolutely no bottom line.","The internet tycoons seated in the front row wore various expressions of surprise.","They, too, could hardly believe that the first phone released by Wanlonghui Group would look like this. Yet the facts were right before their eyes: every detail in the rendering was virtually identical to the Fruit 4.","Still, they managed to restrain themselves. Rather than openly criticizing the phone like the other attendees, they all turned, almost in unison, toward the girl seated in the middle of the first row.","When they saw that her expression remained calm—and that she was even smiling—they grew puzzled.","Could she have another card up her sleeve?","On the other side of the world, the foreigners at the Moscone Convention Center were equally stunned.","“What? What’s the difference between this and the Fruit 4?”","“It’s exactly the same! Apart from the logo, it’s identical!”","“Has this Longguo company gone insane? They’re copying Fruit outright?”","“This is Longguo design? Isn’t this the new phone Fruit just unveiled a few days ago? They took someone else’s exterior, slapped on their own logo, and called it a new product?”","“My God, this is the first time I’ve seen a Longguo company be this bold. They’re actually launching a knockoff openly at an event like this.”","“How ridiculous!”","“...”","As the discussions below the stage neared the point of explosion, Yu Xin lightly tapped the microphone.","“Everyone, please calm down.”","“I know what you’re thinking. Hear me out first.”","Yu Xin’s voice rang throughout the venue through the speakers. The noisy crowd gradually quieted, and everyone wanted to see how the person in charge of Wanlonghui planned to explain this awkward situation.","“I also know that all of you must think the Longyao S1 copied the Fruit 4.”","“To be honest, when I first saw the leaked images of Fruit’s new phone, I was shocked too.”","“At the time, I thought, How could there be such a coincidence?”","“But later, I figured it out. The reason the Fruit 4 copied the exterior of our Longyao S1 is actually quite understandable.”","???","???","Countless question marks seemed to spring above the heads of the audience.","Wait.","What had this girl just said?","Fruit copied Longyao?","It wasn’t Longyao copying Fruit, but Fruit copying Longyao?","“Perhaps truly great designs shine like fireflies in the darkness. No matter where they hide, they always attract everyone’s attention.","“Fruit’s design team probably saw the design plans for our Longyao S1 and was blinded by their radiance. They got so excited that they couldn’t help but borrow the design.”","A restrained wave of laughter swept through the audience.","This woman was vicious. Everyone knew that Longyao had copied Fruit, yet she could claim—without the slightest embarrassment—that Fruit had copied Longyao. She even said that Fruit had been blinded by the brilliance of Longyao’s design.","“I know you don’t believe me. If I were in your shoes, I wouldn’t believe it either.”","“So, now, please look at the giant screen.”","Yu Xin pressed the remote again, and the image changed once more.","Two documents appeared side by side on the giant screen. On the left was Longyao S1’s exterior design patent application; on the right was Fruit 4’s publicly disclosed exterior design patent document. The key dates in both documents were highlighted.","Longyao S1’s exterior design patent application date: December, XXX year.","Fruit 4’s exterior design patent publication date: July, XXX year.","Longyao S1’s application had been filed a full six months before Fruit 4’s patent was made public.","Boom!","The moment they saw the patent application date, everyone at both the capital venue and the San Francisco venue erupted.","Longyao’s patent was actually more than six months older than the Fruit 4’s?","It was almost impossible to believe.","Yet Yu Xin’s next words were the true killing blow.","“As you can see, we have registered the exterior design patent in all major countries and regions around the world, including East Continent, West Continent, and North America. So, as for who copied whom, I believe the answer is self-evident.”","At this point, Yu Xin deliberately adopted a joking tone.","“But it’s all right. Wanlonghui Group is a very magnanimous company, so we have no intention of pursuing Fruit or Mr. Jobs for patent infringement, nor will we demand exorbitant licensing fees.","“Longyao is willing to grant Fruit a free license for this exterior design patent. We have only one requirement: Fruit must publicly acknowledge that the two designs are identical and issue a formal written apology.","“One statement in exchange for a free patent license. How does that sound? Aren’t we being reasonable?”","When the tech-industry bigwigs, reporters, and ordinary spectators in the audience heard this, they were all left speechless.","Was it reasonable? On the surface, yes.","But in reality, anyone could see that this was a massive strategic trap.","If Jobs really issued a public apology, it would amount to admitting before the entire world that Apple had copied the design of a Dragon Nation smartphone. Apple’s aura of greatness would shatter overnight.","But if Jobs refused to apologize, Apple would have to face a multinational patent-infringement lawsuit.","Although Longyao had said it would not pursue the matter, that was the sort of statement one should take with a grain of salt. They were all adults—anyone who took it seriously would be a fool.","In short, no matter what Apple chose, there was only one outcome: the Longyao S1 would ride Apple’s coattails and become famous overnight.","That was a truly ruthless move!","“All right, that’s enough about the design,” Yu Xin said, clapping her hands. In a relaxed tone, she smoothly brought the topic back on track. “Next, let’s take a look at the Longyao S1’s hardware specifications.”","The image on the big screen changed once again, displaying the Longyao S1’s detailed specifications one by one.","“The Longyao S1 features a 3.7-inch capacitive touchscreen with a resolution of 480 by 800 pixels. Its processor is our independently developed LX-A1 chip, based on the ARM architecture, with a clock speed of 800 MHz. It integrates a PowerVR SGX530 graphics processor and comes with 512 megabytes of RAM and 8 gigabytes of internal storage. The rear camera is a 5-megapixel autofocus camera that supports video recording, while the front-facing camera has 300,000 pixels and supports video calls. The battery has a capacity of 1,800 mAh, providing up to a day and a half of battery life under normal use.”","The previous-generation Mi 1 seemed to have used the same 480-by-800 resolution. Although it could not compare with the stunning Retina display on the iPhone 4, at this point in 2010, it was still far ahead of the competition.","With an independently developed chip, a 5-megapixel camera, and a large 1,800 mAh battery, those specifications placed the phone firmly in the upper midrange—or even higher—of the current smartphone market.","“Beyond the hardware, our biggest highlight is another specially recommended application installed on the Longyao S1.”","The moment Yu Xin finished speaking, the large screen behind her abruptly switched images.","A pitch-black cosmic background instantly filled the entire display. Then, a huge blue planet slowly emerged.","It was WeChat’s startup screen: one person, one Earth, and a sense of loneliness and longing for connection distilled to the barest simplicity.","The startup screen alone instantly seized everyone’s attention. It was especially striking.","“WeChat—a brand-new instant-messaging tool for mobile phones.”","The moment those words appeared, Pony Ma’s expression changed in the imperial capital venue.","Oh, no! This was clearly aimed straight at him!"]},{"number":882,"title":"Chapter 882: 883, An Explosively Awesome Phone Launch Event","paragraphs":["“MicroChat—a brand-new mobile instant-messaging app.”","Yu Xin walked to the center of the stage with a smile. She lightly tapped the controller in her hand, and the live display from her phone appeared on the giant screen.","“MicroChat’s biggest innovation is its voice-message function. All you have to do is press and hold the recording button at the bottom of the screen, say what you want to say, and release it. The message will be sent automatically.”","She pressed the recording button and softly said into her phone, “Hello to all our friends in San Francisco.”","A green voice-message bar appeared on the giant screen. She tapped it lightly.","“Hello to all our friends in San Francisco.”","The sound was clear and smooth, without the slightest trace of static.","“In addition, MicroChat supports a social network built around the contacts already saved on your phone. Once you register, any friends in your address book who have already activated MicroChat will automatically appear in your friend list. There’s no need to memorize complicated account numbers—you can add them with a single tap and start chatting right away.”","“MicroChat also includes social-entertainment features such as Drift Bottle and Shake It. Shake your phone, and you’ll be matched with new friends who are shaking theirs at the same time. Any bottle you toss into the digital sea may be picked up by a random user, and you can also retrieve messages from bottles tossed by others.”","“Of course, MicroChat does have one fairly practical drawback at the moment: voice messages and image transfers consume a relatively large amount of mobile data. Without Wi-Fi, users may see their phone bills go up.”","At this point, Yu Xin deliberately paused for several seconds and swept her gaze across the audience.","“To address this issue, the Wanlonghui Group has reached partnerships overseas with Sprint and T-Mobile. Here in China, we’ve also entered into comprehensive partnerships with all three major telecom operators. Any Longyao S1 user who signs up for one of the designated data plans will receive an exclusive subsidy. Any data usage beyond the plan will be fully covered by the Wanlonghui Group, so users won’t have to pay a single extra cent. For specific plan details, please visit the Longyao official website or one of our physical stores.”","“To put it plainly: once you buy a Longyao S1, you’ll never have to worry about data charges again.”","The moment she said this, the audience erupted into enthusiastic applause.","After all, in 2010, mobile data was outrageously expensive both in China and abroad. Many people could afford a smartphone but still refused to activate a data plan.","Yet the Wanlonghui Group had actually partnered directly with telecom operators and agreed to subsidize the cost of mobile data.","Of course, while the domestic plan covered all major operators, the overseas arrangement was limited to selected carriers and was therefore less convenient. Even so, the sheer number of operators they had managed to negotiate with was enough to make people wonder just how much power stood behind the company.","“Now that we’ve covered the hardware and software, let’s take a look at the accessories and see how much value Longyao is offering there.”","Yu Xin tapped the remote again. The screen displayed everything included inside the phone’s packaging.","“An official silicone case, a tempered-glass screen protector, a pair of wired 3.5-millimeter earphones with in-line controls, a charger, a data cable, a SIM-eject tool, and the user manual... Combined with the carrier data subsidy, the total value received by customers who purchase during the first launch phase exceeds 3,000 yuan.”","She repeated the value of the benefits once more.","Yu Xin set down the remote and looked at the countless astonished faces below her. Smiling, she said, “I know what you’re thinking. You’re wondering how a new phone brand like Longyao can offer so many benefits. Are we burning money?”","“To be honest, yes, we are.”","“But Longyao isn’t asking you to take advantage of a bargain and walk away. What we need is an opportunity—an opportunity to get users around the world to give us a try. Because once you do, you’ll discover that this phone is no worse than any international flagship. Its system runs smoothly, its processor is more than capable, its battery lasts, its camera takes crisp photos, its voice messages are convenient, and even its design has been copied by someone else.”","“Hahaha...”","The audience burst into laughter. Only the representatives from the invited Fruit Company sat there with faces as dark as the bottom of a cooking pot.","Yu Xin laughed along with them onstage, then slowly composed herself and solemnly emphasized the price.","“More importantly, it isn’t expensive.”","“The domestic price of the Longyao S1 is 2,999 yuan.”","“The overseas price is 399 U.S. dollars.”","The lights suddenly dimmed.","The curved screen at the center of the stage slowly rose, while a golden spotlight slanted down from the ceiling and landed perfectly on the enormous dragon-shaped logo behind Yu Xin.","“And that’s not all.”","“Before the final minute of today’s launch day arrives, we’re offering one more limited-time benefit. For the next 72 hours, anyone who pre-orders a Longyao S1 can trade in any old phone that still powers on and lights up the screen.”","“No matter what brand it is, what model it is, or what condition it’s in—even if it’s a basic phone worth only a few dozen yuan—as long as it can turn on and display something on the screen, it will qualify for a 1,000-yuan cash discount. Overseas customers will receive the equivalent of 100 U.S. dollars.”","“In other words, bring us any beat-up old phone and you can take home a Longyao S1 for just 1,999 yuan. Overseas customers will pay only 299 U.S. dollars.”","A collective gasp swept through the venue, and the hair on many people’s arms stood on end.","After all those benefits, they were still offering another 1,000-yuan discount through a trade-in program?","This was practically giving the phone away...","No, this was even more outrageous than giving it away!","“Ladies and gentlemen of the press, and all our honored guests, that concludes today’s launch event.”","“I hereby announce that the Longyao S1 has officially launched worldwide!”","“The 72-hour trade-in promotion is now in effect!”","The stage lights suddenly blazed to life.","Thunderous applause and cheers once again erupted throughout the venue.","What an incredible presentation! It had been absolutely spectacular!","They had never seen a phone launch this exciting before. It had completely blown the roof off!","At the front of the Imperial Capital venue, all the industry heavyweights were applauding so hard their hands were nearly swollen.","Lei Yun was clapping the hardest of them all. He was preparing to make phones himself, so he knew better than anyone how difficult it was to build a phone brand in China.","And today, a young woman standing halfway around the world had used a single Longyao S1 to shatter every doubt and criticism aimed at the company.","The launch had also given him countless ideas and filled him with even greater confidence in the upcoming launch of the Rice S1.","Of course, most importantly of all, the Fruit Company had truly run into trouble this time."]},{"number":883,"title":"Chapter 883: 884. Here It Comes Again and Again","paragraphs":["After the launch event ended, the backstage lounge was already packed with people.","Liu Yutong had just been escorted into the lounge through a side entrance by Yuncheng, Blue Butterfly, and the others when a group of industry heavyweights closed in around her as if they had planned it.","Lei Yun was the first to speak.","The man who would one day build the Dami empire wore an expression of genuine admiration.","“Chairwoman Liu, today’s launch event really opened my eyes. Especially that trade-in offer at the end—one thousand yuan for any old phone. That was a ruthless move. I’m already feeling sorry for Apple.”","Liu Yutong smiled. “You’re too kind, Mr. Lei. When your Dami 1 launches, I’ll personally attend the event and lend my support.”","Lei Yun’s eyes lit up. “Then it’s a promise!”","After exchanging a few pleasantries, Lei Yun tactfully stepped aside.","Next came Ma Yunyun, Li Yanhong, Ding Sanshi, and several others, each taking turns to offer their congratulations. One piece of polite small talk followed another, and Liu Yutong handled them all with ease, a smile never leaving her face.","It wasn’t until a somewhat gaunt figure squeezed his way forward that she raised an eyebrow.","Pony Ma.","The head of Big Goose and the undisputed ruler of China’s internet-based social networking sector. Yet there wasn’t the slightest trace of a smile on his face. If anything, he looked rather anxious.","“Chairwoman Liu, congratulations. The launch was a great success.” Pony Ma extended his hand.","Liu Yutong shook it, then looked at him with an amused, knowing smile. “Mr. Ma, I recall that you usually dislike attending events like this. What brings you here today?”","The corner of Pony Ma’s mouth twitched.","Why do you think I came?","The Wanlong Association had invited everyone in the internet industry—everyone except him.","This ticket had only been obtained after he swallowed his pride and went through several layers of connections.","Fortunately, he had come.","If he hadn’t, he might not even have known what had killed him.","But there was no way he could say that to her face. All he could do was give an awkward laugh.","“Chairwoman Liu, you’re joking. I simply wanted to see how far a homegrown Chinese smartphone brand could go. I have to say, the Longyao S1 is truly impressive. Both its specifications and its price are far beyond what I expected.”","Then he changed the subject and brought up WeChat.","“Chairwoman Liu, I’d like to know about your WeChat...”","Liu Yutong pretended not to understand. “What about WeChat?”","Pony Ma said, “Chairwoman Liu, let’s be frank. Big Goose has been deeply involved in instant messaging for many years, and you should be well aware of QQ’s user base. WeChat has entered the market with voice messaging and mobile contact synchronization as its core features. It’s directly targeting our core business. This is no longer a simple matter of competition.”","“To be honest, I thought I was only coming to watch a smartphone launch today. I never expected the Wanlong Association to quietly develop something like this. I have to admit, it’s rather alarming.”","He was speaking from the heart.","QQ was unquestionably the dominant force in Chinese social networking, but its foundation was on the PC. In 2010, the mobile version of QQ offered a truly miserable experience: a bloated interface, sluggish response times, and excessive battery consumption. Most fatal of all, its account system depended on a string of numerical QQ IDs.","WeChat, by contrast, linked directly to users’ mobile contact lists. That single step was practically a dimensional strike.","What truly sent a chill down Pony Ma’s spine was WeChat’s voice-messaging feature.","At the launch event, he had personally watched Yu Xin demonstrate a voice message sent across the ocean. At that moment, only one thought had flashed through his mind:","Once this thing gained traction, QQ’s mobile platform would be finished.","Looking at Pony Ma’s grim expression, Liu Yutong suddenly laughed.","“Mr. Ma, I remember congratulating you when Big Goose Weibo launched last year.”","“Now that the Wanlong Association has launched WeChat, shouldn’t you congratulate me as well?”","Pony Ma: “...”","Can I say that I regret creating Weibo?","When Big Goose Weibo had burst onto the scene the previous year, it had been obvious that it was targeting Weibo.","At the time, Pony Ma had slammed his hand on the table during an internal meeting and declared that they would take half of Weibo’s users within three months. He had even confidently greeted Liu Yutong in person.","Her response had indeed been remarkably magnanimous. She had even said, “Competition is welcome. Let’s work together to grow the market.”","Her gracious attitude had led him to believe, for a time, that he had found a rare kindred spirit. He had even been touched for quite a while.","Only now did he finally understand.","That woman had been holding back a devastating counterattack all along, waiting for the perfect moment to strike.","“Chairwoman Liu, you’re joking. Weibo is Weibo, and WeChat is WeChat. They can’t be lumped together.”","“Mr. Ma, we’ve known each other for quite some time. Just say what you really came here to say.”","That was exactly what Pony Ma had been waiting to hear.","“Chairwoman Liu, I personally welcome your entry into social networking. But I want to point out that although this field may look lively, it’s extremely difficult to do well. The cost of migrating user relationship networks, the scalability of the technical architecture, the stability of server clusters, the concurrent processing of massive volumes of messages... There are simply too many pitfalls. WeChat may look impressive right now, but once its user base reaches a certain scale, one problem after another will emerge.”","“What I’m saying is, rather than burning through money and fighting each other to the death, why don’t we cooperate? Big Goose’s cloud services, CDN nodes, and anti-spam systems are already in place, and they’re the most mature in the country. If WeChat connects to Big Goose’s infrastructure, its costs could be cut by at least half, while its stability would be guaranteed.”","After listening to him, Liu Yutong nodded seriously.","Pony Ma wasn’t trying to bluff her. Social networking products did have extremely high technical barriers, and Big Goose’s accumulated expertise in that area was unquestionably in a league of its own domestically.","However, she had no intention of accepting his proposal.","“I know everything you’ve mentioned, Mr. Ma, and I agree with you.”","“As for cooperation, I think I’ll seriously consider your proposal on the day WeChat’s user base surpasses QQ’s.”","The day it surpassed QQ?","Pony Ma nearly choked.","QQ currently had close to one billion registered users and roughly five hundred million monthly active users. It was, without question, the social networking empire of China’s internet.","WeChat, meanwhile, was a new product that had been in internal testing for less than half a year. Its official version had only just launched alongside the Longyao S1, and it probably had no more than a million registered users at most.","Between a few million users and one billion lay an insurmountable gulf.","But Pony Ma didn’t dare take that gamble.","After all, based on what he currently knew about Liu Yutong, not a single thing this woman had done seemed to have failed.","A hundred-percent success rate in entrepreneurship was terrifying enough.","Since she dared to say that WeChat would surpass QQ, she might truly have the confidence to make it happen.","Pony Ma remained silent for a long time. In the end, he sighed and made his position clear.","“Chairwoman Liu, in that case, we’ll have to meet in the market.”","“We’ll see who’s stronger on the battlefield. But we can still be friends.” Liu Yutong smiled and extended her hand.","The two shook hands, and Pony Ma hurriedly turned and left.","The moment he was gone, several other people eagerly crowded around.","Leading them was Ji Zhe of Qixing Capital, followed by Chu Hai of AEG Capital.","Both men were renowned figures in the domestic investment circle and among the earliest investors to place their bets on projects under the Wanlonghui Group.","When they first met Liu Yutong in Pearl City, she had persuaded each of them to invest a sum of money in exchange for partial stakes in several projects, including Huangquan Internet Café, Wanhui Youxuan, and Weibo.","Although neither of them held a particularly large stake in any one company, they had been both astonished and delighted to discover that every one of those investments had turned out to be a success. Even the Longxin Semiconductor project—the one that had burned through the most money and taken the longest to mature—had finally gotten on track and begun generating its own cash flow.","Based on current market valuations, the money they had invested back then had increased by at least several times, perhaps even more than tenfold.","But that was also where the problem lay.","Their investments had appreciated, but they had never been able to cash out their shares.","The agreements they had signed at the time clearly stated, in black and white, that the shares they held could not be transferred independently. Any transfer required Liu Yutong’s written consent.","In other words, if Liu Yutong did not give them the green light, they could forget about finding someone else to take over their shares.","That left only one ideal way to cash out: taking the companies public.","Once a company was listed, they could do whatever they wanted with their shares after the lock-up period ended, and they would also have something to report to their LPs.","Unfortunately, Liu Yutong’s attitude toward going public had always been impossible to read.","Wanhui Youxuan had met the listing requirements long ago. Weibo had exceeded its user-growth targets for two consecutive years, and its revenue was equally impressive. Yet every time they were filled with anticipation, thinking an IPO could finally be launched, Liu Yutong would casually say a few words and put a stop to it.","She had left them stuck in limbo, and it was driving them crazy.","What made matters worse was that, aside from their investments in Wanlonghui Group progressing smoothly, their other investment projects had been doing poorly over the past two years.","Some had been dragged down by industry-wide downturns, while others had suffered because of problems within their founding teams. Several projects had gone under just last year and this year, costing them a considerable amount of money. The pressure on their funds was becoming very real.","Chu Hai, in particular, was only the head of AEG Capital’s Longguo division, with the headquarters watching over him from above.","AEG Capital had run into some problems overseas as well. Although those issues had not yet affected the independent operations of the Longguo division, Chu Hai wanted to be prepared. He wanted more high-quality assets in his hands—assets that could be liquidated at any time.","“Chairwoman Liu, today’s product launch was a tremendous success. We’re extremely optimistic about the prospects of the Longyao S1.”","“That said, shouldn’t we also start considering taking Wanhui Youxuan and Weibo public? They’ve been operating for almost two years now, and all their metrics have reached the requirements for listing. If we wait any longer, we may miss the optimal window.”","“That’s right, Chairwoman Liu. Several of my LPs have been pressing me for answers and asking when Wanhui Youxuan will finally go public.”","Liu Yutong found it amusing to watch the two men sing the same tune.","Even so, she still had no intention of taking the companies public.","It wasn’t that she had anything against money. The truth was, Wanlonghui Group genuinely wasn’t short of cash right now.","The cash flow of its six major business divisions was extremely healthy. On top of that, the various investment funds under her control were all flush with capital. The group had plenty of money to use without going public.","More importantly, some of the things she was working on were highly sensitive. If the companies went public, they would inevitably have to disclose certain information. After weighing everything carefully, she had decided to hold off for now.","She would consider listing them once the timing was right.","“President Ji, President Chu, I’ve been considering the matter of going public all along, but the timing still isn’t quite right.”","“Please wait a little longer. Once WeChat reaches one hundred million users and Longxin begins mass-producing forty-five-nanometer chips, we can sit down and have a serious discussion about going public.”","Ji Zhe and Chu Hai exchanged a glance, both thinking the same thing.","As expected.","She was brushing them off with another convenient excuse.","And this wasn’t the first time, either. Every time they brought up the subject, she simply stalled them.","“Chairwoman Liu, could you at least give us a rough timeline? Even if you told us to wait another two or three years, we’d have something to report to our LPs.”","Liu Yutong thought for a moment before saying, “How about this? Within the next five years, if the right opportunity comes along, I’ll consider launching an IPO.”","“However, if we still can’t go public within five years, don’t worry. At worst, I’ll buy back the shares you hold at market value. I guarantee you won’t lose money.”","Upon hearing this, Ji Zhe and Chu Hai let out a simultaneous sigh of relief.","Whatever else could be said, Liu Yutong had at least given them a promise.","“Fine. With your word, Chairwoman Liu, we can rest easy.”","“Then we’ll take our leave for now.”","Ji Zhe was just about to pull Chu Hai away when Liu Yutong called out to them.","“President Ji, President Chu, since you’re already here, don’t rush off. Let me tell you about another new project.”","The two men: ???","Again?","How many times had this happened now?","How many times?","How many?","Many times?","Times?","?"]},{"number":884,"title":"Chapter 884: 885. Whoever looks for Liu Yutong again is a dog","paragraphs":["Ji Zhe and Chu Hai looked absolutely miserable, like they were both constipated.","Damn it, not again!","Could they please stop doing this?","Every time they were about to discuss the IPO, Liu Yutong would reach into their wallets... No, that wasn’t quite right. She would make them hand their wallets over to her themselves.","She acted as if their money belonged to her anyway, without the slightest hint of embarrassment.","They complained inwardly, of course, but they would never dare say any of it to her face.","“Chairwoman Liu, are you saying you have some promising project in mind?”","“You’re both veterans of the investment world. You must have noticed the wave of mobile internet development lately, haven’t you?” Liu Yutong asked.","Ji Zhe nodded. “Absolutely. This year alone, I’ve received more than a hundred business plans from mobile-internet startups. Smartphone shipments are setting new records every month, and the number of 3G users is on the verge of surpassing one hundred million. The entire sector is heating up. The outlook is indeed very promising.”","He wasn’t making that up.","The year 2010 was widely regarded by the industry as the dawn of the mobile internet era. The release of the iPhone 4 had ignited the global smartphone market, while the Android camp had begun accelerating its efforts. Meanwhile, the country’s three major telecom operators were forging ahead with their 3G network construction. A brand-new mobile internet age was rapidly approaching.","Everyone knew the windfall was coming. But exactly where the pigs riding that wind would fly was something very few people could predict yet.","“The new project I want to launch will be a next-generation content distribution platform based on the mobile internet.”","“Put simply, it will use algorithms to deliver personalized news and information based on each user’s interests and behavior. Instead of relying on traditional editorial recommendations, we’ll have machines learn every user’s preferences. Different people will see different content—each person will have a completely personalized feed.”","Ji Zhe and Chu Hai exchanged bewildered looks.","Algorithmic recommendations? Personalized content delivery?","What on earth was that?","In both the domestic and international markets of 2010, these two concepts were practically unexplored territory.","China’s major portal websites were still relying on editors to manually arrange their headlines. Search engines were still using keyword matching to handle paid rankings. No one had seriously considered using machine-learning algorithms to rebuild the fundamental logic of content distribution.","Even in Silicon Valley, the idea was still largely confined to academic papers and experimental projects run by a handful of small teams.","Seeing their blank expressions, Liu Yutong wasn’t in a hurry.","The original inspiration for this idea had naturally come from the company known in her previous life as Zijie—a giant that had begun its meteoric rise in 2012 and eventually reached a valuation of hundreds of billions of dollars.","Zijie’s Toutiao had completely overturned the traditional news-app landscape, while Yinfu’s meteoric rise had pushed algorithmic recommendations to the extreme, showing the entire world what it meant to become a black hole for user attention.","It was only natural that people couldn’t understand these concepts at this point. It would have been strange if they had.","“This sounds a bit like Weibo, doesn’t it?” Ji Zhe asked.","Liu Yutong nodded. “They’re completely different.”","“Weibo is a social network driven by follower relationships and key opinion leaders. This product, however, will rely on an algorithmic engine. It will be data-driven. Every click, every second a user spends on a post, every swipe—they’ll all be recorded by the system and turned into fuel for training the model. The longer someone uses it, the better the system will understand them, and the more accurately it will recommend content.”","The two men still looked as though they understood only half of what she was saying, so she switched to a more direct explanation.","“In other words, it’ll know what you like to watch better than your own mothers do.”","Ji Zhe: “...”","Chu Hai: “...”","The analogy was crude, but the two of them instantly understood.","“Besides news and information, the platform will also incubate a new short-video product.”","“For example, users will be able to casually shoot a video on their phones, add music, filters, and special effects, and finish creating it within fifteen seconds. These short videos will likewise be recommended to users who might be interested in them, creating an entirely new way to consume content.”","Fifteen-second short videos?","Ji Zhe instinctively wanted to ask, Who would watch something like that?","But the words reached his lips and he forcibly swallowed them.","His past experience had taught him that whenever this woman in front of him believed in a project, no matter how outrageous it sounded at first, the market would ultimately prove her absolutely right.","From the early days of internet cafés, to Weibo, to today’s phone launch event, every single time had been the same. There had never been an exception.","He could either believe her or believe her. He had no choice.","“Chairwoman Liu, how much do you plan to have us invest in this project?” Chu Hai couldn’t help asking the most important question.","Liu Yutong casually raised one finger. “The two of you need to invest ten billion yuan in total.”","“Ten billion!”","Chu Hai nearly jumped out of his chair.","A brand-new software company, with its business model not even fully developed and its team not yet assembled—and all they had was a concept. Yet she was opening her mouth and demanding ten billion yuan?","Was she kidding?","This wasn’t fundraising. This was daylight robbery!","“Chairwoman Liu, are you serious?”","Liu Yutong glanced at him. Her expression clearly said: Do I look like I’m joking?","“Completely serious.”","“However, Mr. Chu will need to provide the larger share—no less than eight billion yuan.”","Chu Hai completely lost his composure. “Wait, why? Why do I have to put up the larger share? Old Ji is wealthy too!”","He couldn’t understand it. They were both investors, so why were they being treated so differently?","Or did he really look like an easy mark?","Ji Zhe: “???”","Shut up already!","“Mr. Chu, don’t talk nonsense. I’m not as rich as you. Chairwoman Liu’s decision is perfectly sound. I’ll put up the two billion yuan.”","He agreed so readily that it was as if he were afraid Liu Yutong would change her mind if he waited even a second.","Chu Hai nearly passed out.","Damn you. Why did you agree so quickly?","Now that you’ve agreed, I don’t even have room to negotiate.","Ji Zhe had his own calculations to make.","He had no choice but to agree. If Chu Hai couldn’t withstand the pressure and backed out, there was a good chance the larger share of eight billion yuan would fall on him instead. That would put him under even greater pressure.","Rather than let that happen, he might as well sell out his good friend first.","Better his friend die than him.","Besides, even Ji Zhe felt that launching a new project with ten billion yuan was simply too outrageous, even if the idea had come from Liu Yutong. They weren’t acquiring an established physical industry. How could a new venture possibly need that much money at the very beginning?","But he didn’t dare ask.","“Chairwoman Liu, may I ask why?” Chu Hai said.","“Because AEG Capital has foreign investment behind it.”","With that single sentence, Chu Hai fell silent.","He seemed to understand what Liu Yutong meant.","In the field of online content, investment institutions with foreign backing were naturally subject to greater policy restrictions and regulatory scrutiny.","This was especially true for powerful new-media formats such as personalized content recommendations and short videos. Foreign shareholders often created additional obstacles for companies when it came to obtaining licenses and operating in compliance with regulations.","Liu Yutong’s higher demand was, to a certain extent, asking them to pay an additional risk premium.","Beyond that, she might also be planning to expand into overseas markets at the same time.","Otherwise, there would have been no reason for her to make him put up so much money.","Chu Hai had only guessed half the truth. Short-video platforms were certainly going to expand into overseas markets in the future.","But that wasn’t Liu Yutong’s real objective. She had actually set her sights on AEG Capital’s overseas operations—in other words, AEG headquarters. Her plan was to squeeze AEG’s Longguo branch so aggressively that it would be unable to keep sending money to headquarters. Then she would have a chance to acquire AEG Capital outright.","AEG might not be as famous as Gao Sheng and the other major investment firms, but it was still a huge organization. More importantly, it had an extensive network of contacts overseas, and every one of its LPs was a major player in their own right.","However, AEG seemed to have run into difficulties in recent years and might even be on the verge of a major crisis. In her previous life, it had managed to pull through thanks to financial support from its Longguo branch. This time, she intended to drain the branch’s cash flow in advance, preventing it from sending money overseas. Then she would see whether she could find an opportunity to acquire AEG.","If she could successfully take over AEG, her influence overseas would increase dramatically.","That was also one of the reasons she wanted to delay the IPO.","As long as the company didn’t go public, there would be no way for them to raise money and replenish their cash reserves.","Of course, she wasn’t about to tell Chu Hai any of this.","Judging from the look in Liu Yutong’s eyes, Chu Hai understood that he had no choice. He would have to come up with the money whether he wanted to or not.","But honestly, he still felt that eight billion yuan was far too much.","Normally, even the best projects would need several rounds of financing to reach that kind of scale. Yet Chairwoman Liu had merely presented them with a concept. They hadn’t even seen a product prototype, and she was already asking them to put up that much money.","What if it failed? What if they had misjudged the project this time?","What Chu Hai didn’t know was that failure was impossible.","The ten billion yuan they were investing was already a bargain. Once the project took off and its valuation began to skyrocket, even if they begged to get in with ten billion U.S. dollars, she might not be interested.","“President Ji, President Chu, that’s the first matter. There’s a second one,” Liu Yutong said.","The two men stared at her.","There was more?!","Liu Yutong continued, “For Wanhui Youxuan’s next round of financing, President Ji, your side will put up five billion yuan, while President Chu, your side will put up twenty billion.”","Ji Zhe fell silent.","Chu Hai fell silent as well.","Chu Hai quietly pressed a hand to his chest, feeling his blood pressure shoot upward at an uncontrollable rate.","Eight billion plus twenty billion—twenty-eight billion yuan in total.","If he really paid out that much, his ammunition stockpile would be completely drained. He might even have to liquidate some of his shares.","Ji Zhe was in a slightly better position. His total contribution would only come to seven billion yuan, more than twenty billion less than Chu Hai’s.","Thinking of that, he actually began to feel a little sorry for his fellow sufferer beside him.","“Chairwoman Liu, may I ask what this money is for?” Chu Hai asked.","“To wage war,” Liu Yutong replied succinctly.","“You’ve probably noticed that more and more group-buying websites have been appearing on the market recently. There are at least a thousand of them, large and small, and more and more investors are pouring in. Don’t I have to keep them under control?”","The year 2010 would later be known as the beginning of the “Thousand Group-Buying War.”","After Wanhui Youxuan’s group-buying model became a runaway success, it quickly set off an explosion throughout the entire internet startup and investment world.","For a time, entrepreneurs from the capital to Shenzhen rushed into the sector. Group-buying websites, large and small, sprang up like weeds.","Capital from every direction also scrambled to pour money into the market. Advertising wars, subsidy wars, and ground-promotion wars raged with such intensity that the entire industry descended into chaos.","Although Wanhui Youxuan currently held the undisputed top position in the group-buying industry, leading by a wide margin in both user numbers and partner merchants, its market share would eventually be eroded if it failed to keep investing in defense against more than a thousand competitors burning money at a frantic pace.","The group-buying sector had never been a place where early-mover advantage guaranteed an easy victory. Its defenses had to be built with truckload after truckload of real cash.","To protect its position in the market, she had to crush all those copycats.","It was impossible to eliminate every last one of them, but she absolutely would not allow Wanhui Youxuan to fall to second place.","She simply didn’t want to burn through all her own money. Her funds could play a much greater role elsewhere.","And since these two men happened to be sitting in front of her, she might as well burn their money first. Their cash was just sitting idle anyway.","Just as Chu Hai was at a loss for what to do, Liu Yutong spoke again.","“Of course, you do have another option: raise the money and pursue an IPO.”","Both men’s eyes lit up at once.","But Liu Yutong’s next sentence immediately shut that door again.","“However, I should warn you that the IPO valuations of Wanhui Youxuan and Weibo may not deliver the returns you’re expecting. Far too many rivals are watching us. Big Goose, Ali, Baidu—none of them are pushovers. They’ll certainly take advantage of the window before and after the IPO to launch a vicious attack.","“When that happens, not only might you be unable to sell your shares at a good price, but they could also join forces to short the stock. In the end, you might lose both your money and your shares.”","Ji Zhe and Chu Hai fell silent.","They knew Liu Yutong was telling the truth.","Going public had never been a cure-all. For a star company at the center of a storm, an IPO often meant exposing all its cards to the outside world. The slightest misstep could give others an opportunity to seize on a weakness and crush it.","And their opponents were all industry giants. None of them could be called charitable.","“So instead of handing your fate over to the stock price on the secondary market, you might as well keep it in your own hands.”","“I guarantee that within three years at most, those miscellaneous armies will disappear completely. At most, two or three players will survive to the end. By then, it shouldn’t be difficult for Wanhui Youxuan’s valuation to increase several dozen times over.”","Three years. Several dozen times the valuation.","That figure was enough to make any investor’s heart race.","Especially when it came from Liu Yutong—a woman who had never suffered a setback since starting her first business.","After a long silence, Ji Zhe was the first to speak.","“I’m in. Let’s do it!”","Chu Hai glanced at him, then at Liu Yutong. Finally, he nodded as well.","“I’m in too.”","Liu Yutong smiled faintly and extended her hand toward them.","“Welcome back as shareholders of the Wanlong Club.”","When the two men left the lounge, their steps felt almost weightless.","Once they got into the car and closed the doors, they simultaneously wiped away their tears.","How had this money disappeared so easily?","A few sentences, and several dozen billion yuan were gone.","Even robbing a bank couldn’t be this fast.","“President Ji, doesn’t something feel wrong to you?”","“Do you think we owed her something in a past life?”","Ji Zhe gave a distant reply. “Maybe. But it feels like we owe her even more in this life.”","The two seasoned veterans had spent more than a decade fighting their way through the investment world. Their combined personal wealth amounted to at least tens of billions of yuan, while the capital they controlled exceeded one hundred billion.","Yet at that moment, both of them had been fleeced by the same young woman to the point of questioning their entire existence.","“President Chu.”","“Hmm?”","“If I ever come to Chairwoman Liu again to discuss going public, I’m a dog.”","Chu Hai nodded heavily.","“So am I.”"]},{"number":885,"title":"Chapter 885: 886. Learn to Let Yourself Go.","paragraphs":["Not long after the press conference of Longyao S1 ended, a storm swept across the Internet.","On major digital forums, Tieba (Chinese equivalent of Reddit), and Weibo, the discussion posts about Longyao S1 were refreshing at a rate of hundreds per second.","\"I'm stunned by Longyao S1's move. They registered the appearance patent ahead of Fruit and even demanded a public apology from Fruit. Isn't this like rubbing it in Jobs' face? But why am I so excited about it?\"","\"I feel the same way! It's so exhilarating!\"","\"To be honest, at first, I thought Longyao copied the design when I saw the appearance. But when they showed the patent application date, I was completely convinced. They applied for the patent in 2008, a full six months earlier than Fruit 4. That means this design is originally from Longyao. The evidence is irrefutable.\"","\"What's going on with Fruit then? A coincidence? It's impossible. In industrial design, there's no such a coincidental clash. Even the arc of the buttons and the number of holes at the bottom are exactly the same. No one would believe it if they said they didn't copy.\"","\"Either someone inside Fruit saw Longyao's design drawings, or Fruit's product managers were all possessed by Longyao's designers. Anyway, the fact that Fruit 4's appearance patent is later than Longyao's is beyond doubt and can't be whitewashed.\"","\"Does anyone still remember Fruit's press conference? Jobs said on stage that the design of Fruit 4 was revolutionary and unprecedented. Looking back at that speech now is like a public humiliation. It's so embarrassing that I could dig a three - bedroom apartment with my toes.\"","\"Jobs: We're going to redefine the phone. Longyao: Sorry, we defined it earlier than you.\"","\"Hahaha, the one above is so witty!\"","\"Anyway, Longyao's configuration is really top - notch. The LX - A1 chip is developed by their own Longcore. This is unique among domestic mobile phones. Other domestic phones are still using MediaTek and Qualcomm.\"","\"The configuration is just one aspect. What really impressed me is the price of 2,999 yuan and the trade - in program. I have a three - year - old Nokia 6300 at home with a cracked screen, and it can still be traded for 1,000 yuan. Isn't this almost like getting the phone for free?\"","\"Friendly reminder to the one above. You can take away the Longyao S1 for 1,999 yuan, and the additional benefits they offer are worth more than 2,000 yuan. There are supermarket cards, Internet café hours, video memberships, lottery tickets for the Voice of China, free delivery for takeaways, milk tea vouchers, and screen - break insurance. Calculating this way, buying the phone is like getting money back instead of spending it. I even suspect they're here to give out freebies.\"","\"I declare that Longyao S1 is the most worthwhile phone to buy this year. No objections!\"","\"I agree too!\"","\"Take your time to agree. I've already placed an order!\"","\"Wow! So fast! I'll go and make a reservation right away!\"","\"........\"","In sharp contrast to the overwhelming positive reviews of Longyao S1, the reputation of Fruit 4 has collapsed drastically.","Within just a few hours, the discussion about Fruit 4's alleged copying of Longyao S1's appearance design has topped the Weibo hot search list, with a dark red \"Hot\" label next to the topic.","\"A plagiarist doesn't deserve to sell at 4,999 yuan. Fruit 4 should lower the price quickly. I'll consider buying one if it drops to 1,999 yuan. Otherwise, goodbye.\"","\"Fruit copying the design of our Longguo phone is the funniest joke I've heard this year. And the problem is, it's actually true.\"","\"Jobs, come out and apologize! Stop pretending to be dead!\"","\"I have a bold guess. Why was the domestic version of Fruit 4 suddenly taken off the market? Is it because Longyao obtained a protection order for the appearance patent? The timing is too coincidental. It was just a few days after Fruit's press conference that the sales were suspended.\"","\"Very likely. Just a few days after Fruit's press conference, the official announced the suspension of sales. This can't be a coincidence. I think Longyao took legal action and the court issued an injunction.\"","\"The most amazing thing is that the beautiful female CEO surnamed Yu of Longyao said at the press conference that as long as Fruit makes a public apology, they'll authorize the appearance patent for free. This move is really a killer one.\"","\"Of course, they can't apologize. Apologizing means admitting to plagiarism, and Fruit's brand reputation will be ruined. But if they hold out, a patent lawsuit will take several years. During this period, they won't be able to sell a single phone in the country, and the losses will be astronomical. Either way, they're in huge trouble.\"","\"This is a masterful conspiracy. They're doomed no matter what choice they make!\"","\"I'm really curious about Jobs' reaction when he saw the press conference video. Will he fire the entire design team?\"","\"Above, I bet he's already smashing the table.\"","\".......... \"","Under such an overwhelming public opinion offensive, the scalper price of Fruit 4 has suffered a disastrous collapse.","Before the press conference, it was approaching 20,000 yuan. Right after the press conference, it was around 10,000 yuan. After the public opinion fully fermented, it plummeted to about 6,000 yuan, almost being halved twice. The drop was extremely appalling.","In front of the Fruit flagship store in the imperial capital, those scalpers who were beaming with joy a few days ago now all had extremely ugly expressions on their faces.","Who could have thought that the once - hard - to - get Fruit 4 would suddenly become a dud?","What should they do with the remaining stock in their hands?","They're not willing to sell at a reduced price. But if they don't, they're afraid they'll lose everything.","They've all suffered huge losses and are squatting on the roadside, swearing at Longyao phones.","After all, most people at this time aren't as crazy about Fruit phones as they will be in the future. To put it bluntly, most people buy Fruit phones because of their powerful functions, good looks, and high popularity at the time.","Now that there's a more cost - effective Longyao, and most importantly, Longyao's design is the original one. Now no one will think it's low - class to buy domestic phones, right?","If I can't buy Fruit 4, I'll buy Longyao S1!","I can also support domestic products.","Of course, the additional benefits don't really matter.","In front of the Fruit store.","\"Damn it! I bought it for 10,000 yuan, and now no one wants it even at 7,000 yuan. I've lost more than 100,000 yuan on this batch of goods,\" a scalper cursed.","The scalper next to him was in no better situation. He still had several Fruit 4 phones in his hand that couldn't be sold, all stuck in his inventory.","Although a silly girl bought one from him for 12,000 yuan last night, making him earn quite a bit, now he's lost all that profit.","Of course, that silly girl is probably dumbfounded now. She paid so much for a phone and will probably cry her heart out.","At this moment, the girl he called a silly girl was sitting alone on the hotel bed, staring blankly at the phone news.","\"Domestic version of Fruit 4 suspended from sale due to patent dispute, recovery time undetermined.\"","\"Longyao S1 released, shocking the entire digital circle. The rise of domestic mobile phones!\"","\"Fruit 4 copied Longyao S1's appearance design, patent documents exposed!\"","\"Scalper price of Fruit 4 drops below 6,000 yuan, stockpilers lose everything!\"","\"Longyao S1 launches trade - in program, old phones worth 1,000 yuan. The first batch of users are scrambling to buy!\"","\"....... \"","What? The price has dropped?","And Fruit 4 copied?","Then what about the fact that she had spent a full three days in the queue, endured so much hardship, and finally paid twelve thousand yuan to buy this mobile phone from a scalper?","It had only been one night, and now they were telling her that this thing was only worth six thousand yuan?","No, it was probably not even worth six thousand.","Because most people were not willing to buy a mobile phone that had been labeled as a copy.","The girl's heart was bleeding, and her head was buzzing. She couldn't accept this reality for a moment.","Just then, she suddenly thought of that scalper. She thought that since she had just bought it not long ago, it should be returnable, right?","Thinking of this, she couldn't sit still anymore. She directly grabbed the phone and rushed out of the hotel, running all the way back to the entrance of the fruit shop.","Fortunately, the scalper, worried that the phone would be unsellable, had appeared at the entrance of the fruit shop early in the morning, loudly hawking the phones to passers - by.","When the girl saw him, she rushed towards the scalper who had sold her the phone like she had caught a life - saving straw.","\"Big brother! Big brother! I want to return the phone!\"","The tall and thin scalper looked up, and his face obviously changed when he saw her.","\"Sister, it's impossible to return the phone. You checked the goods at that time, and there was nothing wrong with it. We've already settled the deal.\"","The girl's face instantly turned pale.","\"But... but you said at that time that the price would rise after the ban on sales, and you said it could reach twenty thousand! You said so! I spent twelve thousand to buy it!\"","\"Just because I said it would rise, you believed it?\"","The scalper rolled his eyes: \"I also thought I could make a fortune out of this, but what happened? I've lost so much that I'm almost penniless. Who can I complain to? If you want to return the phone, go to the fruit company. It's useless to come to me.\"","\"Then what should I do? I spent twelve thousand to buy something worth only six thousand... Wuwuwu...\" The girl's voice began to choke, and tears were falling one after another.","The scalper was a bit annoyed by her appearance and directly shooed her away, saying, \"Alright, alright, stop getting in the way of my business. If you really want to get your money back, there is a way. Sell it quickly while you can still get more than five thousand. Losing seven thousand is better than losing everything. In a few more days, you probably won't even be able to sell it for five thousand.\"","Seven thousand.","Hearing this number, the girl suddenly felt dizzy.","Seven thousand yuan was the salary of her parents for almost half a year.","But she had lost it all overnight.","She couldn't accept this result.","She couldn't!","The girl suddenly turned around and ran towards the flagship store like a madman, slamming on the glass door frantically.","\"Frauds! You're all a bunch of frauds!\"","\"I queued for three days! Three days! And now you say you won't sell it! Stop selling it!\"","\"Refund my money! Give me my money back!\"","\"....\"","The girl slumped on the ground, holding the newly - bought phone and trembling all over.","Just when she was falling into despair, a familiar black motorcade appeared at the intersection.","The middle one was still a black Maybach, and the rest were all Mercedes - Benz. The grand occasion was quite impressive.","The girl recognized this motorcade at a glance.","It was Liu Yutong.","It was the woman who had outshone her from the very first day of college.","It was the existence that she had been jealous of for a full three years but felt powerless even when being jealous.","Now it was this woman who had personally pushed her into the abyss.","She had also seen those news. The real culprit behind the sharp drop in the scalper price of the Fruit 4 was this woman.","It was because of this woman's ban on the sale of Fruit phones that she had ended up in such a miserable state.","In an instant, all the unwillingness, anger, grievance, and despair erupted in her chest like a volcano.","The more the girl thought about it, the more hatred she felt. Finally, she completely lost her mind. She suddenly got up from the ground and rushed onto the road, spreading her arms and blocking the way right in front of the motorcade.","\"Stop! Stop for me!\"","Fortunately, the leading driver reacted quickly and stepped on the brake hard. The front of the car stopped abruptly less than half a meter away from her.","The black - clothed bodyguards on both sides almost rushed out of the cars at the same time. Several figures instantly surrounded the girl, with cold looks in their eyes.","How dare she block The Young Lady's motorcade! She really didn't want to live anymore!","\"Step back! Step back immediately!\"","The girl was startled by this scene and instinctively took half a step back. But when she thought of all the hardships and grievances she had endured these days, her anger welled up again, and she just decided to take the plunge.","\"Liu Yutong! Come out for me!\"","\"I know you're inside! Come out!\"","The window of the middle Maybach slowly rolled down, revealing a delicate side profile.","Liu Yutong slightly turned her head and looked at the girl blocking the motorcade, with a calm expression.","\"What do you want?\"","She didn't ask who the girl was. It wasn't that she didn't recognize her, but that she didn't want to waste her time on such a person.","The girl was completely enraged by her calm attitude. With red eyes, she said:","\"You know who I am!\"","\"You know who I am! We were classmates in college and lived in the same dormitory!\"","\"But you've ruined me! You made me buy the Fruit 4! You made me spend twelve thousand yuan! Do you know that it was my parents' hard - earned money?\"","\"Tell me, why did you ban the sale of Fruit phones? You can just sell your own phones. Why don't you let others sell them? Why?\"","The more she spoke, the more excited she became. Her voice was hoarse in the end, as if she wanted to pour out all the jealousy and unwillingness she had accumulated over the past three years.","Liu Yutong quietly listened to her rant, and her expression remained calm, even a bit indifferent.","After the girl was tired of scolding, she slowly began to speak.","\"Ling Yan, do you think the whole world owes you?\"","Ling Yan was stunned by her words.","\"Is... isn't it?\"","\"You chose to buy the Fruit phone by yourself, right? No one put a knife to your neck to force you to buy it, and no one made the decision for you, did they?\"","\"Actually, the price of one phone is 4,999 yuan, but you insisted on paying twelve thousand. I know you wanted to wait for the price to rise and then sell it to make a profit. I just didn't expect that this investment would end up in a loss.\"","\"However, is it really appropriate for you to block my car just because you lost money?\"","\"Moreover, the ban on the sale of Fruit phones is because they infringed on the appearance patent of Longyao. This is a legal issue and has nothing to do with you.\"","\"You're standing here shouting at me because you can't accept that you made the wrong choice and that your greedy attempt to make a profit by gambling has failed. You're not hating me; you're hating yourself, but you just dare not admit it.\"","\"You just want to find someone to vent your anger on.\"","Ling Yan: \"I...\"","Liu Yutong: \"You don't need to explain. I know what you're thinking. Do you think I'm better than you in every aspect and you feel it's unfair? But Ling Yan, have you ever asked yourself what you've been doing in school these three years?\"","\"You've been staring at me, comparing, being jealous, and fantasizing about the day when you would see me fall, right?\"","\"It's a pity to disappoint you. My Wanlong Association and I are getting stronger and bigger, while you're still the same as before, or even worse than when you first entered college three years ago.\"","\"To be honest, I didn't even think of your existence until you rushed in front of my car today. Does that really hurt you?\"","Ling Yan trembled all over, and tears welled up in her eyes again. This time, it was not out of anger but humiliation.","Liu Yutong looked at her appearance and finally softened her tone a little.","\"Ling Yan, for the sake of our schoolmate relationship, I'll give you one last piece of advice. Give up your ridiculous vanity and jealousy! Learn to let yourself go and make peace with yourself. You're only a junior in college. You have plenty of opportunities in the future.\"","\"Besides, call your parents and apologize to them when you have time.\"","After Liu Yutong finished speaking, the car window slowly rolled up.","The motorcade restarted, drove around Ling Yan, and headed in the direction of the airport.","Ling Yan stood there alone, watching the black motorcade leave with tears streaming down her face."]},{"number":886,"title":"Chapter 886: 887, Fruit Doesn't Back Down","paragraphs":["Fruit Headquarters, America.","The atmosphere in the conference room was unbearably tense.","Jobs stood at the head of the long table. The confident smile that usually seemed permanently fixed on his face had vanished, replaced by a frighteningly grim expression.","On the projection screen before him, clips from the Longyao S1 launch event were playing on a loop.","A woman from the Dragon Nation stood on the stage at the Moscone Center, speaking fluent English as she delivered the words that sent his blood pressure through the roof.","“Fruit copied the design of our Longyao phone.”","Bang!","Jobs slammed his fist onto the table. Everyone in the conference room flinched.","“Can someone explain to me exactly what happened?!”","The room fell silent.","The legal director in charge of patents was already sweating. He hurriedly flipped through the documents in his hands before explaining, “Mr. Jobs, we conducted a comprehensive search of the phone-design patent databases in all major markets around the world. At the time, we genuinely found no conflicting patents. Longyao’s phone patent... was registered under the category of device accessories.”","“Accessories?”","“Yes. The same category as phone cases. It isn’t classified under mobile phones.”","“Under standard patent-search procedures, no one would look under that category for patents covering a phone’s exterior design. My guess is that they did this deliberately, waiting for us to take the bait.”","Jobs slowly raised his head, his gaze sweeping across everyone seated at the table like a blade.","“In other words, we have a mole in the design department?”","The legal director hesitated, but eventually nodded. “It would appear so.”","“Investigate! Every last one of them!”","“And remove everyone currently working in the design department. Replace the entire team!”","“Yes, sir!”","Jobs drew several deep breaths before he finally managed to calm the throbbing in his temples.","As the head of a technology company whose core competitive advantage was design, he understood better than anyone what this meant.","The revolutionary product he had personally unveiled as the one that would “redefine the smartphone” was now becoming the laughingstock of the entire industry.","That was far more difficult to accept than a mere product failure.","“Tell the legal team to prepare for litigation.”","“Fruit will never accept this kind of malicious provocation. We’ll fight them all the way!”","“Mr. Jobs...”","“We’ve conducted an assessment. If this goes to court, the application date on Longyao’s patent is indeed seven months earlier than ours. In most markets, our chances of winning aren’t very high.”","“Then drag it out.”","“Drag it out until they can’t hold on any longer. Fruit’s legal budget is unlimited!”","That afternoon, Fruit’s official account released a strongly worded statement denying all accusations of plagiarism. It claimed that Longyao’s patent had been maliciously registered and stated that Fruit reserved the right to pursue legal action against the company.","At the same time, Fruit announced that it would file countersuits against Longyao worldwide, demanding that the company immediately stop selling the Longyao S1 and pay damages.","The announcement sent the global tech community into another frenzy.","“Fruit is standing its ground! They’ve declared war head-on! This is getting more entertaining by the minute!”","“Fruit claims Longyao maliciously registered the patent? But the application date is right there. How are you going to prove it was malicious?”","“Who cares about proof? Fruit is obviously planning to bury Longyao under a mountain of money. A multinational patent lawsuit could drag on for three to five years. The legal fees alone would be enough to bankrupt a rising brand.”","“I feel so bad for Longyao. They finally made a great product, only to have a giant come after them.”","“...”","But contrary to everyone’s expectations, the Wanlonghui Group responded quickly—and bluntly.","Less than three hours after Fruit released its statement, Yu Xin, president of Wanlonghui’s Technology Division, posted a message on Weibo. It contained only four words:","“Bring it on!”","Attached was a group photo of Wanlonghui’s legal team.","More than a hundred lawyers in black suits stood in three rows. Each wore a dragon-shaped badge on their chest, with the enormous relief of a coiling dragon on the wall of Wanlonghui’s temporary headquarters behind them.","The lawyer standing at the very front, in particular, looked exceptionally professional in his gold-rimmed glasses.","It didn’t take long for Yu Xin’s post to set the comments section ablaze.","“Holy crap! They’re really going head-to-head! A new brand actually dares to fight Fruit in a global patent war?!”","“Four words, and they’re dripping with swagger! This female CEO is so cool!”","“Has anyone else noticed? The lawyers in the photo are wearing black suits too, just like the men in black at the launch event. Could it be that Wanlonghui’s legal department has trained in combat as well?”","“Don’t make me laugh. Lawyers getting into fights? I can’t even imagine it.”","“I have a wild theory. If Wanlonghui’s lawyers lose a case, do they just settle things with the other side in hand-to-hand combat?”","“That’s hilarious. Lawyers throwing punches—what a sight that would be.”","“...”","But what truly left everyone speechless was the set of figures Wanlonghui released soon afterward.","From the end of the Longyao S1 launch event to the close of its first round of preorders, more than 500,000 units had been ordered in just seventy-two hours.","Five hundred thousand units.","Seventy-two hours.","In the domestic smartphone market of 2010, that was practically an unbelievable figure.","Nokia’s best-selling model in the country was currently moving only four to five hundred thousand units in its first month. Yet Longyao S1, a new brand’s very first product, had reached the same level in just three days.","The response in overseas markets was even more surprising.","After the Longyao S1 launch event in San Francisco, the first batch of 100,000 units shipped to North America sold out within a week.","Feedback from the distributors Longyao had secured in Europe was equally enthusiastic. The first batch of 50,000 units sold out in less than five days after going on sale.","On numerous tech-review websites, the Longyao S1 consistently maintained ratings of four stars or higher.","“This is the smoothest Android phone I’ve ever used.”","“The voice-message feature has completely changed the way I think about mobile chatting. WeChat should be standard on every phone.”","“At $299, it makes me feel like an absolute sucker for having spent $800 on a Fruit 4.”","“...”","Of course, amid all the praise, some people voiced different opinions.","“The Longyao S1’s screen resolution is only 480×800. Compared with the Fruit 4’s Retina display, the difference is still obvious.”","“The system is indeed smooth, but the Long OS app ecosystem is far too small. It’s nowhere near Fruit’s App ecosystem.”","“The chipset’s performance is adequate, at best.”","“...”","Although the criticism was far less common than the praise, every complaint struck at a genuine weakness.","Those shortcomings were indeed problems the Longyao S1 could not avoid for the time being.","Hardware specifications could be built up through the supply chain, but closing the gap in software ecosystems was not something that could happen overnight.","Liu Yutong was well aware of that. It was precisely why she had insisted on adding a “First-Batch User Benefits” program to the launch event.","The goal was simple: use the hardware and special benefits to draw users in first, then gradually build up the ecosystem through time and sustained operations.","Yet just as sales of the Longyao S1 continued to climb and the patent war between the Wanlonghui Group and Fruit erupted, a storm capable of reshaping the entire industry was quietly brewing overseas.","Meanwhile, the first “Longteng Cup” martial arts tournament hosted by the Wanlonghui Group officially opened."]},{"number":887,"title":"Chapter 887: 888, Dragon Soaring Cup Opening","paragraphs":["The day the Wanlong Association’s core membership surpassed ten thousand, Liu Yutong was in her office listening to Yun Cheng’s report.","“Miss, the promotion list for the latest batch of core members has been compiled.”","“After these promotions, our total number of core members has officially surpassed ten thousand—10,086 to be exact.”","“Miss, we’ve accomplished the goal we set back then!” A rare trace of excitement appeared on Yun Cheng’s usually stern face.","Back in Wushui County, when Miss had said she wanted to break away from the Yilian Society and establish the Wanlong Association, they had jokingly come up with the name Wanlong Association and said they would one day grow to ten thousand members.","Everyone knew it was only a joke. No one had seriously believed they could actually do it.","Because it was simply too difficult.","Yet just three years later, they had accomplished what had once seemed like an impossible goal.","Liu Yutong took the thick stack of membership lists and began flipping through them page by page.","It had all started in Wushui County, with just a few dozen street toughs who knew nothing but how to run with the wrong crowd. Now, three full years had passed.","Among the old-timers who had followed her from the beginning, some had passed the bar exam, some had earned associate degrees through adult education, some had become technical specialists, and others had moved into management positions.","Everyone was moving forward, desperately striving to become better.","Of course, most of the names on the list were unfamiliar to her. Or rather, she had seen some of them before but could no longer remember their names. There were simply too many people now.","After casually looking through the list, she closed it.","“Now that we have enough people, get ready to launch the tournament.”","News that the Wanlong Association Group would be hosting the Longteng Cup had been announced half a year earlier, at the annual meeting.","At the time, Liu Yutong had declared in front of more than ten thousand people that once the core membership surpassed ten thousand, they would hold an internal martial arts tournament.","The competition would consist of three categories: combat, physical fitness, and legal knowledge. Liu Yutong herself would present awards to the top three teams and individuals, with total prize money of no less than fifty million yuan.","Now, the core membership had truly surpassed ten thousand.","It was time to fulfill that promise.","The following day.","The rules for the Longteng Cup were quickly announced through the group’s internal channels.","The country was divided into six regional divisions—East China, South China, North China, Central China, Southwest China, and Northwest China—along with a headquarters division directly under the Pearl City headquarters, for a total of seven divisions.","Each division would first hold preliminary ranking rounds, also known as ranking matches. The top one hundred contestants from each division would advance to the next round of elimination matches, followed by the final championship tournament.","To support the competition, they had also created a ranking board.","The Wanlong Rankings.","The Digital Business Group had specially developed an internal scoring system for the rankings. It covered the three dimensions of combat, physical fitness, and the bar exam, producing both an overall ranking and rankings for each individual category.","Each category had specific quantitative standards and corresponding weightings. The rankings were updated once a day and were visible to everyone.","Naturally, the rankings were only published on the group’s internal forum. To ensure fairness, they were also divided into men’s and women’s rankings.","As soon as the rankings appeared, people began challenging one another impatiently, all in the hope of making the list and showing off their abilities.","The rankings changed rapidly. Someone ranked first today might be pushed down tomorrow.","The pressure of this real-time competition drove the group’s entire core membership into a frenzy of training.","The preliminary matches for the Pearl City division were held at the newly renovated training center behind Shunchang Building.","The facility had originally been the Wanlong Association’s security department training base. For the Longteng Cup, it had been expanded to twice its original size and outfitted with regulation fighting rings and a complete set of physical fitness testing equipment.","Of course, two people did not participate in the inaugural Longteng Cup.","One was Ma Da.","His reason for sitting out was simple—and shameless. He said he had to be the commentator and did not have time to compete, and that the younger members should be given more opportunities.","The truth was that his build limited his performance.","The other was naturally Ji Yu.","Ji Yu had already surpassed the limits of ordinary humanity. For safety reasons, he had no choice but to be excluded from the competition.","As soon as the Pearl City ranking matches began, Ma Da took the microphone and climbed onto the stage.","“Brothers and sisters! Today is the third day of the Longteng Cup Pearl City Division preliminary matches!”","“Today, your commentator is none other than Brother Ma!”","“Before the matches begin, let me tell you about the current standings in the Pearl City division.”","“As expected, Brother Yun remains number one in the men’s overall rankings! His current total score is 102.7 points, and he ranks first in all three categories!”","“Brother Yun is awesome!”","The spectators erupted in cheers.","“Brother Yun is awesome!”","“Brother Yun is awesome!”","“...”","On the fighting ring, Yun Cheng stood in a black training uniform, expressionless as he watched his latest challenger step forward.","He had entered the Longteng Cup purely because this was the first tournament. As the head of the security department, he needed to demonstrate his abilities in front of all the brothers and sisters so that they would respect his authority.","After all, the Wanlong Association had far too many core members. Many of the newer recruits had never seen him fight, and it was inevitable that some of them might secretly refuse to acknowledge him.","That was why he had chosen to compete and let his strength speak for itself.","Today’s first challenger was a newly promoted core member of the Pearl City security department.","He was in his early twenties with a well-built physique. As soon as he stepped into the ring, he respectfully cupped his fists in salute.","“Brother Yun, please give me some guidance!”","Yun Cheng gave a slight nod. “Come on.”","Less than ten seconds later, the young man was lying on the ground, staring at the ceiling and questioning his life choices. It had happened so quickly that he had not even seen how he had been taken down.","Still, he had only joined recently and could not compare with those who had been training for years—especially not with an opponent like Yun Cheng.","Ma Da leaped to his feet, microphone in hand, visibly excited.","“Ten seconds! Brother Yun has once again broken his own record for the fastest victory! Don’t be discouraged, brother. At least you lasted ten seconds and made it into double digits!”","“Hahahaha...”","The entire venue burst into laughter.","The defeated young man climbed to his feet, scratched his head, and gave an embarrassed smile. Then he bowed to Yun Cheng and quietly left the ring.","At the same time, he secretly vowed to train twice as hard and fight for a better ranking in the rounds ahead.","The ranking matches were based on overall scores. Losing did not mean immediate elimination. He still had opportunities.","The only person tied with Yun Cheng at the top of the rankings was Chu Yang, another head of the security department. He was likewise a monster whose scores in all three categories were close to perfect.","The two had traded victories in several small-scale bouts, and their scores were extremely close. Chu Yang might rank first today, only for Yun Cheng to overtake him tomorrow. The number-one and number-two positions on the rankings changed almost every day.","According to the schedule, the preliminary matches for the six regional divisions and the Pearl City headquarters division would take approximately three months to complete.","Only after those three months would the elimination rounds begin, which would last about another month before the final championship tournament.","The schedule was not intentionally drawn out. Everyone still had their regular jobs or studies, so most of the matches were held in the evenings.","This was also to prevent the competition from interfering with everyone’s work and careers. So many people were taking part—if they all stopped working for the sake of the competition, the company would be left with countless vacant positions. How could the group continue operating?","That was why the schedule had been stretched out for so long: to give everyone enough time to participate.","The ranking rounds and elimination rounds would end just in time for the group’s annual gala. The final winner could then be decided at the gala, with all the group’s employees in attendance. Wouldn’t that make it even more exciting?","From then on, the preliminary and elimination rounds of the annual competition would begin in August and conclude in December, with the grand finals held at the company’s annual gala the following year."]},{"number":888,"title":"Chapter 888: 889, Catfish, Rice 1 Released (Thanks to 'Luweiya.' for the King of Gifts)","paragraphs":["Just as the Longteng Cup was in full swing, a bombshell announcement broke.","Apple officially announced that the mainland version of the iPhone 4 would resume sales in the Dragon Kingdom.","The news sent the entire internet into an uproar.","Everyone had assumed that, because of the design-patent dispute, the iPhone 4 would be banned from sale in the Dragon Kingdom for at least six months. Yet the ban had been lifted after barely a month.","Digital forums and Weibo exploded in an instant, with speculation flying in every direction.","Some said Apple had paid a fine. Others claimed Apple had reached a settlement with Longyao. Still others said that higher authorities had stepped in to mediate. There was no shortage of theories.","Liu Yutong and the others, however, were not surprised in the least. They had known for quite some time that the ban would be lifted.","The iPhone 4 ban was not merely a matter concerning Apple.","Apple’s supply chain spanned the globe, and a considerable portion of its production capacity and assembly lines were located in the Dragon Kingdom. Just a few of the domestic factories that manufactured products for Apple provided jobs for more than a hundred thousand workers.","Banning the iPhone 4 would hurt more than Apple’s financial statements. It would also affect domestic supply-chain companies and the livelihoods of over a hundred thousand industrial workers.","Of course, the most important development was that, not long before, Apple had signed a long-term cooperation agreement with domestic suppliers in the Dragon Kingdom through mediation by the relevant authorities. The agreement opened up procurement of some core components to local companies.","That was a very important piece of news—extremely important.","At present, the Dragon Kingdom’s mobile-phone industry chain was still immature. The biggest problem was that its domestic smartphone brands were struggling to produce strong contenders. If the entire industry chain was to be upgraded, an outside catalyst had to be brought in.","The Longyao S1’s launch had been a huge success. It had sold more than one million units in less than two months, while overseas sales continued to climb.","Thanks to the Longyao S1’s preinstalled apps and the trade-in campaign, MicroChat’s user base had skyrocketed. Combined with traffic diverted from platforms such as Weibo, the number of registered users had already surpassed twenty million, with daily active users holding steady at more than five million.","But the problem was equally obvious. At the moment, Longyao was the only smartphone brand putting in a truly impressive performance. Yet having only one standout brand was not enough.","The domestic market still needed a heavyweight competitor to stir up the stagnant waters. Otherwise, innovation throughout the industry chain would gradually slow down.","The authorities certainly did not want to see that happen. That was why they had chosen the right moment to loosen the restrictions on Apple and let this catfish back into the pond, forcing the Dragon Kingdom’s mobile-phone industry to develop more rapidly.","Liu Yutong was no stranger to this logic. In her previous life, Xiaomi’s rise had been accompanied by similar industrial considerations. The only difference was that, in this life, her Longyao had become the first company to stand opposite the catfish.","Moreover, before the ban was lifted, an official had already given her advance notice.","Her response had naturally been one of understanding and support.","And she had not been insincere.","Having Apple as a competitor was, in fact, no bad thing for Longyao.","Pressure created motivation, after all.","Besides, the Longyao S1’s sales had already taken off. Even with the iPhone 4 back on the market, it would be difficult for Apple to shake the market position Longyao had established in the short term.","Still, understanding was one thing. When it was time to fire back, they would fire back.","On the very day the iPhone 4 resumed sales, Longyao’s president, Yu Xin, issued a statement through the company’s official channels. The wording was rather interesting.","“Given that Apple has yet to publicly apologize to Longyao for infringing upon our industrial-design patent, Longyao reserves the right to continue pursuing legal action.","“At the same time, we welcome Apple’s participation in fair competition in the Dragon Kingdom market through lawful and compliant means, and we look forward to seeing Apple bring a truly original design to its next product launch.”","The statement sent netizens into hysterics.","Mr. Yu’s Weibo comment section was instantly flooded. The most-liked comments were all poking fun at Apple.","“Welcome to fair competition—but don’t copy my phone’s shell again. Mr. Yu is truly magnanimous.”","“Looking forward to Apple bringing an original design. The sarcasm here is absolutely top-tier.”","“Apple: We’re back on sale. Why are you still hounding us?”","“Longyao: Because hounding you is exactly what we intend to do.”","“But seriously, Longyao really does have class. If it were me, I’d sue Apple into bankruptcy. But Longyao says it won’t pursue the matter as long as Apple apologizes. What do you call that? Magnanimity.”","“The guy above has it wrong. That’s called twisting the knife. Apple will never apologize—not in this lifetime. But as long as it refuses to apologize, Longyao can keep using this incident to humiliate it forever.”","“Hahahaha...”","Meanwhile, at a café in Zhongguancun, Imperial Capital—","A middle-aged man was repeatedly watching a replay of the Longyao S1 launch event on his laptop.","He watched with complete concentration, occasionally pausing the video to jot down notes in a notebook. Sometimes he would rewind and watch the same segment all over again.","This man was Lei Jobs, the founder of Xiaomi.","After watching the replay several times, he finally made an extremely bold decision.","He, too, would use a jaw-dropping price to make the Xiaomi Mi 1 a sensation.","Several days later, the launch event for the first-generation Xiaomi phone was held.","The venue was an ordinary banquet hall. It was not nearly as grand as the National Convention Center, but it had plenty of character and suited Xiaomi’s positioning as a brand for young tech enthusiasts.","A large number of media outlets attended, along with quite a few internet industry heavyweights, including Yu Xin and Liu Yutong.","Lei Jobs stood onstage in his trademark black polo shirt and jeans. Behind him, the screen displayed a render of the first-generation Xiaomi phone.","“Xiaomi Mi 1—1,999 yuan. Born for enthusiasts!”","The moment Lei Jobs announced the price, the entire venue erupted.","At 1,999 yuan, that price was practically enough to grind every competitor in the Dragon Kingdom’s smartphone market into the dirt.","The Longyao S1 cost 2,999 yuan. The iPhone 4 cost 4,999 yuan. Xiaomi’s Mi 1, meanwhile, slashed the price all the way down to 1,999 yuan without cutting corners on specifications. With features such as a Qualcomm processor, a Sharp display, and ample RAM, its on-paper specifications were only a tiny step below those of the Longyao S1.","The tech world exploded instantly. The Xiaomi Mi 1 shot up the Weibo hot-search rankings at a speed visible to the naked eye, while discussion threads on major forums refreshed at a frantic pace.","“1,999! Lei Jobs has gone crazy!”","“The specs are comparable to the Longyao S1, but it’s a thousand yuan cheaper. Is Xiaomi planning to sweep the entire domestic smartphone market?”","“My God, that price is practically an invitation to become friends.”","“Mr. Lei said publicly that Xiaomi’s comprehensive net profit margin on hardware would never exceed five percent. Now that is what I call sincerity! A lot more genuine than certain companies that sell phones for 2,999 yuan while still calling themselves champions of value.”","“Are you taking a shot at Longyao? What’s wrong with you? Do you think developing its own chips costs nothing? Building its own supply chain costs nothing? Do you know how many domestic suppliers every Longyao phone helps support?”","“No, I don’t. I only know that the Longyao S1 is way too expensive.”","“......”","As certain people fanned the flames, supporters of the Longyao S1 and Dami 1 soon began tearing into each other.","Each side had its own claims and its own reasoning. Two phones with clearly different market positions had somehow been dragged into a head-to-head comparison.","It was obvious that someone was deliberately steering the conversation.","Still, this minor war of public opinion was quickly brought to an end by an official announcement."]},{"number":889,"title":"Chapter 889: 890. Alliance of the Light of Domestic Goods","paragraphs":["Seventy-two hours after the Dami 1 launch event ended, the mood in the public discourse began to shift in subtle ways.","On digital forums, message boards, and Weibo, the debate over “Which Is More Worth Buying, the Dami 1 or the Longyao S1?” had escalated from a minor squabble into an all-out war. Supporters on both sides were tearing into each other, while comparison charts, value-for-money analyses, and technical breakdowns flooded the internet.","“1,999 versus 2,999 yuan, with nearly identical specs. Dami wins hands down.”","“The Longyao S1 has a self-developed chip. What does Dami have to compete with that? Qualcomm Snapdragon chips are sourced from outside. What are you going to do if they stop selling to you one day?”","“Is ‘self-developed’ really worth a thousand yuan? Consumers aren’t idiots. People buy whichever one is cheaper.”","“You’re forgetting Longyao’s launch promotions, aren’t you? Trade in your old phone for a thousand yuan off, plus supermarket cards, internet café cards, milk tea vouchers, and more. You could cash out nearly two thousand yuan in benefits. By that calculation, the Longyao S1 is practically free.”","“That was just a launch promotion. It’s long expired.”","“Even if it has expired, it still counts. Apple copied their exterior design patents, and that alone is enough reason to buy Longyao. It’s about having face, you know?”","“......”","Just as supporters on both sides were locked in a furious battle, two Weibo posts published almost simultaneously brought everyone to a sudden silence.","Yu Xin, president of the Technology Business Group of Wanlonghui Group, posted:","“Congratulations, Mr. Lei, on the great success of the Dami 1 launch event. The price of 1,999 yuan is truly astonishing! I wish the Dami 1 huge sales. And as a little preview, Longyao and Dami will be holding a joint press conference at two tomorrow afternoon in the capital, where we’ll announce some important news. Please stay tuned.”","Dami Technology’s founder, Lei Jobs, soon followed with a post of his own:","“Thank you for your kind wishes, Mr. Yu. Tomorrow afternoon, Mr. Yu and I have a date in the capital. See you there. And let me just say this: it’s good news.”","The moment the two posts went live, the comment sections exploded.","“A joint press conference? What are these two companies up to?”","“Mr. Yu and Mr. Lei have a date? What kind of dream pairing is this? I’m shipping them already.”","“They aren’t planning to merge, are they? Please don’t. I’m still waiting to see the two companies wage a price war.”","“A merger is impossible, but some kind of cooperation is definitely on the table. The question is how deep it goes.”","“I have a feeling something big is coming.”","“Same here.”","“.......”","Two days later, in the afternoon, at a conference center in the capital.","The front rows were once again filled with prominent figures. Major players from the internet, investment, and supply-chain industries had gathered yet again.","Unlike the previous event, this press conference was much smaller in scale, with no opening performance.","But the number of media outlets in attendance had not decreased at all. Everyone wanted firsthand information. After all, the sudden decision by Longyao and Dami to hold a joint press conference clearly suggested that something major was about to happen.","Time passed little by little before Yu Xin and Lei Jobs walked onto the stage side by side.","Yu Xin was once again dressed in a black suit, with a dragon-shaped badge pinned to her chest. She exuded a sharp, commanding presence. Compared with three years earlier, she seemed like an entirely different person.","Lei Jobs was still wearing a dark-blue polo shirt with jeans.","Standing together, they made a strikingly mismatched pair: one a tech queen radiating confidence and edge, the other a low-key, pragmatic geeky uncle. Their styles could hardly have been more different.","“Good afternoon, everyone, and thank you for taking time out of your busy schedules to attend this press conference,” Yu Xin began.","“We’ve invited you here today to announce two things.”","“First, Longyao and Dami Technology have officially signed a strategic cooperation agreement. The two sides will launch comprehensive cooperation in three major areas: supply chains, patented technology, and after-sales service.”","“To put it simply, starting today, Longyao and Dami will officially open up their supply-chain systems to each other. We will share selected core patents, jointly build an after-sales service network, and work together to upgrade the domestic smart-phone industry chain.”","The entire room fell silent for a moment. Everyone had been stunned by the announcement.","Opening up their supply chains, sharing patents, and jointly building after-sales services—this was no ordinary cooperation agreement. It was clearly a declaration of alliance among domestic smartphone manufacturers.","Lei Jobs took over:","“I know many people will be asking why Dami and Longyao, despite being competitors, have chosen to work together.”","“The answer is simple: our true competitors have never been each other.”","“Mr. Yu and I both believe that the domestic smartphone market is large enough to accommodate both Longyao and Dami. Our real competitors are the foreign giants that monopolize core technologies and control the supply chain. They hold the chips, the screens, and the operating systems in their hands... and they can choke our industry at any time.”","“If we fight among ourselves, if we undermine each other over tiny price differences, then when they truly make their move, none of us will be able to escape.”","“So Mr. Yu and I talked for several days and ultimately reached a consensus. Instead of fighting separately, we would be better off standing shoulder to shoulder. Longyao has independently developed chips, while Dami has strong supply-chain management capabilities......... By joining forces, we can’t claim that we’ll immediately surpass the international giants, but at the very least, we can let them know that the smartphone industry of Longguo is not something they can squeeze whenever they please.”","As soon as he finished speaking, someone in the audience began to applaud.","In an instant, the entire room joined in.","When the applause finally subsided, Yu Xin spoke again.","“This brings us to the second announcement.”","She pressed a button on the remote in her hand, and the large screen behind them lit up.","“Starting today, Longyao and Dami will jointly establish the Light of Domestic Brands Alliance. The alliance will be open to all domestic smartphone brands. Any company willing to abide by the alliance’s supply-chain standards and patent-sharing agreement may join.”","“The alliance has only eight words as its guiding principle: openness, mutual benefit, growth, and strength!”","As soon as she finished, a line of large, bold characters appeared on the screen behind her:","“Light of Domestic Brands Alliance”","Below the title was a list of the alliance’s specific terms.","For example, alliance members would receive priority access to the Longxin LX series of chips, with prices uniformly reduced by 15 percent.","Alliance members would share a core patent pool covering three major categories—exterior design, system UI interaction, and hardware structure—with a total of XXX patents. No patent licensing fees would be charged among alliance members, while reasonable fees would be collected for external licensing.","The alliance would jointly establish a nationwide after-sales service network. Users of member brands could receive standardized services—including repairs, replacements, returns, and refunds—at any authorized after-sales outlet belonging to an alliance brand.","The alliance would unify supply-chain procurement standards, conduct joint negotiations with upstream suppliers, and eliminate malicious price hikes and hoarding.","Alliance members would jointly fund the establishment of a domestic smartphone industry innovation fund, with an initial size of 5 billion yuan, to support technological research and development by local supply-chain companies.","Alliance members would also jointly publish an annual industry white paper and promote the creation of unified standards for interoperability among smart devices, among other initiatives.","Every clause was packed with substance.","The prominent figures in the audience could no longer sit still. They began whispering among themselves.","“The very first provision grants priority access to Longxin chips. She’s opening up Longxin’s production capacity to the entire industry. Mr. Yu’s commitment is enormous.”","“Not only that, but there’s also free licensing for patents. Take Longyao’s design patent, for example. They could collect tens of billions in patent fees from Apple alone, yet they’re now allowing every alliance member to use it for free. Maybe we should take a page from their book.”","“They’ve even opened up their after-sales service network. That means no matter what brand of domestic phone you buy, you’ll be able to find an authorized service center wherever you go. That kind of experience absolutely blows Apple’s out of the water.”","“Did you see the last item? Jointly establishing standards for interoperability. They’re going head-to-head with Apple’s closed ecosystem and building an open ecosystem for domestic brands.”","“You know, with Mr. Yu and Mr. Lei working together, they might actually pull this off.”","“.........”","Down below, Ma Yunyun turned his head and whispered teasingly to Pony Ma:","“President Ma, look at their vision. Now look at Tencent. When are you going to form an alliance with WeChat?”","He had asked the question deliberately. Everyone in the industry knew that Pony Ma and WeChat were locked in a fierce battle, practically on the verge of coming to blows.","After all, WeChat had targeted Tencent’s core social business. How could Pony Ma possibly sit back and do nothing? He had even stopped messaging Liu Yutong as much and withdrawn his investment in Loongson.","To put it bluntly, he was starting to panic.","Hearing Old Ma’s remark, Pony Ma replied coldly, “I can consider forming an anti-monopoly alliance with WeChat—one dedicated to reporting Alibaba for secretly engaging in monopolistic practices.”","Ma Yunyun: “......”","Meanwhile, on the other side.","Li Yanhong stared at the terms displayed on the giant screen for a long time. After thinking it over carefully, he suddenly lowered his voice and said to his assistant, “After the press conference, go ask whether Baidu can join the alliance.”","The assistant froze, then instinctively asked, “Manager Li, we don’t even make smartphones.”","Li Yanhong shook his head. “Not making them now doesn’t mean we won’t make them in the future. Chips, patents, supply chains... these things are the infrastructure of the smartphone industry. Whoever secures them first will become the one setting the standards. Longyao is making a very big move here. Once they get this system up and running, anyone who wants to enter the game later will have to play by their rules.”","“If Baidu doesn’t act now, then once the tickets for the mobile internet ship are handed out, we won’t even be able to grab standing-room tickets.”","The assistant nodded after hearing this, indicating that he had taken note.","Onstage, Lei Jobs and Yu Xin stood side by side, looking at the industry bigwigs whispering among themselves below. The two exchanged a smile at almost exactly the same moment.","“Mr. Yu, who do you think will be the first to apply for membership?” Lei Jobs asked in a lowered voice.","Yu Xin thought for a moment before replying, “It’ll probably be someone nobody expects.”","Lei Jobs paused, just as he was about to ask what he meant, when someone suddenly stood up from the audience.","Every eye in the room turned toward him. Quite a few people recognized him: Yang Yuan, head of Lianxiang’s mobile division.","Lianxiang Mobile was a long-established domestic brand that had once enjoyed great success, but had not released a genuinely impressive product in several years. Many people had assumed the company had already abandoned its smartphone business.","No one had expected one of its representatives to be there.","“Mr. Yu, Mr. Lei, on behalf of Lianxiang Mobile, I hereby formally apply to join the alliance.”"]},{"number":890,"title":"Chapter 890: 891. The Light of Domestic Products Grows Rapidly Top Elites Under Thirty","paragraphs":["Lianxiang, of course!","That was the undisputed king of the PC era. Although it had never really made much of a splash in the mobile-phone market, even a sick camel was still bigger than a horse. At the very least, it was one of the founding names in China’s consumer-electronics industry, with experience and distribution channels that ordinary new brands simply couldn’t match.","In the early years, Lianxiang computers had sold across the length and breadth of the country. From first-tier cities to tiny county towns no one had ever heard of, Lianxiang stores could be found everywhere. Its strength was undeniable.","With a smile, Yu Xin walked off the stage and approached Yang Yuan, extending her hand.","“Welcome to the alliance, Mr. Yang.”","Yang Yuan shook Yu Xin’s hand and immediately made his position clear. “Lianxiang will give the alliance our full support!”","Lei Jobs watched the scene from the side, secretly sighing with emotion.","He had started Rice not only to prove himself once again, but also because he genuinely wanted to contribute to the development of China’s mobile-phone industry.","That was why he had shouted that slogan at the launch event: the comprehensive net profit margin on hardware would never exceed five percent. It wasn’t that he didn’t want to make money. He wanted to use the most extreme value-for-money pricing to force the entire industry to improve.","But one person’s strength was ultimately limited.","Even if Rice managed to succeed, the lifeline of the supply chain would remain in the hands of outsiders, leaving them vulnerable to being strangled at any moment.","He had never expected Miss Liu to have thought of this long ago. She had specifically asked Yu Xin to contact him, and the two sides had sat down and negotiated through the night. In the end, they had created the initial framework of this alliance.","With a group as powerful as the Wanlong Association leading the charge, he naturally couldn’t have been more pleased.","If the mobile-phone industry of the Dragon Kingdom truly wanted to rise, it would take more than just him. Yu Xin alone wouldn’t be enough either. What they needed was the collective unity of the entire industry, from upstream suppliers to downstream manufacturers.","Today, they had finally taken the first step.","...","The establishment of the Light of Domestic Products Alliance was like a nuclear bomb detonating in the country’s technology and internet circles, stirring up a storm of unprecedented proportions.","Less than twenty-four hours after the press conference ended, more than a dozen domestic mobile-phone brands—including Lianxiang, Jinli, Bubu Gao, OP, and VO—successively announced through their official channels that they had applied to join the alliance.","The speed of the response caught even Yu Xin and Lei Jobs off guard.","Before the press conference, they had privately estimated that three to five brands joining in the first round would already count as a success. After all, although the alliance’s terms were attractive, membership also meant complying with unified supply-chain standards and a patent-sharing agreement. For many brands accustomed to doing things their own way, that might not have been easy to accept.","However, reality proved that domestic phone manufacturers were far more eager to break free from their dependence on overseas supply chains than they had imagined.","In particular, the two core terms—the priority right to purchase Longxin chips and a fifteen-percent discount from standardized prices, along with free authorization through the patent pool—had prompted nearly every domestic manufacturer to rush to submit an application.","One week later, at a convention center in the imperial capital, Yu Xin and Lei Jobs once again stood side by side beneath the enormous emblem of the Light of Domestic Products Alliance. Together with representatives from the twelve domestic mobile-phone brands that had joined in the first round, they signed the alliance charter and posed for a group photo.","The photograph quickly spread across Weibo and all the major digital forums.","“Lianxiang, Jinli, Bubu Gao...all those established domestic brands are here. What an incredible lineup!”","“Twelve domestic mobile-phone brands joining forces—that’s enough to bring tears to my eyes. At last, we won’t have to worry about foreign companies cutting off our supply chains.”","“So it isn’t just Longyao and Rice fighting the battle. The entire domestic mobile-phone industry is gathering strength. Apple and Samsung, you’d better get ready to tremble.”","“I heard Baidu wanted to join too, but they were turned down because they don’t make phones.”","“Hahaha, Li Yanhong is probably saying, ‘I can start making them right now! Wait for me!’”","“That killed me. Mr. Li will probably establish a mobile-phone division overnight.”","“...”","At the same time, with the establishment of the Light of Domestic Products Alliance—and with the deliberate support of senior officials—the name of Yu Xin, president of the Technology Business Group, began appearing regularly in headlines across the country.","This young female executive, just twenty-one years old, had become practically a household name within a few short months, completing a transformation so dazzling that it could only be described as legendary.","China Entrepreneur magazine named Yu Xin its Year 10 cover figure. The cover carried just eight words:","“Yu Xin, the Barrier-Breaker of Domestic Mobile Phones.”","On the cover, Yu Xin wore a black suit, with the familiar dragon-shaped insignia still hanging at her chest. She stood before a massive rendering of the Longyao S1, smiling yet radiating a sharp, unyielding edge.","The magazine devoted twelve full pages to Yu Xin’s life story and the rise of Longyao phones.","Soon afterward, Forbes also named Yu Xin to its list of the “Thirty Most Promising Business Leaders Under Thirty of Year 10,” placing her second.","The list selected only thirty people each year, and everyone who made it was a dazzling rising star in their respective field.","This year, Yu Xin, just twenty-one years old, made the list as co-founder of Longyao Mobile and president of its Technology Business Group, landing directly in second place.","Forbes described Yu Xin this way:","“She used a single phone to change global consumers’ preconceived notions about products made in the Dragon Kingdom. Through one launch event, she also proved to the world that people from the Dragon Kingdom could define the aesthetics of technology.”","It was an extraordinarily high evaluation.","Before this, the international image of products made in the Dragon Kingdom had always been associated with cheapness, knockoffs, and poor quality. Yet Yu Xin and her Longyao S1 had managed to tear away a corner of that label, allowing the world to see something entirely different.","However, what truly set the internet ablaze was not Yu Xin’s ranking, but the person above her.","At the top of the Forbes list was a name that read:","Liu Yutong.","Founder and chairwoman of the Wanlong Association Group.","Age: Twenty-one.","Industry: Diversified business conglomerate.","Estimated net worth: Impossible to estimate.","That “impossible to estimate” naturally left plenty to the imagination.","Yet in the photograph section, there was nothing but a blank space.","Of the thirty people on the list, only the number-one position had no photograph. In its place was merely a gray silhouette.","Once the list was reposted on Weibo, the comments section erupted in discussion.","“Another refusal to make her photo public? How many times has this happened now? Who exactly is this Miss Liu? Is she some kind of supernatural being? Even Forbes can’t get her to cooperate?”","“I’ve heard of the Wanlong Association. I have a distant cousin who works in Pearl City, and he says it’s the largest private enterprise there. But their way of doing things is incredibly overbearing. They always travel with black-suited bodyguards clearing the way, and their presence is more intimidating than a movie godfather’s. I don’t know whether it’s true, though.”","“The person above isn’t exaggerating. I’m a student at a university in Pearl City, and I once saw the Wanlong Association’s motorcade with my own eyes. It was terrifying—easily more than a hundred Mercedes-Benz cars, with license plates that were almost all in consecutive sequences. The whole thing was ridiculously extravagant!”","“More than a hundred Mercedes-Benz cars, with consecutive license plates? My God! That’s intense!”","“I’ve heard that too. Almost everyone in the Wanlong Group wears a black suit, complete with a dragon-shaped pin on the chest. They look like the Dragon Nation’s version of the Mafia. The first time I saw them, I thought they were filming a movie.”","“Hey, hey, don’t make things up. The Wanlong Group is a legitimate company. Just the year before last, they donated more than two billion yuan in BS Province alone and helped build over a hundred schools. Doesn’t your conscience hurt, calling them criminals?”","“A legitimate company? Yeah, right. I don’t buy it.”","“Is the Wanlong Group really that intimidating? Because now I suddenly kind of want to work there.”","“Get a grip, buddy. I heard they conduct background checks going back three generations, have physical assessments comparable to special-forces selection, and even require employees to undergo training for the legal qualification exam. Ordinary people don’t stand a chance of getting in.”","“???”","“......”","As the discussion in the comments grew increasingly absurd, the debate over whether the Wanlong Group was truly a legitimate company flared up on Weibo once again.","The topic made it onto the trending searches almost every few days.","Just as someone had pointed out earlier, there was indeed something about the company’s name that made people’s imaginations run wild."]},{"number":891,"title":"Chapter 891: 892. Zhao Zhu Is Released from Prison.","paragraphs":["In mid-September, outside the Barlizi Prison in Wushui County.","A young woman with short hair and a slender build walked out through the massive iron gate, free once more.","The moment she crossed the threshold, she instinctively raised a hand to shield her eyes from the harsh sunlight and narrowed them.","So this was what freedom smelled like. It wasn’t pleasant at all.","The woman was Zhao Zhu, who had been imprisoned more than three years ago.","She had been released several months ahead of schedule. Thanks to her good behavior and the prison’s sentence-reduction policy, she had regained her freedom early.","More than three years behind bars had changed Zhao Zhu tremendously. The once-arrogant school bully who had thrown her weight around at school had become a woman with a slightly sallow complexion and a much thinner frame. Judging by her appearance alone, she seemed at least five years older than her actual age.","More than three years ago, she had entered through those very gates as an eighteen-year-old high school student.","Now, at twenty-one, she was walking out again.","She had missed the college entrance examination. She had no qualifications, and her youth had been spent. The three most precious years of her life were gone.","And the culprits responsible for all of this were those two bitches, Liu Yutong and Yu Xin.","Zhao Zhu had not told her family that she was being released. She didn’t want anyone to see her looking like this, either.","She planned to disappear for a while and only show herself again once she was ready.","Just then, a three-wheeled motorized taxi came by. She flagged it down and gave the driver the address of Wushui No. 2 High School.","Before long, Zhao Zhu was standing outside the school gates.","She did not go inside. Instead, she sat down at a noodle shop across the road, ordered a bowl of noodles, and watched the familiar school entrance from a distance as she ate.","Three years had passed, but the school had barely changed. The gates were still the same, and the teaching building was still the same. Almost everything looked exactly as it had when she left.","The only difference was the enormous electronic display that had been installed by the entrance. It played the school’s promotional slogans and highlighted the achievements of outstanding alumni.","Zhao Zhu’s eyes drifted toward the screen, and she froze.","A clipped news segment was playing.","On the screen, a poised young woman in a black suit stood at the center of a press-conference stage, speaking confidently. Behind her was a massive dragon-shaped logo and a rendering of the Longyao S1. The audience was packed with people, while camera flashes went off in a frenzy.","Then came a string of impressive titles.","Co-founder of Longyao Mobile. President of the Technology Business Group. Cover figure for Dragon Nation Entrepreneurs magazine’s 2010 issue. Ranked second among Forbes’ 30 Under 30 business elites for 2010...","The woman on the screen wore exquisite makeup and carried herself with confidence and composure. Even with more than a hundred reporters taking pictures of her, she did not show the slightest trace of nervousness.","“Ms. Yu Xin, how is development of the next-generation Longyao S1 progressing?”","“Mr. Yu, there are rumors that the Wanlonghui Group is preparing to go public. Is that true?”","“Mr. Yu, you’re only twenty-one years old. How did you lead Longyao Mobile to such astonishing success in such a short time?”","In response to each question, the girl who had once been so introverted in high school that she was practically reclusive now answered smoothly and confidently.","Zhao Zhu stared at that familiar yet unfamiliar face on the screen. The chopsticks in her hand were nearly crushed.","Yu Xin?","This was Yu Xin?","The timid coward she had slapped, pulled by the hair, and humiliated countless times in the school bathroom?","She had actually made it onto Forbes’ elite list? She had even become the president of some Longyao Mobile?","How was that possible?","How could that useless girl have become so dazzling?","Zhao Zhu could not accept what she was seeing.","That weak, timid coward now stood at a height Zhao Zhu could only look up to, basking in the praise and adoration of society.","The contrast was simply too great.","Especially when she thought about her own situation—more than three years in prison, missing the college entrance examination, her family’s business going bankrupt...","She was in utter ruin.","The more she compared herself with Yu Xin, the more glaring the disparity became.","The more unfair it felt.","“Why?”","“Why her?”","“That life should have been mine! Mine! You stole my life from me!” Zhao Zhu roared inwardly.","Just as she seethed with rage, convinced that the world was unbearably unjust, the old television mounted on the noodle shop wall began broadcasting news from Wushui County’s local station.","“Recently, renowned local entrepreneur Ms. Yu Xin was invited to visit her alma mater, Wushui No. 2 High School. According to reports, Ms. Yu Xin has returned to her hometown for two reasons: first, to visit the teachers and students of her former school; and second, to represent the Wanlonghui Charitable Foundation in implementing a student-aid program...”","“The county authorities attach great importance to this matter and will accompany her throughout the visit...”","Zhao Zhu’s head snapped up when she heard the news.","Yu Xin was coming back?","Back to Wushui County?","Back to No. 2 High School?","In an instant, a mad idea sprang into her mind.","If her life had already been ruined, then no one else was going to have it easy, either."]},{"number":892,"title":"Chapter 892: 893. Meeting an Acquaintance. (Thanks to 'Her Highness Luweiya' for the King of Gifts)","paragraphs":["During this period, Zhao Zhu had been gathering specific information about when Yu Xin would return to Wuxian County and what her itinerary would be.","According to what she had learned, Yu Xin would arrive in Wuxian County in about three days. She would first return to her alma mater, No. 2 High School, for an inspection, then attend a small symposium organized by the county that afternoon. That night, she might stay at the only three-star hotel in the county seat.","That might be her only chance.","Of course, Zhao Zhu now knew from the information she had gathered that Yu Xin and Liu Yutong were both studying at Mingzhu City University of Finance and Economics. She might find an opportunity there as well.","But she couldn’t wait that long.","The more Zhao Zhu learned during this time, the more intense the hatred in her heart became.","She simply couldn’t accept that in just over three years, the outside world had changed so much—that those two bitches had become so powerful and dazzling.","Today, Zhao Zhu came to Fish Joy House in Wuxian County. When she saw the restaurant that had once belonged to her family, she found that its sign had been replaced and the interior completely renovated. It looked much more upscale than before.","She stood outside for quite a while. After some thought, she put on a hat and walked in, intending to see whether the food still tasted the same.","Of course, she also wanted to scout the place out in advance. What if Yu Xin came here to eat? Wouldn’t that give her a chance to slip some rat poison or something into her food?","While Zhao Zhu was waiting in a corner of the dining hall for her food to arrive, a black BMW 5 Series pulled up outside the restaurant.","Zhao Zhu was slightly surprised when she saw the car.","In a small county like Wuxian in 2010, BMWs were still relatively rare luxury cars, especially a brand-new 5 Series. It must have cost at least several hundred thousand yuan.","The car door opened, and a man stepped out of the driver’s seat.","The man looked to be under thirty. He wore an exaggerated floral shirt, had his hair slicked back, and sported a small beer belly. A gold watch gleamed on his wrist. His outfit and bearing made him look exactly like the nouveau riche bosses often seen on television.","But for some reason, the more Zhao Zhu looked at him, the more familiar he seemed.","Soon, the image of a young hoodlum with dyed yellow hair appeared in her mind and gradually merged with the man standing before her.","It was Liu Hao!","He was the underworld big brother she had acknowledged back when she was in high school, her sworn brother.","Back then, the reason she had dared to act so arrogantly at school was largely because she had Liu Hao, a street tough, backing her. Whenever something happened, all she had to do was invoke Liu Hao’s name, and very few students at school dared to provoke her.","She still remembered that she had once led Liu Hao and several of his lackeys to ambush Liu Yutong.","Instead, Liu Yutong’s people had beaten them badly. Liu Hao had even been taken away and detained for quite some time.","After that, Zhao Zhu had never seen Liu Hao again. Later, when Liu Yutong sent her to prison, she completely lost touch with the outside world.","She never expected to run into him here.","But the change in him was simply too drastic.","The Yellow Hair Man was gone, replaced by a man driving a BMW, and his belly had grown several sizes larger.","Naturally, he was also much richer than before.","After getting out of the car, Liu Hao walked straight into the restaurant. He asked about the private rooms, then went directly upstairs.","Zhao Zhu hesitated for a moment before following him.","......","When Liu Hao pushed open the door to the private room, three or four people were already seated inside. They were all old brothers who had once followed him around Wuxian County. Naturally, they were also among the few who had not switched sides and joined the Dragon Society back then. By now, every one of them regretted that decision bitterly.","Regret was one thing, but life still had to go on. Most of them had since married and settled down. Some had opened car washes, while others had gone into transportation. They weren’t doing particularly well, but at least they had left behind the aimless life of blindly drifting around.","One could only mix with the underworld while young. As they grew older, they ultimately had to face reality.","“Brother Hao is here!”","“Brother Hao, sit here! Sit here!”","Liu Hao swaggered over to the seat of honor and plopped himself down, then slapped his BMW’s key fob onto the table. He put on an impressive show of authority.","The old brothers immediately began showering him with praise, flattering him until he was practically floating.","He was just about to start bragging about how profitable the new karaoke club he had opened in Danan City was when the door to the private room was suddenly pushed open from outside.","“Brother Hao.”","Liu Hao looked up and saw a woman wearing a baseball cap standing in the doorway.","The woman was thin and gaunt, with a sallow complexion. She looked somewhat familiar, but for a moment he couldn’t remember who she was.","The other old brothers glanced at one another. None of them recognized her either.","“It’s me, Zhao Zhu.” The woman pushed her cap upward, revealing her entire face.","Liu Hao froze. Then he shot to his feet, his eyes widening.","“Zhao... Zhao Zhu?!”","Of course he remembered Zhao Zhu.","Back then, in Wuxian County, he had led his men to ambush Liu Yutong, only to have one of her subordinates, a man named Yun Cheng, turn the tables and pin them to the ground.","Afterward, Liu Hao had been detained for quite some time. Once he was released, he had slunk off to Mingzhu City, then moved on to Danan City. In the end, he had accidentally helped Liu Yutong out of a difficult situation, which more or less settled the grudge between them. Later, because of Liu Yutong’s intervention, he had become one of the more prominent bosses in Danan City.","Of course, he no longer lived the life of a street tough. It wasn’t that he didn’t want to—it was that he didn’t dare.","Wherever the Dragon Society operated, every so-called underworld boss who caused trouble met a bad end, without exception.","Back then, he had relied on Liu Yutong’s name to build up enough capital. He had opened several entertainment venues, and his life was now fairly comfortable. He had even managed to cultivate himself a beer belly.","Compared with how much he had changed, Zhao Zhu was obviously in far worse shape. She had been sent behind bars and spent several years there.","“Aren’t you... still in prison?” Liu Hao asked instinctively.","The moment the words left his mouth, he realized how inappropriate they sounded and hurriedly corrected himself.","“No, that’s not what I meant. I mean, you’re out?”","“Yeah. I was released early.” Zhao Zhu nodded. “I behaved well, so my sentence was reduced.”"]},{"number":893,"title":"Chapter 893: 894. Borrowing Money (Thanks to 'Her Highness Luweiya' for the King of Gifts)","paragraphs":["Liu Hao looked at her, his heart filled with mixed emotions.","Three years ago, Zhao Zhu could not exactly be called a stunning beauty, but at least she had been a fresh-faced, attractive high school girl. The woman standing before him now had rough, sallow skin and was dressed in cheap clothes. The youthful look she once possessed was completely gone.","“Sit! Sit! Sit down and talk.” Liu Hao came back to himself and hurriedly ushered her to a seat, then told the waiter to bring over another set of bowls and chopsticks.","“Thank you!” Zhao Zhu pulled out a chair and sat down.","The old brothers at the table also remembered who she was and quickly greeted her.","None of them had expected that Brother Hao’s former god-sister would turn into this.","Liu Hao cleared his throat twice and said with concern, “Zhao Zhu, you must have had a hard time in there these past few years.”","“It was all right.”","Zhao Zhu pointed at the car keys in front of him and asked, “Brother Hao, you’re doing pretty well for yourself now. You’re even driving a BMW.”","At the mention of this, Liu Hao immediately perked up and switched into bragging mode.","“Oh, it’s nothing much. I’ve got a few entertainment venues over in Dannan City—four or five of them altogether. I’ve got over a hundred guys working under me. I only bought this BMW last year. It was just a few hundred thousand yuan. I drive it around for fun.”","In reality, those “guys” of his were mostly waiters. Of course, quite a few of them had indeed been his underlings back when he was running around Dannan City, so it could be considered a transformation of sorts.","Only after Zhao Zhu had listened to him finish boasting did she ask, “Brother Hao, do you know how Liu Yutong and Yu Xin are doing now?”","The moment he heard those two names, the smile on Liu Hao’s face gradually disappeared.","The other old brothers also fell silent in unspoken agreement.","Those two names were famous not only in Wuxian County, but throughout the entire business world of Longguo. They were major figures standing at the very top of the pyramid.","They belonged to a completely different world from people like them.","“Zhao Zhu, why are you asking about them? Don’t tell me you’re still thinking about what happened back then.”","“That was all in the past. I don’t have anything to do with them anymore.”","Liu Hao was speaking from the heart. He truly had no connection with them anymore.","Although it was thanks to Liu Yutong’s help that he had achieved what he had today, the two of them really had no contact now. Someone like her would never become friends with someone like him. He simply wasn’t worthy.","Seemingly afraid that Zhao Zhu still had not let go of what happened back then, Liu Hao hesitated for a moment before advising her:","“Zhao Zhu...”","“Your brother has to give you some advice. Let the past stay in the past. Don’t keep thinking about all that nonsense. What kind of person is Liu Yutong? She’s the Dragon Society’s Young Mistress. She has over ten thousand men under her command—over ten thousand, do you understand? Can you even imagine that scene?","“The force she travels with is terrifying. And the businesses she runs now all start at the hundred-million-yuan level. You’d better not provoke her, or you could end up dead without even knowing how it happened.”","“You’re overthinking it, Brother Hao. I just want to know how they’re doing now.”","“I spent more than three years inside and didn’t know anything about what was happening outside. I was just curious,” Zhao Zhu said calmly.","Liu Hao was not entirely convinced.","It was understandable for someone who had spent more than three years in prison to ask about an enemy’s current situation after getting out. But Zhao Zhu’s expression was far too calm. It was so calm that it made him feel slightly uneasy.","“All right.” Liu Hao decided not to say anything more and called for the waiter to bring out the dishes.","The old brothers became lively again, chatting about this and that while drinking, bragging, and laughing loudly.","Zhao Zhu did not bring up Liu Yutong or Yu Xin again. She simply sat there quietly eating, occasionally joining in with a laugh. On the surface, she truly looked like an ordinary person who had finally regained her freedom and only wanted to live a peaceful life.","After several rounds of drinks and once the dishes had been half cleared, Zhao Zhu suddenly put down her chopsticks and said to Liu Hao, “Brother Hao, I’d like to borrow some money from you.”","Liu Hao froze. “Borrow money? How much?”","“One hundred thousand.”","Liu Hao hesitated slightly at the figure.","A hundred thousand yuan was not a huge amount to him, but it was not pocket change either.","The businesses he ran had impressive-looking cash flow, but after deducting wages, rent, and all the other expenses, only so much ended up in his own pocket each month.","More importantly, he was not entirely comfortable with Zhao Zhu’s purpose in borrowing the money.","Seeing his hesitation, Zhao Zhu added, “I want to start a small business and make a fresh start. After spending more than three years inside, I have to find some way to make a living. Don’t worry. I’ll pay you back as soon as I start making money.”","In the end, Liu Hao agreed. He took out his phone and said, “All right. Give me your bank account number, and I’ll have the finance department transfer it to you.”","No matter what, Zhao Zhu had once called him Brother Hao. Back then, he had failed to help her when it mattered most, allowing her to suffer so terribly at Liu Yutong’s hands.","Although, when everything was said and done, she had brought it upon herself, he still felt some guilt as her senior. He would treat this money as compensation.","Once the transfer was complete, Zhao Zhu stood up and gave him a slight bow.","“Thank you, Brother Hao. I’ll be going now.”","“Hey, leaving already? Sit a little longer.”","“No, I still have something to do.”","Zhao Zhu pulled her cap low over her face again and walked out of the private room. She did not disappear from sight until she had left the restaurant and vanished onto the road outside.","Liu Hao stood by the window with his wineglass in hand, watching her retreating figure. He drained a large mouthful of wine, his expression complicated.","Things really had changed.","One of the old brothers beside him came over and could not help asking, “Brother Hao, she didn’t borrow money because she’s planning to cause trouble, did she?”","“Cause trouble? You mean for Liu Yutong?” Liu Hao sneered.","“She wouldn’t dare, even if you gave her ten times the courage! What kind of status does that Young Mistress have now? And what kind of status does Zhao Zhu have? One is in the heavens, the other on earth. How could she possibly go after her?","“She only needs to move a finger, and Zhao Zhu could die without leaving a trace.”","That was what he said, but after Zhao Zhu left, Liu Hao still took out his phone and scrolled through his contacts until he found a number.","He had shamelessly asked for it years ago when he was in Dannan City. It belonged to the female bodyguard who had always stayed by Liu Yutong’s side.","He had no idea whether the number still worked.","The phone rang several times, and to his surprise, someone answered.","“Hello? Who is this?”","“Hello! Sis! How are you? This is Liu Hao—the Liu Hao from Dannan City. We’ve met before. Do you remember me?”","“What do you want?”","Liu Hao briefly explained that Zhao Zhu had come to him after being released from prison, then emphasized at the end, “I don’t mean anything by it. I just thought I should let you know. What if she loses her head and tries to do something? You know...”","“All right. I understand. Thank you.”","After hanging up, Liu Hao let out a long breath.","He had done everything he could. The rest depended on whether Zhao Zhu knew when to stop.","If she did not, there was nothing more he could do.","Less than two minutes after that call ended, the news reached Liu Yutong and Yu Xin’s ears.","[Zhao Zhu has been released from prison and is currently in Wuxian County. She asked about the Young Mistress and Sister Yu, and borrowed one hundred thousand yuan from Liu Hao. Her purpose is unknown.]"]},{"number":894,"title":"Chapter 894: 895. The Last String Broke.","paragraphs":["Yu Xin’s itinerary for this trip back home was packed. First, she returned to her old school, No. 2 High School, to attend the unveiling ceremony for a student-aid fund. She then held a meeting with the county leaders, finalizing the preliminary agreement for the Dragon Society to invest in and build an agricultural-products processing base in Wushui County.","After that, she arranged a lavish celebration for her grandmother’s sixty-eighth birthday.","The occasion was lively. Every distant aunt and uncle she barely remembered showed up, along with relatives who were barely related to her at all.","Although Yu Xin knew most of them had come because of her current status and wealth, she still greeted every guest with a smile and personally welcomed them into the hotel for the banquet.","After all, at her level, there was no need to fuss over such trivial matters. They were nothing more than distant relatives hoping to benefit from her connections.","Once her grandmother’s birthday celebration was over, Yu Xin did not return directly to Pearl City. Instead, she drove alone to the river behind No. 2 High School.","She walked slowly along the riverbank, the heels of her shoes clicking crisply against the newly paved stone path.","The place had changed dramatically.","A little over three years ago, it had been nothing but a bare concrete road, with weeds growing wildly along the river and only a few crooked willow trees standing nearby.","Now, both banks had been landscaped with rows of ginkgo and osmanthus trees. A wooden boardwalk and viewing platforms had also been built, turning the area into the county’s favorite spot for residents to take an after-dinner stroll.","Yu Xin stopped near the place where she had once fallen into the water. Resting her hands on the railing, she gazed at the river flowing slowly before her.","This was the place.","Three years ago, shortly before the college entrance examination, Zhao Zhu had brought several girls here and cornered her. Zhao Zhu had pushed her into the river.","The instant the water rushed into her nose and mouth, she had truly believed she was going to die.","Fortunately, Sister Yutong’s people had arrived in time and pulled her out.","After that, everything changed.","She was no longer the timid girl everyone could bully at will. She had joined the Dragon Society, gained a family of brothers and sisters who were willing to entrust their lives to one another, and built an astonishingly successful enterprise.","Yu Xin stared at the calm surface of the river for an unknown length of time before suddenly speaking.","“Come out.”","Zhao Zhu stepped out from behind a large tree, her expression shifting uncertainly.","“You knew I was here?”","“I knew.”","Yu Xin turned around and leaned against the railing, crossing her arms as she calmly looked at her.","Although Yu Xin stood on the lower ground by the riverbank while Zhao Zhu was positioned higher up on the embankment, Yu Xin somehow looked as though she were looking down at Zhao Zhu from a position of superiority.","That was the pressure created by sheer presence.","“You’ve been following me for three days—from No. 2 High School to the county government offices, then to the hotel entrance. You even waited outside Yuyue Restaurant for forty minutes this morning. Zhao Zhu, you’re really terrible at tailing people.”","Zhao Zhu’s expression changed.","She had never expected that Yu Xin had discovered her movements long ago.","“So what if you knew? You came alone today, and I want to see where you can run!”","With that, she suddenly waved her hand.","A dozen or more hooligans burst out from the landscaped areas on both sides of the riverbank. Their hair was dyed every color imaginable, and they carried steel pipes and baseball bats.","These men had been hired with the one hundred thousand yuan Liu Hao had lent Zhao Zhu.","In a small place like Wushui County, one hundred thousand yuan was enough to hire more than a dozen street thugs to risk their lives for you.","Their leader was a wiry young man with a Mohawk and half a cigarette dangling from the corner of his mouth. He looked Yu Xin up and down, then sneered.","“Sister Zhao, this is the bitch who owes you money? She’s pretty hot. Is she really the only one?”","“She’s the only one. Beat her half to death! I’ll take responsibility if anything happens!” Zhao Zhu said through clenched teeth.","The Mohawk spat out his cigarette butt, took two steps forward with the steel pipe in hand, and said to Yu Xin, “Miss, don’t blame your big brother for being rough. I’m just taking money to solve someone’s problem. If you want someone to blame, blame yourself for offending someone you shouldn’t have—”","He suddenly fell silent.","He had seen the badge on Yu Xin’s chest.","It was a dragon-shaped badge with a platinum finish and a gold border.","As a street thug operating in Wushui County, he knew roughly what the different Dragon Society badges represented.","A silver badge meant an ordinary member. A platinum badge with a gold border signified a core figure of great importance. As for the pure gold badge, there was only one in existence—the Dragon Society’s Young Mistress.","The Dragon Society.","She was actually one of its members! And not just any member—she was a major figure with a platinum badge!","The Mohawk’s body began trembling instinctively. His legs went weak.","The other thugs had not yet realized what was happening, and one of them even urged him on.","“Boss, get moving! She’s just a woman—”","Before he could finish, they heard the sound of numerous footsteps.","The footsteps were dense and heavy, coming from every direction.","The thugs instinctively turned their heads. One by one, their expressions froze.","The dam was filled with countless figures.","They all wore black suits and identical silver dragon-shaped badges.","Twenty people. Fifty. A hundred...","The Mohawk and his men were so terrified that they dropped to the ground.","“We’re finished! We kicked an iron plate! They’re from the Dragon Society!”","The Mohawk finally came to his senses. He scrambled to his knees and frantically kowtowed to Yu Xin.","“Please spare me, sis! Please spare me! I didn’t know you were with the Dragon Society!”","“It was Zhao Zhu! That bitch Zhao Zhu tricked us and said you were a deadbeat who refused to pay your debts. We were deceived! We were deceived!”","The other thugs also fell to their knees and begged for mercy.","They might have been able to bully ordinary people, but compared with the Dragon Society, they were nothing more than ants facing an elephant.","There was no way a bunch of nobodies like them could afford to provoke the Dragon Society.","“Please spare us, sis! We were really deceived!”","“It was Zhao Zhu, that troublemaker! She told us you owed her money, so we came!”","“That’s right, it was all Zhao Zhu! Please be magnanimous and let us go!”","“We’ll never dare do it again! We really won’t!”","The dozen or so men knelt on the ground, crying and begging, their faces smeared with tears and snot. They kowtowed so hard that their foreheads began to bleed.","Zhao Zhu stood among them, her body trembling instinctively as she watched so many men in black appear.","Only those who had truly faced the Dragon Society knew how terrifying it was.","“You useless idiots! A bunch of worthless trash!” Zhao Zhu suddenly screamed hysterically.","Yu Xin did not even spare the kneeling thugs a glance. Her eyes remained fixed on Zhao Zhu as she mocked her.","“Zhao Zhu.”","“After more than three years, this is still all you know how to do? Call a few street thugs to corner someone? Can’t you come up with anything new?”","Yu Xin’s contemptuous gaze enraged Zhao Zhu completely. Her eyes bloodshot, she shouted, “Yu Xin, don’t hide behind your numbers! If you have the guts, fight me one-on-one!”","“One-on-one?”","Yu Xin let out a soft laugh.","“Fine. I’ll give you what you want.”","She immediately took off her suit jacket and casually handed it to one of the men in black. Then she rolled her wrists and said, “Since you want a one-on-one fight, I’ll grant you that wish. If you can beat me, I’ll let you leave. But if you lose... you know what will happen.”","Seeing how completely Yu Xin looked down on her, Zhao Zhu grew even more furious. She smashed the brick in her hand onto the ground, clenched her fists, and charged forward.","She refused to believe she could lose to Yu Xin—the coward she had once known.","But she was wrong.","The moment her fist swung forward, Yu Xin easily dodged it. At the same time, Yu Xin seized her wrist with her left hand and kicked hard at her ankle with her right foot. Zhao Zhu instantly lost her balance and crashed heavily onto the stone pavement, striking her chin and drawing blood.","One move.","It had taken only one move for Zhao Zhu to end up sprawled on the ground.","Zhao Zhu struggled to get back up, but a high heel came down on her back, pinning her in place.","Yu Xin looked down at her from above, her gaze cold and indifferent.","“Zhao Zhu, do you know something?”","“Everything I’ve learned over the years was for dealing with people a hundred times more dangerous than you. What do you think you are?”","“I know you hate me. You hate me for sending you to prison, for living a better life than you. Even now, you still think I ruined your life, don’t you?”","“That’s right! It was you! And that Liu Yutong too!” Zhao Zhu said through gritted teeth.","“What a joke!”","“Who was it that bullied a classmate in the bathroom? Who pushed me into the river? Who brought a gang of thugs to block me outside the school gates? Zhao Zhu, you ended up like this because of the choices you made, one step at a time. You can’t blame anyone else!”","“You bullied me before because you thought I was weak. Now you hate me because you’ve realized I’m stronger than you.”","“From beginning to end, you’ve never changed. You’ll always blame other people for your own misfortunes.”","“Enough!” Zhao Zhu shouted, her eyes red as she tried to cut her off.","“It’s not enough!”","“Zhao Zhu, let me make this clear. In my eyes, you’re nothing now. If I wanted you to disappear from this world, it would be no more difficult than crushing an ant.”","“Lift your head and look at the people around me. Look at who they are, then look at yourself.”","Zhao Zhu stiffly raised her head and swept her gaze over the intimidating crowd of men in black.","No matter how unwilling she was to admit it, she had to acknowledge that the gap between her and Yu Xin was simply too great. She had only refused to admit it all this time.","Yu Xin finally lifted her foot and took a step back.","“I’m letting you go today, giving you one last chance. After all, I’m a law-abiding citizen. I don’t want to get my hands dirty over someone like you.”","“From now on, don’t ever appear in front of me again. And don’t ever appear in front of Sister Yutong again.”","“Otherwise, all it will take is one phone call, and you and your entire family will disappear from this place. I mean every word.”","Zhao Zhu’s whole body suddenly trembled.","Yu Xin did not look at her again. Surrounded by the men in black, she turned and walked along the ginkgo-lined avenue toward the waiting motorcade.","The thugs were taken away as well.","Golden ginkgo leaves were blown down by the wind. One landed on her shoulder before gently sliding to the ground.","Behind her, Zhao Zhu knelt alone in the open space, watching the figure surrounded by men in black grow farther and farther away, becoming more and more indistinct.","This time, what surged through her heart was not hatred, but a feeling of utter powerlessness.","The gap was simply too great.","So great that even her hatred seemed laughable.","All the resentment Zhao Zhu had accumulated during her more than three years in prison, all the revenge she had meticulously planned with a hundred thousand yuan—it was nothing but a joke in the other woman’s eyes.","The woman had not even considered her worthy of taking action against.","Zhao Zhu knelt there and suddenly began to laugh.","At first, it was a low chuckle. Then it grew louder and sharper, until it turned into hysterical laughter.","“Haha... hahaha... hahahahaha...”","The tightly wound string in her mind, stretched taut for more than three years, finally snapped at that moment.","She... had gone mad."]},{"number":895,"title":"Chapter 895: 896. The Great Battle in the Social Sphere.","paragraphs":["“Zhao Zhu went crazy?”","“She did.”","“Not long after I left with my people, the patrol officers found her throwing a tantrum and rolling around on the bridge. They took her to the county hospital, where she was diagnosed with schizophrenia. After that, she was transferred to a psychiatric hospital for treatment.”","Liu Yutong nodded when she heard this.","She had long since stopped feeling anything toward Zhao Zhu. She neither hated nor pitied her.","Although Zhao Zhu had bullied her in high school, Liu Yutong had made sure she received the punishment she deserved.","Besides, over the past three years, Liu Yutong had been busy dealing with the Wanlong Association, and the name Zhao Zhu had practically been erased from her memory.","Now that she suddenly heard it again, she was actually dazed for a moment before remembering what Zhao Zhu looked like.","“Come to think of it, her life is pretty tragic. She’s only twenty-one, right?”","Yu Xin nodded. “Twenty-one. The same age as us.”","From eighteen to twenty-one—the best years of her life—she had wasted away behind bars. Then, only a few days after getting out, she had gone insane.","Sometimes, life was simply that cruel. You took one wrong step, only to realize later that the road ahead was all downhill, and by then, it was impossible to stop.","After sighing over the matter, Liu Yutong asked Yu Xin a question.","“Yu Xin, have you ever thought about taking over for me?”","Yu Xin froze. “Sister Yutong, what did you say?”","“I asked whether you’ve ever thought about becoming the CEO of the Wanlong Association Group.” This was the first time Liu Yutong had asked Yu Xin the question so directly.","Yu Xin shook her head. “To be honest, I haven’t.”","“Why not?” Liu Yutong asked.","“Sister Yutong, you’re the same age as me, but I could never do the things you’ve done. And besides, I’m perfectly happy being your assistant. I really can’t handle being the CEO.”","“I’m already very satisfied with things as they are!”","“Don’t refuse so quickly. How about this? I’ll give you two years. Within those two years, Longyao Mobile must break into the top five of the global smartphone market. When the time comes, we’ll talk again about whether you’ll take over.”","“Sister Yutong, you’re serious? I...”","“I am. I have other things to do, and I wouldn’t feel comfortable handing the Wanlong Association Group over to anyone else.”","Liu Yutong was speaking the truth. She had too many things to deal with now, and she also harbored a grand ambition: to work with the Xuanhuang Association, which had been established earlier, and build a colossal multinational conglomerate.","That would be extremely difficult, especially since expanding overseas was no easy task. She would have to devote a great deal of time and energy to it.","But the Wanlong Association Group was her foundation. She could not simply hand it over to some professional manager. As for veterans like Ma Da, their educational backgrounds and abilities were limited.","Although Xu Shishi was highly capable and had performed exceptionally well, Liu Yutong had never considered her for the position.","After thinking it over, she decided that Yu Xin was the only suitable candidate.","Seeing that Liu Yutong was not joking, Yu Xin could not help but take a deep breath.","“The pressure feels enormous!”","Liu Yutong laughed. “Relax. You still have two years. Do your best!”","Yu Xin nodded firmly. “Sister Yutong, I definitely won’t let you down!”","However, neither of them could have imagined that the originally planned two-year transition would ultimately be delayed for five years.","Of course, that was a story for later.","...","The establishment of the Made-in-China Pride Alliance remained one of the hottest topics in China’s technology industry throughout the second half of 2010.","Most domestic manufacturers were filled with fighting spirit after joining the alliance. All of them wanted to charge to the front and seize as much market share as possible.","In 2010, foreign brands accounted for nearly ninety percent of the country’s mobile phone market. Domestic phones were practically insignificant by comparison.","It was not until the sudden arrival of the Longyao S1 that this deadlock was forcibly broken. After several months of fierce competition, it had barely managed to enter the top ten in the domestic market.","Later, Lei Jobs’s Dami also began to make its move. Although it had yet to enter the top ten, it had sold more than five hundred thousand phones between its launch and the end of the year.","The strong performances of the Longyao S1 and the Dami 1 gave other manufacturers tremendous confidence. They showed everyone that domestic smartphones still had a chance. As long as the products were good enough and offered excellent value for money, consumers were willing to buy them.","Especially before the fourth quarter had even ended, estimates showed that domestic smartphones had already entered the top five in market share.","If someone had presented that figure a year earlier—or even six months earlier—not a single person would have believed that domestic smartphones could rise so quickly.","While the Made-in-China Alliance was thriving and domestic smartphone manufacturers were advancing triumphantly, another fierce war was escalating.","It was the battle between the Big Goose’s GooseChat and WeChat.","The trigger for this conflict was WeChat’s explosive user growth.","After the Longyao S1 launch event, WeChat benefited from the dual boost of being preinstalled on phones and its trade-in program. Combined with traffic redirected from Dami phones, Weibo, and other platforms, as well as its aggressive promotional campaigns later on, its user base soared from just several hundred thousand during the internal testing phase to more than thirty million.","That kind of growth was absolutely unprecedented in China’s mobile internet industry in 2010. It also caught many people off guard.","No one had expected anyone to dare challenge the Big Goose’s dominance in the social networking space in this day and age.","What truly made Pony Ma uneasy was WeChat’s rapid product iteration.","After launching voice messages, WeChat rolled out three major features in succession: group chats, Moments, and official-account subscriptions.","Moments focused on sharing among existing friends. Users could post text, pictures, and voice updates, while friends could like and comment on them. As soon as the feature went live, it rapidly became the biggest driver of increased time spent on WeChat.","Official-account subscriptions, meanwhile, began transforming WeChat from a simple chat app into a content platform.","News outlets, self-media creators, and brands all rushed to join. Users could subscribe to accounts and receive content that interested them. This model—bringing information directly to people—was groundbreaking at the time.","By December 2010, WeChat’s registered users had surpassed fifty million, while its daily active users remained steadily above ten million.","Although that figure was nowhere near QQ’s six hundred million monthly active users, another statistic left Pony Ma feeling suffocated: WeChat users spent three times as long on the app each day as QQ mobile users did.","Three times.","What did that mean?","It meant users preferred WeChat. It meant QQ’s user retention on mobile was being left far behind by WeChat’s overwhelming advantage.","Even more troubling was that WeChat’s user-growth curve was still shooting upward at an almost vertical angle. There seemed to be no way to hold it back.","Pony Ma had even considered using the same tactic he had employed during the recent 630 War—forcing users to choose between the two services.","But he did not dare.","He could go after Zhou Hongyi. He could even dare to confront him in person.","But Liu Yutong?","He truly did not dare provoke her.","So all he could do was swallow his anger and endure it."]},{"number":896,"title":"Chapter 896: 897. Liu Yutong appears in Shencheng.","paragraphs":["Liu Yutong had another trump card that made Pony Ma extremely wary.","That was the mobile phone alliance she had built.","If she wanted to, she could easily find an excuse to have Longyao phones—and even most mobile phones across the country—remove the GooseChat app.","If users couldn’t even download it, how could GooseChat possibly compete with WeChat?","Of course, there was another major reason WeChat had risen so quickly: it continued Longyao’s user benefits program and directly subsidized users’ data charges. That was the truly ruthless move.","Although this cost more than ten billion yuan every month, it brought explosive growth in the user base.","Naturally, Big Goose later introduced data subsidies as well, but for the time being, they had only managed to reach an agreement with China Unicom. Liu Yutong, on the other hand, had used her connections in the capital to secure deals with all three major carriers.","And as 3G began to spread nationwide and smartphone penetration continued to rise, users’ demand for mobile data grew larger and larger.","Under those circumstances, did users even need to think about which app to choose?","During this period, Pony Ma was so anxious that sores had even appeared at the corners of his mouth. He had also lost his temper—something extremely rare for him—at a meeting of the company’s senior executives.","“Three months! Within three months, we must hold back WeChat! If we’re forced out of the mobile social networking market, it’s all over for us!”","“Don’t hold back on resources. Spend whatever it takes!”","“And the features—keep up with them at all costs!”","Big Goose’s response time was fairly quick.","The newly launched GooseChat was updated at an especially rapid pace. Of course, most of those updates involved borrowing ideas from WeChat.","It was practically a one-to-one replica of WeChat, with voice messages, Moments, group chats, official accounts, and more. Even the icon and color scheme looked almost identical.","The only difference was that WeChat was green, while GooseChat was blue.","This kind of strategy was nothing new in the internet industry. Big Goose had used the same approach when it created QQ. Later, when it entered gaming, email, and browsers, it followed the exact same playbook.","First, launch a competing product with similar features as quickly as possible. Then use QQ’s massive traffic pool to funnel users into it, relying on sheer scale to crush the rival to death.","For nearly ten years, this strategy had worked almost every time.","But this time was different.","After GooseChat went online, QQ did indeed begin flooding users with promotions.","Pop-up ads on the PC version, advertisements on QQ’s mobile launch screen, ad placements in Qzone, promotional messages in email signatures... Every product under Big Goose was directing traffic toward GooseChat.","In just one month, GooseChat’s registered users surged to thirty million—at least twice as fast as WeChat’s early growth.","But the problems soon became apparent.","To be honest, GooseChat’s user experience was at least one or two levels below WeChat’s.","The gap had nothing to do with the number of features. It was a difference in product philosophy.","Although Big Goose had borrowed WeChat’s design, it still habitually retained relatively complicated interfaces. This was mainly because its way of thinking had been too slow to change—a common problem among large corporations. As a result, apart from looking like WeChat on the surface, the entire product felt more like a stripped-down version of QQ.","The WeChat team, however, had never been burdened by that mindset.","Zhang Dalong had been personally recruited from Big Goose by Liu Yutong. His consistent philosophy was to simplify—to make things as simple as possible.","After he joined the Wanlong Club, Liu Yutong gave him only one instruction:","“Build the product you want to build. Don’t worry about making money. Focus on perfecting the user experience first.”","Perfect.","In the internet industry of 2010, aside from the Wanlong Club, no other company dared to pursue those two words.","Because perfection meant burning money—an enormous amount of money.","Take the subsidies, for example. Who would be willing to spend more than ten billion yuan a month subsidizing users’ mobile data fees?","No one!","Even Big Goose was still hesitating at this point. Of course, once they came to their senses, they began to follow suit as well.","Regardless, the battle between the two social apps had become so fierce that they were practically beating each other senseless.","While countless onlookers watched the two giants clash and placed their bets on who would ultimately win, something happened in mid-December, in Deep City.","Liu Yutong’s Maybach stopped in front of Big Goose’s headquarters.","The moment the car came to a halt, the security guards in the building grew tense.","It wasn’t because the Maybach itself was particularly rare. Deep City was full of wealthy people. Although Maybachs were uncommon, they were hardly enough to make anyone nervous.","What truly unsettled the guards were the dozen or so black Mercedes-Benz cars following behind the Maybach, along with the group of young men who climbed out of them. They were all dressed in black suits, each wearing a dragon-shaped badge on his chest.","Every one of them wore a black suit. Every one of them had a strong, muscular build. They looked just like the bodyguards in a television drama—intimidating enough to make anyone uneasy.","“Who are these people?”","“No idea. Probably some big shot here for an inspection.”","“Shh, keep your voice down. Don’t let them hear you!”","“...”","While the guards whispered among themselves and tried to guess the visitors’ identities, Pony Ma appeared and personally came downstairs to greet them.","When he saw Liu Yutong, he smiled and extended his hand.","“Director Liu, welcome, welcome!”","“President Ma, you’re too kind!”","The two shook hands before walking side by side into Big Goose’s headquarters.",".........."]},{"number":897,"title":"Chapter 897: 898. I Want to Become the Largest Shareholder of Big Goose","paragraphs":["At the Big Goose Group, in Pony Ma’s office.","After the secretary brought in the tea, Pony Ma dismissed her and casually closed the door behind her.","Only Liu Yutong and Pony Ma remained in the office.","“Director Liu, you made a special trip to Deep City today. Surely you didn’t come all this way just to have tea with me?”","“Of course not. I’m here to discuss business with President Ma.” Liu Yutong had never liked beating around the bush, so she got straight to the point.","“Business? What kind of business?”","“Big Goose’s business, of course.”","At those words, Pony Ma’s pupils contracted slightly.","“Director Liu, I... don’t quite understand what you mean.”","Looking at him with a warm smile, Liu Yutong said, “President Ma, then I’ll be direct. The shares of Big Goose held by you and your founding partners together amount to roughly ten percent. Of the remaining shares, Southfly Capital is the largest shareholder, holding more than thirty percent. The rest are scattered among various institutional and public shareholders.”","“What I want to tell you is that I plan to acquire all of Big Goose’s shares currently held by Southfly Capital. Together with the shares I previously purchased on the secondary market, I’ll become Big Goose’s largest shareholder.”","The smile slowly faded from Pony Ma’s face.","“You want to acquire Big Goose? Director Liu, that’s quite an appetite you have! Do you know how much Big Goose is worth right now?”","“Of course. More than three hundred billion.”","“But that was before WeChat came along. Now, it should be worth only a little over two hundred billion, right?” Liu Yutong said.","Pony Ma replied in a low voice, “Even if it’s only two hundred billion, do you think you can afford to buy it?”","Liu Yutong smiled. “If I want to, I can absolutely come up with an equivalent amount of money. If you don’t believe me, we can put it to the test.”","Pony Ma was speechless.","Though he kept a calm expression on the surface, turbulent waves were already churning inside him.","It wasn’t that he had never estimated Liu Yutong’s wealth. Based on the information he had previously obtained and his own analysis, he had assumed that she could mobilize no more than fifty billion.","But judging from her tone now, she had far more money than he had imagined—possibly enough to swallow Big Goose whole.","How had this woman managed to do it?","Or rather, what gave her the right to be so rich?","“President Ma, don’t overthink this. I’m not here to strip you of your power. I simply want to become Big Goose’s largest shareholder. I have no intention of taking control from you.”","“Even if I become the largest shareholder, you can continue serving as chairman of the board. I won’t interfere with the company’s day-to-day operations at all. You can still decide the company’s strategic direction. I’ll exercise my shareholder rights only at the board level—voting when necessary and speaking up when I have something to say. That’s all.”","Pony Ma continued to regard her darkly. Although she had made such a promise, he didn’t dare take her at her word.","This woman was simply too dangerous—more dangerous than a venomous snake.","He had no intention of agreeing, but he still asked, “What are your terms?”","“The condition is that WeChat becomes part of Big Goose.”","Pony Ma froze. He hadn’t expected Liu Yutong to make such a proposal.","If WeChat were merged into Big Goose, it would no longer be an independent business under the Wanlong Association, but would become part of the Big Goose Group.","In exchange, she would become Big Goose’s largest shareholder, while he would continue to steer the company.","“President Ma, you can take your time and think it over. After all, I’m not trying to drive you out. I only want to become the largest shareholder. You can continue doing exactly what you’ve been doing.”","“If you insist on hearing the truth, I don’t actually want to keep burning money fighting you like this. I don’t think either of us benefits if the conflict continues.”","“Cooperation would be better. We could all make money. Why not?”","Pony Ma was speechless.","He didn’t respond, instead rapidly weighing his options.","This year, Big Goose’s market value had peaked at nearly four hundred billion Hong Kong dollars. But over the past six months or so, the market’s expectations for Big Goose’s future growth had been significantly lowered, and its share price had steadily declined. Its current market capitalization stood at roughly two hundred and eighty billion Hong Kong dollars.","That amounted to approximately thirty-five billion US dollars at the current exchange rate.","Compared with the same period in his previous life, this figure was considerably lower.","The reason was simple: the market wasn’t optimistic about Big Goose’s competitiveness in the era of mobile social networking. Or rather, it believed that WeChat posed a serious threat.","Southfly Capital held more than thirty percent of Big Goose’s shares. Based on a market capitalization of two hundred and eighty billion Hong Kong dollars, those shares were worth more than eighty-four billion Hong Kong dollars, or roughly eleven billion US dollars.","That figure was astronomical to ordinary people. Even Pony Ma couldn’t come up with that much money at present.","But Liu Yutong could.","The several investment firms under her control—especially those overseas—had been growing explosively over the past few years. Their combined assets now amounted to nearly seventy billion US dollars.","The 2008 financial crisis had passed, but its aftershocks would not disappear so quickly. The European debt crisis in the middle of this year, for instance, along with a flash crash in the US stock market, had both allowed her to make a fortune.","On top of that, the technology stocks she had invested in years ago were rapidly appreciating. With all these factors combined, the wealth she had accumulated grew increasingly vast—and increasingly terrifying.","If she mobilized all of it, buying not just one Big Goose Group but two would be no problem.","Still, Liu Yutong didn’t want to remain locked in a life-or-death struggle with Pony Ma.","There was no need for it.","If she could bring Big Goose—and Pony Ma himself—onto her side through this arrangement, it might not be a bad thing.","Pony Ma still refused to give her an answer. Instead, he asked again, “Director Liu, even if you have the money to buy the shares, that doesn’t mean they’ll be willing to sell them to you.”","“Don’t be so absolute, President Ma. As long as Big Goose’s share price keeps falling and its prospects remain bleak, they won’t be able to resist selling.”","“Big Goose and WeChat have been fighting for nearly two months. Have you managed to crush it? Those people aren’t fools. They’re bound to consider whether the value of their shares will continue to shrink.”","“But if WeChat becomes part of Big Goose, the situation will be completely different.”","“With WeChat and QQ combined, Big Goose’s position in the mobile social networking sector will become unshakable. Once the market revalues the company, Big Goose’s market capitalization will climb back above four hundred billion. Reaching a trillion in the future will only be a matter of time.”","“In short, as I said, cooperation benefits both sides.”","“However, I don’t like seeing foreign capital make too much money off the people of our country. If you refuse, then I can only continue fighting you.”","“But I would like to remind you of one thing, President Ma: I may have considerably more capital at my disposal than you imagine.”","That final sentence carried more than a hint of a threat.","Pony Ma fell silent once again. For a moment, he was truly torn.","On one side was Liu Yutong’s forceful demand to become Big Goose’s largest shareholder. On the other was the enormous temptation of bringing WeChat into Big Goose.","It was an extraordinarily difficult choice.","He was afraid that Liu Yutong would sideline him after becoming the largest shareholder, but at the same time, he genuinely wanted to acquire WeChat.","After pondering for a long while...","Pony Ma spoke again. “Are you sure you can guarantee my rights?”","“Of course! I’ve never gone back on my word.”","Liu Yutong paused, then suddenly changed tack. “President Ma, I know you won’t agree right away and that you need time to think it over. How about this? While you’re considering it, let’s make a bet.”","For some reason, she had become increasingly fond of betting with people. Perhaps she simply enjoyed the thrill of having victory within her grasp.","Pony Ma frowned. “A bet? What are we betting on?”","Liu Yutong held up two fingers. “Within two months, MicroChat’s user base must surpass GooseTalk’s by at least thirty million. If I fail, I’ll give up becoming your company’s largest shareholder—and I’ll even give you MicroChat for free.”","“But if I succeed, President Ma, you must cooperate with me in acquiring Nanfei’s shares at a low price. In other words, you cannot reveal to anyone that MicroChat is being merged into Big Goose....”","Pony Ma’s eyes narrowed slightly.","In two months, she wanted to widen MicroChat’s lead to thirty million users.","At present, the two sides were locked in a tight race. MicroChat had fifty million users, while GooseTalk had forty-six million—a gap of only four million.","To widen that lead to thirty million within two months was practically impossible, especially since GooseTalk was also growing rapidly.","No matter how he looked at it, the odds were clearly in his favor.","“You’re that confident?”","Liu Yutong said, “You only need to answer one question: are you taking the bet or not?”","Pony Ma: “...”","Damn! This woman was incredibly intimidating!","Should he take the bet or not?","If he won, the threat posed by MicroChat would be completely eliminated. Big Goose would hold on to its position in mobile social networking and might even become more powerful than before.","If he lost, that would prove MicroChat truly was unstoppable. Rather than watching the stock price continue to plummet, he might as well accept Liu Yutong’s proposal, merge MicroChat into Big Goose, and let her become the company’s largest shareholder.","Although he would be somewhat unwilling to do so, at least he would still be the one at the helm.","Besides, he truly didn’t believe she could pull it off.","“Fine!”","“I’ll take your bet!”","“If MicroChat’s user base is thirty million higher than GooseTalk’s two months from now, I’ll cooperate with you in settling the matter of the shares.”","“It’s a deal!”","Liu Yutong extended her hand, and the two shook on it.","That settled their agreement.","After finishing their discussion about Big Goose, Liu Yutong turned down Pony Ma’s invitation to dinner and went straight to another location.","On the outskirts of western Deep City stood an unremarkable office building.","Big Ginger Innovation Technology Co., Ltd."]},{"number":898,"title":"Chapter 898: 899. Epic-Level Red Envelope Marketing","paragraphs":["Liu Yutong did not hurry back to Mingzhu City after leaving the Dage headquarters. Instead, she had the convoy detour to the western outskirts of Shencheng.","Dajiang Innovation Technology.","The company was still crammed into an unremarkable office building, without even a proper entrance.","When the security guard downstairs saw a convoy of black cars pull up, he was so startled that he immediately called his supervisor.","At the time, Wang Tao was in the laboratory, fine-tuning the flight-control parameters. When the receptionist told him there were visitors accompanied by a large group of black-clad men who looked like members of some kind of organization, he grew nervous as well. Had they offended someone?","By the time he ran downstairs, he was completely dumbfounded by the sight of the numerous men in black filling the lobby.","They were actually members of the Wanlong Association.","The Wanlong Group was already highly renowned in the technology industry.","WeChat, Wan Hui Select, Weibo... and countless other products all belonged to the Wanlong Group.","And, of course, there were the legendary black-clad guards who were said to be terrifyingly formidable.","Wang Tao had never expected to see them with his own eyes.","Under Wang Tao’s nervous yet flattered and enthusiastic reception, Liu Yutong toured the entire Dajiang company and viewed several prototype aircraft they were working on.","After the tour, Liu Yutong stated her purpose directly—she wanted to invest in Dajiang.","The negotiations went smoothly and quickly, taking less than two hours from start to finish.","Liu Yutong’s offer was impossible to refuse: one hundred million yuan for a forty-percent stake. She would not interfere with the company’s technical direction or daily management, retaining only the right to veto major decisions and a seat on the board of directors.","For Wang Tao, who was preparing to seek the company’s next round of financing, this was nothing short of a windfall.","Dajiang’s valuation was still below ten million yuan, yet the Young Lady of the Wanlong Association had opened with an offer of one hundred million, giving the company a valuation far beyond anything he had imagined. And the terms were hardly excessive.","After finalizing the investment in Dajiang, Liu Yutong did not linger in Shencheng. She flew back to Danan City that same day, then transferred to a car and returned to Mingzhu City.","The following two months were exceptionally lively.","First, after several months of fierce competition, the Wanlong Group’s internal Longteng Cup finally produced the two hundred elite contestants who would advance to the finals.","The two hundred contestants were divided into men’s and women’s divisions, with one hundred in each. Every one of them had fought their way through tens of thousands of core members across the seven major competition regions. Their abilities were beyond doubt.","Yun Cheng once again ranked first overall in the men’s division, with Chu Yang close behind in second.","Lan Die ranked first overall in the women’s division, while second place went to Zhang Lin, a twenty-two-year-old senior in college.","She was the biggest dark horse of the inaugural women’s division.","As for Lawyer Zhao, Zhao Tianyi had taken first place in the legal knowledge category without the slightest suspense.","The leaders of the other category rankings were equally impressive.","At the annual meeting in the Mingzhu City Stadium, these contestants would compete for the final overall championship and receive their awards personally from The Young Lady.","Time passed quickly, and before anyone knew it, January was already halfway over.","Just as everyone was looking forward to the arrival of the Spring Festival, a major piece of news exploded across Longguo’s internet industry.","WeChat, a subsidiary of the Wanlong Group, officially announced that it had secured the exclusive naming rights to this year’s CCTV Spring Festival Gala at a staggering price. It had also planned an unprecedented super-red-packet campaign.","On New Year’s Eve, all WeChat users would be able to participate in an interactive red-packet event during the gala, with a total prize pool of one billion yuan.","The campaign would take two forms. The first was collecting the Five Fortunes before the Spring Festival to divide up five hundred million yuan in cash. The second was drawing cash-filled fortune packets on the hour throughout New Year’s Eve, with the largest individual packet containing as much as one million yuan!","One billion!","In the internet industry of 2010 and 2011, that figure was practically the equivalent of a nuclear bomb.","After all, this was only the beginning of 2011!","At the time, most domestic internet companies were still racking their brains over how to monetize value-added services and advertising. An annual advertising revenue of more than one hundred million yuan was enough to make a company an industry giant, while spending money to subsidize users had only just begun to appear in the group-buying sector.","Yet the Wanlong Group had casually thrown out one billion yuan in pure cash red packets, blowing the industry’s ceiling clean off.","Less than half an hour after the announcement, Weibo’s hot-search list had completely exploded.","#WeChat’s One-Billion-Yuan Red Packets# Explosive!","#A New Way to Interact with the Spring Festival Gala# Explosive!","#Collect the Five Fortunes# Boiling!","#Million-Yuan Fortune Packets# Boiling!","The comment section descended into complete chaos, with all kinds of hilarious remarks appearing one after another.","“One billion! I’m terrible at math. Can someone count how many zeroes that is?”","“I did the math. Even if the entire country joined in, everyone would still get an average of seventy cents. That’s a huge sum of money, brothers!”","“Seventy cents? I only make eight hundred yuan a month. Seventy cents is enough to buy me two steamed buns. WeChat is incredible! I’m definitely joining in!”","“Has no one thought about this? What legitimate company would hand out one billion yuan in cash to its users? Could this be an attempt to launder money through red packets?”","“Watch your wording, buddy. Launder what money? The Wanlong Group’s legal department is warning you!”","“Hilarious. You actually dare to provoke the Wanlong Group’s legal department? Have you forgotten what happened to Fruit Phone when it got banned from sale?”","“A million yuan for a single fortune packet... I can already imagine the spectacular sight of the entire country shaking their phones like crazy on New Year’s Eve.”","“My grandmother made me register her for WeChat this afternoon. She says she’s going to win that million-yuan packet. I can’t stop her.”","“My grandfather is the same. He’s seventy this year and absolutely refused to switch to a smartphone before. Today, he took the initiative and asked me to teach him how to use WeChat. The Wanlong Group has truly seized the soft spot of the entire elderly population.”","“At least the older people in your families know how to use phones. My dad can’t even send a text message, but he’s already made me register WeChat accounts for all six members of our family. He says that when the time comes, we’ll all join in together. The more people, the better our chances.”","“This feels even more exciting than the New Year itself!”","“But this is the New Year! The Wanlong Group has practically taken over the Spring Festival Gala.”","“I really want to win that one million yuan! If I get it, I’m quitting my job on the spot and moving back to my hometown to retire!”","“............”","The public frenzy continued to build. But what truly sent onlookers and the entire industry into a collective frenzy was another detail dug up by an eagle-eyed netizen.","Someone discovered that Longfutong, the payment service holding a payment license under the Wanlong Group, was the official designated payment channel for the one-billion-yuan red-packet campaign.","All the red packets users won would be deposited directly into their personal Longfutong accounts. The money could then be used at any of the Wanlong Group’s consumer outlets, including Wanlong Plaza, Wanlong Supermarket, Yuyuefang, Huangquan Internet Cafe, Qingyin Tea Drinks, Wan Hui Select, and more, as well as third-party partner merchants that would soon open nationwide.","The moment this news came out, the entire internet industry exploded once again.","“Holy crap! They’re using the red packets as a gimmick to promote their own payment platform? That move is absolutely ruthless. Every part of it is linked together!”","“If they’re handing out one billion yuan in red packets, how many users are going to link their accounts to Longfutong in the process?”","“Now I’m suddenly worried about Ali! This is going to put a serious strain on Ali’s payment platform.”","“I’m a little worried about Big Goose too. Just look at their marketing strategy—Big Goose doesn’t stand a chance!”","“Exactly! I think GooseChat is doomed. Originally, the two companies had roughly the same number of users, but after this campaign, that might not be the case anymore.”","“Think about it—what kind of exposure does the Spring Festival Gala bring? On New Year’s Eve, hundreds of millions of people across the country will be watching. A casual verbal plug alone could reach tens of millions, not to mention the interactive segments. WeChat is practically rubbing it in Tencent’s face with this move!”","“Big Goose: ‘Well, aren’t you impressive? So noble, throwing a billion yuan in cash right in my face!’”","“Pony Ma probably can’t sleep by now, can he?”","“........”"]},{"number":899,"title":"Chapter 899: 900. Brother Ma's Helplessness, The Invitation Letter.","paragraphs":["Pony Ma of Deep City really couldn’t sleep.","More precisely, the moment he saw MicroChat’s plan for its Spring Festival Gala red-envelope campaign, he called an emergency meeting of the company’s senior executives that very night.","Deep City, Big Goose headquarters.","It was two in the morning. The entire office building was dark except for the lights in this conference room. Outside, Deep City glittered beneath a brilliant night sky, but no one inside had the slightest interest in looking at it.","Pony Ma sat at the head of the long conference table, a printed copy of MicroChat’s Spring Festival Gala red-envelope campaign plan lying in front of him.","His assistant had dug the plan out of Weibo and compiled it into a document. Although it was only three short pages, every word on it seemed to weigh a thousand pounds, pressing down on everyone until they could barely breathe.","Pony Ma had racked his brains but still couldn’t figure out how Liu Yutong planned to pull three million users away from GooseChat within two months.","It wasn’t until this one-billion-yuan red-envelope plan appeared that he truly understood how frightening that woman was.","Any marketing campaign she came up with was explosive. It was like a dimensionality-reduction attack.","More than a dozen people were seated in the conference room, all of them Big Goose’s core executives.","The head of GooseChat’s product division, the head of marketing, the chief technology officer, the person in charge of payment services...","Yet at that moment, every one of them had their head lowered. Not a single person dared to speak first.","After a long silence, Pony Ma finally asked, “Can someone tell me why this plan wasn’t thought up by Big Goose first?”","No one answered.","No one knew how to answer.","“One billion yuan!”","“Wanlong is willing to put one billion yuan into Spring Festival red envelopes, while we—our GooseChat doesn’t even have payment functionality integrated yet. Isn’t that a complete joke?”","The head of payment services braced himself and explained, “Mr. Ma, DragonPay obtained its payment license in the middle of last year. Our own payment license is still going through the regulatory approval process. And even if we urgently integrated payment functionality now, MicroChat has already signed the exclusive sponsorship deal for the Spring Festival Gala. We can’t follow them even if we want to.”","“I’m not here to listen to you report your difficulties.”","“I’m asking why they were faster than us. Why did they get their payment license more than six months before we did? Why could they think of the Spring Festival red-envelope campaign when hundreds of people across our entire team couldn’t?”","“GooseChat’s product manager, what exactly do you do all day?”","GooseChat’s product director was a young man in his early thirties. The moment he was singled out, his face went pale.","He really had nothing to say. He didn’t know how to explain himself.","Was he supposed to tell Pony Ma that almost all of GooseChat’s core functions had been copied from MicroChat, and that even their product-update schedule consisted of following behind MicroChat? They simply had no energy left to come up with an original Spring Festival red-envelope campaign.","Seeing the atmosphere grow increasingly oppressive, the head of marketing finally spoke up.","“Mr. Ma, judging from the current situation, we’re indeed extremely passive. MicroChat’s red-envelope campaign hits us from every possible angle. We have to admit that we’ve fallen behind.”","“First, the Spring Festival Gala’s viewership speaks for itself. On New Year’s Eve, hundreds of millions of people across the country will be watching it at the same time. The exposure will be terrifyingly massive. Second, one billion yuan is an explosive figure. No matter how much users actually receive—even if it’s only a few dimes or pennies—the sense of participation and the buzz it creates will completely overwhelm us.","“On top of that, the ‘Collect Five Blessings’ mechanic encourages social sharing. Once one person takes part, they’ll naturally pull in their entire family. Once the whole family joins, they’ll bring in their entire circle of friends. The speed of that viral spread will be impossible to stop...”","“I don’t need you to analyze this for me. I can see it perfectly well,” Pony Ma interrupted coldly.","“What I want to know is, what can we still do?”","Once again, a suffocating silence filled the room.","“Mr. ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‍Ma, from a technical standpoint, we can urgently integrate a red-envelope feature and launch a small-scale Chinese New Year red-envelope campaign within GooseChat. We won’t use the Spring Festival Gala channel. We’ll rely solely on GooseChat’s own user base and QQ’s traffic to promote it,” the product director said, struggling to come up with a countermeasure.","“How much will it cost?”","“If we want to generate a decent amount of buzz, at least... two hundred million yuan.”","Pony Ma didn’t respond immediately.","Two hundred million yuan was nothing Big Goose couldn’t afford. The problem was whether throwing two hundred million into it would actually achieve anything.","MicroChat had already seized all the momentum. On top of that, its payment infrastructure was far more advanced than GooseChat’s.","Once users finished grabbing MicroChat’s red envelopes, the money could be transferred directly into their DragonPay accounts and spent across more than a dozen consumer scenarios operated by Wanlong: buying groceries at supermarkets, surfing the internet at gaming cafés, ordering takeout, buying milk tea—the service covered practically every aspect of young people’s daily consumption.","And GooseChat?","Its payment license wasn’t even on the horizon. If they sent out red envelopes, users wouldn’t be able to spend the money. Were they supposed to leave it sitting in their GooseChat wallets as digital collectibles?","So this wasn’t a question of whether they should compete. They simply couldn’t compete.","If they forced the issue, they would only expose their own weaknesses even more thoroughly.","Pony Ma thought it over before finally making his decision.","“Begin the technical preparations. Get the red-envelope feature online first. Even if users can only send money and not spend it for the time being, we still have to keep up appearances. We can’t let users open their phones during the Spring Festival and see nothing but MicroChat handing out red envelopes. I’ll personally push the payment-license application.”","At the end of the meeting, he glanced at the Big Goose executives in the room and said coldly, “Let me make this clear now. If GooseChat is completely crushed by MicroChat, then in the new year we’ll have fallen irreversibly behind in the mobile-social market. And when that happens, every single one of you sitting here—every last one—will be held accountable!”","After the meeting ended, the executives hurried out of the conference room one after another.","In the end, only Pony Ma remained seated inside.","Leaning back in his chair, he stared blankly at the MicroChat logo on his phone.","A single person beneath a blue planet, its design simple to the point of arrogance.","At the same time, he remembered what Liu Yutong had said to him:","“Within two months, MicroChat’s user base will exceed GooseChat’s by at least thirty million.”","At the time, he had thought the goal was practically impossible.","After all, GooseChat had QQ’s enormous traffic pool constantly supplying it with new users. The gap between them was only four million. How could MicroChat possibly stretch that gap to thirty million within two months?","But looking at the situation now, did they even need two months?","He could already sense that he was highly likely to lose.","Honestly, no matter how unwilling he was to admit it, he had to acknowledge that the woman nearly twenty years younger than him was truly formidable.","Every move she made was a king-of-the-hill marketing masterstroke—something that could be taught as a case study in business school.","He could already imagine how badly Big Goose’s stock price would fall.","Pony Ma turned off his phone, leaned back against the chair, and closed his eyes.","It was not until the sky outside began to lighten that he finally opened them.","He rose to his feet and returned to his office. Unlocking the bottom drawer of his desk, he took out a dark-gold invitation.","Emblazoned on its cover was a phoenix with outstretched wings, beneath which three large gilded characters read:","—The Dark Phoenix Society."]},{"number":900,"title":"Chapter 900: 901. Match Delayed, New Year's Eve Red Envelope Night Million-Dollar Grand Prize","paragraphs":["On January 20, an announcement suddenly appeared on the Wanlong Association’s internal forum.","“Dragon Soaring Cup Finals Postponed!”","The ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‍announcement itself was simple. It contained only one sentence:","[The Young Lady’s order: The Dragon Soaring Cup finals will be postponed until after the Lantern Festival. Reason: The Young Lady will have a special arrangement at that time.]","Within a minute of the announcement being posted, the comments were already flooding in.","“Postponed? I’ve been waiting to watch Brother Yun and Brother Yang’s showdown. How long are we going to have to wait?”","“They said it’s a special arrangement. Could The Young Lady be handing out money again to surprise us?”","“Think bigger, brother. What’s so surprising about handing out money? I’ll bet fifty cents that The Young Lady is going to enter the competition herself.”","“What?! The Young Lady is going to compete personally? Are you trying to make every one of us forfeit on the spot? Who would dare fight her?”","“No, I mean, what if—just what if—The Young Lady really does enter? Are we supposed to fight or not? If we fight, what if we injure her? If we don’t, what if she thinks we aren’t taking it seriously?”","“To the guy above: you’d better start looking for a cemetery with good feng shui.”","“Hahahaha, I’m dying. The match hasn’t even started, and you’re already making arrangements for your funeral.”","“Seriously, though, did you notice that the announcement said ‘special arrangement,’ not ‘special reward’? I have a feeling The Young Lady is about to stir things up.”","“Let her stir things up. I’m actually looking forward to it. Things are way too boring right now. Those big shots from the outside world aren’t stupid anymore, and no one comes to provoke the Wanlong Association. What a disappointment!”","“Exactly. It’s been ages since anyone came to our door to offer themselves up as a punching bag. My hands are itching.”","“........”","Aside from those comments, some people’s imaginations ran wild.","“Hey, do you think The Young Lady might be planning to launch a rocket and have us hold the tournament on the moon?”","“Brother, where did that imagination of yours come from? A martial arts tournament on the moon? In that case, I strongly recommend making Brother Ji the referee. He’s an alien anyway.”","“Ji Yu: Is that any way to treat someone?”","“.......”","Everyone in the group was chatting enthusiastically when a new message suddenly popped up, instantly silencing them all.","The message had been posted by Liu Yutong herself.","[Although the Dragon Soaring Cup finals have been postponed, every employee of the Group will receive an additional 10,000 yuan as a special Spring Festival bonus. The money will be deposited before New Year’s Eve. In addition, on the day of the finals, the Lantern Festival, I will personally announce a major matter concerning the future development of the Wanlong Association. Everyone must attend. No leave requests will be accepted.]","Not long after the message was posted, the forum erupted once again.","“Long live The Young Lady!”","“10,000 yuan! And it’s on top of our regular pay! I’d like to see who else can top that!”","“What did I say? The Young Lady really is going to stir things up! A major matter! Did you hear that? A major matter!”","“Is this the first time The Young Lady has required everyone to attend?”","“What on earth is this major matter? I’m dying of curiosity! Can we fast-forward straight to the Lantern Festival?”","“Brother Yun, you’re the person closest to The Young Lady. Do you know what the major matter is?”","Amid the flood of messages, Yun Cheng made a rare appearance on the forum and replied:","“I don’t know.”","Lan Die soon appeared as well.","“I don’t know either.”","Ma Da’s messages were always the slowest to arrive—and the longest.","“Ahem. As the head of the Wanlong Association’s Human Resources Department, the chief commentator for the Dragon Soaring Cup, and The Young Lady’s number-one die-hard fan, I, Fatty Ma, hereby solemnly declare: This postponement was a decision The Young Lady made after careful consideration. It absolutely has nothing to do with the fact that Brother Ma failed to make it into the finals and forced the postponement so he could get more time to train. Please do not spread rumors, believe rumors, or pass rumors along!”","The moment his message appeared, a flood of replies popped up beneath it.","“Brother Ma, no one ever said you postponed it to get more time to train. You’re confessing without being accused!”","“I’m dying. Brother Ma, you really don’t have a single clever bone in your body.”","“Brother Ma is probably frantically searching for the delete button right now.”","“Brother Ma: I let the cat out of the bag, and it’s too late to delete the message.”","“Hahahaha, Brother Ma, stop explaining. You’re only making yourself look guiltier.”","“.........”","............","February 2, New Year’s Eve.","Shunchang Tower, Digital Business Group war room.","Zhang Dalong stood before an entire wall of monitoring screens, arms folded across his chest as he watched the real-time data from WeChat’s servers flicker across the displays.","The number of users online, concurrent message volume, the depth of the red-envelope request queue, database read and write latency... The figures were densely packed across the screens.","“Director Zhang, the first wave of lucky packets starts in three minutes.” The voice of the chief technology officer came through his earpiece.","Zhang Dalong picked up the radio and addressed everyone:","“All nodes, pay attention. Execute according to the plan. Team A, handle traffic distribution. Team B, monitor the database. Team C, stand by to switch to the backup cluster at any time. If any idiot’s shaky hands bring down the servers, you can spend tomorrow kneeling on durians in The Young Lady’s office.”","“Received!”","“Team B understands!”","“Team C is in position!”","“..........”","Zhang Dalong set down the radio and picked up the cup of coffee on the table, taking a long gulp.","Ma Da had specially brought the coffee over. He claimed it was some expensive kopi luwak flown in from overseas and said it would help keep them awake.","After one sip, Zhang Dalong nearly spat it out on the spot. It tasted like dirt and carried a strong earthy funk. He wondered if Ma Da had been scammed.","“Brother Long, the Spring Festival Gala livestream has been connected to our real-time interactive system.”","A young engineer wearing thick-rimmed glasses pointed at a side screen and said, “The host should announce the first red-envelope code at around 8:12 p.m. The lucky-packet entrance will open simultaneously.”","Zhang Dalong nodded, his gaze returning to the largest screen in the center. It displayed a real-time heat map of WeChat users online.","From the north to the south, from Shanghai to the remote northwestern borderlands, countless points of light covered the entire map, like a glittering galaxy.","The 2011 Year of the Tiger Spring Festival Gala was unlike those of later years. Most households still watched television, and viewership was frighteningly high.","On top of that, the Wanlong Association had invested heavily in this year’s interactive red-envelope event, driving the Gala’s traffic even higher.","As for exactly how high the traffic peak would climb, even Zhang Dalong had no idea.","Still, the server capacity had already been increased fivefold, and a large number of cloud servers had been rented in advance for elastic scaling. The system should not crash under the strain.","“Sixty seconds to go!”","Zhang Dalong put down his coffee cup and picked up the radio again.","“Everyone, listen up. The New Year’s Eve red-envelope battle officially begins now!”","........","At the same time, deep in the mountains of BS Province.","In a mountain village more than 2,000 meters above sea level, sixty-eight-year-old Apuqubu sat beside the hearth, slowly puffing on a long-stemmed tobacco pipe.","The firewood in the hearth burned brightly, casting a red glow across the old man’s dark, weathered face.","“Grandpa, Grandpa! Give me the phone!”","Xiaomuga rushed in from outside like a gust of wind and immediately grabbed the brand-new Longyao S1 from the table.","The phone had been bought for him last month by his grandson, using money the boy had saved from working away from home. He said that now, even while working outside, he could make video calls with Grandpa and see him whenever he wanted.","Apuqubu had spent a long time learning before he could barely manage to answer video calls. He still didn’t know how to use any of the phone’s other features.","“You little rascal, what are you grabbing it for?” Apuqubu lightly tapped his grandson on the head with his tobacco pipe.","“The Spring Festival Gala is giving out red envelopes! WeChat red envelopes! There’s a billion yuan up for grabs!”","Xiaomuga excitedly unlocked the screen, opened WeChat, and held it up in front of his grandfather.","“Look, Grandpa. When the time comes, tap here and shake it as hard as you can. If you shake out a lucky bag, you get a share of the money.”","“What money? Money falling from the sky? Sounds like a scam to me.” Apuqubu took a puff of his pipe, clearly unimpressed.","“It’s real money. A-Niu from our village collected all five blessings on his phone and won fifty yuan.”","Apuqubu watched skeptically as his grandson poked at the screen.","The display was a riot of bright colors, and he couldn’t make head or tail of it. But his grandson’s excitement reminded him of the first time electricity had reached the village thirty years ago, when everyone had gathered around the light bulb and stared at it in wonder for ages.","“It’s starting! It’s starting!” Xiaomuga suddenly shrieked, clutching the phone and shaking it wildly.","The shout startled Apuqubu so badly that the tobacco pipe in his hand nearly fell into the fire pit.","“Shake it, Grandpa! You shake it too! Harder!”","Xiaomuga shoved the phone into his grandfather’s hand. Seeing how excited his grandson was, Apuqubu shook it a few times as well.","Suddenly, a burst of golden fireworks exploded across the screen, bright enough to sting the eyes. A line of text appeared immediately afterward.","Congratulations! You have won a lucky bag!","Cash prize: 1,000,000 yuan!","Two logs in the fire pit crackled, and from somewhere in the distance came the occasional sound of scattered firecrackers.","The grandfather and grandson stared at the screen, both frozen in shock.","“Grandpa... It says... ones, tens, hundreds, thousands, ten-thousands, hundred-thousands, millions...”","“One million! Grandpa! It’s one million yuan!”","Apuqubu struck his tobacco pipe against the floor and frowned.","“Quit fooling me. How could a million yuan just fall from the sky? This has got to be some kind of scam.”","“It’s not a scam! This is WeChat—the WeChat run by Wanlong Group! It’s a legitimate major company! Everyone in the country uses it!”","Xiaomuga hurriedly explained, “Grandpa, look at this page. It’s the official LongPay page. We have to link a bank card to withdraw the money. Can we link our passbook...? No, wait, I don’t think passbooks work. But I have a bank card—the one I got when I was working away from home.”","Watching the overwhelming excitement on his grandson’s face, Apuqubu suddenly felt something strange stir in his heart.","In his more than sixty years of life, the largest sum of money he had ever seen was the four thousand yuan he’d gotten the year before last from selling two pigs.","He couldn’t even imagine what one million yuan looked like.","“Grandpa, I’ve linked the card!”","“Let’s hurry to the bank in town and see if the money’s really been deposited!”","Before Apuqubu could react, his grandson had already grabbed him and pulled him outside.","“Slow down! Slow down!”","The mountain roads were full of potholes. With flashlights in hand, the grandfather and grandson made their way toward town one careful step at a time.","Since growing old, Apuqubu had never left the house on New Year’s Eve. This time, however, his grandson had dragged him out into the night.","As they walked, he kept looking back at the old house, its lights glowing warmly in the darkness. A thought suddenly rose in his mind.","The times really have changed."]}]);
